experience as well by building rack pipelines using the Pinecone. And I''ve been working with OpenAI as well and Anthropic APIs. This will be giving the, you know, prompt engineering behind the demos. Yeah, this is all pretty basic introvert.","Got you. So coming to this scenario, I''ve been working with different projects like the supplier onboarding automation that is with our current client. So the problem was, you know, we have the massive backlog where the new suppliers will send the product catalog files. So our team, you know, will spend many days manually figuring out what the schema is and writing the mapping rules here and building the ETL jobs. And we are getting, you know, maybe like 30 to 20 new suppliers, maybe like around like maybe three to five days, this will be going to be onboard. So I''m building a multi-agent system as well using Langrave, where we''ll be having the four main agents within a certain graph. First is the layer agent that reads the supplier files, which might be CSV or Excel, and it will generate a schema understanding as well. So then in terms of the mapping agent, this will come, you know, compare the product taxonomy within our Snowflake database. And the third thing was the validation agent. This will be checking the mappings if they are running with some sample transformations. And finally, a code generation agent, that''s kind of DBT model and also the conversion with the Airflow decks. So this is the biggest challenge was like the state management between the different agents because you know, each agent gets messier because that needs like the parsing as well and also different objects, maybe in terms of the SQL queries. So I ended up using a combination of Pythonic models, this structure and stored the air facts mainly in our S3 within the references of the state graph. The other point was the rendering and retrace because some MLMs, you know, they don''t have the generated invalid sequence. So I need to give you feedback