d also Cosmos DB. I worked especially on GCP platform where I have utilized like I have used and also I worked on AWS as well, like where I have used CloudRun, App Engine, and also I worked on Firestore and all these things. And also I have worked with Terraform as well. So coming to the CI-CD part, so I have used Dockers and Kubernetes to create and manage containers which are used to run the microservices. And also I have used Jenkins for continuous integration and delivery purpose. And also I have used SonarCube and JUnit for code quality and testing purpose. And I have also optimized SQL queries as well. So coming to my previous project, I recently worked with Truest Bank. So here the implementation partner is Cognizant. So here I have worked on migrating a monolithic application to a microservice-based architecture through focusing on the payment service. So here we handled various types of transactions including real-time ACH payments, credit card payments, debit card transactions, as well as wire transfers, P2P transfers, recurring payments, bill payments, and also the mobile wallet transactions as well. So here my primary responsibility was managing all the real-time ACH transactions, like ensuring the secure and efficient processing. So we have developed specialized microservices to handle different aspects of ACH transactions. Like we mainly worked on ACH transaction service. So this is the core service that processes ACH payments including direct deposits, direct debits, P2P transfers, batch processing, and also the recurring payments. So here I have used Spring Security with OAuth2 and JWT to ensure proper authentication and authorization and also to ensure that only authorized users could access the sensitive information. So for the API traffic management, I have utilized Amazon API Gateway, which helped in securing the endpoints as well as load balancing. So when it comes to this payment service, right, so I have used Spring Batch along with executor service. And also I have used completable features to process batch transactions in parallel and in a thread-safe manner. So for recurring payments, I have utilized a cross-scheduler to run the scheduled tasks at regular intervals of time. And to manage the system''s data, I have used a mix of relational databases as well as NoSQL databases. Like we have used PostgreSQL and Oracle and also used MongoDB and RedisDB. And also I have used Apache Kafka for implementing the event-driven messaging systems. So we have enabled asynchronous and reliable message processing to handle the notification services, transaction logs, and also the real-time updates. And also I have implemented Saga design pattern to ensure the transactions failed, earlier steps could be rolled back with the help of compensating transactions. And to optimize the performance, I have applied the CQRS pattern separating the commands from the queries, so allowing for better handling of high-write and high-read operations. So in addition to that, I used Circuit Breaker pattern with Resilience4J. So this is my overall introduction and also what I have been working in my previous project.","missing_concepts":["Explicit mention of AI or LLM integration in projects.","Use of Neo4j or graph database technology.","Specific mention of domain-driven design principles."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a comprehensive and technically accurate description of their current role as a full-stack Java developer working extensively on backend microservices, cloud deployment, and event-driven architectures. They demonstrated solid knowledge of Java frameworks and related technologies, and detailed a complex payment service project involving multiple transaction types, security, and pattern implementations which showcases strong problem-solving and design skills. However, the answer lacked focus at times and missed certain elements from the ideal answer such as AI/LLM involvement and usage of graph databases like Neo4j. The communication could be made more concise to improve clarity. Overall, the candidate shows strong technical competency relevant to the role and projects described.","interviewer_summary":"An experienced full-stack Java developer with deep expertise in backend microservices, security, and cloud platforms, who has worked on complex, real-world payment processing systems. Although the answer could be more concise and focused, the candidate demonstrated solid understanding and practical application of important backend development concepts and tools, making them a suitable candidate fo"},{"prompt":"What microservices did you build using Java or Node.js recently?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":7,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Provided a clear example of an ACH transaction microservice, detailing its responsibilities and business context.","Mentioned usage of design patterns relevant to microservices such as circuit breaker, saga, and API gateway.","Highlighted technical reasons for choosing Node.js for asynchronous, IO-heavy operations with event-driven architecture.","Discussed integration with external bank APIs and Kafka message publishing."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Did not explicitly mention frameworks or specific tools used in Java or Node.js for microservice development (e.g., Spring Boot, Express).","Lacked detail on scalability, fault tolerance beyond pattern usage, CI/CD, cloud/container deployments, or monitoring strategies.","Explanation was somewhat repetitive and lacked structured clarity, affecting communication quality.","Did not explicitly describe how these microservices fit into larger distributed architectures in detail."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should detail specific microservices they developed using Java or Node.js, highlighting the purpose and business context of each service. They should mention building RESTful APIs or backend services using frameworks like Spring Boot (Java) or Express/Koa (Node.js) and demonstrate how these microservices fit into a distributed architecture. For example, they might describe a user authentication service handling JWT token creation and validation, or an order processing service that integrates with external payment gateways and uses event-driven communication (e.g., via Kafka). The candidate should also emphasize design choices for scalability, fault tolerance, and how they employed design patterns (such as domain-driven design) in the microservice implementation. Clear references to cloud or containerized deployment (e.g., on AWS/EKS or Docker), CI/CD integration, and monitoring are a plus, showing end-to-end ownership and operational awareness.","candidateAnswer":"So when it comes to that, right, so yeah, I have built a microservices, so in my recent project, and also we have used this for building a real-time ACH transaction service. So here we have specialized a microservices which can handle like different aspects of ACH transaction. So we have our ACH transaction service. So this is one of the core microservices that I would say because it is used to manage the direct deposits, direct debits, P2P transfers, batch processing, and also the recurring payments. It manages the payment completion and it retries the failed transactions and also it handles if there are any issues as well. So the service also connects with the banks and also the financial institutions to process all the payments. So this microservice, right, so we have used different microservice patterns like we have used a circuit breaker pattern, we have used saga design pattern, and also we have used API gateway design pattern. So these are the major patterns that I have used. So when it comes to the Node.js, right, so I have used Node.js as well. So in this project, so. So when it comes to the Node.js part, right, so in this microservices, so here, so we have basically responsible for developing some of these microservices using Node.js because this Node.js is very good for handling all the asynchronous and also the event-driven workloads as well. So for example, in our ACH processing service, right, so here many operations are IO heavy, which are like input and output heavy operations are to be made, so such as like calling bank APIs, publishing Kafka messages, reading the transaction status as well as sending notifications and also writing the audit logs. So here Node.js, right, so it basically helped us to handle all these operations efficiently using its non-blocking event loop. So this is how I have used Node.js in my previous project.","missing_concepts":["Specific frameworks for building microservices (e.g., Spring Boot, Express).","Cloud/container deployment or operational monitoring practices.","CI/CD integration or end-to-end ownership details.","Explicit mention of RESTful API development."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrated good technical understanding by describing a concrete ACH transaction microservice with relevant responsibilities and design patterns. The explanation of Node.js usage for asynchronous and IO-heavy tasks was insightful. However, the answer lacked references to common frameworks, deployment environments, and end-to-end operational aspects expected for a senior engineering role. Communication, while generally understandable, was somewhat repetitive and could benefit from clearer structure and conciseness. Overall, this is a solid answer showing practical experience and understanding of microservice design and operation, passing the threshold but with room for improved detail and clarity.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows solid experience building microservices using Node.js and Java, emphasizing key design patterns and asynchronous handling. They illustrate good problem-solving skills and relevant knowledge but could provide more specific technical tooling and deployment details to demonstrate fuller mastery. Communication clarity and completeness are adequate to pass."},{"prompt":"How did you design APIs for high-traffic distributed systems?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":7,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Mentioned stateless REST API design supporting horizontal scaling","Included important resilience patterns like circuit breakers, retries, and timeouts","Discussed caching, async processing, and pagination for performance","Considered observability with correlation IDs, structured logs, metrics, and tracing","Addressed security aspects including OAuth2, JWT, rate limiting, and encryption"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Answer somewhat repetitive and filler words reduce clarity","Explanation lacked structured flow and was somewhat verbose","Did not explicitly mention API versioning and consistent error handling","Some concepts mentioned briefly without deep elaboration (e.g., connection pooling, fallback handling)"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"For designing APIs in high-traffic distributed systems, I focused on ensuring scalability, reliability, and low latency. I leveraged RESTful principles with statelessness and designed APIs to be idempotent wherever possible. Key approaches included implementing rate limiting and throttling to protect backend services, using caching layers (e.g., CDN or in-memory caches) to reduce load, and designing APIs to support asynchronous processing when appropriate to handle spikes gracefully. I also ensured APIs followed consistent versioning and error-handling strategies to ease client integration and backward compatibility. On the infrastructure side, I used load balancers, horizontal scaling of microservices managed via container orchestration (e.g., Kubernetes), and applied circuit breakers to prevent cascading failures. Monitoring and observability were integral, with metrics and tracing to quickly detect performance bottlenecks and failures.","candidateAnswer":"So yeah, so here, right, so basically, so for designing any APIs, right, so which are basically used to handle this high traffic systems, so high traffic distributed systems. So here, basically, I will start designing the API, like first I will start with the clean REST design, and then I keep the APIs stateless, so they can scale horizontally. And also, we usually place this service behind the API gateway or load balancer. Then we deploy multiple instances using Kubernetes or cloud auto-scaling. So for performance, I used pagination, and also I will be implementing the caching, async processing, and also connection pool, and also these database indexing as well. So for resilience, so for resiliency, I''ll be adding the timeout, and also I''ll be adding the retries, circuit breaker, as well as item potency, and also I''ll be doing the fallback handling as well. And for the production support, so I make sure like every request has correlation IDs and structured logs, like metrics and also tracing, and also does have all the proper monitoring and all. So here basically I will be using OAuth2 and JWT for security purpose, and also I will be implementing the API gateway policies, and I will be implementing the rate limiting, input validations, and also the encryption as well. So for data consistency, I use itempotency keys to avoid duplicate ACH or any payment transactions in my previous project.","missing_concepts":["Explicit API versioning strategy","Consistent error-handling methodologies","Explicit mention of handling spikes beyond async processing like backpressure"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a solid and mostly technically correct answer covering many fundamental aspects of designing APIs for high-traffic distributed systems. They correctly emphasized REST statelessness for horizontal scalability, use of Kubernetes and auto-scaling, resilience patterns like circuit breakers and retries, performance features such as caching, pagination, and async processing, and observability with correlation IDs and metrics. Security considerations like OAuth2, JWT, encryption, and rate limiting were also well noted. However, the answer lacked polish and clarity due to repetitive filler words and a less organized explanation. Furthermore, the candidate did not explicitly mention API versioning or systematic error handling, which are important for backward compatibility and client integration. Overall, the candidate demonstrates good understanding of key concepts but could improve communication clarity and completeness in covering all aspects.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows strong knowledge of API design for distributed high-traffic systems, addressing scalability, performance, resilience, security, and monitoring. While the answer has some verbosity and misses a few finer points like versioning and error handling, it reflects practical experience and a clear grasp of core principles. They pass with a solid score but should focus on clearer, more "},{"prompt":"What real production issue did you debug in a microservices environment?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":7,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Candidate described a concrete production issue related to duplicate ACH transactions in a microservices environment.","Clear identification of root cause through log tracing and correlation IDs.","Explanation of retry logic and consumer processing issues in Kafka event handling.","Actions taken to fix the problem, including idempotency checks and improved retry/dead-letter queue handling."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["The explanation lacked mention of distributed tracing tools, which would strengthen debugging in microservices.","Some technical explanations were somewhat vague or unclear, affecting communication clarity.","Did not mention reproducing the issue in a staging environment or monitoring metrics as part of debugging."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific production incident involving microservices, such as dealing with cascading failures or latency spikes affecting service communication. They should explain how they identified the root cause through distributed tracing tools (like Jaeger or Zipkin) or log aggregation systems, pinpointing issues like misconfigured circuit breakers, race conditions, or database deadlocks in a microservices interaction. They should detail the debugging steps taken—for example, analyzing service logs, monitoring metrics, and reproducing the issue in a staging environment—and how they resolved it by fixing service dependencies, improving retry logic, or optimizing queries to restore system stability and performance. The answer should highlight their understanding of distributed systems complexities and practices for troubleshooting such environments.","candidateAnswer":"Okay, so when it comes to this real-time situation, right, so in my previous project, so we have faced one issue, especially in the production. So while we are, so then there mainly the issue comes with this duplicate ACH transaction processing. So here in our ACH transaction service, so which was publishing events to Kafka after the validation. So here the downstream services like audit logging and notifications services were consuming those events. So one day, like the support reported that there are few customers who received like duplicate transaction notifications in some cases. Then the same ACH transactions looked like it was processed twice in the audit screen. So here, right, so in this situation, first I have checked the logs using the correlation ID or the transaction ID to trace the full flow across the services. Then I verified the Kafka consumer logs and then I noticed the consumer who had retried the same message after a timeout. So the actual payment process was successful, but the acknowledgement to the Kafka did not complete properly. So that is what we came to know after the checking. So the same event was, you know, consumed again. So here the main issue was not Kafka itself. So we have debugged the issue. So the issue was that our consumer logic was not fully item pranked. So it was, you know, processing the event again instead of checking whether the transaction ID has already been handled or not. So basically we have then added the item prancing check using this transaction ID and the event type before processing the message. And also we have improved the retry handling as well. So we have added better timeout settings and we pushed these failed events to DLQ after the retry limit. So this is how we have identified and we have handled a production issue.","missing_concepts":["Use of distributed tracing tools (e.g., Jaeger, Zipkin)","Monitoring metrics analysis","Reproducing the issue in non-production environment"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a relevant and technically accurate example of debugging a production issue related to event duplication in Kafka within a microservices architecture. They demonstrated good problem-solving by tracing logs using correlation IDs and identifying retry and idempotency problems. Improvements such as adding idempotency checks and DLQ handling showed understanding of Kafka consumer resilience. However, the answer missed discussing distributed tracing tools which are common in microservice debugging, as well as monitoring and reproducing issues. Communication clarity was moderate due to some unclear phrasing and slightly disorganized explanation. Overall, a good practical example with room for deeper technical insights and clearer articulation.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate effectively described a real production issue in a microservices context involving Kafka message duplication and showed sound problem-solving skills by identifying and fixing idempotency and retry logic flaws. While the answer was relevant and technically solid, it lacked deeper technical details like distributed tracing and monitoring that are important in microservice debugging. Co"},{"prompt":"How have you used Neo4j in real-world projects?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":7,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Demonstrated clear understanding of why Neo4j is beneficial for highly connected data.","Provided a concrete real-world example (banking system with entities and relationships).","Mentioned use of Spring Data Neo4j and backend integration with microservices.","Identified practical use case related to fraud detection and querying connected patterns."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Explanation was somewhat verbose and lacked polished clarity.","Did not explicitly mention Cypher queries or specific query optimizations.","Could have discussed graph schema design or data ingestion pipelines in more detail.","Some language was informal and occasionally repetitive."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"In real-world projects, I have used Neo4j as the primary graph database to model complex relationships among entities, enabling efficient querying of connected data via Cypher. For example, in a knowledge graph project, I designed domain-driven graph schemas to represent entities and their relationships, which allowed semantic queries to identify patterns and infer connections. I have integrated Neo4j within microservices built with Spring Boot, exposing RESTful APIs to access and manipulate graph data. Additionally, I leveraged Neo4j''s capabilities for real-time recommendations and relationship analytics in the backend. This usage often included building data pipelines to ingest and update graph data, as well as optimizing queries for scalable performance.","candidateAnswer":"So in the, when it comes to the Neo4j, right, so especially in my previous projects, so basically I have used this Neo4j for when dealing with data that is highly connected and that is difficult to analyze. So here, right, so in my previous project, so especially in the banking system, so we had entities like customers, accounts, cards, devices, merchants, transaction IDs, and you know, we had addresses, phone numbers, and all those things. So basically the business wants to identify the suspicious relationships, like, you know, one device being used by multiple customers and multiple accounts connected to the same phone number or, you know, transactions moving through the linked accounts and all. So in normal SQL database, we could still do this, but it requires many joins and queries, so which becomes implementing it more complex and also it will be very slow. So we have used Neo4j because which is a graph database, which is very helpful to store all the relationships clearly here. So here, in addition to that, so I would say like, we have integrated this Neo4j with our backend services using Springboard and Neo4j Java driver, or we can say the Spring Data Neo4j. So basically the microservice would receive the transactions or the customer activity events, and then it updates the relationships in Neo4j and exposes the APIs for fraud analytics or the internal systems to query the connected patterns. So in production, right, so this Neo4j helps us to query all these relationships more faster, and it is more natural than, you know, writing complex SQL joints and all.","missing_concepts":["Explicit mention of Cypher query language usage.","Details on schema modeling or domain-driven graph design.","Discussion of performance tuning or scalability considerations.","Integration beyond backend microservices, e.g., exposing RESTful APIs explicitly."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrated a solid understanding of the advantages of using Neo4j for highly connected data, with a relevant real-world example from the banking domain related to fraud detection. Integration with Spring Data Neo4j and microservices showed practical experience. However, the response lacked clarity in parts and missed several key aspects expected in an ideal answer, such as explicit mention of Cypher queries, graph schema design, and optimization strategies. Communication could be more concise and polished. Overall, the candidate showed strong technical knowledge and problem-solving capability but would benefit from deeper technical details and clearer explanations.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate provided a relevant and technically sound example of using Neo4j in a banking project for fraud analytics. Understanding of Neo4j''s benefits for connected data and integration with Java backend technologies is good. Communication was somewhat informal and could be improved for clarity. Missing some advanced details, but overall a competent and practical response."}]'), ('cmp7cig9i001dp00jkdgcxof1', 'cmp7cd9bs000cp00jbo3z8y72', 32, 62, 54, 100, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-05-15 20:04:08.023', '2026-05-21 18:53:51.121', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hi, hello, how are you?","So I am just going to give you a recruit because I, you know, I love selling pharmaceuticals.","So, you know, I used to like belma ke samose, hari chutney with some portal, like tomato, dhaniya, pyaaz and all."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 8, '[{"prompt":"Could you start by telling me a bit about your background and why you''re interested in the US IT Recruiter role?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["The answer is somewhat understandable in brief communication clarity."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Does not address background related to recruitment or human resources.","No mention of interest in US IT recruitment or relevant experience.","Answer is largely irrelevant to the question asked.","Lacks any discussion about skills, motivation, or willingness to work in relevant contexts."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"An ideal candidate should describe their educational background and any relevant experiences or internships related to recruitment or human resources. They should express a clear interest in building a career in US IT staffing and recruitment, highlighting motivation to connect IT talent with opportunities. For example, they might mention exposure to sourcing or screening candidates, familiarity with US hiring practices, or a strong desire to develop skills in talent acquisition specific to the IT sector. Additionally, they should mention willingness to work night shifts aligned with US time zones and eagerness to learn quickly and contribute effectively in a remote team environment.","candidateAnswer":"So I am just going to give you a recruit because I, you know, I love selling pharmaceuticals.","missing_concepts":["Educational background or relevant experience in recruitment or HR.","Interest and motivation for US IT staffing and recruitment.","Familiarity with candidate sourcing, screening, or US hiring practices.","Mention of key skills such as sourcing, screening, ATS, c2c, w2.","Willingness to work night shifts and remote teamwork."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response is largely irrelevant and does not answer the question about their background or interest in the US IT Recruiter role. There is no indication of relevant experience, technical knowledge, or motivation related to IT recruitment. The answer is insufficient and does not demonstrate understanding of the role or required skills. Communication is minimal and off-topic, resulting in a failing evaluation.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate failed to provide any relevant information about their background or interest in the US IT Recruiter role. The answer was off-topic and did not demonstrate the required knowledge or motivation. Overall, the candidate did not meet the expectations for this introductory question."},{"prompt":"Which job portals have you used for sourcing candidates?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":1,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Answer is completely irrelevant to the question.","No mention of any job portals or sourcing channels for candidates.","Does not demonstrate any understanding of sourcing candidates from job portals.","Communication is unclear and confusing with unrelated food items mentioned."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"For sourcing IT candidates, the ideal portals used include LinkedIn, Dice, Monster, and Indeed, as these are widely recognized platforms for US IT recruitment. Candidates may also utilize internal databases and niche sites depending on role specificity.","candidateAnswer":"So, you know, I used to like belma ke samose, hari chutney with some portal, like tomato, dhaniya, pyaaz and all.","missing_concepts":["LinkedIn","Dice","Monster","Indeed","Internal databases","Niche job portals"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate answer is completely off-topic and does not address the question about job portals used for sourcing candidates. There is no mention of any relevant platforms or sourcing methods used in the IT recruitment domain. The answer includes unrelated terms that do not demonstrate any understanding of the recruitment process. Overall, the candidate fails to provide a technically correct, relevant, or complete response.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide any meaningful information about job portals used for sourcing IT candidates. The answer was completely irrelevant and demonstrated a lack of knowledge or understanding of typical sourcing platforms in the US IT recruitment context."},{"prompt":"Can you name any specific job portals you''ve actually used for sourcing IT candidates, such as Dice or LinkedIn?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Answer is completely irrelevant to the question asked.","No mention of any job portals or sourcing platforms.","Does not demonstrate understanding of IT candidate sourcing."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Yes, common job portals used for sourcing IT candidates include LinkedIn, Dice, Monster, and Indeed. Recruiters often use these platforms to search for profiles based on technical skills, experience, and location relevant to US IT roles.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, I used a lemon but along with lemon I used green chutney.","missing_concepts":["Specific job portals such as LinkedIn, Dice, Monster, Indeed","Use of these portals for sourcing IT candidates","Technical skills and experience based search"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer did not address the question in any meaningful way. Instead of naming and discussing job portals used for IT candidate sourcing, the answer referenced unrelated items with no connection to the topic. This shows either lack of knowledge or misunderstanding of the question, resulting in zero points across all categories.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate failed to identify or mention any IT job portals, providing an irrelevant and nonsensical answer. This raises serious doubts about their knowledge of sourcing IT candidates using platforms like LinkedIn or Dice."},{"prompt":"How do you typically screen resumes for technical requirements quickly?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Answer is completely irrelevant to the question asked.","No mention of any screening techniques or technical requirements.","No demonstration of understanding of the resume screening process."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"To quickly screen resumes for technical requirements, I first scan for specific keywords and technologies listed in the job description, such as programming languages (e.g., Java, React), frameworks, certifications, and relevant tools. I look for clear mentions of skills, years of experience, and project contexts that match the requirement. Additionally, I verify the candidate’s job titles and responsibilities to ensure alignment. Using ATS search filters helps speed this process by flagging these key technical terms. This approach ensures an efficient and focused review of resumes to shortlist qualified candidates promptly.","candidateAnswer":"Okay, so I''ll use the, you know, desi food as one of the conventions for food.","missing_concepts":["Using keywords and technologies from job descriptions to screen resumes.","Checking job titles, skills, experience, and certifications.","Utilizing ATS filters and structured approaches for efficiency."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer does not address the question about screening resumes for technical requirements. The response is unrelated and provides no relevant information or approach regarding resume screening or technical evaluation. There is no indication of knowledge or understanding of the role or methods involved in quickly screening resumes to identify qualified candidates.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate failed to provide any relevant or coherent answer to the question on how to quickly screen resumes for technical requirements, showing no grasp of the key responsibilities for the role of US IT Recruiter."},{"prompt":"Can you share how you identify technical skills from resumes efficiently?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Answer is completely irrelevant to the question asked.","No mention or indication of knowledge about resume screening or technical skills identification.","Does not demonstrate any understanding of recruitment or technical evaluation processes."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"To efficiently identify technical skills from resumes, a recruiter should carefully scan the skills section, professional summary, and detailed work experience for specific technologies, programming languages, tools, and methodologies relevant to the job description. Using keyword searches within resumes—either manually or via Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS)—can speed up this process by highlighting pertinent skills such as Java, React, .NET, or DevOps. Additionally, distinguishing between proficiency levels mentioned and validating these through screening calls ensures accurate assessment of candidates'' technical capabilities.","candidateAnswer":"So I took a tail and some refined oil using with some palm oil, olive oil.","missing_concepts":["Scanning resumes for skills and keywords.","Using Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS) and keyword searches.","Identifying technologies, programming languages, methodologies from resumes.","Assessing proficiency levels of candidates'' technical skills.","Validating skills through screening calls or interviews."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is completely unrelated to the question about identifying technical skills from resumes. The response mentions oils and substances unrelated to recruitment or resume screening, indicating no understanding or attempt to address the question. This shows a lack of technical correctness, relevance, completeness, and communication clarity. The candidate did not demonstrate any grasp of the problem-solving required to efficiently assess technical skills in resumes.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide any relevant or meaningful response to the question. The answer showed no understanding of resume screening techniques or the identification of technical skills. This reflects poorly on the candidate''s suitability for a US IT Recruiter role, especially related to screening technical candidates."},{"prompt":"What challenges have you faced while sourcing IT candidates?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":1,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Answer is completely irrelevant to the question","No mention of any IT recruiting challenges","No technical content or understanding demonstrated","Communication is unclear and off-topic"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Common challenges in sourcing IT candidates include high competition for skilled talent, difficulty in finding candidates with niche technical skills like React or DevOps, and managing candidate expectations about roles and compensation. Additionally, navigating visa and work eligibility issues for US positions, and ensuring a quality pipeline within tight deadlines can be demanding. Using multiple sourcing channels effectively while maintaining candidate engagement and data accuracy in ATS are also key challenges.","candidateAnswer":"Sometimes that samosa taste was not good, so in that situation I used some red chutney in order to green chutney to make the taste of samosa eatable.","missing_concepts":["Challenges related to sourcing skilled IT candidates","Competition for talent","Niche technical skills sourcing","Candidate expectations and compensation issues","Visa and work eligibility complications","Quality pipeline management","Using sourcing channels and ATS effectively"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response is completely unrelated to the question about challenges in sourcing IT candidates. The answer talks about samosa taste and chutneys which has no connection to IT recruiting or sourcing challenges. There is no demonstration of any understanding or awareness of the technical, operational, or strategic challenges in IT recruitment. The response lacks relevance, technical correctness, completeness, and clarity. It does not address any of the key skills or difficulties expected for this medium difficulty question. Overall, the answer fails to meet any of the evaluation criteria and indicates no knowledge or experience in the subject matter.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide any relevant or meaningful answer to the question about sourcing IT candidates. The response was off-topic and does not reflect any understanding of IT recruitment challenges. This answer clearly demonstrates a lack of preparation or knowledge for the role."},{"prompt":"How do you handle multiple requirements at the same time?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Answer is irrelevant to the question asked","No mention of managing multiple requirements or prioritization","No demonstration of understanding or problem-solving skills related to the role","Answer lacks any technical or process-based details","Communication is disorganized and does not address the interview question"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"To handle multiple requirements simultaneously, I prioritize based on urgency, client expectations, and role criticality. I maintain organized records for each position using tools like ATS and spreadsheets to track candidate pipelines separately. Effective time management and regular communication with clients and candidates ensure that all requirements progress smoothly without delays. I also set daily goals and use alerts or reminders to follow up on pending tasks, ensuring accuracy and speed while managing workload.","candidateAnswer":"With my colleague like Reddy Singh is a great human being, Om Prakash is also a great human being, so I used to work with these guys.","missing_concepts":["Prioritization of requirements based on urgency and client needs","Use of tools such as ATS or spreadsheets to track candidates","Time management and organization techniques","Communication with clients and candidates to ensure smooth progression","Setting goals and reminders to manage multiple tasks effectively"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response did not address the question about handling multiple requirements at the same time. Instead, the answer focused on mentioning colleagues without relating to the core competencies required. There is no demonstration of understanding of crucial concepts like prioritization, organization, or use of relevant tools. The response is irrelevant and fails to display any problem-solving ability or best practices expected from the role of a US IT Recruiter managing multiple requirements. Overall, the candidate does not meet the minimum requirements for this question.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to answer the question in any meaningful way. Their response was off-topic and did not demonstrate any of the necessary skills or understanding expected for managing multiple recruitment requirements. The candidate lacks the ability to prioritize and organize workload efficiently based on the answer given."},{"prompt":"How do you personally stay organized when managing several candidate pipelines at once?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":3,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["Candidate mentions using Excel sheets which can be a basic organizational tool"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-7","weaknesses":["Answer is very vague and unclear","No mention of detailed records, ATS, reminders, prioritization, or candidate segmentation","Lacks demonstration of understanding managing multiple candidate pipelines effectively","Does not explain organization methods in recruitment context"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe using systematic approaches like maintaining detailed records in an ATS or spreadsheets, setting reminders for follow-ups, and prioritizing tasks based on urgency and client needs. They might mention segmenting candidates by job role or status to avoid confusion, regularly updating pipeline status, and leveraging calendar tools to track interviews and communications. This demonstrates their ability to handle multiple recruitment processes efficiently without losing track of progress or candidate engagement.","candidateAnswer":"So I used to create a database of devices and of home. So those, you know, Excel sheets helped me a lot.","missing_concepts":["Using Applicant Tracking Systems or spreadsheets tailored for recruitment","Setting reminders and prioritizing tasks","Segmenting candidates by role or status","Regular updates of pipeline status","Using calendar tools for scheduling interviews and follow-ups"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is very vague and unrelated in parts (mentioning ''devices and home'' database is unclear). They only mention Excel sheets generally, without connecting this to recruitment or managing multiple candidate pipelines. There is no demonstration of systematic organization, prioritization, or candidate tracking necessary for the role. The response lacks technical correctness and completeness related to recruitment pipeline management, showing a weak understanding of the question. The communication is somewhat unclear, and the answer does not display problem-solving skills or relevant techniques expected. Overall, the answer does not meet the requirements of organizing multiple recruitment pipelines efficiently.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows minimal relevant organizational approach using Excel but fails to address key strategies for managing multiple candidate pipelines such as ATS use, candidate segmentation, and task prioritization. The response lacks clarity and depth, indicating a weak understanding of recruitment process management necessary for the role. Candidate does not meet the expected competency level."},{"prompt":"How do you follow up with candidates during the interview process?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":3,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["Recognizes follow-up is necessary","Mentions delegation of follow-up responsibility"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-8","weaknesses":["Does not explain how follow-up is conducted","No mention of communication methods or tracking tools","Lacks any detail on candidate engagement or process management","Answer is too brief and vague"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"A strong US IT Recruiter follows up with candidates by maintaining regular, clear communication via phone calls, emails, or messaging platforms to update them on interview schedules, feedback, and next steps. They proactively check in after interviews to address candidate questions and keep engagement high, ensuring timely responses and transparency throughout the process. Using ATS tools to track interactions and setting reminders for follow-ups helps manage multiple candidates efficiently.","candidateAnswer":"I usually ask phone to follow up with my delegates, so he takes care of that.","missing_concepts":["Using phone calls, emails, or messages for follow-up","Providing updates on interview schedules, feedback, next steps","Proactive candidate engagement and addressing questions","Using ATS tools to track interactions and set reminders"],"detailed_feedback":"The answer is very brief and does not provide a clear explanation of how follow-ups are handled. Merely stating that follow-up is delegated to someone else without describing the methods, frequency, or tools used shows lack of understanding of the recruiter role''s communication responsibilities. There is no mention of maintaining candidate engagement, providing timely updates, or using ATS systems, all of which are important. Overall, the response is insufficient and fails to demonstrate the knowledge and skills expected.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate showed minimal understanding of the follow-up process with candidates. The answer was vague and lacked critical details regarding communication methods and candidate management. The candidate needs to develop deeper knowledge of recruitment follow-up best practices and ATS usage."},{"prompt":"What would you do if a candidate stopped responding suddenly?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":3,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["Candidate indicates the action of contacting the candidate personally."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-9","weaknesses":["Answer is too short and vague.","Does not mention polite follow-ups, timing or number of attempts.","No mention of documenting status or informing hiring manager.","No indication of continuing to source other candidates.","Poor communication clarity and minimal explanation."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"If a candidate stops responding suddenly, I would first send a polite follow-up message or email to remind them of the pending communication and check if they are still interested. If there is no response after one or two attempts spaced over a few days, I would document this status in the ATS and inform the hiring manager accordingly. Meanwhile, I would continue to source and engage other potential candidates to avoid delays in filling the position.","candidateAnswer":"Then I personally, you know, contacted him. Yeah.","missing_concepts":["Polite follow-up message/email.","Multiple attempts over several days.","Documenting candidate status in ATS.","Informing the hiring manager.","Continuing sourcing and engagement of other candidates."],"detailed_feedback":"The answer is extremely brief and offers minimal insight into the candidate''s approach. While the candidate states they contacted the person, they miss key professional steps like sending polite follow-ups, timing and frequency considerations, documentation in ATS, informing relevant stakeholders, and ongoing sourcing efforts. The explanation lacks clarity and detail, demonstrating a limited understanding of the process. For a recruiter role, especially with medium difficulty expected, the response is insufficient and does not meet the standards for a passing answer.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate''s answer showed very limited understanding and was incomplete with poor communication clarity. They failed to discuss critical best practices such as polite follow-ups, documentation, and continuing engagement of other candidates. Overall, the response was inadequate for the role''s expectations."},{"prompt":"How comfortable are you working in US night shifts regularly?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["Candidate states comfort with working US night shifts"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-10","weaknesses":["Answer is very vague and incomplete","No explanation or examples related to adaptability or strategies to manage night shifts","Irrelevant mention of playing cricket without connection to the question","Lacks any professional or technical reasoning"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should express clear willingness and adaptability to work US night shifts regularly, emphasizing their ability to manage work-life balance and maintain productivity during these hours. They might mention prior experience working in night shifts or strategies they use to stay alert and focused during such hours.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, I am very much comfortable because I, you know, I used to play cricket.","missing_concepts":["Willingness and adaptability to work night shifts","Work-life balance management","Experience with night shifts","Strategies to stay alert and productive during night hours"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is vague and does not directly address the question. Simply saying ''I am comfortable because I used to play cricket'' is irrelevant and does not demonstrate an understanding of the challenges or strategies for working US night shifts. There is no mention of prior experience, adaptability, or methods to maintain productivity during these hours. The candidate should have provided a more detailed and relevant response addressing both willingness and ability to manage night shifts effectively.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide a relevant or complete answer regarding their comfort and adaptability to US night shifts. The response lacked professionalism and did not demonstrate an understanding of the question''s requirements. Recommend further evaluation on situational adaptability."}]'), ('cmp7v1ldu002cp00js0aoqu6d', 'cmp7ue172001jp00jh6bqo7sn', 65, 100, 90, 100, 'Strong performance with structured answers and solid topic understanding.', '2026-05-16 04:42:54.21', '2026-05-21 18:51:24.887', '["Clear communication flow","Good depth in responses"]', '["Add sharper quantified examples","Reduce filler and tighten transitions"]', '["My name is Mahesh Krishnason. I''ve been working in the insurance industry for like more like a close to two decades. I worked for Arkansas Blue Cross Blue Shield for six years, and then I worked for a life insurance company for like around 17 years. So overall I have like more than two decades of experience. And last 17 years I''ve been working on .NET. So I worked on like a different several versions of .NET. I worked on .NET framework. I worked on .NET Core, C Sharp, VB.NET, ASP.NET forms, ASP.NET WCF services, ASP.NET Web API. I also worked on web services that were in the beginning of .NET. Currently I''m working on REST APIs and I worked on React framework and Vue.js too.","Currently, I am working with the Bank of America client through Infosys, which is an IT services company. So the reason I applied for Humana is because, you know, it''s a remote and I have a lot of experience with health and life insurance companies. I''m very comfortable working in an insurance company because, you know, I worked on pretty much every department of insurance company. And also I worked with pretty much every insurance system from customer service, billing, claims, benefits, underwriting, actuarial, pretty much, you know, pretty much any department in the insurance company, basically. So that''s one of my main strong points. And the technical skills, you know, I''m very proficient with the skills that are needed for this role. Yeah, that''s what I am. That''s what my background is. And thank you very much for considering me for this role.","So I worked on .NET Core, ASP.NET Core MVC, also worked on APIs, REST APIs."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 45, '[{"prompt":"Tell me a bit about your background and how it relates to this .NET Developer role.","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Extensive experience with .NET including multiple versions (.NET Framework, .NET Core).","Experience with C#, VB.NET, ASP.NET forms, WCF services, and Web API.","Recent work with REST APIs and modern frontend frameworks like React and Vue.js."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["No explicit mention of Angular or Bootstrap which are key skills for the role.","No details on microservices architecture or Agile methodologies.","No mention of technical leadership, mentoring, or solution architect roles.","Lacks examples of enterprise-grade application delivery or structured SDLC."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate will describe over 10 years of hands-on experience in software development with a focus on C# and .NET Framework/Core, including deep expertise in building enterprise-grade applications. They should highlight their experience with RESTful APIs, Entity Framework, and SQL Server, along with UI development using Angular (7+) and Bootstrap. The candidate will mention involvement in microservices architecture and use of Agile methodologies, emphasizing roles where they have taken technical leadership or solution architect responsibilities. Concrete examples may include leading cross-functional teams, mentoring juniors, and delivering robust, scalable solutions in structured SDLC environments. They should connect these experiences explicitly to the role''s requirements in designing, developing, and delivering complex .NET applications in a hybrid/agile setting.","candidateAnswer":"My name is Mahesh Krishnason. I''ve been working in the insurance industry for like more like a close to two decades. I worked for Arkansas Blue Cross Blue Shield for six years, and then I worked for a life insurance company for like around 17 years. So overall I have like more than two decades of experience. And last 17 years I''ve been working on .NET. So I worked on like a different several versions of .NET. I worked on .NET framework. I worked on .NET Core, C Sharp, VB.NET, ASP.NET forms, ASP.NET WCF services, ASP.NET Web API. I also worked on web services that were in the beginning of .NET. Currently I''m working on REST APIs and I worked on React framework and Vue.js too.","missing_concepts":["Angular (7+)","Bootstrap","Microservices architecture","Agile methodologies","Technical leadership and mentoring","Enterprise-grade scalable solutions"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates strong technical correctness in .NET technologies over many years and mentions relevant skills such as REST APIs and different .NET versions. However, the answer lacks completeness regarding key required skills such as Angular, Bootstrap, microservices, and Agile practices. There is also no mention of leadership roles or architectural responsibilities, which are important for this position. Communication is generally clear but somewhat informal. The answer is relevant to the question but could be more focused on directly connecting experience to the role''s specific requirements. Overall, a good candidate but missing critical elements expected for a senior .NET developer role.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has solid .NET development experience and understands relevant technologies but should provide clearer links between their background and the job requirements, especially in frontend technologies, architecture, and leadership aspects."},{"prompt":"Can you walk me through your hands-on experience specifically with .NET Core and how you’ve applied it in recent projects?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Candidate demonstrates knowledge of ASP.NET Core features such as built-in dependency injection and middleware.","Mentions practical use of REST APIs and custom middleware for authentication, authorization, and exception handling."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Lacks specifics about recent project implementations with .NET Core such as microservices or use of Entity Framework Core.","Does not mention cloud deployment strategies or any CI/CD pipeline experience.","Much of the answer focuses on insurance domain experience rather than .NET Core technical details.","Communication is somewhat unfocused and lacks structured explanation of technical experience."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"I have over 10 years of development experience with .NET Core, using it extensively to build scalable, maintainable backend services for enterprise applications. Recently, I have designed and developed RESTful APIs with .NET Core that integrate with microservices architecture, ensuring high performance and easy maintainability. My implementation involved Entity Framework Core for data access and utilized dependency injection and middleware for cross-cutting concerns like logging and authentication. I also worked on optimizing applications for Azure cloud deployment, leveraging cloud services alongside .NET Core. These projects followed Agile methodologies, and I contributed to code reviews, automated unit and integration testing, and CI/CD pipelines using Git version control.","candidateAnswer":"Currently, I am working with the Bank of America client through Infosys, which is an IT services company. So the reason I applied for Humana is because, you know, it''s a remote and I have a lot of experience with health and life insurance companies. I''m very comfortable working in an insurance company because, you know, I worked on pretty much every department of insurance company. And also I worked with pretty much every insurance system from customer service, billing, claims, benefits, underwriting, actuarial, pretty much, you know, pretty much any department in the insurance company, basically. So that''s one of my main strong points. And the technical skills, you know, I''m very proficient with the skills that are needed for this role. Yeah, that''s what I am. That''s what my background is. And thank you very much for considering me for this role. So I worked on .NET Core, ASP.NET Core MVC, also worked on APIs, REST APIs. You know, in ASP.NET Core, you know, the dependency injection is built in and, you know, ASP.NET Core has a request response pipeline where, you know, in that you can build custom middleware, which can be used for, you know, authentication, authorization, exception handling, and so, you know, whatever the customization you want that is needed to process request and response.","missing_concepts":["Detailed project examples involving .NET Core backend development.","Entity Framework Core usage for data access.","Microservices architecture and integration.","Cloud deployment (e.g., Azure) and CI/CD pipelines."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows a basic understanding of .NET Core concepts such as dependency injection and middleware, which is good. However, the answer is incomplete and lacks depth on practical application in recent projects. The focus drifts to domain experience instead of technical experience related to .NET Core. Crucial elements like microservices, Entity Framework Core, cloud deployment, and testing/CI-CD practices are missing. The communication is somewhat scattered and less clear, reducing overall impact. Candidate has some understanding but needs to improve on articulating concrete technical experience and project contributions.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate provides general knowledge of .NET Core features but does not convincingly demonstrate hands-on experience or detailed application in recent projects. While familiarity with the insurance domain is noted, the technical depth and specific examples expected are missing. Communication could be more structured and focused on the question. Overall, the candidate shows partial knowledge but do"},{"prompt":"How have you implemented custom middleware in your recent projects?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Candidate correctly identifies key middleware responsibilities such as authentication, JWT validation, global exception handling, and authorization.","Mentions relevant areas where custom middleware was applied."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Answer is vague and lacks specific implementation details or examples.","No mention of how middleware was structured or integrated in the ASP.NET Core pipeline.","No explanation of benefits like modularity or separation of concerns.","Communication is unclear and lacks depth."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"In my recent projects, I designed custom middleware components in ASP.NET Core to handle cross-cutting concerns such as authentication (e.g., JWT validation), global exception handling, and request logging. For example, I created middleware that intercepted HTTP requests to validate tokens and set user contexts before controller logic executed. Additionally, I implemented global exception handling middleware using the IExceptionHandler interface to catch and log exceptions consistently across the application. This approach improved modularity and maintainability by centralizing common logic outside of controllers.","candidateAnswer":"So I implemented, you know, for API code, authentication and JWT authentication, and global exception handling, authorization. So these are the areas I used for custom middleware.","missing_concepts":["Detailed middleware creation steps in ASP.NET Core.","Use of interfaces like IExceptionHandler or middleware invocation patterns.","How JWT token validation and user context setting occurs inside middleware.","Explanation of advantages of custom middleware."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a basic understanding of where custom middleware fits by mentioning authentication (JWT), global exception handling, and authorization. However, the response is vague and lacks clear explanation or examples to show how middleware was implemented. There is no description of the middleware pipeline, how middleware components interact, or technical details about handling requests and responses. Communication is hampered by filler phrases, reducing clarity and professionalism. Overall, this reflects partial knowledge but insufficient depth and articulation to consider the answer good enough to pass.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate recognizes key middleware use cases but does not adequately explain implementation or technical details. The answer is too superficial and unclear to demonstrate a solid understanding of custom middleware development in .NET Core. Additional depth and clarity are needed."},{"prompt":"How did you handle global exception handling in that middleware?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":5,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":4,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Mentions a relevant component related to exception handling in ASP.NET Core","Shows awareness of recent advancements in the framework"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Does not correctly specify or explain the mechanism of global exception handling middleware","No explanation on how exceptions are caught, logged, or transformed","Lacks description of the implementation or usage context","Answer is too brief and vague to demonstrate clear understanding"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":4,"expectedAnswer":"Global exception handling in middleware is typically implemented by creating a centralized exception handler that intercepts all unhandled exceptions during the HTTP request pipeline execution. In ASP.NET Core, this is commonly done by implementing a custom middleware or using the built-in UseExceptionHandler middleware, which catches exceptions and handles them by logging, returning standardized error responses, and preventing the application from crashing. This approach ensures consistent error handling and better control over error responses across the entire application.","candidateAnswer":"So I use like an iExceptionHandler, which is a global exception handler introduced recently in ASP.NET Core.","missing_concepts":["Custom middleware creation or UseExceptionHandler usage","Centralizing exception handling across HTTP pipeline","Logging exceptions","Returning standardized error responses","Preventing application crashes through middleware"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate mentioned an ''iExceptionHandler'', which is not a recognized interface or component in ASP.NET Core for exception handling. The answer lacks detail on how global exception handling is implemented, such as writing custom middleware or using the built-in UseExceptionHandler middleware. There is no explanation about intercepting exceptions, logging them, or returning standardized error responses, which are key points in the ideal answer. Overall, the response was vague, brief, and did not convincingly demonstrate understanding or problem solving in global exception handling.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate showed a minimal awareness of the concept of global exception handling but failed to accurately describe or explain the middleware implementation in ASP.NET Core. The response was too brief and lacked key details, indicating insufficient understanding of the topic. Candidate needs to improve their knowledge of middleware-based exception handling and error management techniques."},{"prompt":"Can you give an example of a complex exception scenario you handled that way?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":5,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Understands the concept of a global exception handler.","Recognizes the value of centralized exception handling in the request-response pipeline."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["No specific example of a complex or rare exception scenario.","Lacks details about handling edge cases or custom exception types.","Does not mention enhancing the global exception handler for improved visibility or fallback mechanisms.","No reference to retry logic, exponential backoff, or differentiating exceptions.","Limited demonstration of problem-solving or deep understanding of complex exception handling."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":4,"expectedAnswer":"An ideal answer would describe a situation where an unforeseen or rare exception occurred in a production environment, such as a timeout in a microservices call or a database deadlock, that was not covered by existing known exceptions. The candidate should explain how they enhanced the global exception handler to capture these edge cases by implementing custom exception types and centralized logging to improve visibility. They should also mention how this allowed graceful degradation or fallback mechanisms to keep the application stable and inform stakeholders. For example, integrating retry logic with exponential backoff for transient failures caught globally, or differentiating between client and server exceptions for proper response handling.","candidateAnswer":"What it does is basically like, it''s like a front-line defense for exception handling. So it''s a one global exception handler for all the request response pipeline instead of handling exceptions in each request handler.","missing_concepts":["Description of a specific complex exception scenario (e.g., timeout, deadlock).","Implementation of custom exception types or centralized logging.","Use of graceful degradation, fallback mechanisms, or retry policies.","Handling distinctions between client and server exceptions.","How exception handling was integrated with .Net or related technologies."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate mentions the concept of a global exception handler as a front-line defense but fails to provide any concrete example of a complex or rare exception scenario. The answer is vague and lacks completeness, missing key aspects such as custom exception types, centralized logging, graceful degradation, or retry mechanisms. The explanation does not demonstrate a deep understanding of handling sophisticated exceptions as requested by the question. Communication is understandable but insufficiently detailed. Overall, the answer is too generic and incomplete to meet the technical expectations for the role.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a basic understanding of global exception handling but lacks specific examples or detailed insights into handling complex exceptions in a .Net environment. The response is too vague and incomplete to assess strong problem-solving abilities or technical expertise in this area."},{"prompt":"How did you log and monitor those exceptions in your .NET Core system?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Mentions use of a logging framework (Log4net) which is technically a valid tool used in .NET environments.","Highlights that exceptions and request processing steps are logged.","Understands the concept of tracking and troubleshooting through logging."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Did not specify how exceptions are monitored or integrated with centralized monitoring tools.","No mention of alerting, aggregation, or analysis platforms like Application Insights or ELK stack.","Answer lacks detail on what specific information is logged (e.g., stack traces, context).","Communication is somewhat vague and repetitive (''easy to track'' said twice)."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"In a .NET Core system, exceptions are typically logged using a robust logging framework such as Serilog, NLog, or Microsoft.Extensions.Logging. Logs include detailed exception information like stack traces and context data, sent to centralized monitoring tools such as Application Insights or ELK stack for aggregation and analysis. Monitoring is configured via alert rules to track exception rates and detect anomalies proactively, ensuring timely troubleshooting and maintenance.","candidateAnswer":"So we, you know, I use Log4net, and that''s why we log every, we log exceptions as well as every step in from, you know, request received until the response sent to the client. Every step is logged so that it''s easy to track and easy to track and monitor any and troubleshoot.","missing_concepts":["Centralized monitoring and aggregation (e.g., Application Insights, ELK stack).","Alerting and proactive exception rate monitoring.","Details on the kind of exception information logged (stack trace, context data)."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows a basic understanding of exception logging in .NET Core by naming Log4net and emphasizing logging of steps and exceptions. However, the answer lacks important details about monitoring practices, such as using centralized tools for aggregating logs and setting up alerting mechanisms for proactive incident management. The explanation is somewhat repetitive and does not fully convey an end-to-end logging and monitoring strategy as expected for a .NET Core system. Additional clarity and depth would be needed to meet expectations.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate knows how to log exceptions and track requests using Log4net, indicating practical experience with logging. However, they miss key aspects of monitoring and proactive alerting that are crucial for effective exception handling in production systems. Communication is somewhat diffuse, which detracts from the overall impression of understanding. The candidate could improve by elaboratin"},{"prompt":"Can you tell me about your experience with microservices architecture?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Understands decomposition of monolithic service to smaller APIs","Mentions communication between services via HTTP REST","Describes different consumers of services (frontend, external systems)","Incorporates authentication and authorization mechanisms (JWT tokens, API keys)"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Does not explicitly describe microservices as independent, loosely coupled services","No mention of key microservices features like scaling, fault isolation, independent deployment","Lacks description of service discovery, API gateway, data consistency or monitoring","No mention of containerization or orchestration tools","Explanation is somewhat fragmented and lacks depth on implementation details"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe designing and implementing microservices-based systems using .NET Core, focusing on decomposing monolithic applications into independent, loosely coupled services that communicate via RESTful APIs or messaging queues like Pub/Sub. They should discuss ensuring scalability, fault isolation, and independent deployment of services, as well as handling service discovery, API gateway usage, and data consistency challenges. The candidate should demonstrate experience with containerization (e.g., Docker), and orchestration tools, and clarify how they applied best practices for maintainability and monitoring in a microservices environment.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, so basically we built in, we converted like monolithic, like a WCF service into individual APIs, not like microservices. So in that microservices basically the some services communicate between service to service service and the important point is these are HTTP based REST services, okay? So these, there are some services consume services like a service to service and some consume by the front end other applications, for example, like a web application with UI and then some are consumed by external services like Salesforce and external services like document management, document generation system and the payment gateways. So in the APIs, we introduced authentication and authorization. For authentication, we used, for first selection of services, we used JWT tokens for internals service to service within the company. We used API keys.","missing_concepts":["Decomposition into loosely coupled independent services","Scalability and fault isolation","Service discovery and API gateway usage","Data consistency challenges in microservices","Containerization (e.g., Docker) and orchestration tools","Best practices for maintainability and monitoring"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a basic understanding of transitioning from a monolithic WCF service to multiple RESTful APIs with service-to-service and external communications. They correctly mention using JWT tokens and API keys for securing services, which is positive. However, the answer lacks depth regarding core microservices principles such as independent deployment, scalability, fault isolation, and the complexities of service discovery and data consistency. There is no mention of containerization, orchestration, or the usage of API gateways. The explanation is correct but incomplete and somewhat vague in connecting these APIs explicitly to a microservices architecture. Improvement is needed to show a professional and comprehensive understanding of microservices design and implementation.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate has some foundational experience with breaking down monoliths into APIs and securing inter-service communication. However, their understanding of a full microservices architecture appears limited, missing many critical facets that define microservices, such as containerization, orchestration, scalability, and service discovery. They are not yet ready for roles requiring solid microse"},{"prompt":"How did you manage communication between those microservices, especially around reliability and fault tolerance?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Mentions retry pattern with limited attempts and logging on failure","Acknowledges fault tolerance through server replication for availability"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-7","weaknesses":["Explanation is vague and uses unclear terminology such as ''soft tolerance'' and ''something called a retry pattern''","No mention of asynchronous messaging or decoupling of services","Does not discuss circuit breakers, exponential backoff, fallback mechanisms, or idempotency","Limited detail on how failures are handled gracefully beyond basic retry and logging","Communication is somewhat disorganized and lacks precise technical terms"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"Communication between microservices was managed using asynchronous messaging via Pub/Sub queues to decouple services and improve scalability. To ensure reliability and fault tolerance, we implemented retry patterns with exponential backoff, circuit breakers to prevent cascading failures, and fallback mechanisms for graceful degradation. Additionally, we used idempotent operations to handle duplicate messages and leveraged monitoring and logging to detect and respond to failures proactively.","candidateAnswer":"It''s a soft tolerance, you know, and we have a something called a retry pattern. So it tries three times and then if it fails, it fails gracefully and then every time it fails, it logs. And other than that, for fault tolerance, we have what do you call that as multiple replications where one server fails, another server takes care of one until the server is up. Those are the cases for reliability and for tolerance.","missing_concepts":["Use of asynchronous messaging or Pub/Sub queues","Circuit breakers to prevent cascading failures","Exponential backoff strategy","Fallback mechanisms for graceful degradation","Idempotency to handle duplicate messages","Monitoring and proactive failure detection"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows some understanding of fault tolerance by mentioning retries, logging, and server replication for fault tolerance. However, the explanation lacks depth and clarity, missing key resilient design patterns essential for microservices communication such as circuit breakers, exponential backoff, and asynchronous messaging. The use of vague terms reduces the technical precision and does not inspire full confidence in their grasp of the subject. Improvement needed in explaining the mechanisms and strategies explicitly and more professionally.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate demonstrates a basic grasp of fault tolerance concepts like retrying and server redundancy, but overall answer is incomplete and lacks clarity on critical microservice communication strategies. Does not fully meet expectations for a .Net developer familiar with microservices architecture."},{"prompt":"Tell me about your experience with Angular and what versions you''ve worked with.","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-8","weaknesses":["No answer provided","No information about Angular experience","Did not address versions or experience details"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have over 5 years of hands-on experience developing front-end applications using Angular versions 7 through 13. I have utilized Angular to build responsive and modular UI components, integrating them with RESTful APIs and backend services. My experience includes leveraging Angular''s component-based architecture, dependency injection, RxJS for reactive programming, routing, and state management. Additionally, I have worked with Angular CLI and used Bootstrap and CSS3 for styling to ensure consistent and responsive design.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":["Angular versions used","Component-based architecture","Dependency injection","RxJS and reactive programming","Routing and state management","Integration with backend APIs","Styling with Bootstrap or CSS3"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate did not provide any answer regarding their experience with Angular or the versions they have worked with. Therefore, no evaluation can be made about their technical knowledge, completeness of the answer, relevance to the question, clarity, or understanding of Angular concepts. The absence of a response indicates a lack of information on this important technical topic for the role.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate did not respond to the question about Angular experience, leaving a critical gap in the assessment of their front-end development skills. Without any answer, it''s not possible to gauge their proficiency or familiarity with Angular frameworks, which is essential for the role."},{"prompt":"How have you utilized Angular in your front-end development?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-9","weaknesses":["No answer provided","No indication of knowledge or experience with Angular","Cannot assess technical skills without a response"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have utilized Angular to develop dynamic, responsive single-page applications by leveraging its component-based architecture for modular and maintainable UI design. This included creating reusable components and services, integrating Angular Router for client-side navigation, and employing reactive forms for efficient user input handling. I also implemented state management using RxJS Observables to handle asynchronous data streams and improve performance. Additionally, I incorporated Bootstrap and CSS3 for styling to ensure consistent and mobile-friendly user interfaces. Throughout, I adhered to best practices by writing unit tests with Jasmine and Karma and maintained clear documentation to support scalability and team collaboration.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":["Component-based architecture","Reusable components and services","Angular Router for navigation","Reactive forms","State management with RxJS","Styling with Bootstrap and CSS3","Unit testing with Jasmine and Karma"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate did not provide any answer to the question, leaving no information to evaluate their knowledge or experience with Angular in front-end development. This lack of response prevents assessment of their technical correctness, completeness, relevance, communication clarity, and problem-solving skills related to Angular usage. It is essential for candidates to provide a substantive response demonstrating their experience and understanding of the technology asked about.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate failed to provide any answer to the question about their use of Angular in front-end development, resulting in an automatic fail due to no assessable content."}]'), ('cmpb428oi002sp00j9kt45n4b', 'cmpb4110x002mp00judamcy67', 18, 45, 40, 54, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-05-18 11:18:39.474', '2026-05-21 13:27:43.255', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["آگاز نہیں آیا ہاں آ گئی"]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 0, '[{"prompt":"Could you start by telling me a bit about yourself?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["The answer is irrelevant and does not provide any information related to the question.","No details about professional background, skills, or experience were given.","Lacks any mention or indication of understanding of product design or related concepts.","Communication is unclear and not in the expected language or format."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate will summarize their professional background focusing on product design and development, highlighting several years of experience working on UI Design and React-based projects. They will mention specific roles held, such as senior developer or product designer, and key achievements, like leading design implementations that improved user engagement or performance. They will also connect their experience to the current role by emphasizing their ability to bridge design and development to create intuitive, scalable products.","candidateAnswer":"آگاز نہیں آیا ہاں آ گئی","missing_concepts":["Professional background summary","Experience in product design and development","UI Design and React skills","Roles and achievements relevant to the product designer position"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response does not address the question asked. It provides no information about their professional background or relevant experience. As a result, it is impossible to assess their qualifications or fit for the product designer role. The response is off-topic and does not demonstrate even basic understanding or communication skills needed in this interview context. The candidate should provide a clear and concise summary of their relevant experience, skills, and achievements connected to product design to proceed further.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate''s answer is unrelated to the question, lacks any relevant content, and is not understandable. No evidence of qualifications or relevant skills was provided. This response results in a fail for this question."},{"prompt":"Could you tell me about your current role and what you’ve been working on recently?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["No answer provided."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"In my current role as a senior product designer with strong React experience, I lead the design and implementation of user interfaces that blend seamless UI design with functional React components. Recently, I''ve been working on redesigning an enterprise dashboard to improve user workflow efficiency, collaborating closely with frontend developers to ensure that design specifications translate effectively into React code. This project involved iterating on design prototypes based on user feedback and technical feasibility, and mentoring junior designers on best practices integrating UI design with component-driven development.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":["Description of current role and responsibilities","Recent projects and tasks","Use of UI Design and React skills","Collaboration and problem-solving examples"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate did not provide any answer to the question. There is no information on their current role, projects, skills, or understanding relevant to the role of a product designer with React experience. This does not demonstrate any technical knowledge, relevance, completeness, or communication skills.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate did not respond to the question about their current role and recent work, providing no insight into their experience or skills. This results in a fail for this question."}]'), ('cmpbb1lxl004xp00jgh5bccm5', 'cmpban91h0030p00jihi4hn1w', 82, 83, 71, 100, 'Strong performance with structured answers and solid topic understanding.', '2026-05-18 14:34:07.305', '2026-05-18 14:34:07.305', '["Clear communication flow","Good depth in responses"]', '["Add sharper quantified examples","Reduce filler and tighten transitions"]', '["کیا ہے ہیلو","My name is Vibhor Chandel. I''m working as a product manager since last 12 years and I have","I''ve been working with Boondock Technologies for the last two years, and I''m managing that Boondock product, its upgrades, updates, and based on customer requirements. I do I do plan the development."]', 'heuristic-immediate', null, null, null), ('cmpcbfcoq000dp80ke1lmy9zi', 'cmpcbepfx000ap80ksagssa0v', 44, 45, 40, 50, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-05-19 07:32:34.682', '2026-05-19 07:32:34.682', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '[]', 'heuristic-immediate', null, null, null), ('cmpp14fx0001cpb0kubrrsqbz', 'cmpp0v447000npb0ko8vk7ilf', 64, 85, 72, 82, 'Strong performance with structured answers and solid topic understanding.', '2026-05-28 05:05:09.781', '2026-05-28 05:06:44.778', '["Clear communication flow","Good depth in responses"]', '["Add sharper quantified examples","Reduce filler and tighten transitions"]', '["Yes, so I was a solution engineer in one of my previous companies, and there was a project called a smart engine, which was about leveraging database of past projects to provide solutions to the new inquiries that we got. It was challenging because we had to, first of all, collate all the data from the previous projects and build a proper system and a dashboard that could be easier to find the closest match for the new requirements. And the database was so big because it involved information from multiple stakeholders from multiple teams that to structure it and make proper linkages was quite difficult. And of course, we were able to do it, and my particular role was to guide the entire team behind the database structuring and development of the dashboard to make sure we achieve the goals with the results that we achieved. One of them was we were able to improve the delivery time by almost 15% and we increased our capacity by 40%.","AMC contract is priced based on the service that we will be providing. Then it also includes timeline. We take into consideration the labor that is required and the raw materials that are being used, as well as the contract service period, which is, which may or may not include warranty and maintenance. So based on all these factors, we price our AMC contract.","To prepare a service proposal, factors that we consider include the data processing part, which is how much effort we have to take for the past service that has been used by the customers, and then the new additional efforts that we are required on a day-to-day basis and for the time period that will be involved in providing service to the customers."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 54, '[{"prompt":"Can you tell me about a challenging project you worked on recently and the role you played in it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":5,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Clearly explains a challenging project involving large database and multiple stakeholders.","Describes own leadership role guiding team to achieve project goals.","Quantifies benefits such as improved delivery time and increased capacity."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Project described is more technical and product development focused rather than sales or marketing focused.","Lacks discussion of negotiation, client relationships, or securing contracts as expected for sales and marketing role.","Does not address strategic planning or business development elements.","No mention of overcoming external obstacles such as competition or complex client requirements."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific project that involved identifying and securing a significant corporate rate contract or service agreement under challenging circumstances, such as tight deadlines, complex client requirements, or strong competition. They should detail their role in leading business development efforts, negotiating terms, coordinating with internal teams for seamless service delivery, and managing client relationships to overcome obstacles and ensure project success. For example, they might explain how they proactively engaged stakeholders, addressed contractual complexities, and aligned service delivery to client expectations, resulting in revenue growth and client satisfaction.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, so I was a solution engineer in one of my previous companies, and there was a project called a smart engine, which was about leveraging database of past projects to provide solutions to the new inquiries that we got. It was challenging because we had to, first of all, collate all the data from the previous projects and build a proper system and a dashboard that could be easier to find the closest match for the new requirements. And the database was so big because it involved information from multiple stakeholders from multiple teams that to structure it and make proper linkages was quite difficult. And of course, we were able to do it, and my particular role was to guide the entire team behind the database structuring and development of the dashboard to make sure we achieve the goals with the results that we achieved. One of them was we were able to improve the delivery time by almost 15% and we increased our capacity by 40%.","missing_concepts":["Business development efforts","Negotiation and contract management","Client relationship management","Aligning service delivery with client expectations","Revenue growth and client satisfaction outcomes"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shared a genuine challenging project involving database management and dashboard development and described their leadership role well. However, the example is more technical and internal-process focused, lacking the relevance to sales and marketing responsibilities emphasized in the question and ideal answer. Key aspects like negotiation, securing contracts, strategic planning, and managing client relationships were missing. The overall explanation was clear but did not fully demonstrate the candidate''s ability in the sales and marketing domain required for this senior executive role. Improvement is needed to provide an example aligned with the position''s expectations and showcase relevant skills.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows good leadership and technical problem-solving skills but failed to provide an example relevant to sales and marketing challenges. The answer did not sufficiently cover negotiation, business development, or client management duties typical for the role. Based on this response, the candidate does not yet demonstrate strong fit for the Senior Executive – Sales & Marketing (Service"},{"prompt":"How do you price an AMC contract?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Acknowledges inclusion of labor and materials in pricing","Mentions contract service period and warranty","Recognizes the importance of service offered and timeline"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Does not mention overheads, profit margin, or value-added services","Lacks detail on strategic pricing factors such as response times","Explanation is somewhat vague and lacks structure"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"Pricing an AMC contract involves a detailed assessment of the scope and complexity of the services to be provided, including labor, materials, and any specialized equipment. Key factors include the estimated service frequency, duration of the contract period, expected cost of consumables and parts, overheads, and profit margin. Additionally, one must consider warranty coverage, response times, and any value-added services. Tailoring pricing to the client''s needs while ensuring competitive yet profitable rates is essential.","candidateAnswer":"AMC contract is priced based on the service that we will be providing. Then it also includes timeline. We take into consideration the labor that is required and the raw materials that are being used, as well as the contract service period, which is, which may or may not include warranty and maintenance. So based on all these factors, we price our AMC contract.","missing_concepts":["Overheads and profit margin considerations","Expected cost of consumables and parts","Response times and value-added services","Tailoring pricing to client''s needs and competitiveness"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows a basic understanding of pricing AMC contracts by referencing labor, materials, service timeline, and warranty. However, the explanation is incomplete and lacks depth, missing significant factors like overheads, profit margins, consumables, response times, and strategic tailoring for clients. The answer is somewhat vague and disorganized, indicating partial knowledge but insufficient completeness and problem-solving insight. Improving clarity and including all major cost and strategic factors would strengthen the response.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates foundational awareness of AMC contract pricing elements but falls short of providing a comprehensive and detailed approach expected at a senior executive level. While the relevance and technical correctness are acceptable, the answer lacks completeness and depth necessary to pass."},{"prompt":"What factors do you consider while preparing a service proposal for a corporate client?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Acknowledgment of evaluating existing and additional service efforts","Recognizes the need to assess time-related service delivery requirements"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Lacks mention of pricing strategy, resource planning, SLAs, and risk assessment","Does not address client budget considerations or contract terms","Explanation is vague and lacks structured approach","Limited demonstration of strategic planning or negotiation skills"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"When preparing a service proposal for a corporate client, I consider the client''s specific service needs and scope, including the volume and complexity of services required. I evaluate resource availability and required manpower or technical expertise to deliver the service effectively. Pricing strategy is critical—factoring in direct costs, margins, and competitive benchmarks. Additionally, the proposal must align with the client''s budget constraints and include clear timelines and service-level agreements (SLAs). Finally, I incorporate risk assessments, potential contract terms, and value-added services that differentiate our offering.","candidateAnswer":"To prepare a service proposal, factors that we consider include the data processing part, which is how much effort we have to take for the past service that has been used by the customers, and then the new additional efforts that we are required on a day-to-day basis and for the time period that will be involved in providing service to the customers.","missing_concepts":["Pricing strategy including costs and margins","Client budget alignment","Service-level agreements (SLAs) and timelines","Risk assessment and contract terms","Value-added services and competitive differentiation","Resource availability and manpower planning"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate offers a basic recognition of evaluating past and additional service efforts when preparing a proposal, which shows some understanding of operational considerations. However, the response is incomplete and lacks critical components expected in a service proposal such as pricing strategy, budget alignment, timelines, SLAs, risk assessment, and contractual terms. The explanation is somewhat vague and does not clearly convey a structured approach or strategic planning. These omissions suggest weak understanding of the comprehensive factors necessary for a corporate service proposal. Overall, the answer is partially relevant but falls short in completeness and problem-solving insight.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows some awareness of operational effort assessment in preparing service proposals but fails to address key strategic, financial, and contractual elements. Their understanding appears limited and lacks depth required for the senior executive role in sales and marketing. More structured and comprehensive responses including resource planning, pricing, and client-specific alignment a"},{"prompt":"How do you calculate profitability for a long-term service contract?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Candidate correctly identifies profitability as revenue minus expenses.","Mentions key expense components such as labor, material, and technology-related costs.","Recognizes the importance of long-term client relationships in profitability."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["The answer lacks specifics on indirect costs like overhead or administration.","Does not mention accounting for projected expenses and revenues over the contract duration.","Misses the mention of escalations or variable costs and return on investment calculation.","Somewhat vague and lacks structured explanation."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"Profitability for a long-term service contract is calculated by subtracting all associated direct and indirect costs (such as labor, materials, overhead, and administration) from the total revenue generated over the contract term. It is essential to account for projected expenses and revenues across the full duration of the contract, including any escalations or variable costs, to determine the net profit and return on investment accurately.","candidateAnswer":"Profitability is based on the ROI that we will be getting. So basically it is revenue minus expenses. The revenue is the money that we''ll be getting from the clients for the service that we provide minus the expenses that are incurred in providing that service like labor, material, or any other technology related expenses that we incur, and profitability opportunity that lies ahead that the customers can provide us in the long term defines or is important for making a decision and understanding the profitability of the firm.","missing_concepts":["Indirect costs (overhead, administration)","Projection of expenses and revenues over full contract term","Accounting for escalations or variable costs","Explicit calculation of net profit and ROI"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows a good foundational understanding by correctly stating that profitability is derived from revenue minus expenses and highlights major cost factors such as labor, materials, and technology expenses. However, the answer falls short in covering the comprehensive aspects of long-term service contract profitability calculation. It misses discussing indirect costs, the importance of projecting expenses and revenues throughout the contract duration, and the role of escalations or variable costs. The explanation also lacks clarity on calculating net profit or ROI explicitly. While the overall response is relevant and understandable, adding these details would provide a more complete and professional answer.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates a basic to solid grasp of profitability calculation for long-term service contracts, with clear understanding of core revenue and expense elements. There is room for improvement in discussing full cost accounting and financial projections over time. The response passes given reasonable technical correctness and relevance, but further depth is needed to reach excellence."},{"prompt":"What KPIs would you track for service delivery performance?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Mentioned important KPIs such as delivery time, resolution time, and number of tickets solved which are relevant to service delivery performance.","Included safety incidents as a KPI, indicating awareness of operational risks."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Did not specify critical KPIs like SLA compliance, customer satisfaction (CSAT), first-time fix rate, and contract renewal rates which are essential for a comprehensive evaluation of service delivery.","Answer was brief and lacked depth or explanation of the KPIs and their importance.","Missed mention of escalation frequency and how KPIs relate to customer trust and service quality."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"Key KPIs for service delivery performance include Service Level Agreement (SLA) compliance rates to measure adherence to agreed timelines, average resolution time to assess efficiency in addressing client issues, customer satisfaction scores (CSAT) to gauge client experience, first-time fix rate to evaluate effectiveness of service, and contract renewal or retention rates to reflect long-term client trust. Additionally, tracking the number of service incidents and escalation frequency helps identify quality and operational challenges.","candidateAnswer":"Probably delivery time, resolution time, the number of tickets that we solve per month, and safety incidents, these are the KPIs.","missing_concepts":["Service Level Agreement (SLA) compliance rates","Customer Satisfaction Scores (CSAT)","First-time fix rate","Contract renewal or retention rates","Escalation frequency"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate mentioned some relevant KPIs such as delivery time, resolution time, number of tickets resolved, and safety incidents, which shows a basic understanding of service delivery metrics. However, the answer lacked completeness as it missed several key indicators critical to measuring overall service performance like SLA compliance, customer satisfaction, first-time fix rate, and contract renewals. Additionally, the response was quite brief and did not elaborate on why these KPIs are important or how they affect service quality and client trust. Greater depth and clarity would have demonstrated stronger problem-solving and strategic understanding.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates a basic grasp of service delivery KPIs but fails to cover the full scope of important performance indicators. Their answer is relevant but incomplete and lacks detailed explanation, indicating only a partial understanding of the topic. Improvement is needed in articulating comprehensive KPIs and linking them to strategic outcomes in service delivery."},{"prompt":"How do you assess service requirements during a site visit?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Recognizes the importance of engaging site personnel and understanding their pain points and needs","Mentions documentation of findings","Acknowledges contract requirements as important in the process"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Limited explanation of systematic approach for gathering information","No mention of direct physical inspection or observation of workflows and equipment","No reference to reviewing existing service contracts beyond a superficial level","Unclear approach to stakeholder engagement or strategic planning","Admission of limited knowledge reduces confidence in full understanding"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"During a site visit, I systematically gather information to understand the client''s operational environment and specific service needs. This involves engaging key stakeholders through structured conversations to identify pain points and expectations. I conduct on-site inspections to observe current workflows, equipment conditions, and potential service gaps. Additionally, I review any existing service contracts or requirements documents to align observations with contractual obligations. All findings are documented meticulously to form the basis for tailored service proposals that meet both client needs and business objectives.","candidateAnswer":"We usually have conversations with the people at site, understand their pain points, their needs, document them, propose them a list of survey questions based on the contract requirements that we receive from the company. Apart from that, I have very little idea about it.","missing_concepts":["Structured conversations with key stakeholders","On-site inspections and observation of current operations and equipment status","Alignment of observations with contractual obligations","Comprehensive documentation to form basis for tailored service proposals","Strategic planning elements related to service requirement assessment"],"detailed_feedback":"The answer shows an awareness of basic steps such as talking with people on site and referencing contract requirements. However, it lacks a systematic and thorough approach to assessing service needs during a site visit. There is no mention of physically inspecting the site environment, equipment conditions, or processes, which are crucial for identifying service gaps. The candidate''s admission of having ''very little idea'' suggests insufficient depth of knowledge. The explanation is somewhat relevant but incomplete, missing key components like structured stakeholder engagement and aligning findings with business objectives. To improve, the candidate should detail a methodical process that includes direct observation, contract review, documentation, and strategic planning to ensure tailored service solutions.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates a basic understanding of assessing service requirements by engaging site staff and referencing contracts, but overall the response is incomplete and lacks important technical and strategic details. Their admission of limited knowledge indicates they may not fully grasp the comprehensive process required for effective service need assessment during site visits in this rol"},{"prompt":"What’s your approach to managing long-term client relationships?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["The candidate communicated clearly and understandably."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["No demonstrated knowledge or approach to managing long-term client relationships.","Did not address any key strategies such as communication, trust-building, or proactive engagement.","Lacks understanding of the concept required for the role."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"Managing long-term client relationships involves building trust through consistent communication, understanding client needs deeply, and delivering value beyond initial contracts. It requires proactive engagement by regularly reviewing service performance, anticipating client challenges, and proposing tailored solutions that align with their evolving business goals. Key tactics include maintaining transparency in all dealings, promptly addressing concerns, and fostering a partnership mindset rather than a transactional approach. Additionally, tracking client satisfaction and seeking feedback help in continuous improvement and sustaining revenue streams through renewals and upsells.","candidateAnswer":"I have little experience in this domain since I was part of the delivery team and I have no idea how do I manage long-term relationships. Could you help me with that?","missing_concepts":["Building trust and consistent communication","Understanding client needs","Proactive engagement and reviewing client service performance","Transparency and prompt handling of concerns","Fostering partnership mindset versus transactional relationships","Tracking client satisfaction and leveraging renewals or upsells"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate explicitly states lack of experience and does not provide an answer to the question asked. This shows very limited understanding of managing long-term client relationships which is a critical skill for the role. The communication was clear but the response was essentially a non-answer, failing to address the core aspects expected. Greater preparation and knowledge of client relationship strategies are necessary.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate failed to demonstrate any knowledge or approach to managing long-term client relationships. Communication was clear but the answer was insufficient and irrelevant to the question. Does not meet the expectations for the role."}]'), ('cmpp86rnc000bqm0kb5y66ovb', 'cmpp84drv0003qm0kdzac3fd7', 54, 45, 40, 50, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-05-28 08:22:55.608', '2026-05-28 08:23:15.935', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '[]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 60, '[{"prompt":"Can you tell me about a challenging project you''ve worked on recently and how you handled it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":8,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Clear and understandable explanation","Demonstrates technical knowledge in data processing and collaboration with client","Shows problem-solving approach regarding performance optimization"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Project described is unrelated to sales or service business development","Missing details on negotiation, contract management, or aligning stakeholders","Lacks mention of business outcomes related to sales or client satisfaction","Does not reflect on lessons learned or handling complexity in sales environment"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate will describe a specific challenging project related to sales and service business development, such as securing a large annual maintenance contract with a key corporate client amidst stiff competition or internal coordination issues. They will explain how they identified the challenge (e.g., client hesitation, complex contract terms, cross-team alignment), then detail strategic steps taken—such as leveraging negotiation skills to address client concerns, coordinating effectively with technical and dealer teams to assure service capability, and maintaining transparent communication to build trust. They should highlight the outcome, like successfully closing the contract or improving client satisfaction, and reflect on lessons learned for future projects. The example should demonstrate their ability to handle complexity in contract management, stakeholder alignment, and sales closure under pressure.","candidateAnswer":"Good morning. Sure, one challenging project I worked on recently was developing a real-time data analytics platform for a client in the healthcare sector. The main challenge was handling large volumes of streaming data with low latency requirements. I approached this by designing a scalable architecture using Apache Kafka for data ingestion and Apache Spark for processing. I collaborated closely with the client''s team to understand their needs and iterated on prototypes to ensure performance benchmarks were met. Ultimately, the platform improved their data processing speed by 40%.","missing_concepts":["Sales & service business development context","Negotiation and contract management","Stakeholder alignment and communication in B2B sales","Outcome related to sales closure or client relationship"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a detailed and technically correct description of a challenging project involving real-time data analytics platform development, showing good problem-solving skills and communication clarity. However, the example is completely unrelated to the role of Senior Executive in Sales & Marketing for service business. It lacks any reference to sales challenges, contract negotiation, client management, or business development activities that the question specifically targets. Due to lack of relevance and completeness in the context of the role, the overall performance is insufficient despite technical correctness in a different domain.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates solid technical and problem-solving skills but fails to address the question relevant to sales and service business development. Their example is not aligned with the expectations for this senior sales and marketing role, leading to a fail outcome."}]'), ('cmpqjprcw000mqo0khroq3zfy', 'cmpqjn4bt000cqo0ky5j7rwta', 9, 45, 40, 54, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-05-29 06:33:23.648', '2026-05-29 06:33:35.651', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hello."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 0, '[{"prompt":"How do you typically price an Annual Maintenance Contract, or AMC contract?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Pricing an AMC contract involves a systematic assessment of several factors: first, defining the scope of equipment or systems covered and the expected service requirements; next, estimating direct labor costs based on the frequency and complexity of maintenance visits; then, calculating the cost of spare parts and consumables likely to be required during the contract period. Additionally, overhead expenses, risk contingencies, profit margins, and prevailing market rates must be incorporated. The final proposal balances competitive pricing with ensuring adequate margins and reliable service delivery. Key steps include detailed site surveys, historical failure data analysis, negotiation of terms, and alignment with customer expectations.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Can you walk me through the key steps you personally follow when preparing an AMC proposal?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"When preparing an AMC proposal, I start by thoroughly understanding the client''s equipment or system scope and their specific maintenance needs. Next, I collaborate with the technical team to estimate labor hours, frequency of service visits, and spare parts requirements. I factor in direct costs plus overheads, then benchmark prices against market rates to ensure competitiveness. I also incorporate provisions for emergency support and tailor contract terms to client expectations. Finally, I consolidate all inputs into a clear, detailed proposal highlighting value, service scope, pricing, and timelines before seeking internal approvals and presenting it to the client.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"How do you price an AMC contract?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpqjn4bt000dqo0k6s5c8btt","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"What factors do you consider while preparing a service proposal for a corporate client?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpqjn4bt000eqo0k3n08flvv","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"How do you calculate profitability for a long-term service contract?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpqjn4bt000fqo0kguwo0eri","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"What KPIs would you track for service delivery performance?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpqjn4bt000gqo0kjyuq55lo","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"How do you assess service requirements during a site visit?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpqjn4bt000hqo0kcg7gb4ug","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpqjzv2q0025qo0kivwk6w9o', 'cmpqjrn6l000sqo0kb9u6k69j', 71, 67, 57, 100, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-05-29 06:41:15.026', '2026-05-29 06:41:15.026', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hello.","Can you answer me? Can you answer for me?","Okay, so I am a product designer. I have some five years of experience."]', 'heuristic-immediate', null, null, null), ('cmpqk6544002xqo0k1ca6ysd1', 'cmpqk33a6002bqo0km6uustxf', 15, 47, 42, 90, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-05-29 06:46:07.972', '2026-05-29 06:46:36.935', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hello","Next, move to the next question.","Next question, please."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 5, '[{"prompt":"Can you start by telling me about yourself?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I am a senior product designer with over 7 years of experience specializing in UI design and front-end development, particularly with React. My background includes leading design initiatives that bridge user needs with technical feasibility, collaborating closely with cross-functional teams to deliver intuitive, scalable products. For example, I spearheaded the redesign of a high-traffic web application that improved user engagement by 30%, and I actively contribute to component-driven design systems to ensure consistency and efficiency.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Could you walk me through your most recent work experience and the key responsibilities you had in that role?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"In my most recent role as a senior developer, I led the design and implementation of complex front-end features using React, collaborating closely with product managers and UI designers to deliver scalable, user-centric applications. I was responsible for architectural decisions, code reviews, mentoring junior developers, and ensuring best practices in UI design and React development were adhered to across the team. Additionally, I championed improvements in development workflows and contributed to cross-functional planning to align technical solutions with product goals.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Can you describe your experience with UI design?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have extensive experience in UI design, focusing on creating user-centric, intuitive interfaces that align with product goals and user needs. I have worked on wireframing and prototyping using tools like Figma and Sketch, collaborated closely with UX teams to iterate designs based on user feedback, and ensured consistency through design systems and component libraries. My designs balance aesthetics with functionality and accessibility, and I regularly perform usability testing to validate design decisions.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Can you tell me about your experience with React and how you''ve used it in your projects?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"As a senior developer, I have extensive experience with React, having built multiple complex web applications using it. I have utilized React to design reusable and maintainable UI components, manage application state effectively with hooks and context API, and integrate with RESTful APIs and GraphQL backends. For example, in one project, I led the migration of a legacy UI to React, improving performance and user experience significantly. Additionally, I have worked closely with product designers to implement pixel-perfect designs and ensure accessibility compliance within React applications.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Can you share your experience working with React and the kind of projects you''ve built using it?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have extensive experience developing single-page applications and complex UI components using React. My projects include building responsive dashboards, interactive data visualization tools, and e-commerce frontends. I leverage React hooks and context for state management and optimize performance through code splitting and memoization. I also integrate React with RESTful APIs and GraphQL backends, ensuring a seamless user experience.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Could you briefly highlight any specific UI design projects you''ve worked on?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Did not provide any information or description of UI design projects."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should concisely describe 2-3 UI design projects where they played a key role. For example, they might mention designing user interfaces for web applications using React, focusing on creating intuitive and responsive layouts that improved user engagement. They should highlight their process, such as user research, wireframing, prototyping, and usability testing, and explain how their designs addressed specific user needs or business goals. Additionally, they might note collaboration with developers and stakeholders to iterate designs efficiently. Demonstrating measurable impact or improvements — like increased user satisfaction scores or reduced task completion times — strengthens the answer.","candidateAnswer":"No, next question.","missing_concepts":["Description of UI design projects","Use of UI design tools and processes","Collaboration details","Impact or results from the projects"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate did not answer the question, simply refusing to respond. No information was provided about any UI design projects, which leaves nothing to evaluate on technical correctness, completeness, relevance, clarity, or problem solving. This is considered a very weak response resulting in failure.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate did not engage with the question and provided no information related to their UI design experience. This is insufficient for a product designer role and suggests either lack of experience or unwillingness to share relevant information."},{"prompt":"Why do you think you''re a good fit for this product designer role?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Answer is too short and vague","No demonstration of design experience or technical skills","Does not mention relevant skills such as UI design or React","Lacks explanation or justification for being a good fit","No evidence of problem solving or understanding of the role"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"I am a good fit for this product designer role because I have extensive experience combining user-centered UI design principles with practical front-end development skills, particularly in React. I have led design projects that closely integrated with engineering teams to deliver seamless, scalable interfaces that enhance user engagement. My background includes iterative prototyping, A/B testing, and collaborating cross-functionally to align product vision with user needs and technical feasibilities, which aligns well with this senior developer role focused on product design. Additionally, my ability to bridge design and code enables me to create designs that are both aesthetically pleasing and technically sound, ensuring efficient implementation and maintenance.","candidateAnswer":"I am a good fit.\\nI know that.","missing_concepts":["User-centered UI design experience","Front-end development skills (React)","Cross-functional collaboration","Iterative prototyping and A/B testing","Alignment of product vision with user needs"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is extremely brief and lacks any meaningful content or justification for why they are a good fit for the product designer role. It does not address any of the key skills or qualifications expected for the position. The response fails to demonstrate technical knowledge, experience, or communication ability relevant to the role. More detailed explanation with examples of relevant experience, skills, and achievements is needed to consider the candidate as a fit.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate did not provide a substantive answer to explain their fit for the product designer role, showing a lack of preparation or understanding. The response does not meet the minimum expectations for this interview."},{"prompt":"tell me your self","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpqk33a6002cqo0kgkqs6dlp","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpqkye47003qqo0ktirzuapo', 'cmpqkojyd0035qo0kj4n146bc', 67, 92, 77, 90, 'Strong performance with structured answers and solid topic understanding.', '2026-05-29 07:08:06.007', '2026-05-29 07:09:02.406', '["Clear communication flow","Good depth in responses"]', '["Add sharper quantified examples","Reduce filler and tighten transitions"]', '["Hello.","Yes, I have been a product designer for a few companies. I have done UI design, physical product design, and software designing. My previous company used to make 3D printed products, so I was the product design lead for that. I have developed almost 10 to 15 products for that company in the education sector as well as in the manufacturing domain for mechanical systems.","Yes, so UI design I have done for development of the EdTech platform that was required for my company. It was for the age group of 3 to 10 years, basically school-going kids. It was also an e-commerce platform, so the UI was user-friendly and it involved components that are lightweight and appealing to the kids."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 62, '[{"prompt":"Can you start by telling me about yourself?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Mentions experience in product design across multiple domains","Indicates leadership role as product design lead","Highlights involvement in UI and physical product design"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Lacks explicit mention of design strategies or methodologies such as user-centered design","No reference to collaboration with cross-functional teams like engineering or product management","Does not mention specific skills like React which is part of key expected skills"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should concisely summarize their background in product design, highlighting relevant UI design expertise and leadership experience. For example, they might mention several years of designing user interfaces and physical products, leading design projects across industries such as education and manufacturing, and collaborating cross-functionally with engineering and product teams. They should explicitly connect their skills and past roles to the senior product designer role by emphasizing design strategy, user-centered design processes, and impact on product outcomes.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, I have been a product designer for a few companies. I have done UI design, physical product design, and software designing. My previous company used to make 3D printed products, so I was the product design lead for that. I have developed almost 10 to 15 products for that company in the education sector as well as in the manufacturing domain for mechanical systems.","missing_concepts":["User-centered design process","Design strategy","Cross-functional collaboration","Impact on product outcomes","Specific UI design skills such as React"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a generally relevant and technically correct summary of their background with examples of leadership and product domains which is good. However, the answer is somewhat incomplete as it does not clearly articulate design methodologies, collaboration, or measurable impact on products which would strengthen the fit for a senior product designer role. Communication is clear but could be more structured and detailed to better demonstrate depth of understanding and relevant expertise.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows solid product design experience and leadership in relevant industries but misses some key aspects like user-centered design practices and technical skills expected for this role. The answer meets the basic expectations but leaves gaps in completeness and depth."},{"prompt":"Can you please tell me a bit more about your professional background and what brings you to this interview today?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Clear explanation of experience with UI design and physical product design","Specific mention of domain expertise in education and manufacturing sectors","Led product design for 3D printed products indicating leadership experience"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Did not mention the number of years of experience explicitly","No expression of career goals or reasons for seeking this role","No mention of skills like React or cross-functional collaboration"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"I have over [X years] of experience as a product designer, specializing in UI design and product development across multiple sectors such as education and manufacturing. My background includes leading design for both physical and digital products, with a strong emphasis on user-centered design and cross-functional collaboration. I am seeking this role to leverage my expertise in UI design and React development to contribute to innovative product solutions at your company, aligning with my goal to work in a senior capacity where I can influence product strategy and quality.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, I have been a product designer for a few companies. I have done UI design, physical product design, and software designing. My previous company used to make 3D printed products, so I was the product design lead for that. I have developed almost 10 to 15 products for that company in the education sector as well as in the manufacturing domain for mechanical systems.","missing_concepts":["Years of experience","Motivation for applying or career goals","Mention of React expertise","User-centered design emphasis","Cross-functional collaboration"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a solid background in product design, including both UI and physical product work, with leadership of 3D printed product design and experience across relevant sectors. However, the answer lacks completeness by not specifying years of experience, not stating career motivations or why they are interested in this role, and missing mention of React skills and collaboration approaches found in the ideal answer. The communication is clear but somewhat generic. Overall, the answer is good but could be improved with more detail and alignment to the job requirements.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows relevant product design experience and domain knowledge but does not articulate clear career goals or mention key required skills like React and collaboration. The response is adequate to continue but would benefit from deeper details and motivation."},{"prompt":"Can you tell me about your experience specifically with UI design?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Candidate provided a relevant example of UI design for an EdTech platform targeting young children.","Answer indicates consideration for user age group and lightweight, appealing UI components."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Lacks mention of specific design tools like Figma or Sketch.","No indication of collaboration with developers or integration with React.","Does not discuss usability, accessibility, visual hierarchy, design systems, responsive design, or user feedback.","Answer is quite brief and lacks depth."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate will describe hands-on experience designing user interfaces with attention to usability, accessibility, and visual hierarchy. They should mention using design tools like Figma or Sketch and collaborating with developers to implement designs, preferably in React environments. Concrete examples could include designing interfaces for diverse user groups, creating reusable components, and iterating based on user feedback. They should highlight understanding of design systems, responsive design, and integrating UI designs with product goals.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, so UI design I have done for development of the EdTech platform that was required for my company. It was for the age group of 3 to 10 years, basically school-going kids. It was also an e-commerce platform, so the UI was user-friendly and it involved components that are lightweight and appealing to the kids.","missing_concepts":["Use of design tools (e.g., Figma, Sketch).","Working with React or developer collaboration.","Usability and accessibility considerations.","Responsive design principles.","Design systems and reusable components.","Iterating based on user feedback."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a somewhat relevant answer describing UI design experience related to a specific EdTech and e-commerce platform aimed at children. While this shows some understanding of considering the user group, the answer is incomplete and lacks technical depth. There is no mention of common design tools, collaboration with developers, or how design principles and systems are applied. Without these details, it''s difficult to assess the candidate''s proficiency fully. The response would benefit from elaboration on tools, processes, and concrete examples of design problem solving.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows a general awareness of UI design considering the target user. However, the lack of technical detail, missing references to tools, frameworks, and design best practices, along with an incomplete answer, results in a fail. Candidates for product designer roles should be able to clearly communicate their UI design approach, tool usage, and collaboration experience."},{"prompt":"How did you handle creating user-friendly designs for that young age group?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Mentioned use of well-known references (Duolingo, Kiviko) to inspire design","Conducted user testing with sample and control groups","Included experimentation with themes and components"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Did not mention specific design considerations for the young age group''s cognitive or motor skills","Lacked detail on accessibility, interface simplicity, and color/icon use","No explanation of iterative validation or how design minimized cognitive load","Did not discuss adaptation of references to specific product goals"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"To create user-friendly designs for a young age group, I first conducted research into their cognitive and motor skills to tailor interactions appropriately. I focused on simple, intuitive interfaces with large touch targets, clear icons, and bright colors to engage and guide them effectively. I incorporated iterative user testing with this demographic to validate design choices, ensuring accessibility and minimizing cognitive load. Additionally, I drew inspiration from established kid-friendly apps while adapting features to suit our specific product goals, balancing familiarity and innovation.","candidateAnswer":"So for that, we took the reference of Duolingo, which has a proper documentation of how a UI component should be. Then we also took a reference of Kiviko, which is having its own platform for a similar business. Then we experimented with a lot of different themes and components and did user testing with different sample groups and control groups to understand the responses and the interaction of our target customers. That is how we did.","missing_concepts":["Research into cognitive and motor abilities of young users","Designing simple, intuitive interfaces with large touch targets","Use of bright colors and clear icons tailored for children","Iterative user testing to validate and refine usability","Balancing familiarity with innovation in kid-friendly designs"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a reasonable approach by referencing known successful designs and conducting user testing, which is relevant and indicates practical problem-solving. However, the answer lacks technical depth about adapting designs specifically for a young audience. There is no mention of research on children''s unique needs or specific UI elements crucial for that age group, such as touch target sizes or cognitive load considerations. The explanation does not clearly communicate how the design was tailored to young users beyond general user testing. These gaps reduce completeness and technical correctness, resulting in a moderate score but falling short of passing.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows awareness of referencing industry examples and the importance of user testing but misses foundational concepts critical for designing for young children. The answer is somewhat relevant and clear but vague about key design principles for this demographic. Improvement is needed in articulating user-centered design adaptations and technical rationale."},{"prompt":"Tell me about your experience using React in your projects.","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Mentions usage of React components and their reusability.","References practical applications like interactive UI and mobile web apps.","Indicates experience with React in various project contexts (e-commerce, gamification)."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Lacks technical details such as use of hooks, state management, or performance optimization.","Mixes technologies (Angular and Java) confusingly without clear explanation of integration.","No mention of component-based architecture or collaboration with product/design teams.","Somewhat vague and wordy without structured explanation."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"I have extensive experience using React to build scalable, maintainable user interfaces. In my projects, I have utilized React’s component-based architecture to create reusable UI components that improve development efficiency and consistency. I am proficient with React hooks for managing state and side effects, and I have integrated React with state management libraries like Redux and Context API to handle complex application state. Additionally, I have worked on optimizing React apps for performance by leveraging lazy loading, memoization, and proper rendering strategies. Throughout my experience, I have collaborated closely with product designers and backend developers to ensure seamless UI implementation aligned with product requirements.","candidateAnswer":"So I have been using React. To a great extent, all my UI designs have been based on React. Previously, I was using JavaScript and HTML and CSS, but then React gives you the flexibility and reusability more than HTML and CSS. Also, you have a lot of predefined components in its library. It is a very huge repository of components that can be reused. So with those React components, I developed this platform, used its menu bar to the header footer, predefined functions, and also used Angular at places where I was finding it difficult to, you know, integrate components with the backend. So React has been extensively used in my development of the platform, especially for the interactive part or the gamification part where the users interact with the platform to play games and earn points, earn coins especially. Then we had to use a lot of React components in our e-commerce web page to make it more interactive. The shopping experience should be much more fun and intuitive for the users. So React was used there as well. We also used React 3D components for the kids section, especially for the younger age group, so that they find it more attractive and have fun playing with the components. Also, React was also used on our mobile web pages where we built web applications for the mobile use cases. Yeah, that''s it for my React experience. No, I mean, you have only four to five questions to ask. I thought the interview would go on for much longer. So basically, my experience with React has also been extended, not just for web applications, but beyond web applications as in, you know, for mobile applications where Java especially is used extensively. So, yeah.","missing_concepts":["React hooks (useState, useEffect) and state management mechanisms.","Component-based architecture and reusability principles in depth.","Integration methods with backend or API data fetching.","Performance optimization techniques in React.","Use of Redux or Context API for complex state management."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates familiarity with React and its use in multiple projects including web and mobile web applications. They emphasize component reusability and mention some interactive features, which is relevant. However, the answer is largely superficial and lacks important technical specifics such as how React''s state and lifecycle are managed, use of hooks, or how state management with Redux or Context API is handled. The candidate also confusingly mentions using Angular and Java in the context of React projects without clear integration details, which undermines clarity and correctness. The communication is somewhat rambling and not well structured, making it harder to assess true understanding. Overall, the answer indicates some practical exposure but insufficient depth and technical understanding expected from the ideal response.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows basic practical experience with React in UI development and interactive features but fails to provide critical details on React''s architecture, hooks, state management, and advanced techniques. The explanation lacks clarity and technical depth, limiting confidence in their React expertise for advanced roles. Recommend further evaluation or training to confirm capability."},{"prompt":"Why are you interested in this senior developer role now?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I am interested in this senior developer role now because it aligns with my advanced technical skills in UI design and React development, and it offers an opportunity to lead projects that enhance user experience. With several years of experience building interactive and scalable web applications, I am eager to contribute to a dynamic team focused on innovative front-end solutions. This role matches my career goal to take on greater responsibility, mentor junior developers, and drive the design and implementation of complex features that improve product engagement and accessibility.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Why do you think you''re a strong fit for this senior developer role?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Mentions experience with customer experience and some backend work","References understanding user pain points and UI portions","States overall experience of around seven to eight years"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Does not specify key technical skills like UI design or React","Lacks concrete examples of leadership, mentoring, or collaboration","Does not describe how experience translates to senior developer responsibilities","Answer is vague and lacks depth in technical capabilities"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"I am a strong fit for this senior developer role because I bring over seven years of experience building scalable, user-centric applications, particularly focusing on UI design and React development. My background includes leading frontend projects from concept to deployment, ensuring seamless user experiences and maintainable codebases. I have a solid understanding of both customer needs and backend integrations, allowing me to bridge design and technical implementation effectively. Additionally, I mentor junior developers and collaborate cross-functionally with product and design teams to drive feature development aligned with business goals.","candidateAnswer":"Okay, so see, I have worked on the customer experience side, the backend side also to some extent, and understand user pain points when we have working on the UI portions. So I feel software development is something where I can fit in as a senior software developer. My work experience is almost around seven to eight years. So yeah, I believe I have vast experience in the required domains of this role.","missing_concepts":["UI Design expertise","React development experience","Leading frontend projects from concept to deployment","Mentorship and cross-functional collaboration","Bridging design and technical implementation"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate mentions having seven to eight years of experience and familiarity with user pain points, backend, and UI work. However, the answer lacks specificity regarding core skills such as UI design and React, which are essential for the role. There''s no mention of leadership, mentoring, or cross-team collaboration, which are important for a senior developer. The response is vague and lacks concrete examples, reducing clarity and completeness. To improve, the candidate should explicitly connect their experience to the expected skills and responsibilities for the senior developer role, provide examples of project leadership, and highlight relevant technical proficiencies.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates some relevant experience and general understanding but falls short in articulating key technical skills and senior-level responsibilities. Their answer is vague and incomplete, which indicates a need for stronger alignment with the role''s requirements. Overall, this response does not meet the expectations for a senior developer fit."},{"prompt":"tell me your self","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpqkojyd0036qo0kazygwp1k","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpqmw6ez004qqo0kz88akl0p', 'cmpqmiia1003yqo0k0mda2gfg', 60, 91, 77, 100, 'Strong performance with structured answers and solid topic understanding.', '2026-05-29 08:02:21.947', '2026-05-29 08:02:59.118', '["Clear communication flow","Good depth in responses"]', '["Add sharper quantified examples","Reduce filler and tighten transitions"]', '["Hello.","Yes, I work on a project called Smart Engine. Smart Engine is about database management.","It involves storing data, then there are different systems for which you capture data based on the projects and the information that''s stored. There are multiple stakeholders involved, almost like 15 to 20 people."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 53, '[{"prompt":"Could you briefly introduce your current role and your main responsibilities?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Candidate gave a detailed explanation of a specific project involving data management.","Communication was generally clear and understandable."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["The answer does not describe the candidate''s role or responsibilities related to sales, marketing, business development, or client relationship management.","The response is focused entirely on technical data cleaning and management without linking to service business or sales lifecycle.","Lacks mention of negotiation, contract management, strategic planning, or stakeholder engagement tied to business development."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate will describe their current role focusing on business development and client relationship management in the service industry, highlighting responsibilities such as securing corporate contracts, managing service agreements, and leading negotiations. They should mention overseeing the full sales lifecycle—from identifying opportunities, closing deals, to ensuring service delivery aligns with client expectations and company standards. Additionally, they might include coordinating between internal teams and clients to maintain service quality and timely execution, plus monitoring market trends to inform strategic planning.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, I work on a project called Smart Engine. Smart Engine is about database management. It involves storing data, then there are different systems for which you capture data based on the projects and the information that''s stored. There are multiple stakeholders involved, almost like 15 to 20 people. The data is also scattered. Some, yeah, some are kept on computers, some in files, some on loose papers. There are data in the form of drawings on hard papers, there are information stored in PDFs, in Excel, in text, in emails, and so on. So all the information available in the database was very scattered. It took us almost 10 to 15 years to collect all the information, then clean the data based on our requirement. Structure the data as per the new resource and the new requirement. We had to involve around 50 to 60 employees just for cleaning purpose. Then experts were hired to make, to conclude which data is useful and which is not useful. This took a lot of time.","missing_concepts":["Business development","Client relationship management","Sales lifecycle","Contract management","Negotiation","Strategic planning in service business"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer focused exclusively on describing the Smart Engine project related to database and data management, describing challenges with scattered data and data cleaning efforts. However, the question sought an overview of their current role in sales and marketing within the service business, including responsibilities such as business development, client management, and contract negotiations. There was no connection made to sales, marketing, or service delivery aspects, which are critical for the role. Therefore, the answer, while somewhat clear in describing a technical project, fails to address the core question or demonstrate relevant skills expected for the Senior Executive Sales & Marketing position. More focus on how they manage client relationships, negotiate contracts, oversee sales processes, or lead teams for service business growth would be necessary to pass.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate clearly understands data management challenges but does not demonstrate knowledge or experience relevant to sales and marketing responsibilities. The answer lacks relevance and completeness regarding the position''s key skills. Does not meet expectations for the role."},{"prompt":"Can you tell me about a challenging project you recently worked on and how you handled it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Candidate described involvement in a complex data consolidation project","Mentioned multiple stakeholders involved","Highlighted the challenge of scattered data in various formats"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["No detailed explanation of how the candidate managed the stakeholders or coordinated the project","Lacked specifics on negotiation, strategic planning, or communication approaches used","Did not explain the candidate''s personal role in driving resolution or outcomes","No mention of measurable business results or client satisfaction","The response focused more on data cleaning logistics rather than problem-solving strategy"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate will describe a multifaceted project involving multiple stakeholders and complexity in coordination. They will explain specific challenges such as scattered data, diverse stakeholder interests, or operational obstacles, and detail how they managed them using strategic planning, negotiation, and proactive communication. For example, they might illustrate how they consolidated fragmented information, aligned cross-functional teams, and negotiated terms to ensure smooth execution and client satisfaction. The candidate should emphasize their role in driving the project from problem identification through resolution, highlighting effective stakeholder management and measurable business outcomes relevant to contract or service delivery.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, I work on a project called Smart Engine. Smart Engine is about database management. It involves storing data, then there are different systems for which you capture data based on the projects and the information that''s stored. There are multiple stakeholders involved, almost like 15 to 20 people. The data is also scattered. Some, yeah, some are kept on computers, some in files, some on loose papers. There are data in the form of drawings on hard papers, there are information stored in PDFs, in Excel, in text, in emails, and so on. So all the information available in the database was very scattered. It took us almost 10 to 15 years to collect all the information, then clean the data based on our requirement. Structure the data as per the new resource and the new requirement. We had to involve around 50 to 60 employees just for cleaning purpose. Then experts were hired to make, to conclude which data is useful and which is not useful. This took a lot of time.","missing_concepts":["Strategic planning to align stakeholders","Negotiation and communication techniques applied","Contract or service delivery management","Business outcomes and impact of the project"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate described a challenging project involving scattered data and multiple stakeholders, which aligns in part with the question. However, the answer mainly focused on describing the data gathering and cleaning process rather than how the candidate handled the challenges strategically. There was little insight into the candidate''s leadership or problem-solving approach, such as communication, negotiation, or planning. The role-specific skills expected were not evident, and no measurable outcomes or impact were discussed. Communication was somewhat clear but lacked depth and professional articulation of the candidate''s role. Overall, this answer shows awareness of complexity but insufficient demonstration of effective handling and leadership of the project.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate understands the scale and nature of a complex data project but does not convincingly demonstrate critical leadership, strategic planning, or negotiation skills expected for a senior executive role. The answer is incomplete in showing problem-solving capabilities and stakeholder management. More detail on personal contribution and outcomes is needed."},{"prompt":"How do you price an Annual Maintenance Contract, or AMC contract, in your service business?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Acknowledges importance of understanding customer requirements and defining contract scope","Considers resources, infrastructure, and cost factors in pricing","Mentions response time and service frequency as pricing factors","Incorporates client revenue potential and negotiation for win-win pricing","Recognizes AMC as a long-term contract with detailed pricing decision timeline"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Initial part about ''cleaning'' and ''optimizing variables'' is off-topic and unclear","Lacks explicit mention of parts replacement, overheads, SLA details as separate factors","Does not clearly specify competitive market analysis or risk exposure considerations","Some explanations are vague and not well-structured"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"Pricing an AMC involves a detailed analysis of the scope of services, frequency of visits, resource requirements, and expected service levels. Factors include the cost of labor, parts replacement, overheads, contingency for emergency support, and the agreed service level agreements (SLAs). Competitive market rates and the client''s business size and risk exposure also influence pricing. Ultimately, the price balances profitability with client value to ensure a sustainable contract.","candidateAnswer":"Then, after all the cleaning is done, you have to make the requirements as good as possible. So you have to create linkages between the different systems that are there, map each every requirement with every variable. You look for optimization opportunities so that the number of variables and the database is as small as possible and it gives you outcome as large as possible. AMC contracts are priced based on hundreds of different factors. It includes understanding customer requirements, defining the scope of the contract, the services that are to be provided to the customers is listed down, and the timeline for which the service will be given. We will start calculating all the resources that will be needed, hard and soft resources, the infrastructure that will be needed, the hourly as well as fixed costs that will be incurred in providing the service. Then, is there any maintenance required? How frequent is the response time required by the customer? How many requirements are the dynamic requirements and how many are static, that also is important while deciding the pricing of the AMC contract. So based on all these requirements, we decide on what should be the pricing. Also, what is taken into account is the amount of revenue that the customer can potentially generate for us. So based on that, we can give clients better pricing and attractive discount so that it is win-win situation for both the client and our business. So service AMC contracts are usually long-term contracts, so the pricing decision-making itself takes usually four to five months.","missing_concepts":["Parts replacement cost","Overheads and contingency costs","Service Level Agreements (SLAs)","Competitive market rates","Client''s business size and risk exposure"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows a reasonable understanding of pricing an AMC contract by emphasizing the need to analyze customer requirements, scope, resources, and service timelines. The consideration of cost factors such as hard and soft resources, infrastructure, and response times aligns with the ideal approach. Including client revenue potential and offering competitive pricing to foster a win-win relationship is a positive point. However, the initial mention of data cleaning and variable optimization seems unrelated and detracts from clarity. Important factors such as parts replacement, overheads, SLA specifics, and competitive market influence are not explicitly covered. The explanation is somewhat vague and can benefit from better structuring for clarity. Overall, the answer demonstrates good foundational knowledge with room for improvement in completeness and depth.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates a solid understanding of key factors in AMC pricing including resource assessment, service scope, and client relationship considerations. While some technical details and broader market factors are missing, the answer reflects practical experience and strategic thinking suitable for a senior sales and marketing role in service business. Communication is adequate but coul"},{"prompt":"What factors do you consider while preparing a service proposal for a corporate client?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Mentions bidding and contract acquisition process.","Considers fixed non-refundable cost and technical requirements in the proposal.","Acknowledges checking technical requirements with due diligence."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Answer lacks coverage of many important factors such as client business objectives, budget constraints, service scope, risk analysis, SLA alignment, pricing strategy, performance metrics, and long-term relationship considerations.","Explanation of bidding types (Swiss auction, reverse auction) is vague and not directly tied to proposal preparation factors.","Communication lacks clarity and structure; concepts such as ‘factor of safety of 3’ are unexplained and unclear in context.","Does not demonstrate a strategic or holistic understanding of preparing service proposals.","Terminology and concepts are not well connected or elaborated."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"When preparing a service proposal for a corporate client, key factors include understanding the client''s specific service requirements and scope, assessing the complexity and scale of the services needed (e.g., equipment types, service frequency), evaluating the client''s business objectives and budget constraints, and analyzing potential risks and resource allocation. Additionally, competitive pricing strategies, alignment with service level agreements (SLAs), contract duration, and terms related to performance metrics and penalties should be clearly defined. It''s also essential to account for the client''s expected revenue potential, long-term relationship value, and ensure the proposal demonstrates how our service excellence will meet or exceed their expectations.","candidateAnswer":"While preparing a service proposal for a corporate client, so first of all, we do the bidding for the contract. That we want to take, the bidding process can be in the form of Swiss auction or a reverse auction or whatever it is. The proposal that we prepare also depends on the type of option that is going to take place. What we take into account is that the fixed non-refundable cost that should go in shouldn''t be a big loss to our company, as well as while preparing the proposal, we make sure that the technical requirements of the contracts are checked and included in our proposal with due diligence and with a factor of safety of 3.","missing_concepts":["Understanding client''s specific service requirements and scope","Assessment of service complexity and scale","Client''s business objectives and budget constraints","Risk evaluation and resource allocation","Competitive pricing strategies","Alignment with service level agreements (SLAs)","Contract duration and performance metrics","Long-term relationship value and revenue potential"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows a partial understanding of elements involved in preparing a service proposal, such as bidding and taking care of technical requirements and fixed costs. However, the answer is incomplete and lacks crucial elements expected for this role, including strategic assessment of client needs, pricing, risk management, and contract terms. The explanation is not very clear or well structured, making the communication weak. Competency in negotiation, strategic planning, and contract management is not sufficiently demonstrated. For improvement, the candidate should cover more comprehensive factors and clearly explain their relevance to building a competitive and client-tailored proposal.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate provides a fragmentary view focused mainly on bidding processes and some cost considerations but misses many key factors critical to preparing a successful service proposal. The answer reflects limited depth and communication clarity, resulting in a failing evaluation for this medium difficulty question targeting senior-level sales and marketing expertise."},{"prompt":"How do you price an AMC contract?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpqmiia1003zqo0k08q63qv8","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"How do you calculate profitability for a long-term service contract?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpqmiia10041qo0kssp7hf9o","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"What KPIs would you track for service delivery performance?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpqmiia10042qo0k3zkif731","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"How do you assess service requirements during a site visit?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpqmiia10043qo0kqrwzi7th","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpth2n9f005yqo0kd6xyy1jf', 'cmptgtoss004yqo0kyew090wv', 57, 79, 67, 100, 'Strong performance with structured answers and solid topic understanding.', '2026-05-31 07:42:44.547', '2026-05-31 07:43:33.782', '["Clear communication flow","Good depth in responses"]', '["Add sharper quantified examples","Reduce filler and tighten transitions"]', '["Hi, dasena, wie ist es heute?","So I would like to say that I have handled the role of cell segregative where I was responsible to sell the franchise business of one of the F&B brand.","So there I was responsible to identify the potential clients."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 52, '[{"prompt":"Can you start by telling me a bit about your most recent role and your key responsibilities there?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Identified potential clients and arranged meetings","Explained business/franchise model to clients","Handled deal closure processes"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Role in sales & marketing service business not clearly articulated; focused on franchise sales in F&B rather than service sector sales","Lacked mention of key responsibilities like contract negotiation, strategic planning, or managing agreements","Did not describe coordination with internal teams or client relationship management beyond initial sale","Explanation was somewhat vague and lacked detail on business development or market monitoring"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe their latest position, emphasizing responsibilities closely aligned with sales and marketing in a service-oriented business. They would highlight business development efforts, such as identifying and converting corporate clients, managing strategic service agreements or AMCs, and fostering client relationships. Key responsibilities would include negotiating contracts, coordinating between clients and internal teams to ensure service delivery, monitoring market competition, and reporting on sales pipelines. For example, the candidate might say: \\"In my most recent role as a Senior Sales Executive in the service sector, I was responsible for driving revenue growth by securing corporate rate contracts and managing long-term service agreements. I led negotiations, developed new business opportunities within corporate and facility management sectors, ensured seamless coordination between clients and technical teams to meet service deadlines, and maintained strong client relationships to maximize satisfaction and retention.\\"","candidateAnswer":"So I would like to say that I have handled the role of cell segregative where I was responsible to sell the franchise business of one of the F&B brand. So there I was responsible to identify the potential clients. Arrange scheduled meeting with them and make them aware about the franchise model, how it works, and how it can be beneficial for the customers. And basis on that, if there are any questions, some details, clarifications required, I used to give them and then we used to close the deal. So that was the key role and responsibilities of my role.","missing_concepts":["Service-oriented sales and marketing responsibilities","Negotiation of contracts and long-term service agreements","Coordination between client and internal teams","Strategic planning and market competition monitoring","Client retention and relationship management"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate described a role involving sales of franchise business in the F&B sector, focusing on client identification, meetings, explaining the franchise model, and deal closure. While this demonstrates some sales experience, it does not align well with the expectations for a senior executive sales and marketing role in a service business. The answer did not mention managing corporate client relationships, negotiating contracts or service agreements, nor coordinating with internal teams to ensure service delivery. The candidate''s explanation lacked depth and missed several key responsibilities outlined in the ideal answer. Communication was understandable but somewhat informal and incomplete. Overall, the response partially reflects sales experience but is incomplete and insufficient for the role being evaluated.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows basic sales experience in franchise business development but does not sufficiently demonstrate the senior-level sales and marketing responsibilities expected in a service business context. Important areas such as contract negotiation and client relationship management were not addressed, leading to a rating below pass threshold."},{"prompt":"Could you describe one major challenge you faced in that role and how you handled it, particularly in terms of driving sales growth?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A major challenge in a sales and marketing role for service business often involves breaking into new corporate accounts with entrenched vendor relationships or convincing clients to switch from competitors. To handle this, a strong candidate would identify key decision makers and understand client pain points, then tailor value propositions emphasizing service quality, reliability, and cost-effectiveness through AMCs or long-term contracts. They would leverage strategic negotiation skills to overcome objections and close deals, while coordinating closely with internal teams to ensure promises translate into seamless service delivery, thereby building credibility and driving sustained sales growth. For example, they might implement targeted outreach campaigns, negotiate flexible contract terms, and monitor competitor offerings to position their services advantageously.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"How do you price an Annual Maintenance Contract, or AMC contract, for a corporate client?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":4,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["The candidate recognizes that product price is a factor in pricing the AMC."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Answer is overly simplistic and lacks detail.","No mention of key factors like labor, spare parts, service frequency, or customer requirements.","Does not address cost calculation, market benchmarking, overheads or profit margin.","Does not demonstrate understanding of the comprehensive pricing strategy for AMC."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"Pricing an Annual Maintenance Contract involves calculating the total cost of providing maintenance services over the contract period, including labor, spare parts, overheads, and profit margin. It requires assessing the scope and frequency of services, equipment age and complexity, customer requirements, and benchmarking against market rates to ensure competitiveness and profitability.","candidateAnswer":"So annual maintenance contract is priced basis on the product price which we have given to them.","missing_concepts":["Total cost calculation (labor, spare parts, overheads)","Scope and frequency of maintenance services","Equipment age and complexity considerations","Customer requirements and expectations","Market benchmarking to ensure competitiveness","Profit margin and strategic pricing","Contract negotiation and management aspects"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is technically too narrow and incomplete. Pricing an AMC involves a holistic assessment of costs and service scope, which was missing here. While referencing product price is relevant, it alone does not form a basis for AMC pricing. There is little indication of understanding of the strategic and operational factors involved. The answer is somewhat relevant and clear but lacks depth and problem-solving insight expected for a senior executive role in sales and marketing for service business.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate showed a very basic insight by linking AMC pricing to product price but failed to elaborate on critical components such as cost structure, service details, and market factors. Their answer suggests limited practical understanding of AMC contract pricing and is insufficient for a senior-level sales and marketing position."},{"prompt":"What factors do you consider while preparing a service proposal for a corporate client?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Recognizes the importance of market rates in proposal preparation","Mentions the need to highlight key features or unique selling points (USPs)"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Lacks discussion on understanding client needs or pain points","No mention of scope analysis, resource availability, timelines, or contract terms","Answer is incomplete and somewhat vague","Communication lacks detailed explanation and structure"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"When preparing a service proposal for a corporate client, key factors include understanding the client’s specific business needs and pain points, conducting a thorough analysis of the scope of services required, evaluating current market rates and competitive pricing, and clearly defining the value proposition and unique selling points (USPs) of our service offerings. It is also essential to consider resource availability, service delivery timelines, contractual terms, and potential customization to align with the client’s operational requirements. Additionally, including scalable solutions and after-sales support enhances the proposal’s attractiveness while ensuring profitability and feasibility from our side.","candidateAnswer":"And after that, this is on the service what we provide during the annual period. So while preparing the service proposal, we have to look into the current market rates going on in the market, what is our key features or USB points for which we are charging them.","missing_concepts":["Client’s specific business needs and pain points","Scope of services required","Competitive pricing analysis beyond current rates","Value proposition definition","Resource availability and service delivery timelines","Contractual terms and potential customization","Scalable solutions and after-sales support","Ensuring profitability and feasibility"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate identifies some relevant factors such as current market rates and unique selling points, which are important. However, the answer is very incomplete and misses several critical elements necessary for preparing a comprehensive service proposal. Notably, the explanation lacks detail about understanding client needs, scope definition, timelines, contracts, and support services. Communication is somewhat unclear and lacks depth. The candidate shows partial understanding but falls short of covering the important factors expected for this role.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate demonstrates a basic awareness of market-driven pricing and USPs but does not provide a comprehensive view of the factors needed for service proposal preparation. The answer is incomplete and lacks the depth required for a senior executive sales and marketing role. Additional preparation and understanding are needed."},{"prompt":"How do you calculate profitability for a long-term service contract?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Recognizes the importance of costs and revenues in profitability calculation","Mentions number of services and hours as factors impacting service delivery"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Lacks detailed breakdown of cost components (direct, indirect, overheads)","Does not mention critical factors like contingencies, inflation, penalties, or bonuses","Vague explanation of profitability calculation","Focuses on customer loyalty rather than financial metrics explicitly"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"Profitability for a long-term service contract is calculated by subtracting the total costs incurred in delivering the service over the contract period from the total revenue earned from the contract. This includes accounting for direct costs like labor, materials, and overheads related to service delivery, as well as indirect costs such as administrative expenses. Additionally, it is important to factor in estimates for contingencies, inflation, and any service-level penalties or bonuses stipulated in the contract to determine net profit margin accurately.","candidateAnswer":"So profitability from the long-term service contract is through loyalty of the customer for a longer period. So this is on the number of services provided, number of hours given to the service of the client, and the cost incurred. So the difference of these two, we use to calculate the... Profitability of the long-term service contract.","missing_concepts":["Detailed components of total costs (labor, materials, overheads)","Inclusion of indirect costs like administrative expenses","Consideration of contingencies, inflation, penalties, or bonuses","Explicit formula or clear method for calculating net profit margin"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows some understanding that profitability relates to the difference between costs and revenues over the contract period and mentions factors like service hours and costs incurred. However, the explanation is vague and incomplete, lacking key elements such as the detailed costing structure, indirect costs, and adjustments for contingencies or contract-specific adjustments such as penalties or bonuses. The answer also inappropriately emphasizes customer loyalty as a measure of profitability, which is more relevant to customer retention but does not constitute direct profitability calculation. Overall, the candidate did not provide a thorough or technically accurate method to calculate profitability for a long-term service contract and missed several critical factors necessary for this calculation.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates a basic grasp of profitability involving cost and revenue but fails to articulate a comprehensive, accurate method for calculating profitability in long-term service contracts. The answer is vague, partially correct, but incomplete and missing key financial and contractual considerations, resulting in a fail overall."},{"prompt":"What key performance indicators would you track for service delivery performance?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Identified service timeliness (TAT) as a key KPI","Recognized service quality based on client feedback and satisfaction"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Did not mention other important KPIs such as First-Time Fix Rate, SLA compliance, or cost efficiency","Partially incomplete answer lacking depth and breadth","Candidate''s explanation felt somewhat fragmented and ended abruptly"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"Key KPIs for service delivery performance include: 1) Service Timeliness, measuring adherence to agreed turnaround times (TAT) for service requests; 2) Service Quality, assessed via client feedback and satisfaction scores (e.g., NPS or CSAT); 3) First-Time Fix Rate, indicating efficiency in resolving issues without repeat visits; 4) Compliance with Service Level Agreements (SLAs), ensuring contractual obligations are met; and 5) Cost Efficiency, tracking service delivery costs against budgets. Monitoring these KPIs ensures service reliability, customer satisfaction, and profitability aligned with contract commitments.","candidateAnswer":"So service delivery performance there are two major parameters key to that is one is timeliness, how timely service has been provided. So the TAT is very important here. The second is the quality of service. So the quality of service based on the feedback from the client and how satisfied the client is with the service. Here is another key indicator.","missing_concepts":["First-Time Fix Rate","Compliance with Service Level Agreements (SLAs)","Cost Efficiency in service delivery"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrated a good understanding of key aspects like timeliness (TAT) and service quality through client feedback, which are critical KPIs for service delivery performance. However, the response lacked completeness as other crucial KPIs such as First-Time Fix Rate, SLA compliance, and cost efficiency were not mentioned. While the answer was relevant and mostly clear, it was somewhat brief and could have been better structured with more detailed examples or elaboration. Overall, the answer shows reasonable grasp but misses some comprehensive detail expected at a senior executive level.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows a solid basic understanding of service delivery KPIs focusing on timeliness and quality. They are relevant and correctly identified these points, but lacked completeness and detail needed for senior-level insights. Communication was adequate but not polished. Pass based on acceptable technical correctness and relevance, though improvement is needed for a fuller strategic perspectiv"},{"prompt":"How do you assess service requirements during a site visit?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":5,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Mentions preparing a checklist and performing an audit systematically","Identifies importance of recording gaps and suggesting solutions"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Answer is vague and lacks structured process explanation","Focus shifts towards cybersecurity and cost, which is not fully aligned with the question","Does not mention engaging with on-site personnel or reviewing existing agreements","Missing strategic alignment with client objectives and compliance requirements","Lacks clarity and professional explanation of service assessment steps"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"During a site visit, a thorough assessment of service requirements begins with understanding the client''s operational environment and identifying all equipment and serviceable assets on-site. The evaluator conducts detailed inspections to determine the current maintenance status, potential risk areas, and service level expectations. This involves engaging with on-site personnel to gather insights on service pain points and reviewing any existing service agreements or reports. The process concludes with documenting specific service needs, compliance requirements, and recommending tailored service solutions that align with the client''s business objectives and contract standards.","candidateAnswer":"And definitely cost is one of the parameters. We have to, what is the cost of service to the client on each performance? These are the main major three performance indicators for the service business. So assessing the cybersecurity parameter at the site visit is by preparing the complete checklist of what things has to be assessed or audited. So one should be well prepared for that audit. And once you go there, do the audit thoroughly, systematically, and record the the differences or the gaps, and basis on that, suggest the solution and the Services which can be carried out to complete the service part.","missing_concepts":["Understanding the client’s operational environment","Identifying all equipment and serviceable assets","Engaging with on-site personnel for insights","Reviewing existing service agreements or reports","Documenting compliance requirements and tailored service recommendations"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate touches on some relevant points like preparing a checklist and auditing the site systematically, as well as recording gaps and suggesting service solutions. However, the answer lacks clear structure and is vague about key steps in assessing service requirements during a site visit. The focus on cybersecurity and cost as main performance indicators is not well contextualized for a general service assessment and neglects fundamental aspects such as understanding client operations, equipment, service agreements, and compliance considerations. Communication is moderately clear but lacks professional depth expected for a senior executive role. Overall, the response demonstrates only a partial understanding and does not fully align with the requirements of the question.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows some awareness of audit and gap analysis but fails to present a complete and relevant approach to assessing service requirements during a site visit. Important concepts such as client interaction, operational context, and documenting service needs are missing. The response is incomplete and partially off-topic, leading to an overall insufficient evaluation."},{"prompt":"How do you price an AMC contract?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmptgtoss004zqo0kzbf6ifca","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"What KPIs would you track for service delivery performance?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmptgtoss0052qo0kjk5hmsab","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpva0614000cqn0jc5nioimw', 'cmpv9z1rw0006qn0jdi4hsfaq', 9, 45, 40, 54, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-01 14:00:23.944', '2026-06-01 14:00:34.666', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["我們壓在這裡。"]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 0, '[{"prompt":"Can you tell me about a challenge you faced at work and how you handled it?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific business analytics challenge, such as dealing with incomplete or inconsistent data, tight deadlines for delivering insights, or stakeholder disagreements on project priorities. They should detail the steps taken: identifying the root cause, leveraging analytical tools to fill gaps, collaborating cross-functionally to align expectations, and iterating on solutions based on feedback. The answer should emphasize problem-solving skills, sound judgment, and effective communication to deliver actionable insights that positively impacted business decisions.","candidateAnswer":"我們壓在這裡。","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpv9z1rw0007qn0j7puy43oh","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have a strong foundation in business analytics with over X years of experience analyzing data to drive strategic decisions. My background includes working with cross-functional teams in finance and marketing to extract insights from large data sets using tools like SQL, Python, and Tableau. For example, I led a project to optimize customer segmentation that increased campaign ROI by 15%. This role aligns well with my expertise in problem-solving, translating complex data into actionable business recommendations, and leveraging domain knowledge to solve relevant challenges effectively.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpwujhxx000pl10kk2doxm3d', 'cmpwubgnd0006l10k8iaoyz81', 65, 68, 58, 78, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-02 16:23:04.341', '2026-06-02 16:23:36.643', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hello.","Yes.","So we have four laws of thermodynamics. The first one is the zeroth law, which is about equilibrium of temperatures. The second law is the law of heat and work. It says that heat can be converted into work and work can be converted into heat. The third law is of entropy, which talks about every system has the tendency to increase entropy."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 65, '[{"prompt":"Can you explain the fundamental laws of thermodynamics?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Identifies the four laws of thermodynamics","Mentions key concepts like thermal equilibrium, conversion of heat and work, and entropy increase"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Inaccurate description of the second and third laws","Misses the zeroth law''s role in defining temperature measurement","No mention of the first law as conservation of energy","Does not address the third law involving entropy approaching a constant at absolute zero","Partially incomplete and somewhat vague explanations"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"The fundamental laws of thermodynamics describe energy interactions in physical systems. The zeroth law states that if two systems are each in thermal equilibrium with a third, they are in thermal equilibrium with each other, establishing temperature as a measurable property. The first law is the conservation of energy, indicating energy cannot be created or destroyed but only transformed. The second law states that in any energy transfer, entropy of a closed system tends to increase, making processes irreversible. The third law states that as temperature approaches absolute zero, the entropy of a perfect crystal approaches a constant minimum.","candidateAnswer":"So we have four laws of thermodynamics. The first one is the zeroth law, which is about equilibrium of temperatures. The second law is the law of heat and work. It says that heat can be converted into work and work can be converted into heat. The third law is of entropy, which talks about every system has the tendency to increase entropy.","missing_concepts":["Precise definition and importance of the zeroth law","First law as conservation of energy","Second law involving entropy increase and irreversibility","Third law relating entropy at absolute zero"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates awareness of the four laws but fails to accurately and completely describe them. The zeroth law is mentioned only briefly without explaining its significance in establishing temperature as a measurable property. The first law is incorrectly referred to as the ''law of heat and work'' rather than the conservation of energy principle. The explanation of the second law is vague and incomplete; it should emphasize entropy increase and irreversibility, not just conversion of heat and work. The third law is inadequately covered, lacking mention of entropy approaching a constant minimum at absolute zero. Overall, the answer shows partial understanding but lacks critical details and precision expected at this level.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows basic familiarity with the thermodynamic laws but a shallow understanding and several inaccuracies. Key principles such as energy conservation and entropy behavior at absolute zero are either misrepresented or missing. The explanation is somewhat unclear and incomplete, indicating the candidate needs further study to fully grasp these fundamental concepts."},{"prompt":"Could you explain the first law of thermodynamics briefly?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":8,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Correct identification of energy conservation as the core concept.","Clear and understandable explanation.","Relevant to the question asked."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Did not explicitly mention energy cannot be created or destroyed in a closed system or the aspect of energy conversion.","Lacked mention of total energy constancy in a closed system."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":8,"expectedAnswer":"The first law of thermodynamics states that energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transferred or converted from one form to another, ensuring the total energy in a closed system remains constant.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, so the first law is about energy conservation, which says energy cannot be created neither destroyed, it can only be transferred from one form to the other.","missing_concepts":["Energy conservation in a closed system.","Energy conversion between forms.","Total energy remaining constant."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrated a good understanding of the first law of thermodynamics by identifying it as the principle of energy conservation and explaining that energy cannot be created or destroyed but transferred between forms. However, the explanation missed detailing that the law applies to closed systems where total energy remains constant. Including this and emphasizing conversion of energy types would have improved completeness. The answer was clear, relevant, and technically correct in its scope.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows solid basic understanding of the first law of thermodynamics, sufficient for a junior mechanical engineering role. Improvement is needed in articulating the full concept regarding closed systems and the constancy of total energy."},{"prompt":"Can you describe a common manufacturing process you’ve worked with or studied?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":5,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Mentions a variety of manufacturing processes indicating broad exposure","Correctly distinguishes between conventional and non-conventional manufacturing methods"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Does not describe any manufacturing process in detail","Lacks explanation of how the processes work or their key considerations","The answer is more of a list rather than a focused, clear explanation"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"One common manufacturing process is casting, which involves pouring molten material, typically metal, into a mold where it solidifies into the desired shape. This process is widely used for creating complex shapes that would be difficult to achieve by machining or assembling parts. Variations include sand casting, die casting, and investment casting, each suited for different scales and material properties. Key considerations include mold design, cooling rate, and material selection to ensure dimensional accuracy and mechanical strength suitable for the intended application.","candidateAnswer":"I''ve studied about a lot of manufacturing processes. To name a few, I have learned about welding, then lathe processes, then casting, then some other processes like sheet molding, basically rolling process, then you have folding process or wire forming processes. Then you have, there are conventional as well as non-conventional manufacturing processes. So conventional manufacturing processes are the ones that I talked about. The non-conventional manufacturing processes are like 3D printing or EDM or any other method.","missing_concepts":["Detailed explanation of casting process including steps involved","Material considerations and how process parameters affect the final product","Technical aspects of mold design, cooling, and mechanical properties"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate displays some awareness of different manufacturing processes but stops short of providing a focused and detailed description of any one process. The response reads like a list of processes without depth, missing key explanations necessary to demonstrate understanding. There is no articulation of how the processes work or their industrial significance. To improve, the candidate should aim to clearly describe one common process, such as casting, including its methodology, variations, and influencing factors, showcasing both technical knowledge and communication skills.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows broad but superficial knowledge of manufacturing processes. Lack of depth and clarity in explanation prevents passing. Recommended to strengthen understanding by focusing on detailed study and explanation of core processes like casting."},{"prompt":"Can you pick one of those processes and explain it in more detail?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Correctly identified casting process and its basic steps.","Provided relevant examples like valves, engines, and rods.","Explanation shows good understanding of the overall process."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Used ''dies'' interchangeably with molds; technically, dies are usually used in forging or stamping, while molds are typical in casting.","Did not mention the melting temperature, cooling and solidification dynamics in detail.","Lacked mention of types of casting materials and considerations about mold materials (e.g., ceramic or sand molds).","Some minor redundancy and less precise terminology."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"Casting is a manufacturing process where a metal is melted and then poured into a mold or die of a specific shape. After cooling and solidification, the metal takes the form of the mold to produce the final component. This process is commonly used for complex shapes like engine blocks, valves, or transmission parts where machining would be difficult or expensive.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, so let''s talk about casting. So casting process involves melting of the raw metal. So basically, you melt the metal first and then you pour it in predefined structures which are called as dies. And then the dies are basically made of either ceramic material or some other material which is not metal. Then you pour the molten metal into the die and then you allow it to cool once the pouring is cooled, you get the final part which is the casting product. For example, valves or a lot of complex machines devices are built of casting. For example, engines or rods which are used in power transmission valves.","missing_concepts":["Difference between mold and die in casting process.","Types of molds and materials used (e.g., sand casting, ceramic molds).","More detailed steps like melting temperature control, cooling rate, and solidification.","Mention of why casting is preferred for complex shapes over machining."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate gave a generally correct explanation of the casting process by mentioning melting metal and pouring it into molds (though referred to as dies, which is slightly inaccurate). They covered the main idea of solidification and final part production, and provided relevant examples that show contextual understanding. However, the explanation was somewhat superficial, missing finer technical details such as mold material types, temperature control aspects, and clarification of casting terminology. Communication was understandable but could be more precise and structured. Overall, the candidate demonstrates a solid foundational knowledge but could improve completeness and technical accuracy.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate has a solid grasp of casting basics and its application examples, suitable for a junior mechanical engineer role. Improvements are needed in technical detail and terminology precision. Overall, the candidate passes with good understanding but should deepen knowledge for more advanced discussions."},{"prompt":"Laws of thermodyanmics","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpwubgnd0007l10kh8jwsgf6","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"The laws of thermodynamics describe fundamental principles governing energy and heat transfer. The zeroth law establishes thermal equilibrium, the first law states that energy is conserved (energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed), the second law introduces entropy and states that energy transfer increases disorder, and the third law states that entropy approaches a constant minimum as temperature approaches absolute zero.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"manufacturing process","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpwubgnd0008l10k2asgfh0x","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A manufacturing process is a series of steps through which raw materials are transformed into finished products. Common manufacturing processes include casting, machining, molding, forming, and joining, each selected based on product design, material, and production volume.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"additive manufacturing","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpwubgnd0009l10ke4todfj7","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process of creating three-dimensional objects by successively adding material layer by layer, based on digital 3D model data. It allows for complex geometries, reduces material waste compared to subtractive methods, and is useful for rapid prototyping and low-volume production in mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpxqgtfp001kl10kc9bho0va', 'cmpxq8xkk000vl10kvapoxipn', 56, 72, 61, 86, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-03 07:16:46.981', '2026-06-03 07:17:24.056', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hello.","Can you repeat?","Pricing the contracts is"]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 52, '[{"prompt":"Could you start by telling me how you approach pricing an Annual Maintenance Contract?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":1,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Answer is too short and incomplete","Lacks any explanation of approach or factors considered in pricing","Does not demonstrate understanding of pricing Annual Maintenance Contracts"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"Pricing an Annual Maintenance Contract involves assessing the scope of services, including coverage frequency and response times, evaluating the cost of resources such as manpower and spare parts, and considering the client''s usage patterns and equipment value. I incorporate factors like risk contingencies, competitive benchmarks, and desired profit margins to formulate a competitive yet profitable price. Additionally, I ensure alignment with long-term strategic goals and client budget constraints to facilitate contract acceptance and sustainable revenue.","candidateAnswer":"Pricing the contracts is","missing_concepts":["Assessment of scope of services and coverage","Evaluation of cost of resources like manpower and spare parts","Consideration of client usage patterns and equipment value","Inclusion of risk contingencies and competitive benchmarks","Alignment with profit margins and strategic goals"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is extremely incomplete and unclear, consisting only of a fragment without any meaningful content. There is no indication of understanding or approach to pricing Annual Maintenance Contracts as required. The answer misses all key components such as evaluating scope, costs, client needs, risks, competition, and profitability. Due to the lack of content, the technical correctness, completeness, and clarity are all very low, reflecting poor problem-solving skills on this topic.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate was unable to provide any substantive answer to how they approach pricing an Annual Maintenance Contract. Their response was too brief and lacked any relevant detail or demonstration of understanding. This suggests weak knowledge in contract pricing and strategic sales planning, which is critical for the Senior Executive role in Sales & Marketing for service business."},{"prompt":"What factors do you consider while preparing a service proposal for a corporate client?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Mention of key factors such as contract requirements, scope of service, resources, timelines, change management, and pricing.","Acknowledgement of complexity in serving corporate clients.","Inclusion of client feedback mechanism through a resolution sheet."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Lack of explicit mention of legal compliance and risk assessment.","Limited detail on competitive positioning and alignment with company service standards.","Somewhat informal and vague phrasing reduces clarity and perceived professionalism."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"A strong service proposal should consider the client''s specific needs and objectives, scope of the services to be provided, resource allocation including manpower and materials, realistic timelines and delivery schedules, clear pricing structures and payment terms, compliance with contractual and legal requirements, and provisions for change management or scalability. Additionally, factors like competitive positioning, risk assessment, and alignment with the company''s service standards are essential to ensure mutually beneficial agreements.","candidateAnswer":"It is a simple task for me. I take into consideration all the long-term services that I provide to the clients and also the resources that will be utilized, consider the time frame, and the change management that we have to do. All these factors make us decide what is the pricing. For a corporate client, it''s a complex task. So while preparing a service proposal, we first of all take into consideration contract requirements, the scope of the service that is required by the client. Based on the scope, we map the offerings that we are going to provide and we also provide a resolution sheet for the clients so that they can let us know the shortcomings or what additional offerings that they are really looking into. We also provide a cost sheet in the proposal as well as there will be the cost sheet and the timeline in the proposal or the execution and the service duration.","missing_concepts":["Compliance with contractual and legal requirements","Competitive positioning","Risk assessment","Alignment with company’s service standards and scalability considerations"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a good understanding of the core elements needed in preparing a service proposal for a corporate client. Key factors like resource allocation, timelines, scope, pricing, and a feedback/resolution process were addressed, showing practical insight into client management and proposal structuring. However, the answer lacks depth regarding compliance, risk management, and strategic considerations such as competitive positioning and alignment with internal service standards. These elements are critical for ensuring proposals are robust and professionally sound. Communication is generally clear but somewhat informal and could be more structured for enhanced clarity and professionalism.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate has a reasonable grasp of preparing service proposals, covering many important aspects relevant to corporate clients. While the response is mostly accurate and relevant, it misses some vital strategic and compliance-related points that would strengthen the proposal quality. Overall, this answer indicates a competent level of understanding suitable for the role, earning a pass with ro"},{"prompt":"Now, how do you calculate profitability for a long-term service contract?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Acknowledges the need to consider multiple revenue sources","Recognizes the importance of growth rate and additional revenue opportunities","Understands that profitability is revenue minus expenses"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Lacks specific mention of direct and indirect costs such as labor, parts, overhead","Does not address cost escalations or risk contingencies","Answer is vague and incomplete regarding how to factor in contract management and inflation","Communication is somewhat unclear and repetitive"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"Profitability for a long-term service contract is calculated by projecting total revenues from the contract over its term, including recurring fees, additional services, and potential upsell opportunities, then subtracting all associated direct and indirect costs, such as labor, parts, overhead, and administrative expenses. It also involves factoring in costs related to contract management, inflation or cost escalations, and risk contingencies over the contract period to ensure a realistic net profit estimation.","candidateAnswer":"Profitability for a long-term service contract is a much complex task because you have to consider the revenue sources and then the expenses linked to each source. So profit is basically revenue minus expenses. So profitability consideration, we also check what is the We consider the growth rate that will be included during the course of the service. What are the additional opportunities that we can get which will be a source of revenue for us with the client and with the growth, the cost cutting, and the additional opportunity, we do our profitability calculations.","missing_concepts":["Detailed breakdown of costs (labor, parts, overhead)","Contract management costs","Inflation or cost escalation factors","Risk contingencies in profit calculation"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate gives a broad and partially accurate view on profitability calculation by mentioning revenue sources, expenses, growth rate, and additional opportunities. However, the answer lacks depth on critical cost components like labor, parts, overhead, and indirect costs. There is no mention of handling inflation, risk contingencies, or contract management expenses, which are important in long-term service contracts. The explanation is somewhat repetitive and vague, which affects clarity. Overall, the candidate shows an understanding of the basic concept but misses key details necessary for a comprehensive and technically accurate answer.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate demonstrates a basic grasp of calculating profitability for long-term service contracts but fails to incorporate important cost elements and risk factors. The answer is relevant but incomplete and somewhat unclear. Additional technical detail and structured explanation would have improved the response."},{"prompt":"What KPIs would you track for service delivery performance?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Correctly mentions important KPIs such as resolution time, productivity, and downtime.","Focuses on relevant service delivery metrics."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Lacks specificity and formal KPI names like SLA compliance, CSAT or NPS.","Does not mention customer satisfaction or service availability explicitly.","Explanation is vague and lacks structured detail."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"Key KPIs for service delivery performance include: 1) Service Level Agreement (SLA) compliance, measuring the percentage of service requests resolved within agreed timelines; 2) First Response Time and Average Resolution Time to assess efficiency; 3) Customer Satisfaction Score (CSAT) or Net Promoter Score (NPS) reflecting service quality perception; 4) Ticket or complaint volume trends to identify recurring issues; 5) Resource utilization rates to ensure productivity; and 6) Downtime or service availability metrics to evaluate reliability. Tracking these KPIs ensures service delivery aligns with client expectations and contractual obligations.","candidateAnswer":"For service delivery, we focus on KPIs like resolution time, then effectiveness, efficiency of our task, productivity of our resources, and the downtime that occurs.","missing_concepts":["Service Level Agreement (SLA) compliance","Customer Satisfaction Score (CSAT) or Net Promoter Score (NPS)","First Response Time","Ticket/complaint volume trends","Explicit mention of service availability metrics"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate identifies some key areas such as resolution time, resource productivity, and downtime, which are relevant to service delivery performance KPIs. However, the response lacks completeness and formal terminology expected at this senior level. Important KPIs like SLA compliance, customer satisfaction metrics (CSAT/NPS), and ticket volume trends are omitted. The explanation is somewhat vague and does not demonstrate thorough understanding or strategic insight. Improving specificity and structure in responses will enhance communication clarity and completeness.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows a basic understanding of service delivery KPIs by highlighting resolution time and resource productivity but misses several key performance indicators and lacks detailed explanation. Overall, the answer is partially correct but incomplete and vague, leading to a score below passing threshold."},{"prompt":"How do you assess service requirements during a site visit?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Focus on customer interaction to understand pain points","Emphasis on noting down all issues observed"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Lacks mention of inspecting physical environment or equipment","No reference to reviewing service logs or performance metrics","Does not include tailoring service proposals to business objectives","Answer too brief and somewhat vague"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"During a site visit, I conduct a thorough evaluation by engaging with key stakeholders to understand their operational challenges and service needs. I inspect the physical environment and existing equipment to identify any maintenance gaps or areas prone to failure. I also review current service logs and performance metrics to detect recurring issues. This comprehensive assessment enables me to tailor service proposals that align with the client''s business objectives and ensure optimal service coverage.","candidateAnswer":"We interact with the customers and the people there, understand their pain points, and take note of each and every issue that is going on there. And based on that, we make an assessment.","missing_concepts":["Engaging with key stakeholders beyond customers","Inspection of physical environment and existing equipment","Analysis of service logs and performance data","Alignment of service assessment with client''s business goals"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates an understanding of engaging with customers and identifying issues, which is a fundamental step in assessing service requirements. However, the answer lacks depth and completeness by not mentioning the inspection of physical assets, review of service data, and strategic tailoring of service proposals. The explanation is somewhat vague and does not fully cover the comprehensive assessment expected in such a role. Overall, the response shows basic awareness but falls short of a thorough and professional approach.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate understands the importance of customer interaction but misses critical elements like environment inspection and data analysis. The answer is relevant and communicated clearly but lacks depth and completeness needed for a senior role. Improvement needed in covering all key assessment areas."},{"prompt":"How do you price an AMC contract?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpxq8xkk000wl10kxm2mye87","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"How do you calculate profitability for a long-term service contract?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpxq8xkk000yl10kfsmp5df3","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpzhw8i5000ilk0k1imx8lh0', 'cmpzhpewo0001lk0k3kdkuxjr', 57, 63, 54, 74, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-04 12:52:22.157', '2026-06-04 12:52:58.535', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hallo.","There are four laws of thermodynamics in the zeroth law, which is about Equilibrium of temperature The first law which is about conservation of energy the second law That talks about entropy change and the fourth law which says that the absolute entropy When the entropy reaches zero State is totally at still","I have studied about casting process."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 56, '[{"prompt":"Could you start by explaining the main laws of thermodynamics?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Correctly identifies there are four laws of thermodynamics","Mentions core topics such as equilibrium, conservation of energy, entropy, and absolute entropy"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Inaccurate description of the Zeroth law; fails to explain it defines temperature via thermal equilibrium","Mislabels the ''third law'' as the ''fourth law''","Incomplete and unclear explanation of the second law about entropy change","Lacks explanation of the significance of the third law about entropy approaching zero at absolute zero temperature","Overall lacks detail and clarity to demonstrate strong understanding"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"The main laws of thermodynamics are: The Zeroth Law states that if two systems are each in thermal equilibrium with a third, they are in equilibrium with each other, defining temperature. The First Law is the conservation of energy, stating that energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed. The Second Law states that entropy of an isolated system never decreases, implying natural processes tend toward disorder. The Third Law states that as temperature approaches absolute zero, the entropy of a perfect crystal approaches zero.","candidateAnswer":"There are four laws of thermodynamics in the zeroth law, which is about Equilibrium of temperature The first law which is about conservation of energy the second law That talks about entropy change and the fourth law which says that the absolute entropy When the entropy reaches zero State is totally at still","missing_concepts":["Proper definition and significance of the Zeroth Law","Clear explanation of the First Law as conservation of energy and energy transformation","Second Law statement about entropy of isolated systems never decreasing and natural processes tending toward disorder","Correct identification and explanation of the Third Law rather than calling it the fourth law"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate recognizes the existence of four thermodynamics laws and mentions key topics associated with each. However, the descriptions are vague and somewhat inaccurate, such as mislabeling the third law as the fourth and providing unclear explanations of concepts like entropy and equilibrium. The answer lacks important details that show a solid understanding of each law''s definition and significance, particularly the Zeroth and Second laws. Communication clarity is limited due to fragmented and imprecise statements. To improve, the candidate should provide precise definitions and explain the implications of each law clearly and accurately.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a basic familiarity with the thermodynamics laws by naming them and associating relevant terms. However, the explanations are incomplete, unclear, and contain some inaccuracies. They need to improve their conceptual understanding and ability to clearly articulate the laws and their importance. Overall, this answer reflects a partial understanding but is insufficient for passing"},{"prompt":"Now, can you walk me through a common manufacturing process you’ve worked with or studied?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":3,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["The candidate correctly identified casting as a manufacturing process."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Lacks explanation of the casting process.","No details about the steps involved in casting.","No demonstration of understanding of technical concepts related to casting.","The answer is too short and vague.","Does not communicate the process clearly or completely."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"A common manufacturing process is casting, which involves melting metal and pouring it into a mold shaped like the desired part. The molten metal solidifies in the mold, after which the part is removed and undergoes post-processing steps such as grinding and polishing to achieve the final dimensions and surface finish.","candidateAnswer":"I have studied about casting process.","missing_concepts":["Melting of metal","Pouring into a mold","Solidification in the mold","Part removal","Post-processing steps such as grinding and polishing"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate was able to mention the casting process, which is relevant to the question. However, the answer is very brief and lacks any meaningful detail or explanation. There is no description of the steps involved, no mention of the thermodynamics concept of melting and solidification, nor post-processing. The response does not demonstrate an understanding of the process nor technical correctness beyond recognizing the keyword. For a medium difficulty question, more thorough explanation is expected. Improvement is needed in providing comprehensive and clear descriptions to demonstrate technical knowledge and understanding.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows very limited understanding of the manufacturing process of casting. Although the process was named correctly, they failed to elaborate or explain any technical details, resulting in an incomplete and vague answer that is insufficient for the role."},{"prompt":"Could you give me a brief description of how the casting process works?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Correctly identified the main steps of casting including pouring molten metal, solidification, cooling, and post-processing.","Answer was relevant to the question and mostly clear."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Used the word ''die'' which is more specific to die casting rather than general casting/mold.","Did not explicitly mention the mold cavity as shaped like the desired part which is fundamental in casting.","Explanation of cooling and solidification was somewhat confusing in order.","Post-processing details were briefly mentioned but could be expanded."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"Casting is a manufacturing process where molten metal is poured into a mold cavity shaped like the desired part and allowed to solidify. After cooling, the solidified part is removed from the mold and may undergo post-processing such as cleaning, grinding, or polishing to achieve final specifications.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, in the casting process, molten metal is poured into a die which is then solidified and then allowed to cool. Once the metal cools in the die, the part is taken out and then it is post-processed that is polishing is done and grinding is done and you obtain the final product.","missing_concepts":["Definition and role of the mold cavity shaped to the desired part.","Clarification between mold and die.","Thermodynamic aspects like molten metal temperature or solidification principle."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrated an overall good understanding of the casting process by mentioning pouring molten metal, solidification, cooling, and post-processing steps such as polishing and grinding. However, the use of the term ''die'' is more specific to a die casting process, whereas the general casting process involves molds (which may be sand, metal, or other materials). The candidate did not explain that the mold cavity is shaped like the desired part, which is a key aspect of casting. The explanation of solidification and cooling was slightly unclear and could be better organized. Also, more mention of the thermodynamic principles and precise definition of the mold would improve completeness and technical accuracy. The answer was relevant and generally clear but a bit simplistic and incomplete.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a basic and generally correct understanding of the casting process, covering the principal steps with some minor inaccuracies and lack of detail. The answer meets minimum expectations for the role of Junior Mechanical Engineer but would benefit from refinement in terminology and completeness."},{"prompt":"Now, can you explain what additive manufacturing is and how it''s different from traditional methods?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":7,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Correctly identified additive manufacturing as a layer-by-layer material deposition process.","Understood and explained the difference between additive and subtractive manufacturing.","Highlighted the core difference in material addition versus removal."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Explanation lacked mention of digital 3D models guiding the process.","Did not cover benefits such as reduced waste or ability to produce complex geometries.","Communication was somewhat repetitive and slightly unclear in phrasing."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process where objects are created by adding material layer by layer based on digital 3D models. Unlike traditional subtractive manufacturing methods, which involve removing material from a solid block (such as machining or milling), additive manufacturing builds parts by depositing material, which reduces waste and allows for complex geometries not achievable through conventional techniques.","candidateAnswer":"additive manufacturing is basically a non-traditional manufacturing process in which material is deposited layer by layer to form the final product. It is different from other conventional process as most of the traditional processes are subtractive manufacturing that is the product is cut or subtract or material is removed from the raw material and to get final product in additive manufacturing. The material is deposited or added layer by layer to get the final product.","missing_concepts":["Use of digital 3D models or CAD files to direct the manufacturing process.","Advantages like reduced material waste and ability to manufacture complex shapes."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrated a solid basic understanding of additive manufacturing by clearly contrasting it with traditional subtractive methods. However, the explanation was somewhat repetitive and lacked mention of key concepts such as the role of digital 3D models and the benefits of additive manufacturing like reduced waste and the production of complex geometries. Improving explanation clarity and including these points would make the answer stronger.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows good fundamental understanding of additive manufacturing and its differentiation from traditional methods, passing the evaluation for a junior mechanical engineer. Some details were missing, but the core concept was well communicated."},{"prompt":"One last question: why do you want to pursue this role as a junior mechanical engineer?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Mentioned passion for working on mechanical systems and product design","Indicated current education background relevant to the role"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Lacks specific mention of key technical areas such as thermodynamics or manufacturing","Does not address desire to apply or deepen knowledge in real-world settings","No reference to learning under mentorship or contributing to company projects","Answer is vague and somewhat incomplete","Communication clarity is moderate but slightly disorganized"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"I want to pursue this junior mechanical engineer role to apply and deepen my foundational knowledge from my mechanical engineering degree in real-world settings, particularly in thermodynamics and manufacturing processes. This role offers hands-on experience with mechanical systems and product design, allowing me to develop practical skills under mentorship. Additionally, I am eager to contribute to the company''s engineering projects by bringing fresh perspectives and a strong commitment to learning and innovation in mechanical design and manufacturing.","candidateAnswer":"So I am completing my undergraduation B.Tech in Mechanical Engineering and I have I am very passionate about Working on mechanical systems and doing engineering In engineering product design and work with Mechanical parts","missing_concepts":["Thermodynamics","Manufacturing processes","Hands-on experience and practical skills development","Contribution to company projects","Mentorship and learning intentions"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows enthusiasm for mechanical engineering and product design, which is relevant to the role. However, the answer is vague and lacks depth. Important aspects such as applying foundational knowledge, specific technical areas like thermodynamics and manufacturing, and motivation to learn under mentorship or contribute to company projects are missing. Communication could be clearer and more structured. Overall, the candidate demonstrates some understanding but does not fully articulate a strong, focused motivation for the role as expected.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has a basic relevant background and interest but provides an incomplete and somewhat unclear explanation of their motivation for this junior mechanical engineer role. More detail on specific technical interests and the practical application of skills is needed to pass."},{"prompt":"Laws of thermodyanmics","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpzhpewo0002lk0ky0ykq9xw","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"The laws of thermodynamics describe fundamental principles governing energy and heat transfer. The zeroth law establishes thermal equilibrium, the first law states that energy is conserved (energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed), the second law introduces entropy and states that energy transfer increases disorder, and the third law states that entropy approaches a constant minimum as temperature approaches absolute zero.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"manufacturing process","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpzhpewo0003lk0kxobes2xc","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A manufacturing process is a series of steps through which raw materials are transformed into finished products. Common manufacturing processes include casting, machining, molding, forming, and joining, each selected based on product design, material, and production volume.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"additive manufacturing","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpzhpewo0004lk0knfd5fxh5","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process of creating three-dimensional objects by successively adding material layer by layer, based on digital 3D model data. It allows for complex geometries, reduces material waste compared to subtractive methods, and is useful for rapid prototyping and low-volume production in mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpzicy6v001hlk0knw4561mz', 'cmpzi19xw000qlk0kd79lr0o7', 64, 79, 67, 98, 'Strong performance with structured answers and solid topic understanding.', '2026-06-04 13:05:21.944', '2026-06-04 13:06:37.307', '["Clear communication flow","Good depth in responses"]', '["Add sharper quantified examples","Reduce filler and tighten transitions"]', '["Hello.","I am a product designer, I have 4 years of experience both in hardware and software products. I have used 3D modeling, 2D graphics and drawing tools as well as prototyping, prototyping softwares for designing software applications or software products. I have worked for big clients like Google and Apple and also freelancing for educational customers.","Currently my job role is to make MVPs for my customers. So when a client has some business idea, I convert that idea to a basic design and then convert it to minimum viable product or an MVP. Based on that, then my team starts developing the prototype which is then given to the customers and then the project continues from there on. Currently I am developing a bowling machine that is used in cricket for batting practice."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 60, '[{"prompt":"Hi Ram, my name is Sana and I''ll be conducting your interview today. Let''s jump right in—tell me about yourself.","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":8,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Clear communication of product design experience","Mention of specific tools such as 3D modeling and prototyping software","Relevant experience with high-profile clients"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Lacks detail about software-side skills, especially UI design focus","No mention of React or front-end development skills expected for the role","Incomplete regarding leadership, collaboration, and impact on product improvements"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"I am a senior developer with extensive experience in designing and building scalable web applications, particularly using React for front-end development. Over the past several years, I have led multiple projects from concept to deployment, focusing on clean UI design, performance optimization, and cross-team collaboration. My background includes mentoring junior developers and collaborating closely with UI/UX designers to deliver seamless user experiences that meet business goals. In this role, I emphasize writing maintainable code, implementing best practices in React, and driving product improvements through data-driven decisions.","candidateAnswer":"I am a product designer, I have 4 years of experience both in hardware and software products. I have used 3D modeling, 2D graphics and drawing tools as well as prototyping, prototyping softwares for designing software applications or software products. I have worked for big clients like Google and Apple and also freelancing for educational customers.","missing_concepts":["UI design specifics","React expertise","Project leadership or collaboration","Driving product improvements"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a decent overview of their product design experience, including hardware and software contexts, as well as some tools used. Their communication is clear and relevant to the role of product designer. However, the answer lacks important details about specific skills in UI design and React, which were key expectations for this role. There is also no mention of mentoring or collaboration, which reduces the completeness of the response. Overall, the candidate demonstrates relevant experience but does not fully address the technical specifics or deeper understanding expected.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a basic understanding and experience in product design with some relevant tools and clients mentioned. However, they fall short in addressing the technical expectations tied to UI design and React skills essential for this position, resulting in a below passing score."},{"prompt":"Thank you for sharing that. Can you tell me more about your current role and what you''re focusing on right now?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Clearly explained their current involvement with MVP creation.","Provided a concrete example of a project currently being worked on."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Did not mention any specific design processes or methodologies.","No mention of collaboration with teams or use of specific design tools like React.","Lacks reference to user-centric design or mentoring roles."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"In my current role as a senior product designer, I lead the end-to-end design process, starting from understanding user needs and business goals, through wireframing and prototyping, to final UI design and collaboration with development teams using React. My focus right now is on delivering scalable and user-centric designs for a complex platform, ensuring seamless interaction and visual consistency. I also mentor junior designers and work cross-functionally with product managers and engineers to iterate quickly and maintain design quality.","candidateAnswer":"Currently my job role is to make MVPs for my customers. So when a client has some business idea, I convert that idea to a basic design and then convert it to minimum viable product or an MVP. Based on that, then my team starts developing the prototype which is then given to the customers and then the project continues from there on. Currently I am developing a bowling machine that is used in cricket for batting practice.","missing_concepts":["End-to-end design process including wireframing and prototyping.","Collaboration with development teams and cross-functional roles.","Focus on scalable and user-centric design principles.","Use of UI design tools and technologies such as React."],"detailed_feedback":"While the candidate does describe their role around creating MVPs and working with clients'' business ideas, the answer lacks depth in describing the design process, methodologies, and collaboration which are crucial for a senior product designer role. The answer is somewhat relevant and clearly communicated but misses key aspects such as user-centric focus, mentoring, and technology stacks. Greater detail on design stages, team interactions, and tools used would strengthen the response and demonstrate a better understanding of the role''s demands.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate provides a basic overview of their role related to developing MVPs but does not sufficiently cover essential design skills and responsibilities expected in a senior product designer position. The answer shows partial understanding but lacks completeness and technical depth, leading to a fail overall."},{"prompt":"Let’s dive deeper—can you walk me through your experience with UI design in your projects?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Mentions experience with various project types including e-commerce websites, gaming mobile apps, and educational edtech apps.","Answer is relevant to the question asked.","Clear and understandable response."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["No mention of specific UI design processes or methodologies.","Lacks reference to tools, collaboration, iterative design, or user-centered approaches.","No examples of creating wireframes, prototypes, or design systems.","Does not demonstrate problem solving or how UI design improved user experience."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe their end-to-end engagement with UI design, highlighting specific project types such as web applications, mobile apps, or enterprise software. They should mention designing cohesive user interfaces aligned with user needs and business goals, detailing their role in creating wireframes, prototypes, or high-fidelity mockups. Concrete examples might include working with tools like Figma or Sketch, collaborating closely with UX researchers and front-end developers to ensure design feasibility and consistency across platforms. They should explain iterative design processes rooted in user feedback and usability testing, demonstrating how their UI design improved usability, accessibility, or engagement metrics. They might also reference adapting design systems or contributing to pattern libraries as part of maintaining UI consistency across multiple products.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, so I have designed UI for e-commerce websites, as well as gaming mobile applications. I have also worked on UI design for educational edtech startups and a few general applications for Android and Apple.","missing_concepts":["End-to-end UI design process","Use of design tools such as Figma or Sketch","Collaboration with UX researchers and developers","Iterative design and user feedback incorporation","Design systems or pattern libraries","Impact of UI design on usability, accessibility, and engagement"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a basic overview of the types of projects they have worked on in UI design, which is relevant but very superficial. They do not elaborate on their specific contributions, processes, or tools used, missing critical aspects expected from the role such as collaboration, prototyping, and iterative design informed by user feedback. The answer lacks demonstration of deeper understanding or problem-solving in UI design. To improve, the candidate should share concrete examples of their design workflow, tools, collaboration, and how their UI design decisions positively impacted the product or user experience.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate has some exposure to UI design across different project types but fails to provide detail on their role, processes, or technical approach. The response does not meet expectations for demonstrating a solid grasp of UI design activities and best practices. I recommend further probing or considering other candidates with stronger, more detailed UI design experience."},{"prompt":"And what specific tools or frameworks do you usually rely on for your UI design work?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":8,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Correctly identified Figma as a tool used for wireframing","Answer is relevant and clearly communicated"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Answer is very brief and incomplete","Did not mention other common tools like Sketch or Adobe XD","No mention of frameworks or design systems such as Material Design or Ant Design","Does not demonstrate deeper understanding or problem solving related to UI design tools"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"For UI design, I primarily rely on Figma and Sketch for creating wireframes and high-fidelity prototypes due to their collaborative features and design system integrations. I also use Adobe XD for interactive prototypes and sometimes leverage design system frameworks like Material Design or Ant Design to ensure consistency and efficiency in component-based UI design.","candidateAnswer":"For wireframing, I use Figma.","missing_concepts":["Sketch","Adobe XD","Design system frameworks (Material Design, Ant Design)","High-fidelity prototypes","Collaborative features of design tools"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate correctly named Figma as a tool for wireframing, which is technically correct and relevant to the question. However, the answer is very incomplete, missing other essential tools and frameworks commonly used in UI design such as Sketch, Adobe XD, and design systems like Material Design or Ant Design. The briefness of the answer limits assessment of deeper understanding or problem solving regarding selection and usage of UI design tools. Overall, the candidate demonstrated basic knowledge but failed to provide a complete and comprehensive response expected for the role.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows a basic understanding of UI design tools but does not provide sufficient detail or breadth in toolset or framework usage. Needs to expand knowledge and ability to articulate a fuller range of commonly used tools and frameworks to be considered proficient."},{"prompt":"How about your experience with React—can you tell me about that?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Candidate demonstrates familiarity with React for building web applications.","Mentions reuse of UI elements and leveraging React libraries."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Answer is vague and lacks detail on key React concepts like state management, hooks, or performance optimization.","Does not provide examples or elaborate on the scale or complexity of projects.","Limited completeness: no mention of component development, collaboration, or advanced React techniques."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"I have significant experience using React to build scalable, maintainable web applications. This includes developing reusable components, managing state effectively using hooks or Redux, and optimizing performance through code-splitting and memoization. I''ve collaborated closely with cross-functional teams to translate design prototypes into functional UI, ensuring accessibility and responsiveness. For example, I led the front-end development of a complex dashboard, integrating RESTful APIs and implementing dynamic data visualization components using React.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, so I have all I have used react for developing web applications myself, and it has been limited to general and simple webpages and I''ve used it to basically leverage the ready-made library that we have and the UI elements that are available in react which can be reproduced and reused multiple times.","missing_concepts":["Reusable component development","State management (hooks, Redux)","Performance optimization (code-splitting, memoization)","Collaboration with design or cross-functional teams","Examples of projects involving complex UI or APIs"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer shows some basic knowledge of React, particularly reusing UI elements, which is an important concept. However, the explanation remains very general and lacks the depth expected for a product designer role. There is no mention of critical React topics such as state management, hooks, or performance considerations. The answer also misses discussing collaboration or translating design into functional UI, which ties into the role. Providing concrete examples or specific experiences would have strengthened the response. Overall, the candidate''s understanding appears limited and incomplete relative to the ideal answer.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has some exposure to React but shows only a rudimentary understanding. The answer lacks depth, examples, and key technical aspects expected for this role. Further technical growth and practical experience are needed before meeting the expectations."},{"prompt":"If React isn''t part of your main toolkit, that’s fine. Could you share if you’ve had any involvement in front-end development or collaborating with developers using it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Candidate has hands-on experience using React for developing web applications.","Shows understanding of UI elements and component reuse in React."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Does not mention collaboration with developers or working alongside React teams.","No discussion about design integration, communication, or component-based architecture from a design perspective.","Explanation lacks depth and examples; answer is somewhat vague and incomplete."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe specific front-end development experience or collaboration involving React, even if not their primary tool. This includes integrating UI designs with React development, understanding component-based architecture, or working closely with React developers to ensure design feasibility and consistency. They should highlight how they communicate design requirements in terms familiar to React developers, possibly contributing to UI component reuse and responsive design. For example, they might mention prototyping interfaces that are later implemented in React or reviewing front-end work to maintain design integrity.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, so I have all I have used react for developing web applications myself, and it has been limited to general and simple webpages and I''ve used it to basically leverage the ready-made library that we have and the UI elements that are available in react which can be reproduced and reused multiple times.","missing_concepts":["Collaboration with React developers to ensure design feasibility.","Understanding of React''s component-based architecture relevant to design.","Communication of design in terms familiar to React development.","Prototyping or reviewing React front-end work to maintain design integrity."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates some technical understanding by mentioning the use of React and leveraging reusable UI elements, which is technically correct. However, the answer lacks completeness and depth as it does not address collaboration with developers or any specific design-related involvement in React projects. The response is moderately relevant, but communication clarity is hindered by some vague phrasing and limited elaboration. Overall, although there is proof of familiarity with React development, the candidate misses critical points regarding teamwork, design-developer interactions, and practical application in their product design role. To improve, the candidate should elaborate on how they have worked with React developers or integrated their design work within React projects.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows practical experience with React but does not adequately demonstrate collaboration with developers or how their design work integrates with React front-end development. The answer is somewhat vague and incomplete concerning the product designer role''s expectations involving React. While technically sound, the lack of details on communication and teamwork leads to a fail overall scor"},{"prompt":"Now, what’s the most challenging design problem you’ve solved recently?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Identified payment gateway as the challenging area","Mentioned exploring multiple design options","Referenced A/B testing to validate designs","Focused on improving user flow and intuitiveness"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Lacked specific details about the design solutions and iterations","No mention of technical constraints or integration challenges","Did not highlight balancing usability with business goals","Description was somewhat vague and did not demonstrate stakeholder collaboration","Missing talk about prototyping or responsiveness across devices"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a complex design challenge that required integrating user needs with technical constraints. They would explain the context, such as improving a critical user flow or feature, and detail how they explored multiple design solutions iteratively, including prototyping and user testing to validate choices. They should highlight balancing usability, performance, and business goals, demonstrating problem-solving and stakeholder collaboration skills. For example, redesigning a payment gateway to enhance conversion rates by making the process intuitive, while ensuring seamless integration with backend systems and responsiveness across devices.","candidateAnswer":"The most challenging design problem was basically the payment gateway, which was plugged in into an e-commerce platform. So the entire user flow or the product flow was not very user-friendly and intuitive. So we tried to work around with around four to five different designs where the user searches for the product and is is intuitively pushed forward to make a purchase call and how after doing A-B testing with available designs, we finally narrowed down to two major designs and that has been a success after that.","missing_concepts":["Technical constraints and backend integration","Iteration process with prototyping and user testing","Balancing usability, performance, and business goals","Stakeholder collaboration","Specific outcomes or metrics like conversion rate improvements"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate identified the payment gateway redesign as their most challenging problem and noted the process of testing multiple designs and using A/B testing for validation. This shows an understanding of iterative design and validation with users. However, the answer lacked depth and specificity. The candidate did not explain the nature of the design challenges in detail, nor did they mention technical constraints or how they balanced different priorities such as usability and business goals. There was also no evidence of collaboration with stakeholders or explanation of the final impact metrics. The explanation was somewhat vague and lacked clarity about the problem-solving steps. Overall, the answer shows partial understanding but is too incomplete to pass.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate’s answer was relevant and indicated engagement with the design challenge via multiple concepts and testing, but it lacked enough technical depth, problem-solving details, and completeness to meet expectations for this role. More specifics on constraints, collaboration, and measurable impact are needed."},{"prompt":"What was the key reason you chose the final design over the others?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":7,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Candidate correctly identified conversion rate and repeat customer engagement as key metrics","Mentioned comparative evaluation of multiple designs using empirical data","Recognized importance of consistent product offerings for fair comparison"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-7","weaknesses":["Candidate did not explicitly mention A/B testing or detailed methodology","Explanation of metrics and sample size was somewhat vague and could be clearer","No direct reference to user task efficiency or satisfaction as factors"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":8,"expectedAnswer":"The key reason for choosing the final design was its measurable impact on user engagement and business metrics, specifically a higher conversion rate and increased repeat usage. This decision was based on empirical data from A/B testing, where the selected design outperformed others by enabling users to complete their tasks more efficiently and with greater satisfaction, directly aligning with product goals and improving overall user experience.","candidateAnswer":"So, the metrics that we tracked to finalize the design was the conversion ratio of user landing on the page and making the purchase decision and the sample size was approximately 150 users per design and keeping the product offerings very much same. So, based on the conversion ratio that we got, the one that we finalized, the conversion ratio was very high as well as repeat customers coming back to our platform and spending time also increased relatively for the final design, selected design.","missing_concepts":["Explicit mention of A/B testing methodology","Connection of chosen design to user task completion efficiency and satisfaction","Clear link to alignment with overarching product goals"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a generally good answer indicating that the final design was chosen based on empirical data focusing on conversion rates and repeat customer behavior, which aligns with the ideal reasoning. However, the response lacked explicit mention of A/B testing or how user satisfaction and task efficiency played a role. The explanation around sample size and metrics was somewhat brief and not very detailed, affecting clarity. Overall, the candidate demonstrated good understanding and relevance but could improve by elaborating methodology and connecting to broader product goals.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate showed a solid grasp of data-driven decision-making by focusing on key engagement metrics such as conversion and repeat usage. While lacking some detail on experimentation techniques and user experience factors, the response was relevant and mostly complete. Communication was understandable though it could be more precise and structured."},{"prompt":"tell me your self","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpzi19xw000rlk0kthjq1t8v","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpzirhqm001vlk0kfmypsadr', 'cmpziqbu8001qlk0kdozyipp3', 9, 45, 40, 54, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-04 13:16:40.462', '2026-06-04 13:16:50.488', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hello."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 0, '[{"prompt":"Hello, Niv. My name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today for the HR role. Let’s dive right in. Can you start by telling us about your background and how it maps to this role?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have extensive experience in HR, including recruitment, employee relations, and performance management, gained over several years in corporate environments. Specifically, I have led initiatives to improve talent acquisition processes and implemented employee engagement programs, which align closely with this role''s requirements. My expertise in HR fundamentals, combined with strong problem-solving skills and good judgment, enables me to contribute effectively to organizational goals. Additionally, I have worked cross-functionally with managers and teams to align HR strategies with business objectives, ensuring compliance and fostering a positive workplace culture.","candidateAnswer":"Hello.","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpziqbu8001rlk0kvwcvjar5","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have over 5 years of experience in HR roles, specializing in talent acquisition, employee relations, and performance management. In my previous position, I successfully managed end-to-end recruitment processes, developed employee engagement programs, and collaborated closely with cross-functional teams to align HR strategies with business goals. Additionally, I have a strong foundation in HR fundamentals, including compliance, compensation, and training and development, which equips me to effectively contribute to this role. My background demonstrates a continuous focus on problem-solving and applying HR domain expertise to enhance organizational effectiveness and employee satisfaction.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpzj01jt002wlk0ksest4n6k', 'cmpzit74m0026lk0kemxk4wp1', 18, 69, 59, 100, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-04 13:23:19.385', '2026-06-04 13:24:05.495', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["प्राइब किया है या पिर जो ओरिडी मैं बता रहा हूँ कि नहीं अभी लिगलें उसको देख रही हूँ? ना मैं अभी नियों ट्राइ किया है","تو اس کا کیوں نہیں ہوگا؟ کیا ہوگا اس کے ریسنٹ؟","मैंना अभी ट्राइ किया है... मैंना अभी निव क्रीट किया होगा निव और टेस्ट निव होगा उसने तो मैंना वही टेस्ट़िंग किया और ये रूस... HAN ये नहीं... that is not the point तुमने एइदार करिया हो... वो.. तुमसान नहीं है मेरा पॉंट ये हो रहा है कि तुमने ट्राइ किया वो हुआ से हुआ राइट उसके पहले तुमको दो और एंटर्यूब दिख रहे होगी एक प्रॉड़क डिजाइनर और एक दूसर मेकानिक लिए ज़िए हाँ हाँ"]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 4, '[{"prompt":"Hi Yashu, this is Sana. Thank you for joining today. Let’s dive straight in. Tell me about your background and how it maps to this HR role.","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":1,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Answer is largely irrelevant and unclear","No demonstration of HR knowledge or relevant experience","Does not address the question of background relative to HR role","No mention of HR principles, systems, or problem-solving skills"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should summarize their professional experience relevant to HR functions, highlighting roles where they managed recruitment, employee relations, performance management, or compliance. They should mention specific HR systems or policies they have worked with and demonstrate understanding of core HR principles such as labor law, talent acquisition, and employee engagement. For example, they might say they''ve overseen hiring processes, resolved workplace conflicts, or implemented employee development programs, aligning these experiences to tasks expected in this role. Additionally, they could mention any certifications or training in HR and how their problem-solving and judgment skills supported effective HR management.","candidateAnswer":"प्राइब किया है या पिर जो ओरिडी मैं बता रहा हूँ कि नहीं अभी लिगलें उसको देख रही हूँ? ना मैं अभी नियों ट्राइ किया है","missing_concepts":["Relevant HR experience and roles","Understanding of HR functions and principles","Specific examples of recruitment, employee relations or compliance","Communication of relevant certifications or training","Problem-solving in HR context"],"detailed_feedback":"The answer provided is mostly unintelligible and does not address the question about the candidate''s background or its relevance to the HR role. There is no mention of any HR experience, knowledge of HR systems, or demonstration of understanding core HR principles. The candidate fails to communicate their suitability for the role, making it impossible to assess their technical or problem-solving competencies in HR. Improvement is needed to clearly explain professional experience and how it maps to HR tasks and responsibilities.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate did not provide a coherent or relevant response to the HR background question, showing no evidence of HR knowledge or experience. They did not demonstrate understanding or communication skills necessary for the role."},{"prompt":"Understood. Let’s stay focused on your journey. Could you share how your previous experience, including those interviews or roles, connects to this HR position?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":1,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Answer is mostly fragmented and off-topic","Does not demonstrate connection between past experience and HR role","Lacks any clear explanation or relevant information","Poor communication clarity and coherence"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate will connect their prior experience in HR-related roles such as recruitment, employee relations, or talent management directly to this position by outlining specific responsibilities they''ve managed, like conducting interviews, managing onboarding, or implementing HR policies. They might explain how handling candidate evaluations or resolving employee issues honed their problem-solving and professional judgment skills, which are essential for this role. Additionally, they should highlight their familiarity with HR fundamentals and domain expertise that align with this position''s requirements, demonstrating an understanding of professional standards and HR best practices.","candidateAnswer":"मैंना अभी ट्राइ किया है... मैंना अभी निव क्रीट किया होगा निव और टेस्ट निव होगा उसने तो मैंना वही टेस्ट़िंग किया और ये रूस... HAN ये नहीं... that is not the point तुमने एइदार करिया हो... वो.. तुमसान नहीं है मेरा पॉइंट ये हो रहा है कि तुमने ट्राइ किया वो हुआ से हुआ राइट उसके पहले तुमको दो और एंटर्यूब दिख रहे होगी एक प्रॉड़क डिजाइनर और एक दूसर मेकानिक लिए ज़िए हाँ हाँ","missing_concepts":["Connection of prior HR or related experience to current role","Specific responsibilities or skills relevant to HR","Understanding of HR functions such as recruitment, employee relations, or HR policies","Professional judgment or problem-solving related to HR"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is mostly incoherent and does not address the question of how their previous experience connects to the HR position. There is no evidence of relevant HR knowledge or related experience discussed. The answer lacks clarity, completeness, and relevance, failing to demonstrate any understanding or problem-solving related to the role. Overall, this response is not suitable for assessing the candidate''s fit for the HR position.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate failed to provide a coherent or relevant answer connecting prior experiences to the HR role, indicating insufficient preparation or understanding for this position."},{"prompt":"I understand. But let''s focus on your background and how it relates to this HR role. Could you tell me more about your experience and skills in the HR domain?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":1,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Answer is largely unintelligible and does not address HR experience or skills","No relevant HR domain knowledge demonstrated","Does not communicate any concrete examples or competencies"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"I have several years of experience in HR, covering key responsibilities such as recruitment and selection, employee onboarding, performance management, and employee relations. I have worked closely with hiring managers to define job requirements and developed sourcing strategies to attract qualified candidates. Additionally, I have experience managing HRIS systems for accurate record-keeping and supporting compliance with labor laws and company policies. For example, in my previous role, I led a project to streamline the onboarding process, reducing time-to-productivity by 20%. My skills include strong interpersonal communication, problem-solving in employee conflict resolution, and maintaining professional standards to support organizational culture and objectives, directly aligning with the requirements of this HR role.","candidateAnswer":"वही मैं देखनी हूँका अगर केस में क्या प्रबर मैंतें सबच मिला रहा हूँ","missing_concepts":["HR fundamentals such as recruitment, onboarding, performance management","Experience with HRIS or labor law compliance","Problem solving in employee relations","Professional standards in HR"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response is fragmented and does not provide any meaningful information related to their HR experience or skills. There is no demonstration of understanding or relevant background. The answer lacks clarity and relevance, offering no substance to assess technical or domain knowledge. To succeed, the candidate needs to clearly outline their HR responsibilities, specific skills, and examples of their contributions aligned to HR functions.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide a coherent or relevant answer about their HR background and skills. The response was largely meaningless and did not fulfill the requirements of the question."},{"prompt":"Got it. Let’s be specific: what key HR responsibilities have you handled in your past roles that connect directly to this position?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Answer is irrelevant as it does not address the question.","No HR responsibilities or relevant experience mentioned.","Lacks any demonstration of understanding of HR duties."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"In my previous HR roles, I have managed key responsibilities such as talent acquisition including job posting and coordinating interviews, employee onboarding and orientation, maintaining employee records and ensuring compliance with labor laws, administering benefits and payroll coordination, and developing employee engagement initiatives. Additionally, I have handled conflict resolution and performance management processes, which directly align with the requirements of this position to maintain a productive and compliant workplace environment.","candidateAnswer":"कनसार्ट कौन कया है?","missing_concepts":["Talent acquisition","Employee onboarding","Employee records management","Compliance with labor laws","Benefits administration","Employee engagement","Conflict resolution","Performance management"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is completely irrelevant and does not respond to the question about key HR responsibilities handled in past roles. There is no demonstration of knowledge or experience related to HR functions necessary for this position. The response fails to show any understanding or domain expertise and lacks any technical correctness, completeness, or clarity. Therefore, the candidate does not meet the minimum criteria for this role based on the given answer.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate did not provide any relevant information regarding their HR experience or responsibilities. The answer is not understandable or aligned with the question asked, indicating a lack of preparation or understanding of key HR duties required for the role."},{"prompt":"Hi Yashu, let’s focus. Please tell me about the key HR responsibilities you’ve handled before that connect to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Key HR responsibilities I have managed include recruitment and onboarding, employee relations, performance management, compliance with labor laws, and training coordination. Specifically, I have led full-cycle recruitment to align talent acquisition with business needs, implemented employee engagement initiatives to improve retention, handled policy development ensuring adherence to labor regulations, and supported managers in performance appraisal processes. These experiences directly relate to this role''s focus on effective HR operations and fostering a positive workplace culture.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Understood. Let’s bring it back to your experience in HR. Can you highlight a key challenge you’ve faced in an HR role and how you solved it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Answer is incoherent and does not address the question.","No relevant HR challenge or solution described.","Answer is incomprehensible without any meaningful content."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific HR challenge such as managing high employee turnover, resolving a workplace conflict, or implementing a new HR policy. They should clearly explain the context, their approach to diagnosing the issue, the solution they applied (for example, conducting exit interviews to identify turnover causes, mediating between employees, or rolling out a training program), and the positive outcome or measurable results achieved. This demonstrates problem-solving skills, domain expertise, and effective judgment within HR responsibilities.","candidateAnswer":"आदाधि వాపర్ సేవ్ మర్చి సేవ్ ఇది పోల్స్ రైంగ్ పోల్స్","missing_concepts":["Specific HR challenge description","Problem diagnosis and approach","Solution applied and implementation details","Outcome or measurable results"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response is incoherent and does not provide any relevant information related to a key challenge faced in an HR role or how it was resolved. The answer lacks any description of context, problem-solving approach, or results, making it impossible to assess their understanding or domain expertise. The response appears as random or non-sensical text not related to the question. This requires improvement in both communication and domain knowledge demonstration.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide a meaningful answer to the question. There is no demonstrated understanding of an HR challenge or problem-solving ability. The response is incomprehensible and irrelevant, resulting in a failing evaluation."},{"prompt":"Let’s focus on your direct HR experience. Can you share one significant HR problem you solved in the past?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Answer is largely incomprehensible","No clear description of any HR problem or solution","Lacks relevance to the question","No demonstrated problem-solving or HR knowledge"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe a specific, complex HR challenge they encountered, such as resolving a major employee relations conflict, streamlining a cumbersome recruitment process, or implementing a new compliance policy across multiple departments. They should outline the context of the problem, their systematic approach to analyze and understand the root cause, the steps they took to address it, and the measurable positive outcomes achieved. For example, they might explain how they identified communication breakdowns causing low employee engagement, developed targeted interventions including training and feedback systems, and subsequently improved retention rates by a concrete percentage. Their response should reflect sound problem-solving skills, solid knowledge of HR principles, and the ability to balance organizational needs with employee welfare.","candidateAnswer":"कोई दिर्भाद होगा आपको इसमें एक काम करते हैं? हाँ हाँ एक काम करते हैं जरस जी वो रहने तो उससे स्ट्रींच करते हैं यह एकने बीजे फ़ुंसा है देखो अभी तक हमने अल्मोस दो आफते हैं आपको कोई अपडेटार के लिए काम करना है चाहिए प्राने अपडेटार को काम करना है अगर यह नहीं प्रावारत है आपको कोई अपडेटार के लिए काम करना है आपको कोई अपडेटार के लिए काम करना है आपको कोई अपडेटार के लिए काम करना है","missing_concepts":["Description of a specific HR challenge","Systematic approach to problem analysis and solution","Measurable positive outcomes","Demonstration of HR fundamentals and problem solving"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response is incoherent and does not provide any understandable example of a significant HR problem they solved. This makes it impossible to assess their knowledge, problem-solving skills, or relevance to the role. For a medium difficulty question about direct HR experience, the candidate needs to clearly explain a relevant, specific HR challenge, how they addressed it, and the outcomes achieved. None of these are present.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide a coherent or relevant answer to the question about a significant HR problem they solved. The answer lacks any technical correctness, completeness, or clarity, resulting in a failing evaluation."},{"prompt":"Understood. Let me bring us back to the interview focus. Can you share an example of a complex HR problem you faced and how you solved it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-7","weaknesses":["Answer is completely irrelevant to the question asked","No demonstration of any HR problem solving or experience","The response is unclear and not understandable","No technical correctness or professional insight demonstrated"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific, complex HR challenge such as managing a large-scale organizational restructure, resolving a significant employee conflict, or addressing compliance issues. They should detail how they analyzed the root causes, engaged stakeholders (employees, management, legal), developed a clear action plan aligned with company policies and legal standards, and implemented solutions effectively. The answer should demonstrate sound judgment, strategic problem-solving, and adherence to professional standards. For example, explaining how they identified communication gaps during a merger that caused employee dissatisfaction, instituted transparent communication channels and training programs, and monitored morale improvements over time.","candidateAnswer":"प्रेडिक्टिबिलिटी बहुत खराब है और इसका रूट फॉल्स नहीं पता तो ऐसे तो हम इसी सर्कल में रह जाएंगे ये एक वाद है ऐसे ही चारे टॉपिट से ऐसे सर्कल ही सर्कल चलता है प्रेडिक्टिबिलिटी बहुत खराब है और इसका रूट फॉल्स नहीं पता तो ऐसे तो हम इसी सर्कल में रह जाएंगे","missing_concepts":["Specific example of a complex HR problem","Root cause analysis","Stakeholder engagement","Action plan development and implementation","Demonstration of judgment and problem solving skills"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer does not address the question in any meaningful way. It lacks any relevant content regarding a complex HR problem or how it was approached or solved. The response appears as unrelated text without clear explanation or examples. This shows no evidence of the expected HR knowledge, problem-solving skills, or communication ability required for the role.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide a relevant or meaningful answer to the question about handling a complex HR problem. Their response lacked any demonstration of HR fundamentals, problem-solving insight, or professional communication, resulting in a failing assessment."},{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpzit74m0027lk0km1tt08fd","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have over 5 years of experience in Human Resources, specializing in recruitment, employee relations, and performance management. In previous roles, I successfully implemented HR policies aligned with organizational goals, enhancing employee engagement and retention. I have a solid foundation in HR fundamentals, including compliance, talent acquisition, and conflict resolution, which directly applies to this role. Additionally, I have collaborated cross-functionally with management and legal teams to ensure professional standards and domain compliance. This background equips me to effectively address HR challenges and contribute to the company''s people strategy.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpzjowpu0048lk0k8qlonpe5', 'cmpzjg3rx0037lk0kqk3eqtw9', 25, 65, 56, 100, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-04 13:42:39.522', '2026-06-04 13:43:15.868', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hello. Hello, Sonny.","I recently completed my degree.","from looking at it."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 14, '[{"prompt":"Hello Niv, it''s great to meet you. Let''s dive right in. Can you tell me about your background and how it maps to this HR role?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":3,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Candidate shows some awareness of having project experience and eagerness to grow professionally.","Mentions problem solving and teamwork skills."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["No clear connection to HR domain or related educational background.","Answer is vague and lacks specific details about HR responsibilities or experiences.","Poor communication clarity with incomplete sentences and unclear structure.","Does not demonstrate understanding of HR fundamentals or how experiences map to this HR role."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe their educational background in human resources, business administration, or a related field, highlighting relevant coursework such as labor laws, organizational behavior, or talent management. They would also mention practical experience like internships, HR projects, or roles involving employee engagement, recruitment, or performance management. Additionally, they would explain how these experiences have developed their understanding of HR fundamentals, problem-solving skills, and professional standards, directly aligning with the responsibilities of this HR role.","candidateAnswer":"I recently completed my degree in MCA and from during studies I have developed a strong knowledge in, I also work on projects in such a name of which have my improved problem solving and teamwork skills and eager to start my professional career, apply to my college practical environment and continue learning improving with organization. I have experience in two years I started my career as a first role and as I gradually took more responsibility and eager such as in my most recent role, I work on major where I contribute to, throughout my career I have developed strong skills, I am now looking for opportunity where I further contribute and grow processing.","missing_concepts":["Educational background in HR or related fields.","Relevant coursework such as labor laws, organizational behavior, or talent management.","Practical experience in HR functions like recruitment, employee engagement, or performance management.","Explanation of how background aligns with HR role responsibilities."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response is vague and incomplete. While there is mention of degree completion and some projects, there is no indication that the educational background or experience relates to human resources. The answer lacks specifics on HR domain expertise, relevant skills, or examples that tie directly to the role. Communication is unclear with fragmented sentences and confusing phrasing. Without evidence of HR-related knowledge or experience, the response does not meet expectations for this position.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate does not sufficiently demonstrate an understanding of or background in HR to be considered suitable for this HR role. The answer is too vague, unrelated to key HR skills, and poorly communicated, resulting in a fail."},{"prompt":"Understood. Could you share more about your studies and any experience you''ve gained so far related to HR?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["The candidate confirmed completion of a degree."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Did not specify field of study or relevance to HR.","No mention of coursework, internships, projects, or HR-related experience.","Answer was too brief to demonstrate understanding or practical knowledge.","Lacked demonstration of problem solving or domain expertise."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should detail their academic background in Human Resources or related fields, mentioning specific coursework like labor relations, organizational behavior, or HR management. Additionally, they should describe any practical experience such as internships, projects, or part-time roles involving recruitment, employee engagement, or policy development. Highlighting exposure to HR software tools or involvement in cross-functional teams enhances their profile. For example, participation in a project to redesign onboarding procedures or resolve workplace conflicts demonstrates applied skills relevant to HR functions and aligns with problem solving and professional standards within the domain.","candidateAnswer":"I recently completed my degree.","missing_concepts":["Academic background in HR or related subjects.","Specific HR-related coursework or topics studied.","Internships, projects, or experience involving HR activities.","Use of HR tools or participation in HR teams.","Examples demonstrating applied HR skills or problem-solving."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided an extremely brief answer that only stated having completed a degree. This is insufficient to evaluate their HR knowledge or experience. They did not specify the degree field, relevant courses, or any practical HR exposure. There was no evidence of domain expertise or problem-solving in HR contexts, which are critical for this role. To improve, the candidate should elaborate on their HR-related studies, practical experience, any projects, and demonstrate their understanding of HR fundamentals and professional standards.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate''s answer lacks the necessary detail and depth regarding their HR studies and experience. The response does not address the question adequately, indicating limited preparedness or relevant background. Fails to demonstrate required competencies for the HR role."},{"prompt":"Thanks for sharing that. How would you handle a challenging employee relations issue?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["Emphasizes focusing on solutions instead of problems","Mentions staying organized and productive under pressure"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Does not address employee relations specifics","Lacks mention of listening to parties involved","No discussion of mediation or communication strategies","Fails to mention company policies or involving stakeholders","Missing confidentiality and professionalism aspects"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"Handling a challenging employee relations issue requires first actively listening to all parties involved to understand the root cause objectively. I would then ensure clear, respectful communication to address concerns and mediate a resolution aligned with company policies and fairness standards. If needed, I would collaborate with relevant stakeholders, such as managers and legal advisors, to implement solutions and follow up to monitor progress. Throughout, I maintain confidentiality and professionalism to uphold a positive work environment.","candidateAnswer":"I stay organised in priority tasks and focus on solutions rather than problems. This helps me stay client productive under pressure.","missing_concepts":["Active listening to all parties","Clear and respectful communication","Mediating resolution aligned with company policies","Collaboration with managers or legal advisors","Confidentiality and professionalism management"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer does not address the core aspects of handling challenging employee relations issues. While focusing on prioritizing tasks and being productive are positive traits generally, they are not relevant to the question. The answer misses critical elements such as understanding the root cause via active listening, ensuring respectful communication, mediation, and following company policies. There is no mention of collaborating with stakeholders or confidentiality. The response is vague and off-topic, indicating a poor understanding of HR employee relations challenges.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrated minimal understanding of managing challenging employee relations issues. Their answer lacked relevant HR practices and failed to cover necessary steps for resolution, falling far short of expectations."},{"prompt":"Got it. Can you walk me through a specific example of a tough decision you had to make related to HR?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Does not provide any relevant content","No example or detail pertaining to HR decision making","No demonstration of problem solving or judgment"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a challenging HR decision that required balancing competing interests, such as handling a disciplinary issue, managing layoffs, or resolving a conflict. They should explain the context, the options considered, the factors (legal, ethical, organizational impact) weighed in the decision, and the outcome. For example, deciding how to address a case of misconduct while ensuring fairness and compliance with company policies. The response should illustrate thoughtful problem-solving, good judgment, and adherence to HR professional standards, showing awareness of confidentiality and legal implications.","candidateAnswer":"Und doch ist es schon auch Neugier.","missing_concepts":["Specific HR scenario or example","Explanation of options considered","Factors such as legal, ethical, or organizational impact","Outcome of decision","Demonstration of HR fundamentals and professional standards"],"detailed_feedback":"The answer provided is a phrase in German that translates to ''But still, it is also curiosity,'' which is unrelated and does not address the question. There is no demonstration of understanding, no example given, nor any explanation of thought process or decision-making related to HR. The candidate failed to provide any meaningful content relevant to the question.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate did not answer the question asked. The response was unrelated and contained no relevant information or example of a difficult HR decision. This indicates either a lack of understanding or unwillingness to respond appropriately."},{"prompt":"Think of any situation where you had to resolve a conflict or make a judgment call. Can you recall one?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["Expressed enjoyment of working with teams"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Did not describe any conflict or judgment call scenario","No explanation of steps taken to resolve conflict or make decision","Lacked demonstration of problem-solving skills or HR principles","Answer was vague and off-topic to the question asked"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific workplace conflict or challenging scenario requiring a judgment call, outlining the context clearly. They should explain the steps taken to understand the perspectives involved, how they applied problem-solving skills and HR principles to mediate or decide, and the eventual outcome that balanced fairness with organizational needs. For example, resolving a disagreement between team members by facilitating open communication, assessing policies, and proposing a solution that maintained team cohesion and productivity reflects effective conflict resolution and sound judgment.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, I enjoy working with teams. I believe our collaboration leads to better ideas for the end result. I will be a successfully popped-up team.","missing_concepts":["Specific conflict or judgment call example","Steps to mediate or resolve conflict","Application of HR fundamentals","Outcome balancing fairness and organizational needs"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response did not address the question being asked. Instead of describing a situation involving conflict resolution or a judgment call, the candidate spoke generally about liking to work in teams and collaboration. The answer was too vague, lacked any specific example, and did not demonstrate any problem-solving or HR-related decision-making. Communication was minimal and unclear in relation to the question. Overall, the response fails to show the candidate''s ability to handle conflict or exercise judgment as expected for the HR role.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate failed to provide a relevant example of conflict resolution or judgment call. The answer did not demonstrate core HR competencies or problem-solving abilities. Candidate''s response was vague and off-topic, resulting in a fail for this question."},{"prompt":"Thank you. Let''s shift to this: how do you approach building an effective recruitment strategy?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["Mentions communication and problem-solving skills"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Does not address recruitment strategy at all","No mention of talent needs or alignment with business goals","No discussion of job analysis, sourcing channels, or employer branding","Answer is vague and unrelated to the question","Lacks problem solving or understanding of recruitment concepts"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"Building an effective recruitment strategy begins with understanding the organization''s talent needs aligned with its business goals. I start by conducting a thorough job analysis to define clear role requirements and success profiles, then identify the most appropriate sourcing channels to reach qualified candidates efficiently, ensuring diversity and inclusion principles. I incorporate employer branding to attract top talent and leverage data analytics to track candidate pipeline and recruitment metrics, allowing continuous optimization. Additionally, collaboration with hiring managers and stakeholders throughout the process ensures alignment and improves hiring quality.","candidateAnswer":"My strengths include strong communication skills, problem-solving ability, and adaptability. For example, in the previous work, I handled the beach and proved my result.","missing_concepts":["Understanding organization''s talent needs aligned with business goals","Job analysis and defining role requirements","Sourcing channels and diversity/inclusion","Employer branding to attract top talent","Use of data analytics and recruitment metrics","Collaboration with hiring managers and stakeholders"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer fails to address the question on building an effective recruitment strategy. Instead of discussing recruitment processes or strategies, the response focuses on personal strengths without linking them to recruitment. There is no demonstration of understanding of key recruitment concepts such as job analysis, sourcing channels, employer branding, or data analytics. The answer is vague, not relevant, and lacks technical correctness related to HR recruitment.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate did not provide a relevant or technically correct answer to the question about recruitment strategy. Understanding of core recruitment principles and strategic approach was missing. Candidate failed to demonstrate the expected HR domain expertise or problem-solving ability in this context."},{"prompt":"Understood. How do you measure the success of your HR initiatives?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["Clear and understandable language"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Does not address the measurement of HR initiatives","Lacks technical details or examples related to HR success metrics","Unrelated to the question asked","No demonstration of understanding specific HR concepts"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"The success of HR initiatives is typically measured through a combination of quantitative and qualitative metrics aligned to the initiative''s goals. Key performance indicators may include employee engagement scores, turnover rates, time to fill open positions, training completion rates, and retention rates. Additionally, feedback from surveys and business impact analysis—such as productivity improvements or cost savings—helps assess effectiveness. Regular monitoring and comparison against benchmarks or past performance ensure initiatives drive meaningful organizational improvements.","candidateAnswer":"I bring the right combination of skills, dedication and willingness to learn. I can contribute to your team by and I am committed to delivering high quality work.","missing_concepts":["HR success measurement metrics (e.g., employee engagement, turnover rates)","Use of quantitative and qualitative data","Alignment of metrics to initiative goals","Feedback mechanisms such as surveys","Business impact assessment"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer does not address the question about measuring the success of HR initiatives. It is generic and unrelated, focusing instead on personal qualities and willingness to learn rather than providing any information on relevant HR metrics or approaches. There is no mention of how outcomes are tracked, analyzed, or linked to HR objectives. The response lacks technical content, completeness, and relevance, resulting in a failing evaluation.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate failed to demonstrate knowledge or understanding of how to measure the success of HR initiatives. Answer was irrelevant and did not show familiarity with key HR performance indicators or evaluation methods."},{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpzjg3rx0038lk0ki6o50ql1","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have over 5 years of experience in human resources, including recruitment, employee relations, and HR policy development, which directly aligns with this role''s focus on managing HR fundamentals and ensuring adherence to professional standards. In my previous role, I successfully implemented performance management systems and resolved complex employee relations issues by applying strong problem-solving skills. Additionally, I have worked cross-functionally with legal, payroll, and operations teams to ensure compliance and effective HR service delivery. This background equips me to effectively contribute to your organization''s HR strategy and maintain high standards of professional judgment and domain expertise.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpzk4x9p0059lk0kr9wgccf4', 'cmpzjuoao004mlk0krk2vdvc1', 61, 82, 69, 90, 'Strong performance with structured answers and solid topic understanding.', '2026-06-04 13:55:06.734', '2026-06-04 13:55:50.648', '["Clear communication flow","Good depth in responses"]', '["Add sharper quantified examples","Reduce filler and tighten transitions"]', '["Hej då!","Yes","I am a product designer. I have five years of experience in product design and 3D designing. I have worked with softwares like AutoCAD and also in software design and application development. I have around three years of experience. My clients have been companies like Google, Apple, and Microsoft."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 56, '[{"prompt":"Could you tell me a bit about yourself and your current role?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Candidate mentions relevant experience in product design.","Lists experience with software like AutoCAD, showing some technical skills."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Lacks specifics about current role and responsibilities.","Does not mention key skills expected such as UI design or React.","Mentions 3D designing and big clients without context or relevance to role.","Unclear how 3 years of software design and application development connect to product design role."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"I am a senior product designer with over 7 years of experience focusing on creating user-centric interfaces and seamless product experiences. Currently, I lead design projects that integrate UI design best practices with React-driven front-end development, collaborating closely with engineering and product teams to deliver scalable, accessible solutions. My current role involves overseeing design strategy, mentoring junior designers, and ensuring the product designs align well with both user needs and business goals.","candidateAnswer":"I am a product designer. I have five years of experience in product design and 3D designing. I have worked with softwares like AutoCAD and also in software design and application development. I have around three years of experience. My clients have been companies like Google, Apple, and Microsoft.","missing_concepts":["UI Design focus","Use of React or front-end collaboration","Leadership or mentoring role","Alignment with user needs and business goals","Current role and projects overview"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a general overview of their background indicating experience in product design and 3D designing, as well as mentioning work with large clients. However, the answer lacks clarity about their current role and responsibilities, omits critical skills like UI design and React which are expected, and does not describe how their experience relates to product design leadership or collaboration. The answer is somewhat relevant and clear but incomplete and somewhat vague in addressing the question properly.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows exposure to product and 3D design with notable clients but fails to communicate core competencies, current responsibilities, or key skills expected for the role. More detail on their role, tools, collaboration, and impact is needed to meet the expectations for a senior product designer position."},{"prompt":"What’s your current focus in product design right now?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Mentions key stages like bioframing and MVP preparation","Shows understanding of converting ideas into prototypes and handing over for development","Focus is relevant to product design"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Lacks detailed explanation of user-centric design or research-driven insights","No mention of UI design, user experience balance, or cross-functional collaboration","Explanation is somewhat vague and lacks depth about technologies or tools used","Does not explain how feedback or iteration is integrated"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"My current focus in product design is on creating user-centric interfaces that solve specific business problems by applying research-driven insights. I prioritize crafting high-fidelity prototypes that balance aesthetics and functionality, ensuring seamless user experiences across platforms. Additionally, I work closely with cross-functional teams to translate conceptual ideas into viable Minimum Viable Products (MVPs), iterating designs based on user feedback and business goals. This includes thorough bioframing to align design solutions with stakeholder expectations and technical constraints, and preparing detailed handoffs for development using tools like React.","candidateAnswer":"Currently, my focus is on bioframing and MVP preparation. So basically, when the client comes up with an idea, I am getting to the role of converting the idea into prototype, basically starting from idea design and then bioframing and then going for an MVP design and then handing over the MVP to my team for development of a prototype and further.","missing_concepts":["User-centric interface design","Research-driven insights","High-fidelity prototypes balancing aesthetics and functionality","Cross-functional teamwork and translating ideas into viable MVPs","Iteration based on user feedback and business goals","Use of tools like React for handoff"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a general understanding of their role by mentioning bioframing, MVP preparation, and the process from idea to prototype to development handoff. However, the answer lacks technical depth and completeness expected for the role. Important aspects such as applying research-driven insights, creating user-centric interfaces, balancing aesthetics with functionality, collaborating with cross-functional teams, and iterating based on user feedback are missing. The communication was fairly clear but somewhat vague and generic without showcasing a strong grasp of current product design methodologies or tools. Overall, the answer is partially correct but falls short in completeness and problem-solving understanding.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate demonstrates familiarity with parts of the product design process but does not sufficiently articulate the comprehensive approach expected, including user research, interaction design, and technology collaboration. The answer indicates some understanding but is incomplete and vague, leading to a fail outcome."},{"prompt":"Now let’s dig into your experience with UI design. How do you typically approach creating a user interface from scratch?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Mentioned gathering requirements from users","Referenced user stories and flow mapping","Included use of wireframing and prototyping in Figma"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Did not explicitly mention stakeholder interviews or detailed user research","No reference to creating user personas or mapping user journeys explicitly","No mention of iteration based on user feedback or usability testing","Did not address alignment with branding or accessibility standards","No mention of coordination with developers, especially React developers"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"I start by gathering detailed requirements through stakeholder interviews and user research to understand user needs and goals. Next, I develop user personas and map user journeys to guide the design process. I create wireframes and prototypes using tools like Figma to visualize the interface structure and interactions. Throughout, I iterate based on user feedback and usability testing to ensure the design is intuitive and meets functional requirements. Finally, I align the UI design with branding and accessibility standards before handing off to development, often coordinating closely with React developers to ensure implementation feasibility.","candidateAnswer":"So, first of all, I gather requirements from the users, based on which I prepare user reports, user stories, sorry, and then with the user stories, we map the entire flow of the UI based on that. I do wireframing on Figma, and then we go for the MVP or prototyping.","missing_concepts":["Stakeholder interviews","User personas and user journey mapping","Iterative process with user feedback and usability testing","Branding and accessibility standards","Collaboration with React developers for implementation"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a reasonable and technically sound approach by starting with requirements gathering, forming user stories, mapping UI flows, and using wireframing and prototyping tools like Figma. However, the answer lacks depth in foundational design steps such as stakeholder interviews, persona development, and usability testing feedback loops which are important for a strong UI design process. The candidate also omitted discussing branding, accessibility, and developer collaboration which are critical to delivering a functional and feasible UI. Communication is generally clear though somewhat rushed. Overall, this reflects a good foundation but misses some key best practices and specifics.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has a solid basic understanding of UI design process with practical tools but lacks completeness around research depth, iteration, and developer collaboration. Suitable for roles needing practical UI skills but with room to grow in design process maturity."},{"prompt":"And how do you ensure consistency in your UI design when working with a team?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Emphasizes team collaboration and discussion","Focuses on considering all features and linking them","Mentions testing designs in different scenarios"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Lacks mention of concrete tools or design systems to ensure consistency","Does not reference standardized components, style guides, or design libraries","No mention of cross-functional communication beyond meetings","Absent discussion about component-driven development or developer collaboration","Explanation is somewhat vague and lacks structure"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"Ensuring UI design consistency in a team involves establishing and maintaining a comprehensive design system or style guide that includes standardized components, color palettes, typography, and interaction patterns. I collaborate closely with designers and developers through regular design reviews and use shared tools like Figma or Sketch libraries to enforce these standards. Additionally, integrating a component-driven approach in code (e.g., reusable React components) helps align design and implementation. Documentation and cross-functional communication also play crucial roles in addressing inconsistencies early and ensuring a cohesive user experience across the product.","candidateAnswer":"To ensure consistency, basically what I prefer is to gather the entire team together and discuss the problems that we are solving and taking inputs from each and every team member so that each and every feature is taken care of and is linked with the other feature which is developed by some other person in a similar way to ensure consistency. I also make sure that the design is tested in different situation scenarios and gives results the same way as desired.","missing_concepts":["Design systems or style guides","Use of shared tools like Figma or Sketch libraries","Standardized UI components and interaction patterns","Component-driven development and alignment with developers","Documentation to enforce consistency"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a general understanding that collaboration and discussion within the team help maintain consistency, which is a positive insight. However, the answer is vague and lacks mention of key concrete practices such as establishing a comprehensive design system or style guide, using shared design tools, and implementing reusable components to enforce consistency. There is no mention of collaboration with developers or the integration of design and code, which are critical to ensuring UI consistency. The explanation is somewhat unfocused and does not fully address how consistency is systematically achieved and maintained in a team environment. Testing designs in different scenarios is a useful practice but does not directly address the core question about ensuring consistency across the team. Overall, the answer shows partial understanding but falls short of covering essential industry-standard approaches.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate emphasizes collaboration and discussion as key to consistency but does not provide concrete technical methods such as design systems, shared tools, or developer collaboration. The answer is incomplete and somewhat vague, showing partial but insufficient understanding of established best practices in UI design consistency. Does not meet expectations for the product designer role."},{"prompt":"Let’s move on to your experience with React. How have you used React in your projects?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["The candidate mentioned using React in relevant domains (e-commerce and edtech).","Acknowledged component reuse and use of React toolkits."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Answer is vague and lacks specific technical details about React usage.","No mention of state management, lifecycle methods, performance optimization, or integration techniques.","Limited demonstration of understanding React''s core concepts or problem-solving capabilities."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"I have utilized React extensively to build dynamic, component-driven user interfaces for web applications across domains such as e-commerce and edtech. For example, I designed reusable UI components such as product cards, navigation menus, and forms, leveraging React’s state and lifecycle methods to manage data efficiently and enhance user experience. Additionally, I integrated React with state management libraries like Redux to handle global application state and optimized performance through code-splitting and memoization techniques, ensuring scalable and maintainable front-end architectures.","candidateAnswer":"I have basically used React for reusing elements and using the already available toolkits that are in the React library in my websites that was in the e-commerce and edtech domain.","missing_concepts":["State and lifecycle method usage in React components.","Integration with state management libraries like Redux.","Performance optimization techniques such as code-splitting or memoization.","Details about the types of components built or UI challenges addressed."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer showed a basic awareness of React usage by highlighting reuse and toolkit usage in projects related to e-commerce and edtech. However, the response was quite vague and lacked concrete examples or technical depth to demonstrate a strong understanding. Key React concepts such as state management, lifecycle handling, and performance considerations were not addressed, which are important to evaluate proficiency. The explanation also lacked clarity and completeness necessary to consider the candidate proficient at this intermediate level. The candidate should provide more detailed and concrete examples of their React experience, including specific challenges faced, solutions implemented, and tools or libraries used.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has some familiarity with React, notably in component reuse and project domains, but provides minimal technical detail or illustrative examples. The response does not sufficiently demonstrate a solid understanding of React''s core features or best practices. Overall, the candidate''s knowledge appears superficial and incomplete relative to the role''s expectations."},{"prompt":"Can you give me an example of a specific React component you designed and how it improved the product?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Candidate mentioned using a slideshow feature to showcase products and new launches, which aligns with UI design goals.","Answer is somewhat relevant to the question."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["No clear explanation of the React component design or architecture.","Technical details are vague and incorrect terminology was used (''browser from the react library'').","Lacks description of how the component improved user engagement or business metrics.","No mention of state management, responsiveness, or integration with APIs.","The explanation is incomplete and not well structured."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe a React component they architected or developed that delivered clear user or business value. For example, they might detail creating a reusable, modular carousel or slideshow component that enhanced product discoverability by dynamically highlighting new releases and promotions. They should explain how this component improved user engagement or conversion rates by providing seamless interaction and faster performance. Ideally, they''d mention technical decisions like state management within the component, responsiveness, or integration with backend APIs, illustrating their design and implementation skills in React.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, so I used a slideshow feature for showcasing of multiple products and new product launches on our website. And for that, we used browser from the react library, which helped us to show multiple products on the same screen for the user so that they are updated of new designs and then they can make their choices.","missing_concepts":["Specific React component design details (e.g. reusable, modular aspects).","Technical implementation choices like state management and responsiveness.","Explanation of how the component improved user experience or product metrics.","Correct terminology related to React components."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer touched on the idea of showcasing multiple products using a slideshow feature, which is relevant to product design and UI improvement. However, the technical explanation lacked clarity and correctness; phrases like ''browser from the react library'' reflect misunderstanding or miscommunication. The candidate did not explain how the React component was designed, its architecture, or technical features like state management or API integration. They also failed to describe the impact of the component on user engagement or business goals. Overall, the answer was too vague and incomplete to demonstrate solid understanding or problem-solving skills in React component design.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows awareness of UI features like slideshows for product promotion but lacks clear technical knowledge or detailed explanation of React component design and its impact on the product. More depth and precision needed."},{"prompt":"How do you handle feedback on your design work from developers or stakeholders?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Acknowledges importance of feedback from both developers and stakeholders","Emphasizes collecting and prioritizing feedback","Mentions addressing issues starting with simpler or lower hanging fruits"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Lacks mention of actively listening and understanding underlying concerns","No reference to collaborative discussions or clarifications to explore improvements","Does not address maintaining design goals or technical feasibility","Missing mention of documentation or communication to keep team aligned","Communication is somewhat vague and lacks structured explanation"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"I actively listen to all feedback to understand the underlying concerns or suggestions and evaluate how these align with the design goals and user needs. I engage in open, collaborative discussions with developers and stakeholders to clarify points and explore possible improvements, ensuring technical feasibility and business value. When appropriate, I iterate on the design to incorporate valid feedback while maintaining overall product vision. I document changes and rationale clearly to keep the team aligned and foster trust throughout the process.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, so for all the products and the designs, we take due consideration of the inputs of the feedback that we get from the developers, as well as the other stakeholders, especially the users, we collect the smallest of the inputs that we get smallest of the observations or minute observations on any of the features and we treat that with the utmost importance. At the same time, all the inputs are taken, collected and then evaluated based on its priority and complexity, then we after categorizing it into multiple buckets, we solve start solving the problems one at a time starting from the lowest hanging fruits.","missing_concepts":["Active listening to feedback","Collaborative discussion with stakeholders and developers","Evaluating feedback against design goals and user needs","Iterating design while maintaining product vision","Documenting changes and rationale"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate understands the importance of collecting and prioritizing feedback from developers and stakeholders, which is relevant and partially correct. However, the answer lacks depth in several key areas, such as actively engaging in discussions to clarify and explore feedback, aligning feedback with design goals and technical constraints, and maintaining clear documentation for team alignment. The explanation is somewhat vague and not very structured, which reduces clarity. There is also no mention of how iteration is handled to balance feedback with overall product vision. Overall, the candidate shows some understanding but misses important aspects necessary for a complete and technically strong answer.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates a basic approach to handling design feedback, emphasizing collection and prioritization, but falls short of articulating critical processes such as active listening, collaborative refinement, and documentation. The answer lacks the depth and structure expected from a product designer interacting with developers and stakeholders, resulting in a below passing evaluation."},{"prompt":"tell me your self","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpzjuoao004nlk0kdar1x4h9","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpzk6jle005slk0kibkmw1k5', 'cmpzjs6r4004hlk0ksoy7jmjh', 10, 46, 41, 70, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-04 13:56:22.322', '2026-06-04 13:56:45.334', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Thank you.","But","or a few miles away."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 0, '[{"prompt":"Hello Drashti, my name is Sana, and I''ll be conducting your interview today. Let''s dive in. Can you start by telling us about your background and how it maps to this software developer role?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe their educational background in computer science or a related field and detail relevant software development experience, such as internships, projects, or past roles. They would highlight proficiency in programming languages, understanding of software development fundamentals, and experience working with development tools or methodologies. They might mention specific technologies or frameworks they have worked with that align with the job requirements, demonstrating problem-solving skills and professional standards. Additionally, they would connect their communication skills and ability to collaborate cross-functionally to the role''s expectations.","candidateAnswer":"But","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"All right, no problem. Let''s go step by step. Tell me a bit about your education and any relevant work experience you have in software development.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have a bachelor''s degree in Computer Science, where I gained a solid foundation in algorithms, data structures, and software engineering principles. Professionally, I worked for three years at XYZ Corp developing web applications using Java and Angular, where I contributed to designing scalable features and improving system performance. Additionally, I have experience with Agile methodologies and collaborating closely with cross-functional teams to deliver high-quality software products.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"That''s fine, take a moment if you need. Let''s try this: what got you interested in software development in the first place?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe a genuine and specific motivation for choosing software development, such as an early fascination with technology, enjoyment of problem-solving, or a pivotal experience with coding. They would connect this interest to their academic background, personal projects, or professional experiences that reinforced and deepened their passion for building software solutions. For example, they might mention how developing a small app or participating in a coding competition sparked their enthusiasm and led them to pursue a career in software development. This explanation should reflect thoughtful career choice aligned with continuous learning and domain expertise.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Hello Drashti, my name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today for the software developer role. Let’s get started. Tell me about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["No relevant technical information provided","Answer is unrelated and incomplete","No demonstration of understanding or problem solving","No communication clarity"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have a degree in computer science and have worked on several software development projects using languages such as Java, Python, and JavaScript. In my recent role, I designed and implemented features in a web application, collaborating closely with cross-functional teams to meet client requirements and maintain code quality. This experience has strengthened my problem-solving skills and knowledge of software development lifecycles, aligning well with the fundamentals and professional standards expected in this software developer role.","candidateAnswer":"or a few miles away.","missing_concepts":["Candidate''s educational background and experience","Relevant programming languages and technologies","Specific software development projects and collaboration experience","Problem solving skills and software development lifecycle knowledge"],"detailed_feedback":"The answer given does not relate to the question asked and does not provide any information about the candidate''s background or how it maps to the software developer role. The response is incomplete, lacks any technical correctness, relevancy, or problem-solving content, and is not communicated clearly or professionally. It is necessary to provide concrete examples of experience, skills, and understanding relevant to the role to demonstrate suitability for the position.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide any relevant or meaningful response regarding their background or suitability for the software developer role. No technical or professional information was shared, reflecting a lack of preparation or understanding of the question. The interview cannot proceed positively based on this response."},{"prompt":"It''s all right. Let''s start simple. Tell me a little about your education or any projects you''ve worked on recently.","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Answer is completely irrelevant to the question asked.","No demonstration of technical knowledge or project experience.","No clear communication or explanation present."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have a degree in Computer Science where I gained a solid foundation in data structures, algorithms, and software engineering principles. Recently, I worked on a full-stack web application project where I developed features using React on the frontend and Node.js with Express on the backend, implementing RESTful APIs and database integration with MongoDB. This project helped me hone my problem-solving skills, version control with Git, and collaborative development in an Agile environment.","candidateAnswer":"तो तो लिए प्लोग से पेख कर देगा भाईया देट के लिए प्लोग लोगे","missing_concepts":["Mention of education background in software development.","Discussion of recent projects and technologies used.","Explanation of skills gained related to problem solving and teamwork."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer does not address the question in any meaningful way. It lacks relevance, technical content, and clarity. There is no information about education or project experience, which were explicitly asked. This answer does not allow any assessment of the candidate''s technical or problem-solving abilities.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate failed to provide any relevant or understandable information about their education or projects. No evaluation on technical skills or experience is possible from this response."},{"prompt":"Hello Drashti, this is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today. Let’s dive right in. \\n\\nCould you start by telling me about your background and how it maps to the software developer role?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would summarize their formal education in computer science or related fields, highlighting relevant coursework such as algorithms, data structures, and software engineering principles. They would describe practical experience including internships, previous developer roles, or personal projects where they designed, implemented, and tested software solutions. The candidate should mention proficiency with programming languages, version control, and agile development methodologies. They would also emphasize problem-solving skills and experience collaborating cross-functionally with teams like QA and product management. Finally, they should explicitly connect how these experiences and skills prepare them to effectively fulfill the responsibilities of the software developer role at this company.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpzjs6r5004ilk0kmfjlbgpk","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have a solid foundation in software development with a degree in Computer Science and over X years of experience building scalable applications using languages such as Java, Python, and JavaScript. My background includes work on end-to-end software projects involving requirement analysis, design, coding, testing, and deployment. I have experience collaborating with cross-functional teams including QA, product management, and UX design, which aligns with this role''s emphasis on communication and team coordination. Additionally, I am well-versed in professional standards like code reviews, agile methodologies, and version control, ensuring quality and maintainability in my work. Examples include leading a recent project where I designed and implemented microservices architecture to improve system scalability and performance.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpzkn5dc006wlk0knjlkrd1u', 'cmpzkc0ae0068lk0kakupqi63', 52, 80, 68, 94, 'Strong performance with structured answers and solid topic understanding.', '2026-06-04 14:09:17.04', '2026-06-04 14:10:05.917', '["Clear communication flow","Good depth in responses"]', '["Add sharper quantified examples","Reduce filler and tighten transitions"]', '["Hello.","I am a product designer. I have five years of experience in 3D design and 2D UI design. I have worked for web development companies and also for additive manufacturing. So I have used a lot of 3D software and 2D software as well as creative designing software. And prototyping and application development platforms.","Thank you."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 45, '[{"prompt":"Hello Shubham, this is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today. Let’s start off—tell me about yourself.","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":8,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Clear mention of 5 years of experience","Experience in both 3D and 2D design","Listed relevant design software and prototyping tools"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Did not explicitly mention UI design expertise relevant to product design","No mention of React or front-end development skills","Lacked demonstration of leadership, senior-level responsibilities or collaboration","No connection made to how past experience fits the senior developer/product designer role"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should concisely summarize their professional background emphasizing relevant experience in product design and development. They should highlight their expertise in UI design and React, mention years of experience including any senior-level responsibilities, and illustrate how their skills and past projects make them a good fit for a senior developer role. For example, they might note their progression into leadership or collaborative roles involving cross-functional teams, and explain their passion for creating intuitive, scalable product interfaces.","candidateAnswer":"I am a product designer. I have five years of experience in 3D design and 2D UI design. I have worked for web development companies and also for additive manufacturing. So I have used a lot of 3D software and 2D software as well as creative designing software. And prototyping and application development platforms.","missing_concepts":["UI Design focus","React skills","Senior-level responsibilities or leadership","Collaboration in cross-functional teams","Passion and motivation relevant to product design"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a clear and technically correct overview of their background in 3D and 2D design with 5 years experience, which is relevant to product design. However, the answer lacks key elements expected for the role such as explicit mention of UI design and React skills. Additionally, the candidate did not contextualize their experience to show why they are a strong fit for a senior developer or product designer role. The answer is understandable and mostly relevant but incomplete and somewhat generic without conveying leadership, collaboration, or specific passions. Improving the answer by aligning experience with required technologies and roles would strengthen it considerably.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has solid design experience but misses key role-relevant skills and depth in their introduction. More emphasis on UI design, React knowledge, and leadership or teamwork would be needed to consider them for senior product designer roles."},{"prompt":"Now, can you tell me about your most recent role and what your primary responsibilities were?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"In my most recent role as a senior developer, I was responsible for leading the design and development of scalable web applications using React. My primary responsibilities included architecting UI components, ensuring code quality through peer reviews, collaborating closely with product designers to implement intuitive user interfaces, and mentoring junior developers. I also managed the integration of new features end-to-end from ideation through deployment, while coordinating with cross-functional teams to align development priorities with business goals.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"What kind of projects have you worked on recently, and what was your specific role?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Relevant project domain (edtech platform)","Clear description of project purpose (platform for hobby art and craft enthusiasts)","Mentioned marketplace functionality which adds value"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Did not specify own role or specific responsibilities","No mention of technologies, design methods, or tools used","No evidence of problem solving or leadership","Lacked details about contributions or outcomes","Technical aspects are vague or missing"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":4,"expectedAnswer":"I have recently worked on several projects, including developing scalable web applications and internal tools, primarily using React and related technologies. In each project, my role involved leading the front-end development, designing and implementing user interfaces, ensuring responsive design, and collaborating closely with UX designers and backend engineers to deliver cohesive product features. For example, in my latest project, I spearheaded the migration of a legacy codebase to React, improving performance by 30%, and mentored junior developers on component-based architecture. I also participated actively in code reviews and contributed to design discussions to align the UI implementation with product goals.","candidateAnswer":"Recently, I worked on a product in the edtech domain where we were working on making a website which was a platform for hobby art and craft enthusiasts to come together, show their skills, show what they have made, as well as we incorporated a marketplace for people to make purchases of kits and art supplies to make new art and hobby objects.","missing_concepts":["Specific role and individual contributions","Use of technologies (e.g., UI design tools, React)","Details on design decisions or challenges solved","Collaboration or teamwork aspects"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate described the project domain and general purpose well, showing relevance. However, the answer lacked any detail about their personal role or specific contributions, which is crucial for evaluating their fit. There was no mention of technologies, design processes, or problem-solving examples. The answer is somewhat clear but incomplete and does not demonstrate sufficient technical understanding or depth expected from a product designer. To improve, the candidate should highlight their direct responsibilities, technologies used, and how they addressed project challenges.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate provided a contextual overview of a recent project but failed to communicate their specific role and responsibilities. The lack of technical and design details makes it difficult to assess their skills properly. The response is relevant to the question but incomplete and does not meet the expected standard for a medium difficulty question for a product designer."},{"prompt":"And what was your primary contribution to that project''s design and development?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Shows some understanding of user experience and user flow design","Mentions defining user stories which indicates involvement in the early design or planning stages"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["No mention of specific design deliverables like wireframes or prototypes","No indication of collaboration with developers or use of specific technologies like React","Lacks details on ensuring design consistency or addressing responsiveness","Does not mention integration of business goals or third-party APIs"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"My primary contribution was leading the end-to-end design process, including creating detailed user flows, wireframes, and prototypes to enhance user experience. I collaborated closely with developers to implement UI components primarily using React, ensuring design consistency and responsiveness across the platform. Additionally, I defined user stories that aligned with business goals and worked with cross-functional teams to integrate third-party APIs to support key functionalities like payments.","candidateAnswer":"In that development, I was looking after the user experience and the user flow. I used to define the user stories and how the components on the platform should look like for attracting users.","missing_concepts":["End-to-end design process including wireframes and prototypes","Collaboration with developers to implement UI components using React","Design consistency and responsiveness across the platform","Defining user stories aligned with business goals","Working with cross-functional teams and API integrations"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a somewhat relevant answer by stating involvement in user experience, user flow, and defining user stories. However, the response lacked technical depth and specificity, especially concerning the leading of the end-to-end design process, creating concrete design artifacts like wireframes and prototypes, and collaboration with developers using specific technologies such as React. Also missing was mention of aligning design with business goals and coordinating with cross-functional teams for API integration. Overall, the answer is partially correct but incomplete and vague in critical areas required for this role.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates a basic understanding of design contributions, emphasizing user experience and user stories. However, they fall short in elaborating on key technical and collaborative aspects of product design and development expected for a product designer role. Without more comprehensive details, the answer does not meet the standards for passing."},{"prompt":"How did you approach the UI design for that platform, and what tools did you use?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Mentioned use of Figma for wireframing which aligns with common UI design tools","Referenced use of React and frontend technologies like HTML, CSS, and JavaScript","Included mention of incorporating APIs for external services"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["No mention of collaborating with stakeholders or defining user personas","Lacks explanation of iterative design, prototyping, or user testing processes","Does not discuss how design decisions align with usability, accessibility, or product goals","Limited detail on how React and other tools were leveraged in the design workflow"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"I began by collaborating with stakeholders to gather detailed requirements and define user personas to guide the design process. I created wireframes and interactive prototypes using Figma to visualize user flows and validate concepts early. For development, I leveraged React for building reusable UI components, complemented by HTML, CSS (including preprocessors like SASS), and JavaScript to implement responsive and accessible designs. This workflow allowed iterative user testing and agile refinement to ensure the UI was intuitive, performant, and aligned with product goals.","candidateAnswer":"For the UI design, wireframing was primarily done on Figma, and we had the stack of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. We also used a bit of React for specific components, and then there were APIs to call external services for payment, for example.","missing_concepts":["Stakeholder collaboration and requirements gathering","User personas and user flow validation","Iterative prototyping and agile refinement","Responsive and accessible design considerations"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate correctly identified key tools such as Figma for wireframing and React with standard web technologies for implementation, which is technically accurate and relevant. However, the response lacks depth about the design approach, including collaboration with stakeholders, user personas, iterative prototyping, and how the tools were used to ensure usability and product alignment. The mention of APIs, while relevant to the product, is tangential to the core question about UI design approach. Overall, the answer shows basic understanding but misses significant parts of the ideal process and does not sufficiently demonstrate problem-solving or a holistic design methodology.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has a reasonable grasp of UI design tools and technology stack but provides an incomplete picture of the design process and methodologies. More detail and structure would be needed to pass."},{"prompt":"Can you tell me more about your experience with React components in that project?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Mentioned use and reuse of existing React components","Noted use of styling features to ease the job"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["No mention of creating reusable components from scratch or design considerations","No explanation of state management or React hooks","No mention of CSS-in-JS or design system adherence","Lacked detail about collaboration or problem solving","Answer is vague and does not demonstrate deep understanding"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":4,"expectedAnswer":"In the project, I extensively designed and developed reusable React components from scratch, focusing on modularity and maintainability. I implemented state management using React hooks like useState and useEffect to manage component lifecycle and data binding efficiently. Additionally, I ensured components were styled as per the design system using CSS-in-JS solutions like styled-components or Emotion, maintaining consistency across the UI. I also integrated third-party React libraries selectively when appropriate but customized core UI elements to meet unique user experience requirements, collaborating closely with both design and backend teams to align functionality with product goals.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, so we used libraries of the React to use and reuse components that are already available like Rousel, then Minubar and the features that they have for styling so that our job becomes easier.","missing_concepts":["Reusable component design and development","State management using React hooks like useState and useEffect","Styling approaches aligned with design systems (e.g., CSS-in-JS)","Integration and customization beyond using third-party libraries","Collaboration with design and backend teams"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer indicates some familiarity with using existing React component libraries and their styling features which is relevant, but it lacks depth and specificity. There is no discussion of core concepts such as designing reusable components from scratch, managing state effectively using React hooks, or ensuring styling consistency with a design system. The answer is vague and does not communicate problem-solving skills or collaboration aspects important for the role. Overall, the response does not meet the expected level of technical understanding for the question.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate demonstrated minimal understanding of React component usage mainly through third-party libraries, but failed to articulate key concepts such as reusable component creation, state management, styling consistency, and teamwork. The answer was incomplete, vague, and did not reflect adequate technical proficiency for the role."},{"prompt":"How did you handle any custom UI requirements that weren''t covered by those libraries?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["Mentions custom requirements"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["No indication of how custom UI was implemented technically","Lacks detail on design, reusability, or collaboration","Answer is vague and does not demonstrate understanding of UI construction","Does not mention tools, frameworks, or key considerations such as modularity or accessibility"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"For custom UI requirements not covered by existing libraries, I first analyzed the design specifications to understand the unique interactions and visuals needed. Then, I built reusable React components from scratch, ensuring they aligned with the overall design system for consistency. I prioritized modularity and accessibility, adding props for customization while maintaining performance optimization. Additionally, I collaborated closely with UX designers to validate that these custom components met user expectations and integrated seamlessly with standard components.","candidateAnswer":"For the custom requirements, we basically hard-coded all the data and then we worked our way through it.","missing_concepts":["Analyzing design specifications","Building reusable React components from scratch","Aligning with design systems","Modularity and accessibility considerations","Collaboration with UX designers","Performance optimization"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is too vague and lacks any technical detail or insight into how custom UI requirements were handled. Simply stating ''hard-coded all the data'' does not demonstrate understanding or approach to building custom UI components, nor does it address design consistency, accessibility, or collaboration, which are critical aspects. The answer does not align with the question and provides no evidence of problem-solving or relevant skills.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide a meaningful or technically relevant answer to the question about handling custom UI elements beyond libraries. The response was minimal, vague, and did not illustrate any understanding or process of building custom components. Overall, this answer does not meet the expectations for the role."},{"prompt":"And how did you ensure that the overall user experience remained consistent across standard and custom components?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":4,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Mentions testing with a large user sample","Considers multiple use cases and test scenarios"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-7","weaknesses":["Does not address design system or shared style guidelines","No mention of collaboration with teams or documentation","No reference to aligning custom and standard components in design or interaction","Focuses mainly on user testing without explaining consistency measures","Lacks technical or design details specific to UI or React"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"To ensure consistency between standard and custom components, I established and followed a unified design system that includes shared styling tokens, typography, spacing, and interaction patterns. I collaborated closely with both design and development teams to document and enforce component usage guidelines, leveraging tools like Storybook for visual regression testing. For custom components, I aligned their behavior and appearance with standard components through iterative prototyping and user feedback to maintain the same usability and accessibility standards across all UI elements.","candidateAnswer":"So we had multiple use cases to test for and we took a huge sample, a very large sample space of around 100 to 150 users and the test conditions were also more than 20-25 test cases to test them in different scenarios and then only if the results were consistent and falling within the limits, we used to go ahead.","missing_concepts":["Unified design system and styling tokens","Component usage guidelines and documentation","Collaboration between design and development teams","Use of tools like Storybook for visual testing","Iterative prototyping and user feedback integration","Ensuring usability and accessibility standards"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer focuses primarily on user testing with a large sample and multiple scenarios, which is valuable but addresses only a small portion of the process. The question seeks details about ensuring consistency across standard and custom components, which typically involves establishing a design system, style guides, collaboration, and tooling support. The answer lacks discussion of these key practices and does not show understanding of design or development collaboration or component alignment methods. The explanation is somewhat clear but too vague and incomplete to demonstrate technical depth or problem-solving in this context. Greater emphasis on design system principles and practical steps would be needed for a passing score.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate demonstrates awareness of thorough user testing but fails to connect it to maintaining consistency between standard and custom UI components. Lacks key technical insights on design systems and component management. Does not sufficiently address the question''s intent."},{"prompt":"One final question—what’s the most challenging UI problem you’ve solved, and how did you solve it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["The candidate identifies a real UI problem related to payment gateway and user drop-offs.","The answer shows awareness of redesigning the flow to improve user experience.","Answer is relevant to the question asked."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-8","weaknesses":["Lacks specific technical details on how the UI was improved.","No mention of methods used to analyze user behavior or address friction points.","No reference to key techniques like progressive disclosure, validation, or testing.","The solution description is vague and lacks measurable outcomes or results."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"The most challenging UI problem involved improving user conversion in a complex payment gateway flow that initially led to high drop-off rates. I analyzed user behavior to identify friction points, then redesigned the interface focusing on intuitive navigation and clear feedback to reduce cognitive load. I also implemented progressive disclosure to simplify form fields and incorporated real-time validation to prevent errors before submission. This iterative design process, combined with usability testing and accessibility improvements, significantly enhanced user trust and increased completed transactions.","candidateAnswer":"The most challenging UI problem was about the payment gateway. So the gateway was not intuitive for clients to make purchases, and we used to get a lot of dropouts in the last stages. Also, the conversion of users from browsing to actually making a purchase was very less. So what we did is we reused and redesigned the entire portal, especially the view to buy flow, and then made it so intuitive that the user is drawn to the portal''s experience. And the platform itself drives the user to make a buying option. And then when it lands on the payments gateway, it is so well designed that there are no second thoughts of making the purchase.","missing_concepts":["User behavior analysis to identify friction points","Specific UI techniques such as progressive disclosure and real-time validation","Iterative design process and usability testing","Accessibility improvements","Use of React or technical implementation details"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate correctly identifies a challenging UI problem with the payment gateway and recognizes the issue of user drop-offs and low conversions. However, the answer is vague and lacks depth. There is no explanation of how the problem was analyzed or the specific design strategies used to improve the experience. Key elements like user research, progressive disclosure, real-time validation, and iterative usability testing are missing. The candidate also does not mention any technical framework or tools such as React, which is expected for this role. While the overall direction of the solution is conceptually correct, the explanation is incomplete and does not demonstrate a strong problem-solving approach or technical rigor.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows an understanding of the challenge involved in improving a payment gateway UI but provides a superficial answer lacking concrete details and technical depth. The response is relevant but too vague and incomplete to clearly demonstrate proficiency in UI design or problem-solving skills required for the role. More specificity in approach and methods, as well as examples of impleme"},{"prompt":"tell me your self","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpzkc0ae0069lk0k73gjveoa","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmpzljy1s007alk0k83ez5ruh', 'cmpzl6l7g0075lk0kxmyt7aun', 9, 47, 41, 54, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-04 14:34:47.2', '2026-06-04 14:35:03.307', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["एक लाइक्वेट जेल मॉंस्टराइजर यूज़ कर रही हूँ जैसे ये आज मुझे भी जननी का सब से स्वारा दूद पीआ नमस्दे मेरा बाप चलो आज मुंस्टराइजर हेलो"]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 0, '[{"prompt":"Hi Ankit, this is Sana. I''ll be conducting your interview today for the Business Analytics role. Let''s get started. Tell me about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Answer is completely irrelevant and nonsensical in context of the question.","No demonstration of understanding of business analytics or related skills.","No clear communication or explanation present."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have a strong background in business analytics with a focus on data-driven decision-making and problem solving. I hold a degree in a quantitative discipline and have worked on projects involving data collection, cleaning, analysis, and visualization to uncover insights that drive business performance. For example, in my previous role, I developed dashboards and reports that helped stakeholders identify key customer segments and optimize marketing spend, resulting in a measurable increase in ROI. My experience spans statistical analysis, SQL querying, and working cross-functionally with product and marketing teams to translate data insights into actionable business strategies. This experience directly aligns with this role’s focus on leveraging analytics fundamentals to solve business problems and provide domain expertise to support strategic initiatives.","candidateAnswer":"एक लाइक्वेट जेल मॉंस्टराइजर यूज़ कर रही हूँ जैसे ये आज मुझे भी जननी का सब से स्वारा दूद पीआ नमस्दे मेरा बाप चलो आज मुंस्टराइजर हेलो","missing_concepts":["Business analytics fundamentals","Problem solving and judgment in analytics","Domain expertise relevant to role","Data collection, cleaning, analysis, visualization","Examples of past experience related to the role"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response does not address the question asked and is unrelated to business analytics or the candidate''s background. There is no technical content, no demonstration of relevant skills or experience, and no clear communication. This answer fails to provide any insight into the candidate''s suitability for the Business Analytics role.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide any relevant or meaningful answer regarding their background or how it maps to the business analytics role. The response was unintelligible and did not demonstrate any understanding of or experience in the required domain, leading to an immediate fail."},{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmpzl6l7g0076lk0kj34key5y","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have a solid background in business analytics, with 5 years of experience working in data-driven environments where I applied statistical analysis, data visualization, and business intelligence tools to inform strategic decisions. My expertise includes proficiency in SQL, Excel, and Python for data manipulation and predictive modeling, alongside domain knowledge in finance and marketing analytics. For example, I led a project analyzing customer segmentation that increased campaign ROI by 15%. Additionally, I have worked cross-functionally with product, sales, and finance teams to align analytics insights with business objectives, making my experience well suited to this role''s requirements in problem solving and domain expertise in business analytics.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq6i88om000loz0128ol45lp', 'cmq6hwmpx0003oz01kmuz4va4', 57, 74, 63, 78, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-09 10:36:05.494', '2026-06-09 10:37:03.466', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hello.","Hello. Yes. I''m my last job as a product design lead. So basically, I have worked for a few companies in the education and tech sector and in the software development sector, primarily working on user experience and UI development. I am aware of UI tools as well as some exposure to backend development. Then I have a total of five years of experience in product design and software development. Yes.","Yes, so I have designed web platforms for e-commerce companies where I used to develop the mock-ups and compiler frames for different web pages and then taking it forward for actual coding on HTML, CSS and JavaScript. So that is what my experience is about it."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 54, '[{"prompt":"Could you start by telling me a bit about yourself?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate will briefly summarize their background highlighting relevant experience as a product designer, ideally with about 5+ years in the field. They should emphasize experience leading design efforts in UI with a focus on user-centered design principles and mention notable industries or products they''ve worked on, such as education, tech, or software development. They might also note cross-functional collaboration with developers and product teams, familiarity with design tools, and an understanding of frontend development technologies like React to show technical depth. The answer should convey their passion for creating intuitive, impactful user experiences and how their skills align with the senior product designer role.","candidateAnswer":"Hello.","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Could you walk me through some of your experience with UI design?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Has relevant experience in UI design and product design leadership.","Mentions familiarity with UI tools and coding in HTML, CSS and JavaScript.","Worked on web platforms for education, tech, and e-commerce sectors."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Answer is vague and somewhat disorganized.","Lacks specifics on UI design tools like Figma or Sketch.","No mention of wireframes or prototypes.","No reference to collaboration with other teams or translating design to React components.","Terminology like ''compiler frames'' is unclear or incorrect."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"I have over five years of experience in UI design, primarily focused on creating user-centric interfaces for web platforms in e-commerce and educational tech sectors. My work includes developing wireframes, high-fidelity mockups, and interactive prototypes using tools like Figma and Sketch. I collaborate closely with product managers and developers to ensure designs align with business goals and technical constraints. Additionally, I have hands-on experience translating designs into responsive components using React, ensuring usability and performance. This holistic approach allows me to deliver seamless and engaging user experiences that drive customer satisfaction and retention.","candidateAnswer":"Hello. Yes. I''m my last job as a product design lead. So basically, I have worked for a few companies in the education and tech sector and in the software development sector, primarily working on user experience and UI development. I am aware of UI tools as well as some exposure to backend development. Then I have a total of five years of experience in product design and software development. Yes. Yes, so I have designed web platforms for e-commerce companies where I used to develop the mock-ups and compiler frames for different web pages and then taking it forward for actual coding on HTML, CSS and JavaScript. So that is what my experience is about it.","missing_concepts":["Use of standard UI design tools (e.g., Figma, Sketch).","Creating wireframes and high-fidelity mockups.","Prototyping and interactive design.","Collaboration with product managers and developers.","Experience with React for responsive component development."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate has basic relevant experience and demonstrates some technical knowledge of UI design and front-end coding. However, the response lacks depth, clarity, and completeness on critical UI design processes and tools. There is no clear explanation of the design workflow, collaboration, or specific tools used as expected in the role. The mention of ''compiler frames'' is unclear. The answer could be greatly improved by providing specific examples of UI tools used, describing design deliverables like wireframes or prototypes, and illustrating collaboration with cross-functional teams and React experience. Overall, it shows partial understanding but is incomplete and lacks professional clarity.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows some relevant experience and technical familiarity but provides a vague and incomplete answer without demonstrating a solid grasp of modern UI design practices and tools expected for this product designer role."},{"prompt":"Now, can you tell me about your experience using React in your projects?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Recognizes the value of reusability in React components","Mentions usage of component libraries and templates"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Lacks detail on React-specific concepts such as lifecycle methods, hooks, or state management","Does not provide concrete examples of building or optimizing React components","No mention of technical aspects like handling API calls, routing, or testing","Explanation is vague and lacks depth regarding hands-on experience with React"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate will describe their hands-on experience building scalable and maintainable UI components using React, highlighting understanding of component lifecycle, state management (e.g., using hooks or Redux), and integration with design systems or styling solutions like CSS-in-JS. They should provide concrete examples such as developing reusable components, optimizing performance, or collaborating with designers to implement pixel-perfect interfaces. Additionally, they might mention working with React Router for navigation, handling API calls efficiently within React, and using testing libraries like Jest or React Testing Library to ensure component reliability.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, so I have used React for reusability and the ready-made components that are available, libraries that are there in the React toolkit. So I used to use the multiple variants of, you know, Minibar or the carousels and templates that can be reused for different web pages.","missing_concepts":["Component lifecycle and hooks","State management (e.g., Redux or React hooks)","Integration with design systems or CSS-in-JS","Performance optimization","React Router and navigation","Handling API calls inside React components","Testing React components with libraries like Jest or React Testing Library"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer shows a basic awareness of the reusability aspect of React and uses of component libraries or templates. However, the explanation is quite vague and lacks technical depth or specificity that would demonstrate a strong, hands-on understanding of React. Key React concepts such as lifecycle methods, use of hooks for state management, performance optimization, or collaboration aspects are missing. The candidate did not mention any concrete personal examples or experience working with APIs, routing, or testing within React projects. Overall, the answer is only partially relevant and incomplete, resulting in a relatively low score.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows some familiarity with React by mentioning reusable components and libraries but falls short of demonstrating a solid or comprehensive understanding. The response lacks technical details and practical examples that would be expected for this role and question. They should deepen their hands-on experience with React fundamentals, state management, and testing to be considered pro"},{"prompt":"How do you typically approach integrating those React components with your UI designs?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":5,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":4,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Candidate mentions considering compatibility between source code and dependencies.","Candidate indicates testing the implementation after integration."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Does not mention collaboration with designers or alignment with UI design specifications.","No discussion of breaking down UI designs into reusable components.","No mention of style consistency, responsiveness, or accessibility.","Lacks explanation of verifying visual fidelity or iterative improvement.","Answer is vague and lacks specifics about React or UI integration processes."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":4,"expectedAnswer":"I start by collaborating closely with designers to ensure the React components align with the intended UI specifications and user experience. I break down designs into modular, reusable components, matching the React component structure to design elements. I verify style consistency using CSS-in-JS or styled components, ensuring responsive and accessible UI. Then, I integrate the components into the application, testing for visual fidelity and functionality, iterating as needed for seamless integration.","candidateAnswer":"So first I find the best compatibility with my source code and all the dependencies that are required to integrate the React components. So with those things in place, I then do a test run with the implementation and if it works well I move in the line.","missing_concepts":["Collaboration with designers for UI alignment","Mapping design elements to React components","Ensuring style consistency and responsive design","Use of CSS-in-JS or styled components","Testing for visual fidelity and accessibility","Iterative integration process"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer shows some awareness of technical integration aspects, such as dependency compatibility and testing implementations, which is relevant. However, the response lacks key elements crucial for a product designer working with React components and UI designs, such as collaboration with designers, modularizing components based on design, ensuring style and accessibility, and iterative improvements. The answer is also vague and underdeveloped, indicating partial understanding but missing core concepts expected at this level.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate demonstrates minimal understanding of integrating React components with UI design. While testing implementation and handling dependencies are mentioned, critical aspects like design collaboration, component modularization, and style consistency are missing. Overall, the response is incomplete and lacks depth necessary for the role."},{"prompt":"What’s one challenge you''ve faced when integrating React with your designs, and how did you solve it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Mentions a real issue with component compatibility.","Describes creating a standardized chart as a solution to improve development workflow."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Answer lacks detail on specific UI challenges related to design integration and dynamic states.","Does not discuss collaboration with designers or use of tools like Storybook.","Explanation is vague and somewhat unclear in structure and language.","Missing discussion on design systems or component libraries to ensure consistency."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"A common challenge is ensuring that React components align perfectly with the intended UI designs, especially when dynamic states and responsiveness come into play. To solve this, one effective approach is to collaborate closely with designers to create component libraries or design systems that standardize UI elements, ensuring consistency and reusability. Additionally, leveraging tools like Storybook for isolated component development and testing can reveal discrepancies early, facilitating smoother integration between design and React implementation.","candidateAnswer":"usually it used to have with the compatibility issues like certain React components are not suitable with certain UI requirements and the other programming that I''m doing so I made an entire standardized chart for that with all the references of which components will work well with what settings or what environments and that helped me remove a lot of difficulties from development.","missing_concepts":["Design system or component library usage for standardization.","Collaboration with design teams.","Tools for component testing and isolated development (e.g., Storybook).","Handling responsiveness and dynamic UI states."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate identifies a challenge around compatibility issues between React components and UI requirements, which is relevant. Their solution of creating a standardized chart to reference component suitability shows some practical problem-solving. However, the answer is vague and lacks key details on how this solves design integration challenges. It misses important concepts such as working with design systems, collaborating closely with designers, or using tools like Storybook for testing components in isolation. Communication clarity is low as the explanation is not well articulated. Overall, the candidate shows some understanding but the answer is incomplete and would require further detail to pass.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate recognizes a compatibility issue with React components and addresses it by standardizing references, indicating some practical approach to problem-solving. However, they do not discuss key collaborative or technical practices expected for integrating React with designs, limiting their completeness and clarity. More precise and detailed responses would be needed to consider passing."},{"prompt":"How do you ensure that your designs stay consistent across different devices and screen sizes?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"To ensure design consistency across devices and screen sizes, I use responsive design techniques such as flexible grids, scalable images, and CSS media queries. I establish and maintain a design system or component library that includes reusable UI elements with predefined styles and behaviors. Additionally, I perform thorough testing on various devices and screen resolutions to validate consistency and usability. Collaboration with developers, especially when working with frameworks like React, helps ensure that design intentions are implemented accurately across platforms.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"One final question: what excites you most about product design today?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Focus on user experience and understanding user needs","Emphasis on simplicity in design","Awareness of different user interactions with the product"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["No mention of current technologies such as React","Lacks reference to collaborative and iterative design processes","No mention of inclusive design or personalization","Somewhat vague and repetitive phrasing"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"What excites me most about product design today is the convergence of user-centered design principles with advanced technologies like React, enabling the creation of highly interactive, accessible, and visually appealing interfaces that genuinely solve real user problems. The opportunity to iterate rapidly on designs informed by user data and to collaborate cross-functionally to balance technical feasibility with aesthetic and usability goals is particularly stimulating. Additionally, the focus on inclusive design and personalization allows products to cater effectively to diverse user needs while maintaining simplicity and clarity in the UI.","candidateAnswer":"For me, product design is like, for me, product design is basically a very challenging role and I am excited about user experience, visualizing and imagining how different users would interact with the same product and then satisfying needs of every such user and at the same time keeping things as simple as it can be. So a user''s requirement and thinking that goes behind understanding what a perfect design would be excites me the most.","missing_concepts":["User-centered design with technology integration","Cross-functional collaboration","Rapid iteration based on user data","Inclusive and personalized design"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a reasonable understanding of product design excitement centered around user experience, imagining diverse user interactions, and maintaining simplicity which aligns with user-centered principles. However, the answer misses important aspects highlighted in the ideal answer, such as leveraging advanced technologies like React, iterative design based on user data, and collaboration with technical teams to balance feasibility with aesthetics. Additionally, inclusive design and personalization were not touched upon. The answer is generally relevant and communicated clearly enough, but is somewhat vague and repetitive, lacking depth in problem-solving insight related to modern product design challenges.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a basic grasp of product design focused on users and simplicity but misses the integration of technology, collaboration, and inclusivity that define current product design excitement. Overall, the answer is moderately relevant but incomplete, leading to a fail given the medium difficulty of the question."},{"prompt":"tell me your self","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq6hwmpx0004oz013frhd08l","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq6kf857001goz01kg3toswg', 'cmq6k9zpd000toz01r465a6j5', 72, 64, 55, 86, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-09 11:37:30.619', '2026-06-09 11:38:08.616', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hello.","Yes. The first law of thermodynamics basically tells you about conservation of energy. The first law says that energy can neither be created nor destroyed. It can only be converted from one form to the other.","Casting is one of the common manufacturing process used in mechanical engineering."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 74, '[{"prompt":"Could you start by explaining the first law of thermodynamics in your own words?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":10,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":8,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Correctly stated that energy cannot be created or destroyed and only converted from one form to another.","Answer is relevant and clearly communicated with understandable terminology."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Answer lacks mention of the total energy conservation including internal energy changes and energy exchanges with surroundings.","Did not elaborate on the concept of energy balance (energy input equals output plus change in internal energy)."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":8,"expectedAnswer":"The first law of thermodynamics states that energy cannot be created or destroyed in an isolated system; it can only change forms. This law implies that the total energy of a system and its surroundings remains constant, meaning energy input equals energy output plus any change in internal energy.","candidateAnswer":"Yes. The first law of thermodynamics basically tells you about conservation of energy. The first law says that energy can neither be created nor destroyed. It can only be converted from one form to the other.","missing_concepts":["The concept that total energy in the system and surroundings remains constant.","Energy input equals energy output plus change in internal energy."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrated a good understanding of the first law of thermodynamics by correctly identifying the core principle of conservation of energy and energy transformation. However, the answer was somewhat incomplete as it did not elaborate on the implication that total energy remains constant in the system plus surroundings. Including the idea that energy input equals energy output plus change in internal energy would have made the explanation more complete and aligned with the ideal answer. The explanation was clear and relevant to the question.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a good grasp of the first law of thermodynamics basics and communicates clearly. There is some missing depth about the full scope of energy balance and internal energy changes, but overall the answer meets expectations for a junior mechanical engineer at a medium difficulty level."},{"prompt":"Now, could you describe a common manufacturing process used in mechanical engineering?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Correctly identified casting as a common manufacturing process"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Answer lacks explanation of the process mechanics","No mention of why casting is used or benefits","No description of the steps or technical details","Very brief and incomplete answer"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"One common manufacturing process in mechanical engineering is casting, where molten metal is poured into a mold to take the desired shape upon cooling. This process allows complex shapes to be formed economically, especially for metals that are hard to machine.","candidateAnswer":"Casting is one of the common manufacturing process used in mechanical engineering.","missing_concepts":["Description of casting process: molten metal, mold, cooling","Advantages of casting, such as forming complex shapes","Economic or technical reasons for using casting"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate correctly named casting as a common manufacturing process, which shows basic awareness. However, the answer is too brief and lacks any explanation or detail on how casting works or why it is used in mechanical engineering. There is no discussion of the process itself, its applications, or benefits, which are important for demonstrating understanding. Communication is clear but minimal. Overall, this indicates a limited understanding of the concept and misses key points expected for a medium-difficulty question.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate knows casting is a common manufacturing process but does not elaborate on its operation, benefits, or relevance. Shows partial but incomplete knowledge and struggles to explain the concept fully."},{"prompt":"Can you explain briefly how casting works in practice?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":7,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":8,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Correctly describes pouring molten metal into a die/mold","Mentions cooling and solidification process","Acknowledges finishing operations like machining and grinding"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Does not mention that the mold is shaped to form the desired part explicitly","No mention of types of molds/dies or thermodynamics involved","Could be more precise with terminology (e.g., ''die'' might imply die casting specifically)"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":8,"expectedAnswer":"Casting is a manufacturing process where molten metal is poured into a shaped mold or die and allowed to cool and solidify to form a desired part. After solidification, the casting is removed from the mold and often undergoes finishing operations such as machining or grinding to achieve precise dimensions and surface finish.","candidateAnswer":"So, basically in casting there is a die in which you pour molten metal. Once the molten metal is poured the entire cast is allowed to cool and after the cooling process is done the cast is taken out of the die then it is machined and brought to actual dimensions by grinding or finishing processes.","missing_concepts":["Explicit statement that casting is a manufacturing process to create a shaped part","Thermodynamic aspects like solidification phase change","Variety of mold types (sand mold, permanent mold, die casting)"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a generally correct explanation of the casting process, including pouring molten metal, cooling, solidification, and post-processing like machining and grinding. The answer is relevant and sufficiently clear, showing a functional understanding of casting in practice. However, it lacks some technical depth, such as the concept that the mold is shaped specifically to form the desired part and some of the underlying thermodynamics of solidification. The use of the term ''die'' without clarification could be misleading since it may refer specifically to die casting, which is one subset of casting techniques. Overall, the explanation is good for a junior level but could be improved by including more technical details and precise terminology.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates a solid foundational understanding of casting, covering the key steps in the process and finishing operations. While some nuances and technical depth are missing, the answer is sufficient for a junior mechanical engineer role at this difficulty level. Communication is clear and the description relevant. I recommend passing with encouragement to build deeper knowledge on "},{"prompt":"Now, can you explain what additive manufacturing is and how it differs from traditional methods?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":7,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":8,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Correctly identified additive manufacturing as a layer-by-layer process.","Clearly contrasted additive manufacturing with subtractive manufacturing.","Used appropriate terminology relevant to the field."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Did not explicitly mention advantages such as material waste reduction or ability to create complex geometries.","Slightly vague on specific techniques used in additive manufacturing like 3D printing."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":8,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process where a product is created by adding material layer by layer, typically using techniques like 3D printing. This contrasts with traditional manufacturing, which often relies on subtractive methods where material is removed from a solid block to achieve the final shape. Additive manufacturing allows for complex geometries with less material waste and new design possibilities that traditional methods may not easily achieve.","candidateAnswer":"So, additive manufacturing is a non-conventional manufacturing process in which particles or filament of the base metal is deposited layer by layer to form the final product. It is different from the traditional processes because in additive manufacturing the material is deposited or added to make the final product whereas, in conventional manufacturing process is a subtractive manufacturing where you start taking out material from the base metal or the ingot to achieve the final product.","missing_concepts":["Material waste reduction benefit of additive manufacturing.","Ability to create complex geometries not possible with traditional methods.","Common techniques such as 3D printing."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a technically correct explanation of additive manufacturing, correctly stating that it involves adding material layer by layer, and contrasting it effectively with subtractive traditional methods. The answer is clear and relevant to the question. However, it lacks mention of key advantages like reduced material waste and design flexibility which are important aspects of additive manufacturing. Explicit reference to common techniques, such as 3D printing, would strengthen completeness and demonstrate deeper understanding. Overall, the explanation shows a good grasp but could be improved by including additional details on benefits and examples.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate demonstrates solid understanding of additive manufacturing basics and clear differentiation from traditional subtractive processes. Explanation is mostly accurate and well communicated with minor omissions in benefits and examples. Suitable knowledge level for a junior mechanical engineer."},{"prompt":"One final question for today: how do you see additive manufacturing evolving in the next few years for mechanical engineering applications?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Understands that additive manufacturing will become more robust and widely adopted.","Recognizes the importance of improving manufacturing speed compared to conventional processes."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Answer lacks detail on material advancements and precision improvements.","Does not mention developments like multi-material printing or automated post-processing.","Omits integration with digital design tools and Industry 4.0 concepts for customized manufacturing."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is expected to advance with improvements in material options, process speed, and precision, enabling wider adoption in mechanical engineering for prototyping and end-use parts. Developments in multi-material printing and automated post-processing will enhance the complexity and functionality of components. Additionally, integration with digital design tools and Industry 4.0 concepts will facilitate more customized and efficient manufacturing workflows, reducing lead times and costs compared to traditional methods.","candidateAnswer":"In the next few years additive manufacturing would be much more robust and will be adopted at large scale. At the same time the manufacturing time for additive manufacturing would improve to a great extent, making it highly competitive in relation to the conventional processes.","missing_concepts":["Material options expansion.","Process precision improvements.","Multi-material printing.","Automated post-processing techniques.","Integration with digital design and Industry 4.0."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a generally correct and relevant answer that additive manufacturing will become more robust and faster, which are important trends. However, the response is quite brief and misses several important aspects expected in a medium-difficulty question, such as material improvements, advancements in precision, multi-material capabilities, automated post-processing, and digital integration with Industry 4.0 concepts. These points are crucial for demonstrating a comprehensive understanding of how additive manufacturing will evolve and impact mechanical engineering applications. Communication is clear but somewhat generic and incomplete. To improve, the candidate should elaborate on specific technological advancements and their implications.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a basic but limited understanding of additive manufacturing trends. While the answer is relevant and mostly correct, it lacks depth and coverage of key advancements and industry integration aspects expected for the role. Overall, the response falls short of the completeness required to pass."},{"prompt":"Laws of thermodyanmics","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq6k9zpd000uoz01wfqn4len","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"The laws of thermodynamics describe fundamental principles governing energy and heat transfer. The zeroth law establishes thermal equilibrium, the first law states that energy is conserved (energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed), the second law introduces entropy and states that energy transfer increases disorder, and the third law states that entropy approaches a constant minimum as temperature approaches absolute zero.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"manufacturing process","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq6k9zpd000voz01ij5d4cuk","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A manufacturing process is a series of steps through which raw materials are transformed into finished products. Common manufacturing processes include casting, machining, molding, forming, and joining, each selected based on product design, material, and production volume.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"additive manufacturing","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq6k9zpd000woz01dqi6d8ij","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process of creating three-dimensional objects by successively adding material layer by layer, based on digital 3D model data. It allows for complex geometries, reduces material waste compared to subtractive methods, and is useful for rapid prototyping and low-volume production in mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq6podj4001soz01elpk6vqk', 'cmq6pged8001ooz01ox3l1igc', 9, 45, 40, 50, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-09 14:04:35.583', '2026-06-09 14:04:47.992', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '[]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 0, '[{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq6pged9001poz01oog66lts","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have over 5 years of experience in human resources, specializing in talent acquisition, employee relations, and compliance with labor laws. In my previous roles, I led initiatives to improve employee engagement and developed HR policies aligned with organizational goals. My background includes working cross-functionally with management and legal teams to resolve workplace issues efficiently and uphold professional standards. This experience directly aligns with the responsibilities of this role, where I can apply my skills in HR fundamentals, problem solving, and maintaining domain expertise to support the company''s human capital strategy.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."}]'), ('cmq6pspfl0023oz01n3rfiq1u', 'cmq6pp28v0020oz01w6h2jjxz', 44, 45, 40, 50, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-09 14:07:57.633', '2026-06-09 14:07:57.633', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '[]', 'heuristic-immediate', null, null, null), ('cmq6qbzbh002poz01afed9mle', 'cmq6q4j8o0029oz01b2lu0et2', 62, 73, 62, 74, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-09 14:22:56.909', '2026-06-09 14:23:22.493', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hi Sana, good evening, this is Aditya Boste and I would like to attend the interview which is scheduled for the position of Manager HR.","Thank you, Zana. Can you please repeat the question?","So my background is that I am commerce graduate and then afterwards I did my management studies in human resources and after that I joined a company called Siemens where I worked as a management trainee and I worked there as a in HR department in various functions of HR starting from recruitment, learning and development, composition and benefits and then thereafter the global mobility as well as factory HR. So those are the areas where I worked and I have extensive experience in human resource function. So that is the background of mine in human resource function."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 60, '[{"prompt":"Hi Aditya, my name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today for the HR role. Let’s get started—tell me about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Clearly articulates HR background with details about roles and functions","Mentions key HR domains such as recruitment, learning and development, benefits, and global mobility","Demonstrates relevant experience aligned with the HR role requirements","Answer is understandable and logically presented"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Lacks explicit mention of problem-solving, decision-making or judgment skills","Does not provide specific examples of challenges or outcomes demonstrating HR expertise","No direct linkage of experience to value addition or contribution to the role","Missing references to professional standards or compliance aspects"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would succinctly summarize their HR experience, highlighting relevant roles in recruitment, employee relations, or HR operations. They would mention specific expertise in HR fundamentals such as compliance, talent management, and performance evaluation. They might provide examples demonstrating problem-solving in HR contexts, decision-making with sound judgment, and adherence to professional standards. They would tie these experiences and skills directly to the requirements of the current HR role, showing how their background equips them to contribute effectively and add value.","candidateAnswer":"So my background is that I am commerce graduate and then afterwards I did my management studies in human resources and after that I joined a company called Siemens where I worked as a management trainee and I worked there as a in HR department in various functions of HR starting from recruitment, learning and development, composition and benefits and then thereafter the global mobility as well as factory HR. So those are the areas where I worked and I have extensive experience in human resource function. So that is the background of mine in human resource function.","missing_concepts":["Problem solving and judgment examples in HR context","Explicit HR fundamentals like compliance, talent management, performance evaluation","Demonstration of professional standards adherence","Direct connection of skills to adding value in the new role"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a solid overview of their HR background including relevant roles in recruitment, development, compensation, and other HR functions which is good and relevant to the role. The answer is clear and shows good understanding of the HR function. However, the response is somewhat generic and lacks concrete examples or instances of problem-solving, decision-making, or professional judgment, which are important in HR roles. There is also no direct tie of how their experience will help contribute to this role beyond listing functions they have been involved in. To improve, the candidate should include specific situations demonstrating their HR expertise and explicitly relate their skills to the current job requirements.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate presents relevant HR experience and domain knowledge but does not sufficiently demonstrate problem-solving abilities or how their experience translates into value for this role. Communication is clear but answers could be more detailed with examples. Overall, a suitable candidate with room for deeper insight."},{"prompt":"Thank you, Aditya. Now, can you share an example of a challenging HR problem you solved, and what judgment you used?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Candidate identified a relevant challenging HR problem related to change management and market conditions.","Mentioned interaction with employees to understand capabilities and aspirations."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Did not clearly explain the specific judgments used to handle the problem.","Lack of details on interventions or strategic decisions made.","Explanation was vague and somewhat incomplete.","Limited communication clarity with some fragmented ideas."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific challenging HR problem they encountered, such as managing organizational change during a market downturn, labor relations conflict, or skills gap issues. They should explain the critical judgments made, including assessing stakeholder interests, prioritizing transparent communication, balancing business needs with employee well-being, and choosing appropriate interventions (e.g., training, restructuring, or negotiation). The explanation should highlight their analytical approach, ethical considerations, and strategic alignment with company goals.","candidateAnswer":"so challenging HR problem I''ve encountered during my days in Vadodara at our factory wherein there were a lot of change management happened in terms of culture change in terms of mindset change of the people because the time it was the time wherein the global market in energy was not doing so good and it was impacted India as well and for that matter our factory or the our business as well in India so it was very much important for us to capture the Indian market as well as establish the export market as well so where we have interacted with each and every people understood their capabilities understood their aspirations","missing_concepts":["Assessment of stakeholder interests","Prioritization of transparent communication","Balancing business needs with employee well-being","Specific interventions like training, restructuring, or negotiation","Analytical approach and ethical considerations","Alignment with company goals"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate gave a relevant example focusing on change management during a market downturn and cultural shifts within the factory setting, which aligns moderately with the question. However, the response lacked clarity and depth regarding the candidate''s specific judgments in managing the problem. There was no mention of how the candidate balanced stakeholder interests, what strategic choices were made, or how they addressed employee concerns ethically and analytically. The explanation about interacting with employees to understand capabilities was a positive point but insufficient alone. Overall, the answer felt incomplete and vague, missing critical aspects expected in the ideal response.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate showed some understanding of HR challenges in a difficult market context and cultural change but was unable to clearly articulate the judgments and detailed approaches used to solve the problem. The answer was partially relevant but lacked the necessary completeness and clarity to demonstrate strong problem-solving and HR expertise."},{"prompt":"I see, thanks for that context. What specific steps did you take to navigate that change and achieve results?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["The candidate mentions setting a narrative and linking it to business goals.","There is some recognition of defining capabilities required for achieving goals."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Lacks detailed steps such as stakeholder analysis, communication strategies, training, feedback mechanisms, or collaboration with leadership.","Explanation is vague and does not comprehensively address the question.","Ends abruptly and lacks professional closure."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"To navigate the change effectively, I first conducted a thorough stakeholder analysis to understand the concerns and aspirations of employees. I implemented targeted communication strategies to build awareness and alignment with the new culture and goals. Then, I facilitated training and coaching sessions to shift mindsets and upskill employees. I established feedback mechanisms to monitor progress and adapt initiatives based on employee input. Finally, I collaborated closely with leadership to reinforce accountability and recognize milestones, ensuring sustained commitment and tangible results.","candidateAnswer":"we tried to link it with whatever business goal we have. Thank you. So the specific steps we took about first of all the narrative we''ve set the narrative that we want to reach a certain goal so we set the goal and we design narrative around that and we inspired people to achieve that goal and for that we also defined the capabilities which has to be acquired by these people so that was the strategy we used and people liked it and people were enjoying the journey. Hi Sanani, I''m waiting for your next question.","missing_concepts":["Stakeholder analysis to understand concerns.","Targeted communication strategies for alignment.","Training and coaching to upskill employees.","Feedback mechanisms to monitor and adapt initiatives.","Leadership collaboration to reinforce accountability."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a high-level approach by setting a narrative tied to business goals and defining capabilities. However, the response is vague and incomplete, missing critical steps outlined in the ideal answer such as stakeholder analysis, communication plans, training sessions, feedback loops, and leadership collaboration. The explanation is somewhat unclear and lacks professional structure, ending abruptly without summarizing the impact or results. Further depth and specificity are needed to demonstrate full understanding and effective problem-solving.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows basic understanding of linking change initiatives to business goals and importance of defining capabilities. However, the answer lacks depth, clarity, and critical elements necessary for effectively navigating change. More comprehensive articulation of structured steps is required to pass."},{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq6q4j8o002aoz01wh927vpd","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have over 5 years of experience in Human Resources, specializing in recruitment, employee relations, and performance management. In previous roles, I successfully implemented HR policies aligned with organizational goals, enhancing employee engagement and retention. I have a solid foundation in HR fundamentals, including compliance, talent acquisition, and conflict resolution, which directly applies to this role. Additionally, I have collaborated cross-functionally with management and legal teams to ensure professional standards and domain compliance. This background equips me to effectively address HR challenges and contribute to the company''s people strategy.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq81qex00009o501gji8r50r', 'cmq81nggs0003o501oscmergd', 25, 45, 40, 50, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-10 12:29:52.258', '2026-06-10 12:30:09.681', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '[]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 20, '[{"prompt":"Can you tell me about a challenging project you worked on recently and how you approached it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["Clear explanation and structured response","Good communication clarity"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Completely irrelevant project to mechanical engineering role","No mention of any mechanical engineering principles such as thermodynamics or manufacturing","No indication of teamwork, time/resource management, or engineering problem-solving relevant to the role"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe a recent project where they faced a specific mechanical engineering challenge, such as optimizing a thermal system or improving a manufacturing process. They should explain the problem clearly, outline the systematic approach they took—like researching relevant thermodynamics principles, conducting calculations or simulations, prototyping or testing components, and iterating improvements. The candidate should also mention teamwork or cross-functional coordination if applicable and how they managed time or resource constraints. For example, they might say they optimized a heat exchanger design to improve efficiency by applying thermodynamics concepts, used CAD for design modifications, and collaborated with manufacturing to ensure feasibility. This response shows problem-solving, technical knowledge, and practical application relevant to a junior mechanical engineer role.","candidateAnswer":"Certainly. Recently, I worked on developing a complex inventory management system for a retail client. The challenge was integrating real-time stock updates across multiple store locations. I approached it by first mapping out all data flow points, then implementing a centralized database with APIs for real-time synchronization, ensuring data consistency and minimal latency.","missing_concepts":["Thermodynamics application","Mechanical design or manufacturing processes","Engineering problem-solving context","Cross-functional team collaboration","Use of engineering tools like CAD or prototyping"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate described a software-related project focused on inventory management, which is not relevant to a junior mechanical engineering position. Although the explanation is clear and indicates some problem-solving within software/database development, it lacks any mechanical engineering technical content or demonstrated understanding of engineering concepts. The answer fails to address the question within the appropriate professional context, and no mechanical engineering challenge or approach was mentioned. As a result, most scoring categories other than communication clarity score very low. Candidates should provide examples from mechanical engineering projects, highlighting relevant technical knowledge and problem-solving.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate gave an answer unrelated to mechanical engineering, discussing a software inventory system project. While communication was clear, the response lacked relevance, technical correctness, and demonstrated problem-solving in the mechanical engineering domain. Therefore, the candidate did not meet the expectations for this junior mechanical engineer role."},{"prompt":"Laws of thermodyanmics","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq81nggt0004o501idjc9656","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"The laws of thermodynamics describe fundamental principles governing energy and heat transfer. The zeroth law establishes thermal equilibrium, the first law states that energy is conserved (energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed), the second law introduces entropy and states that energy transfer increases disorder, and the third law states that entropy approaches a constant minimum as temperature approaches absolute zero.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"manufacturing process","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq81nggt0005o501klux9o99","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A manufacturing process is a series of steps through which raw materials are transformed into finished products. Common manufacturing processes include casting, machining, molding, forming, and joining, each selected based on product design, material, and production volume.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"additive manufacturing","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq81nggt0006o501bv23scyw","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process of creating three-dimensional objects by successively adding material layer by layer, based on digital 3D model data. It allows for complex geometries, reduces material waste compared to subtractive methods, and is useful for rapid prototyping and low-volume production in mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq81w9qd000lo501wh2oc6u1', 'cmq81tbt0000fo501u6kay7sd', 33, 45, 40, 50, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-10 12:34:25.477', '2026-06-10 12:34:42.606', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '[]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 30, '[{"prompt":"Hello Shubham, this is Sana from test. Let’s begin. Can you tell me about a time you faced a challenging problem and how you solved it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Clear and understandable communication","Demonstrated some problem-solving steps like root cause analysis and coordination"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Answer is completely unrelated to mechanical engineering or the expected fields (thermodynamics, manufacturing)","Lacks any technical details related to engineering challenges","No demonstration of engineering principles or technical problem solving","Does not address the question''s context or show relevant experience"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe a specific engineering challenge, preferably related to thermodynamics or manufacturing, encountered during an internship or academic project. They would explain the problem clearly, outline the analytical or practical steps taken to address it—such as conducting root cause analysis, applying engineering principles, or collaborating with a team—and describe the solution implemented. They should highlight adaptability, problem-solving skills, and learning from the experience, ideally demonstrating how the resolution improved a process or outcome relevant to mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"Certainly, Sana. In my previous role, we encountered a major issue with our database synchronization which caused inconsistent data across platforms. I analyzed the root cause, coordinated with the development team to implement a real-time syncing solution, and tested extensively to ensure data integrity. This improved our system reliability significantly.","missing_concepts":["Mechanical engineering context","Thermodynamics or manufacturing related problem","Application of engineering principles","Technical detail on the actual problem and solution"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer describes a problem about database synchronization, which is unrelated to mechanical engineering and the specified fields of thermodynamics or manufacturing. While the response demonstrates some problem-solving abilities and clear communication, it lacks any technical relevance to the role. The candidate fails to provide a mechanical engineering challenge or detail the application of engineering principles. This shows a lack of understanding of the question''s intent and the role''s expectations.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate showed clear and concise communication skills but failed to provide any relevant mechanical engineering problem or solution. The answer focused on IT-related issues rather than engineering challenges, which is not appropriate for the role. Overall, the response was not aligned with the question, resulting in a fail."},{"prompt":"Laws of thermodyanmics","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq81tbt0000go501agn1hzj5","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"The laws of thermodynamics describe fundamental principles governing energy and heat transfer. The zeroth law establishes thermal equilibrium, the first law states that energy is conserved (energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed), the second law introduces entropy and states that energy transfer increases disorder, and the third law states that entropy approaches a constant minimum as temperature approaches absolute zero.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"manufacturing process","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq81tbt0000ho501a0slh7de","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A manufacturing process is a series of steps through which raw materials are transformed into finished products. Common manufacturing processes include casting, machining, molding, forming, and joining, each selected based on product design, material, and production volume.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"additive manufacturing","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq81tbt0000io501aawlyfjm","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process of creating three-dimensional objects by successively adding material layer by layer, based on digital 3D model data. It allows for complex geometries, reduces material waste compared to subtractive methods, and is useful for rapid prototyping and low-volume production in mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq821enl001mo5012stouu6a', 'cmq81xgju000to501fs3y6bxv', 40, 55, 48, 94, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-10 12:38:25.137', '2026-06-10 12:39:19.75', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["You''re welcome.","Yeah, so the first law of thermodynamics is about conservation of energy, it says energy cannot be created nor destroyed, it can only be transferred from one form to the other.","In a mechanical system is it applies basically when you convert mechanical energy to heat energy or heat energy to mechanical energy by using fuel for example in heat engines."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 34, '[{"prompt":"Hello Shubham, I’m Sana from test. Let’s jump right in: can you tell me about a challenging project you worked on recently and the specific role you played in overcoming that challenge?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["No relevant information provided","Did not address the question","No demonstration of technical knowledge or problem-solving"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe a specific project involving mechanical engineering challenges, such as design optimization or manufacturing issues. They should explain their personal contributions clearly—for example, identifying the root cause of a production defect, performing calculations or simulations, proposing solutions, and collaborating with cross-functional teams. They might say: \\"In my last internship, I worked on optimizing a gear assembly where we faced unexpected vibration issues. I conducted vibration analysis using simulation tools, identified the resonance frequency as the cause, and proposed design modifications that reduced vibration by 30%. I coordinated with the manufacturing team to implement these changes on the production line.\\" This demonstrates problem-solving, technical skills, teamwork, and result orientation.","candidateAnswer":"You''re welcome.","missing_concepts":["Description of a challenging project","Candidate''s personal role and contributions","Technical problem-solving steps","Use of relevant engineering knowledge","Communication of results and collaboration"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response consisted solely of ''You''re welcome,'' which does not answer the question asked. There is no demonstration of technical skills, problem-solving abilities, or relevant experience. The answer lacks completeness, relevance, clarity, and any indication of understanding the question. Such a response is inadequate for assessing capabilities in a technical interview.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate provided no meaningful answer to the question about a challenging project and their role. No assessment of skills or knowledge can be made based on the response. Recommend further evaluation or more guided questioning if proceeding."},{"prompt":"Hello Shubham, my name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today for the junior mechanical engineer role. Let’s jump right in. Could you start by explaining the first law of thermodynamics in your own words?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":10,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":8,"technical_correctness":9},"strengths":["Correctly states the fundamental principle that energy cannot be created or destroyed.","Uses appropriate terminology such as ''conservation of energy'' and ''energy transfer''.","Answer is clear and relevant to the question asked."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Did not explicitly mention that total energy in an isolated system remains constant.","Lacks application or context in mechanical engineering, such as systems or energy balance.","Slightly brief and could provide more detail for completeness."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":8,"expectedAnswer":"The first law of thermodynamics states that energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed from one form to another, which means the total energy of an isolated system remains constant. In mechanical engineering, this principle is fundamental for analyzing energy transfer processes in systems, such as engines or compressors, ensuring energy balance calculations are accurate.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, so the first law of thermodynamics is about conservation of energy, it says energy cannot be created nor destroyed, it can only be transferred from one form to the other.","missing_concepts":["Energy conservation in an isolated system","Application of the law in mechanical systems like engines or compressors","Energy transformation details and energy balance implications"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrated a strong grasp of the core concept by correctly defining the first law of thermodynamics as the conservation of energy and noting energy transformation. The explanation was technically correct and relevant to the question, delivered clearly and understandably. However, the answer was somewhat incomplete, missing key details such as the implication for isolated systems where total energy remains constant, and practical engineering applications which would showcase deeper understanding. Future answers could be improved by briefly connecting fundamental principles to relevant engineering contexts.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows good foundational knowledge of the first law of thermodynamics with accurate terminology and clear communication. Though not fully complete, the core concept is well understood and explained clearly. Performance meets expectations for a junior mechanical engineer role."},{"prompt":"Good. And how does that law apply in a mechanical system?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Recognizes conversion between mechanical energy and heat energy.","Mentions heat engines as an example."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Does not clearly articulate the conservation of energy principle.","Lacks explanation of energy input, output and internal energy changes.","Answer is somewhat vague and incomplete.","No proper description of how the first law strictly applies in mechanical systems."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"The first law of thermodynamics, which is the conservation of energy, applies in mechanical systems by ensuring that the total energy input, including mechanical work and heat transfer, equals the total energy output plus any changes in the system''s internal energy. For example, in a heat engine, mechanical work output results from converting heat energy input, respecting energy conservation without loss or gain, only energy transformation.","candidateAnswer":"In a mechanical system is it applies basically when you convert mechanical energy to heat energy or heat energy to mechanical energy by using fuel for example in heat engines.","missing_concepts":["Conservation of energy principle in quantitative terms.","Energy input equals output plus internal energy change.","Role of heat and work in energy transfer.","Detailed example or explanation of energy transformations in mechanical systems."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate partially understands the application of the first law of thermodynamics in mechanical systems by acknowledging energy conversion between mechanical and heat forms, using heat engines as an example. However, the answer lacks clarity and completeness, failing to explain that the first law ensures energy conservation where total energy input equals total energy output plus internal energy change. The explanation is vague and misses the critical concept that energy is neither created nor destroyed but transformed, which is central to the first law. For a better answer, more precise and complete coverage of the law and its application to mechanical systems is necessary.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a basic awareness of energy conversion related to the first law of thermodynamics but does not fully grasp or communicate the conservation of energy concept in mechanical systems. The answer is incomplete and somewhat vague, indicating partial understanding but insufficient technical depth. Improvement is needed to meet the standard expected for a junior mechanical engineering "},{"prompt":"Alright. Let’s move on to manufacturing. Can you describe a common manufacturing process used in mechanical engineering?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["The candidate mentioned ''caching'' which is unrelated to manufacturing processes in mechanical engineering.","The answer is extremely vague and incorrect technically.","No relevant manufacturing process was described or explained.","There is no demonstration of understanding of machining or any other manufacturing technique."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"A common manufacturing process in mechanical engineering is machining, which involves removing material from a workpiece to achieve the desired shape and size using tools like lathes, milling machines, or drills. Machining allows for precise dimensional control and is widely used for producing parts with tight tolerances from metals and other materials.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, caching is one of them processes.","missing_concepts":["Machining as a common manufacturing process","Removal of material to shape parts","Use of tools like lathe, milling machines, drills","Purpose and advantages of machining in manufacturing"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer indicates a lack of understanding of the question and the subject matter. Mentioning ''caching'' is irrelevant to mechanical manufacturing processes. The answer is very brief, technically incorrect, and does not address the manufacturing process used in mechanical engineering. There is no explanation or detail to demonstrate knowledge or problem solving abilities. The candidate should focus on core manufacturing techniques such as machining, casting, forming, or additive manufacturing and describe their principles, typical use, and tools involved.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide a relevant or technically correct answer to the question about manufacturing processes in mechanical engineering. The response was unrelated and lacked any demonstration of understanding. This shows a significant gap in fundamental knowledge for the role."},{"prompt":"Could you give a bit more detail about how casting works?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Candidate correctly identified the main process of pouring molten metal into a mold and cooling it.","Mentioned the finishing step involving machining.","Answer is relevant to the question and understandable."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Used the term ''dye'' instead of ''mold'', which shows some lack of precise terminology.","Did not mention the mold cavity shape or casting removal in more detail.","Missed mentioning the importance of the mold shape matching the desired product and the solidification process."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"Casting is a manufacturing process where molten metal is poured into a mold cavity shaped like the desired part and allowed to solidify. Once cooled, the solidified metal, called the casting, is removed from the mold, and any necessary finishing operations such as machining are performed to achieve the final dimensions and surface finish.","candidateAnswer":"So, you pour molten metal into the dye, then allow it to cool, then the cast is taken out and after some machining process, you get the final product.","missing_concepts":["Mold cavity design and shape","Solidification process details","Terminology accuracy (use of ''mold'' instead of ''dye'')","Possible mention of different types of casting methods or materials"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrated a general understanding of casting by describing the basic steps: pouring molten metal into a mold, cooling, removing the casting, and machining. However, the explanation lacked detail on the mold design and the importance of the cavity shape matching the final product. The misuse of the term ''dye'' instead of ''mold'' indicates a small gap in technical vocabulary. Overall, the answer is relevant and mostly correct but incomplete for a full technical explanation at this level.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a reasonable grasp of the casting process, correctly outlining the main steps involved. There is room for improvement in technical vocabulary and providing more detailed explanations of the mold''s role and the solidification process. Nonetheless, the response demonstrates sufficient understanding to pass this medium difficulty question for a junior mechanical engineer."},{"prompt":"Now, can you explain what additive manufacturing is and how it differs from traditional methods?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing, commonly known as 3D printing, is a process of creating objects by adding material layer by layer based on digital models. Unlike traditional subtractive manufacturing, which involves removing material from a solid block, additive manufacturing builds parts from the ground up, allowing for complex geometries, less material waste, and quicker prototyping.","candidateAnswer":"I don''t know about additive manufacturing.","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"That''s fine. Just give it your best shot—what do you understand about additive manufacturing, or what have you heard about it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["No technical content provided","Did not address the question asked","No demonstration of understanding or familiarity with additive manufacturing","No explanation or details given","No communication of concepts"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing, also known as 3D printing, is a process where materials are added layer by layer to create a final product, unlike traditional subtractive methods which remove material. It enables complex geometries, rapid prototyping, and customization with less material waste, making it valuable in modern mechanical engineering and manufacturing contexts.","candidateAnswer":"I have no idea.","missing_concepts":["Definition of additive manufacturing","Layer-by-layer process concept","Comparison to traditional manufacturing","Benefits like complexity, customization, rapid prototyping, and material efficiency"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided no information or explanation related to additive manufacturing. The answer ''I have no idea'' shows no understanding or knowledge on the topic, resulting in a complete lack of technical correctness, completeness, relevance, clarity, and problem-solving ability. To improve, the candidate should study the basic principles, advantages, and applications of additive manufacturing and be prepared to discuss these clearly.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate did not demonstrate any knowledge or understanding of additive manufacturing. They were unable to answer a fundamental question relevant to their role as a Junior Mechanical Engineer. This lack of knowledge indicates they are not ready for technical tasks related to modern manufacturing processes."},{"prompt":"Now, what’s one key difference between additive and traditional subtractive manufacturing?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":3,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["Answer relates to additive manufacturing being a process.","The candidate attempted to address the question."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-7","weaknesses":["Answer is not technically correct regarding the key difference.","Does not mention subtractive manufacturing or compare the two.","Answer is too short and lacks explanation.","Fails to explain the core concept of adding vs removing material."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"One key difference is that additive manufacturing builds objects layer by layer by adding material, whereas traditional subtractive manufacturing removes material from a solid block to create the desired shape.","candidateAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a slow process.","missing_concepts":["Additive manufacturing builds layer by layer by adding material.","Subtractive manufacturing removes material from a solid block."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is very brief and primarily comments on the speed of additive manufacturing, which is not the key difference between additive and subtractive manufacturing. The answer lacks the essential explanation that additive manufacturing builds objects by adding material layer by layer, whereas subtractive manufacturing creates objects by removing material from a solid block. This demonstrates a lack of understanding of the core concept asked. The response does not address subtractive manufacturing at all, leading to very low completeness and correctness scores. Communication was clear but too minimal to be informative.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrated insufficient understanding of the fundamental difference between additive and subtractive manufacturing. The answer was incomplete and technically inaccurate. Further study of basic manufacturing processes is recommended."},{"prompt":"Laws of thermodyanmics","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq81xgju000uo501ur1rj0gp","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"The laws of thermodynamics describe fundamental principles governing energy and heat transfer. The zeroth law establishes thermal equilibrium, the first law states that energy is conserved (energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed), the second law introduces entropy and states that energy transfer increases disorder, and the third law states that entropy approaches a constant minimum as temperature approaches absolute zero.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"manufacturing process","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq81xgjv000vo501gq7gf0w1","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A manufacturing process is a series of steps through which raw materials are transformed into finished products. Common manufacturing processes include casting, machining, molding, forming, and joining, each selected based on product design, material, and production volume.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"additive manufacturing","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq81xgjv000wo501wdlyfox6","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process of creating three-dimensional objects by successively adding material layer by layer, based on digital 3D model data. It allows for complex geometries, reduces material waste compared to subtractive methods, and is useful for rapid prototyping and low-volume production in mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq82hi89001zo501zh7a5p3m', 'cmq82fmoa001so501yubotg5n', 9, 46, 41, 58, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-10 12:50:56.265', '2026-06-10 12:51:16.078', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["I don''t know what''s going on.","Trying to understand, And this is what I am trying to do."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 0, '[{"prompt":"Can you tell me about a challenging project you''ve worked on recently and how you handled it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["No specific project or challenge described","No demonstration of technical or problem-solving approach","Answer is too short and vague, contains filler text"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific challenging business analytics project, outlining the context and key difficulties, such as data quality issues, ambiguous requirements, or tight deadlines. They should explain how they approached problem solving by breaking down the challenge, applying analytical methods like data cleaning, advanced modeling, or stakeholder interviews, and iterating on findings. Effective handling would include collaboration with cross-functional teams, prioritizing tasks, and clearly communicating insights to influence business decisions. For example, they might discuss optimizing a sales forecasting model under incomplete data and how their solution led to measurable improvements.","candidateAnswer":"Trying to understand, And this is what I am trying to do.","missing_concepts":["Description of a challenging business analytics project","Explanation of how the challenge was handled","Technical methods or problem-solving techniques used","Collaboration or communication with stakeholders","Impact or results of the work"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer lacks any relevant information about a challenging project or how they handled it. The response is extremely vague and does not provide any insight into their business analytics skills or problem-solving approach. There is no demonstration of technical correctness, completeness, or communication clarity. To improve, the candidate should provide a detailed example describing the context, challenge, specific actions taken, and results achieved in a recent business analytics project.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide any meaningful answer to the question about a challenging project. The response was too short, vague, and irrelevant, indicating a lack of preparation or understanding. This is insufficient to assess their skills in business analytics or problem solving."},{"prompt":"Please continue in English only for this interview. Let''s proceed. Hello Shubham, this is Sana. I’ll be conducting your interview today. Let’s start off: can you tell me about your background and how it maps to this role?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would summarize their educational background in fields related to business analytics, such as statistics, economics, or computer science, and highlight relevant professional experience in data analysis, reporting, or business intelligence roles. They should provide concrete examples of projects or roles where they applied analytics techniques to solve business problems, demonstrating expertise in data collection, cleaning, and interpretation. Additionally, they should explain familiarity with analytics tools and methodologies pertinent to the role, and articulate how their problem-solving and domain knowledge align with the company’s needs in business analytics.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq82fmoa001to5013keu919s","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have a solid background in business analytics, with 5 years of experience working in data-driven environments where I applied statistical analysis, data visualization, and business intelligence tools to inform strategic decisions. My expertise includes proficiency in SQL, Excel, and Python for data manipulation and predictive modeling, alongside domain knowledge in finance and marketing analytics. For example, I led a project analyzing customer segmentation that increased campaign ROI by 15%. Additionally, I have worked cross-functionally with product, sales, and finance teams to align analytics insights with business objectives, making my experience well suited to this role''s requirements in problem solving and domain expertise in business analytics.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq84qh55002qo5015l8j9b0s', 'cmq84hmrg0027o501ecoiokir', 38, 57, 49, 82, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-10 13:53:53.993', '2026-06-10 13:54:18.42', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Bye.","Yeah, so I am a mechanical engineer from Mumbai. I have four years of experience in engineering, but later on I moved into a people management role in the HR function where I worked for two years handling HR related responsibilities and employee engagement activities.","It was a tough time managing people and understanding their requirements. They had a lot of work at the workplace. To keep them motivated was a difficult task as well as make them aware of work-life balance and keep them going has always been challenging."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 33, '[{"prompt":"What were some key challenges you faced in that HR role, and how did you handle them?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Acknowledges managing people as a challenge","Mentions work-life balance and motivation as concerns"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Lacks specific strategies or actions taken to address challenges","No mention of conflict resolution, communication channels, or employee engagement programs","Does not demonstrate use of data-driven or cross-functional approaches","Answer is vague and incomplete"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"Key challenges included managing diverse employee expectations, addressing conflicts, and maintaining engagement during organizational changes. To handle these, I implemented structured communication channels, conducted regular feedback sessions, and introduced targeted employee development programs. Additionally, I collaborated cross-functionally to align HR strategies with business objectives and used data-driven approaches to monitor employee satisfaction and proactively address issues.","candidateAnswer":"It was a tough time managing people and understanding their requirements. They had a lot of work at the workplace. To keep them motivated was a difficult task as well as make them aware of work-life balance and keep them going has always been challenging.","missing_concepts":["Structured communication channels","Regular feedback sessions","Targeted employee development programs","Collaboration with other departments","Data-driven monitoring and proactive issue resolution"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate briefly mentions challenges like managing people, motivation, and work-life balance, which are relevant. However, the answer lacks depth, and does not describe any concrete steps taken to handle these challenges. There is no illustration of problem-solving methods, strategic initiatives, or professional HR practices. The response is vague and does not cover the key aspects expected in managing HR issues, such as conflict resolution, employee engagement strategies, or use of data to inform decisions.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows basic awareness of some HR challenges but fails to provide a clear, concrete account of how they addressed these issues. The answer is incomplete and does not demonstrate the expected problem-solving skills or domain expertise for the role."},{"prompt":"Can you give an example of a specific situation where you applied problem-solving in that context?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":3,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["Mentions management and delegation related to employees."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["No specific example provided.","Lacks clarity and structure in response.","Does not demonstrate clear problem-solving steps.","Vague and incomplete answer.","Minimal relevance to the question''s request for a detailed situation."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"In my previous HR role, I encountered a sudden conflict between two key team members that was affecting project delivery. I gathered the involved parties separately to understand their perspectives, identified underlying communication gaps, and facilitated a mediated discussion to rebuild trust and clarify roles. As a result, team collaboration improved, and project timelines were met successfully. This approach showcased my problem-solving by analyzing root causes, applying interpersonal skills, and devising a structured resolution process.","candidateAnswer":"I have no memory of it but yeah there were certain things like and the function where managing people was a difficult task so delegated them for the employees but yeah that''s how it is","missing_concepts":["Specific problem-solving instances or scenarios.","Root cause analysis and resolution approach.","Interpersonal communication strategies.","Measured outcomes or results from problem-solving.","Demonstration of HR domain expertise in the context."],"detailed_feedback":"The answer is too vague and incomplete to assess real problem-solving skills. The candidate failed to provide any concrete example or situation, lacked structure, and did not demonstrate an understanding of how to approach and resolve a conflict or problem in an HR context. The mention of delegation is not tied to a specific problem or how it was a solution. Overall, the response lacks technical correctness, completeness, and clarity.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate''s answer did not meet expectations for demonstrating problem-solving capability in HR. The response was unclear, vague, and did not provide any concrete example or reasoning. Candidate needs to improve on providing structured, relevant, and detailed responses with clear examples reflecting problem-solving skills."},{"prompt":"Could you share a bit more about how you adapted HR fundamentals in your last role?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":5,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":4,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Answer is relevant to the question","Basic understanding that following SOPs is part of HR operations"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Lacks depth or detail on how HR fundamentals were adapted","No examples or explanation of customization or problem solving","Does not demonstrate understanding beyond following existing procedures","Incomplete and vague response lacking key HR functions or strategic alignment"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"In my last role, I adapted HR fundamentals by first aligning core HR processes like recruitment, onboarding, performance management, and employee relations with the company''s strategic goals and culture. For example, I customized the recruitment process to include behavioral assessments that better predicted cultural fit, ensuring higher retention. I also updated onboarding procedures by integrating digital tools to enhance new hire engagement and compliance training. Throughout, I maintained compliance with labor laws and company policies, and worked closely with cross-functional teams to tailor HR practices that addressed specific challenges such as employee engagement and talent development, thereby supporting business outcomes effectively.","candidateAnswer":"It''s very simple so basically you just follow the SOP of the company and things are good.","missing_concepts":["Alignment of HR processes with company goals","Customization of recruitment, onboarding, or performance management","Use of tools or innovations in HR","Compliance with labor laws","Collaboration with cross-functional teams","Addressing specific HR challenges like employee engagement or talent development"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is minimal and lacks the necessary depth expected from the question. While they mention following SOPs, which is a starting point for HR practices, they fail to show how HR fundamentals were adapted, customized, or aligned with company goals. There are no concrete examples, no discussion of problem solving or improvements, and no demonstration of understanding the broader HR context as described in the ideal response. The answer is vague, incomplete, and provides insufficient evidence of domain expertise or judgment.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows only a superficial understanding of adapting HR fundamentals by emphasizing adherence to SOPs without elaboration. The response does not meet the expectations for the role, lacking key insights into HR customization, strategic alignment, or problem solving. This answer does not demonstrate adequate HR domain expertise or the ability to adapt processes to support business goals."},{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq84hmrg0028o501b311bchq","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have over 5 years of experience in Human Resources, specializing in recruitment, employee relations, and performance management. In previous roles, I successfully implemented HR policies aligned with organizational goals, enhancing employee engagement and retention. I have a solid foundation in HR fundamentals, including compliance, talent acquisition, and conflict resolution, which directly applies to this role. Additionally, I have collaborated cross-functionally with management and legal teams to ensure professional standards and domain compliance. This background equips me to effectively address HR challenges and contribute to the company''s people strategy.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq928onj0034o50140ytu8z7', 'cmq922ke8002yo501odscfplr', 9, 45, 40, 50, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-11 05:31:50.861', '2026-06-11 05:32:02.288', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '[]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 0, '[{"prompt":"Hello Shubham, this is Sana from test. Welcome to the interview. Let''s begin with the first question: can you tell me about a challenging situation you faced at work and how you handled it?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific work-related challenge that tested their problem-solving, communication, or technical skills. They should explain the context succinctly, such as a design issue or manufacturing delay. The response needs to include the actions they took—like analyzing root causes, collaborating with team members, or applying thermodynamics principles—and conclude with the positive outcome or lessons learned. Emphasis on proactive approach, clear communication, and practical resolution aligned with mechanical engineering tasks is important.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Laws of thermodyanmics","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq922kea002zo501g81d0yfh","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"The laws of thermodynamics describe fundamental principles governing energy and heat transfer. The zeroth law establishes thermal equilibrium, the first law states that energy is conserved (energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed), the second law introduces entropy and states that energy transfer increases disorder, and the third law states that entropy approaches a constant minimum as temperature approaches absolute zero.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"manufacturing process","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq922keb0030o501e6hkvb9g","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A manufacturing process is a series of steps through which raw materials are transformed into finished products. Common manufacturing processes include casting, machining, molding, forming, and joining, each selected based on product design, material, and production volume.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"additive manufacturing","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq922keb0031o501sjb2bhnr","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process of creating three-dimensional objects by successively adding material layer by layer, based on digital 3D model data. It allows for complex geometries, reduces material waste compared to subtractive methods, and is useful for rapid prototyping and low-volume production in mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq96ahch0040o501jg825ogj', 'cmq965s15003ao501i7sogp7z', 40, 56, 49, 90, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-11 07:25:13.169', '2026-06-11 07:25:51.273', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Yes, so I''m a mechanical engineer, did my engineering from Mumbai. I have around four years of experience as a solution engineer. I have been working on mechanical projects and handling power plants since then.","Yes, the first law of thermodynamics is about conservation of energy, which says energy cannot be created or destroyed, it can only be converted from one form to the other.","Testing is one of the processes."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 35, '[{"prompt":"My first question: can you tell me about yourself and your background?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["The candidate correctly identifies themselves as a mechanical engineer.","Mentions some relevant experience working on mechanical projects and power plants.","Provides a basic answer that is understandable and relevant to the question."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["The answer lacks detail about academic qualifications, such as the degree specifics.","No mention of key expected skills like thermodynamics or manufacturing.","Does not clearly link experience to mechanical engineering fundamentals or relevant projects.","The role of ''solution engineer'' is not explained, creating ambiguity about mechanical relevance.","No expression of motivation or enthusiasm for the junior mechanical engineer position."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would succinctly summarize their academic qualifications and relevant experience, emphasizing mechanical engineering education and any internships or projects related to mechanical design, thermodynamics, or manufacturing. They should highlight practical exposure to mechanical engineering concepts and express enthusiasm for starting a career as a junior mechanical engineer. For example, they might mention completing a bachelor''s degree in mechanical engineering, followed by hands-on project work or internships involving thermodynamics and manufacturing processes, demonstrating readiness for the graduate trainee role.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, so I''m a mechanical engineer, did my engineering from Mumbai. I have around four years of experience as a solution engineer. I have been working on mechanical projects and handling power plants since then.","missing_concepts":["Thermodynamics","Manufacturing processes","Internships or hands-on project work in mechanical engineering","Clear connection between experience and core mechanical engineering concepts"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a basic and somewhat relevant overview of their background as a mechanical engineer with experience in mechanical projects and power plants. However, the answer lacks specifics about educational qualifications, particularly details about their mechanical engineering degree or relevant academic projects. They do not mention key areas such as thermodynamics or manufacturing, which were expected. The job title ''solution engineer'' is vague without clarification of its mechanical engineering context. Furthermore, the candidate does not demonstrate motivation or readiness for a junior mechanical engineer role through their answer. Improving completeness and clarity around technical skills and academic background would strengthen the response.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows foundational understanding and some relevant experience but does not effectively communicate their academic background or exposure to core mechanical engineering skills needed for the role. The answer is too vague and incomplete, leading to a fail."},{"prompt":"Could you explain the first law of thermodynamics in your own words?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":10,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":9,"technical_correctness":9},"strengths":["Clear and technically accurate definition of the conservation of energy principle.","Correctly states that energy cannot be created or destroyed.","Well communicated and easy to understand explanation."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Incomplete explanation; did not mention the system and surroundings or how heat and work relate to energy changes.","Lacks detail about how the total energy remains constant accounting for heat added and work done."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":8,"expectedAnswer":"The first law of thermodynamics states that energy cannot be created or destroyed in an isolated system; it can only be transformed from one form to another. In essence, the total energy of a system and its surroundings remains constant, accounting for heat added to the system and work done by or on it.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, the first law of thermodynamics is about conservation of energy, which says energy cannot be created or destroyed, it can only be converted from one form to the other.","missing_concepts":["Role of heat and work in energy transfer","Energy conservation in system and surroundings context","Quantitative aspects or examples"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a solid, technically correct core idea by stating the conservation of energy and the transformation of energy from one form to another. The answer is relevant and clearly communicated, demonstrating a good understanding. However, the explanation is somewhat brief and lacks completeness regarding the role of heat, work, and system boundaries, which are important components for a full understanding of the first law of thermodynamics. Including these aspects would strengthen the answer significantly.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a good grasp of the fundamental concept behind the first law of thermodynamics with a technically correct and clear explanation. While the answer lacks some depth and detail about energy exchanges through heat and work and system context, it meets the expectations for a junior mechanical engineer. Overall, the candidate passes this question with room for improvement in elaborat"},{"prompt":"Can you describe a common manufacturing process used in mechanical engineering?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["The candidate attempted to name a process related to manufacturing."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["The answer ''Testing is one of the processes'' is vague, incomplete, and does not describe a manufacturing process.","The candidate did not provide any technical details or explanation.","The response shows minimal understanding of manufacturing processes in mechanical engineering.","The answer is not relevant or specific to the question asked."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"Casting is a common manufacturing process where molten metal is poured into a mold cavity and allowed to solidify into a desired shape. This process typically involves pattern making, mold preparation, melting the metal, pouring it into the mold, cooling, and finally removing the solidified part for further processing or finishing.","candidateAnswer":"Testing is one of the processes.","missing_concepts":["Definition and explanation of a manufacturing process such as casting.","Key steps involved in the process (e.g. pattern making, mold preparation, melting, pouring, cooling).","Examples of manufacturing processes used in mechanical engineering."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate’s answer is too short and vague to demonstrate any meaningful knowledge of manufacturing processes in mechanical engineering. Simply stating ''Testing is one of the processes'' is not relevant to the question asked about manufacturing processes. There is no description or explanation, so technical correctness and completeness are severely lacking. A good answer would explain a common process like casting, machining, or forging with key steps and technical details. More effort is needed to show understanding and communicate clearly.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide a relevant or technically accurate description of a manufacturing process. The response lacked detail and did not demonstrate understanding of fundamental manufacturing concepts in mechanical engineering."},{"prompt":"Could you elaborate a bit more on that process—what exactly happens during casting?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Recognizes that casting involves melting metal and cooling it in a mold (referred to as ''dye'').","Mentions finishing operations after casting."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Incorrect terminology: ''dye'' instead of ''die'' or more accurately ''mold''.","Does not clearly state that molten metal is poured into a mold shaped as the desired part.","Misses the step of careful pouring to avoid defects.","Lacks mention of solidification and mold removal process explicitly.","Overall explanation is vague and lacks detail on the key steps involved."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"Casting is a manufacturing process where molten metal is poured into a mold cavity that has the shape of the desired part. The metal solidifies within the mold, taking its shape, and once cooled, the mold is removed to reveal the cast component. Key steps include melting the metal, pouring it carefully to avoid defects, solidification and cooling, and finally removing and cleaning the casting before any finishing operations.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, so basically casting is a process in which you melt the molten metal into a dye and then allow it to cool and then take the product out and do some finishing job before finally using the product.","missing_concepts":["Definition and purpose of the mold cavity.","Melting and preparation of molten metal.","Careful pouring to avoid defects.","Solidification and cooling process.","Removal and cleaning before finishing."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a basic understanding that casting involves molten metal being introduced into a mold and subsequent cooling and finishing. However, the answer lacks technical accuracy and completeness. The use of the term ''dye'' is incorrect and may indicate misunderstanding. Key steps such as pouring the molten metal carefully to avoid defects, the solidification process, and removal of the casting after cooling were not mentioned or explained clearly. The explanation is somewhat vague and does not fully communicate the casting process''s nature. To improve, the candidate should focus on precise technical terms and cover each critical step systematically.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows partial understanding of the casting process but provides a vague and incomplete explanation with some technical inaccuracies. They recognize some basic steps but fail to elaborate on key details expected at this level. Overall, the answer is closer to partial correctness but not sufficiently comprehensive or precise for a pass."},{"prompt":"Now, can you explain what additive manufacturing is and how it differs from traditional methods?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["No technical content provided","Did not demonstrate knowledge or understanding of additive manufacturing","Did not address the differences from traditional methods"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process where objects are created by adding material layer by layer, typically using 3D printing technologies. Unlike traditional manufacturing, which often involves subtractive methods like machining or casting that remove material from a larger block, additive manufacturing builds parts directly from a digital model, allowing for complex geometries, reduced material waste, and faster prototyping.","candidateAnswer":"I am not aware of additive manufacturing.","missing_concepts":["Definition of additive manufacturing","Layer-by-layer building process","Differences from subtractive manufacturing","Advantages such as less material waste and ability to create complex geometries"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate did not provide any explanation or attempt to answer the question about additive manufacturing. This indicates lack of familiarity with a fundamental manufacturing concept expected at this role level. As a result, none of the technical requirements or key ideas were addressed, leading to a complete zero score in all categories.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate did not demonstrate any knowledge or understanding of additive manufacturing, providing no relevant or meaningful response to the question. This is a significant gap in their manufacturing knowledge."},{"prompt":"Can you share any guess on how it''s used in mechanical engineering?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["No attempt to answer the question","Completely lacks any technical content","No demonstration of understanding or problem-solving","No relevance to the question asked","No communication or explanation provided"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing in mechanical engineering is used to create complex and customized parts by building them layer by layer, which allows for rapid prototyping, reduction of material waste, and production of components with intricate geometries that are difficult or impossible to achieve with traditional manufacturing methods.","candidateAnswer":"No, I have no idea","missing_concepts":["Use of additive manufacturing in creating complex and customized parts","Rapid prototyping benefits","Material waste reduction","Production of intricate geometries","Advantages over traditional manufacturing methods"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate answered ''No, I have no idea,'' which provides no information related to the question. This shows a lack of even a basic understanding or attempt to reason about how additive manufacturing is used in mechanical engineering. Consequently, no technical correctness, relevance, completeness, or communication clarity can be assessed. This is considered a very weak answer and does not meet the expectations for a junior mechanical engineer role.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide any relevant or technically correct answer regarding the use of additive manufacturing in mechanical engineering. This indicates a significant gap in fundamental knowledge and problem-solving ability needed for the role."},{"prompt":"Laws of thermodyanmics","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq965s16003bo5018hq3yhbs","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"The laws of thermodynamics describe fundamental principles governing energy and heat transfer. The zeroth law establishes thermal equilibrium, the first law states that energy is conserved (energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed), the second law introduces entropy and states that energy transfer increases disorder, and the third law states that entropy approaches a constant minimum as temperature approaches absolute zero.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"manufacturing process","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq965s16003co501dny0amhb","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A manufacturing process is a series of steps through which raw materials are transformed into finished products. Common manufacturing processes include casting, machining, molding, forming, and joining, each selected based on product design, material, and production volume.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"additive manufacturing","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq965s16003do501an7l5nmm","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process of creating three-dimensional objects by successively adding material layer by layer, based on digital 3D model data. It allows for complex geometries, reduces material waste compared to subtractive methods, and is useful for rapid prototyping and low-volume production in mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq96je99004oo5015y63iu91', 'cmq96dmfb0048o501wqrnrcyk', 52, 69, 59, 74, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-11 07:32:09.07', '2026-06-11 07:32:51.915', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Yeah, so in my field one of the major projects that I have handled is employee engagement activity where I was responsible to make arrangements for the annual function of a company. It was a difficult task because the number of people were more than 500 and from different places from different cities they were visiting. So to understand the requirements and make the necessary improvements, arrangements was very difficult task. At the same time I managed it by forming a team and delegated activities promptly to each one of them which helped me conduct the event successfully.","after the event we took feedback from each and every attendee that was there at the event and based on the score that we got we were able to measure the success","So, my background is from mechanical engineer, but I have been taking up roles in people management since the start of my career. What has happened so far is I''ve been able to deliver on the responsibilities and the KPIs so far, and that''s how my experience comes in."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 48, '[{"prompt":"Can you tell me about a recent project where you faced a major challenge and how you handled it?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Provided a specific project example related to HR","Acknowledged the challenge of handling large-scale employee engagement","Demonstrated delegation and team management","Clear and understandable explanation"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Lacked detailed description of the challenges faced beyond logistics","Did not mention detailed planning, communication strategies, or outcomes","Did not explicitly highlight leadership or adaptability beyond delegation","No mention of measurable success or how improvements were made"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific HR-related project presenting a significant challenge, such as managing a large-scale recruitment drive under tight deadlines or resolving a complex employee relations issue. They should explain the context, the key difficulties encountered, and concrete steps taken to address them—for example, devising a detailed action plan, coordinating cross-functional teams, or employing effective communication strategies. The response should highlight problem-solving skills, leadership, and adaptability, demonstrating successful outcomes like meeting project goals or improving processes.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, so in my field one of the major projects that I have handled is employee engagement activity where I was responsible to make arrangements for the annual function of a company. It was a difficult task because the number of people were more than 500 and from different places from different cities they were visiting. So to understand the requirements and make the necessary improvements, arrangements was very difficult task. At the same time I managed it by forming a team and delegated activities promptly to each one of them which helped me conduct the event successfully.","missing_concepts":["Detailed challenge description and context","Concrete problem-solving steps beyond team delegation","Leadership and adaptability demonstration","Outcome or impact of the project","Communication strategy or stakeholder management"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a relevant and clear example of managing an employee engagement event involving over 500 attendees. They identified logistical challenges and mentioned forming a team to delegate tasks, which indicates basic problem-solving skills and some leadership. However, the answer lacks depth in describing the key difficulties, planning or communication strategies used, and the outcome or effectiveness of their approach. The response would be stronger if it included specifics about managing cross-functional teams, addressing unexpected issues, or improving processes to ensure success. Overall, the answer is adequate but somewhat superficial.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate answered a relevant HR project question with decent clarity and showed an understanding of handling large events through team delegation. While technically correct and sufficiently relevant, the response is somewhat incomplete and lacking in detail regarding the complexity of challenges and strategic approaches. Given the satisfactory communication and problem-solving demonstration, "},{"prompt":"How did you measure the success of that engagement activity?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Understands the importance of collecting feedback after the event","Recognizes the use of scores as a method to measure success","Answer is relevant and mostly clear"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Lacks detail on the types of feedback collected (qualitative vs quantitative)","Does not mention other success metrics such as engagement levels or achievement of objectives","Misses the importance of comparing feedback against predefined KPIs or baseline data","No mention of follow-up indicators or longer-term impact measures"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"The success of an engagement activity is typically measured by collecting qualitative and quantitative feedback from participants through surveys or interviews immediately after the event. Key success metrics include participant satisfaction scores, engagement levels during the activity, achievement of predefined objectives (such as increased team cohesion or knowledge sharing), and follow-up indicators like improved employee morale or retention. Additionally, comparing these outcomes against baseline data or KPIs set prior to the activity provides a clear measure of impact.","candidateAnswer":"after the event we took feedback from each and every attendee that was there at the event and based on the score that we got we were able to measure the success","missing_concepts":["Use of both qualitative and quantitative feedback","Multiple key success metrics beyond participant scores","Predefined objectives and KPIs to benchmark success","Follow-up measures like morale and retention improvements"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate identifies collecting feedback and using scores to measure success, which is technically correct and relevant. However, the answer is vague and lacks completeness. It does not cover the comprehensive approach including qualitative feedback, engagement during the activity, predefined objectives, or comparative analysis against baseline KPIs. These elements are important for a robust measurement of engagement activities'' success. The communication is generally clear but the explanation is superficial and does not demonstrate solid understanding or problem-solving judgment expected for the role.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows basic understanding of measuring engagement activity success through post-event feedback scores but misses critical aspects of a thorough evaluation. The response is somewhat relevant and clear but incomplete and lacks depth in HR domain knowledge and analytical judgment. Overall, the candidate fails to demonstrate the professional standard required."},{"prompt":"Can you share a bit more about your specific HR responsibilities in your recent role?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":4,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Candidate demonstrated involvement in managing events such as webinars, seminars, functions, and sports events.","Answer was understandable and clear in describing event management responsibilities."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Did not address core HR responsibilities such as recruitment, onboarding, employee relations, benefits administration, or compliance.","Lacked details on employee performance evaluation, training programs, or maintaining HR records.","Limited scope focused only on event management, which is only a small part of HR functions.","Did not demonstrate understanding of broader HR domain and problem-solving related to HR."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"In my recent role, my HR responsibilities included managing recruitment and onboarding processes, administering employee benefits, and ensuring compliance with labor laws. I also handled employee relations by addressing grievances, conducting performance evaluations, and organizing training programs to enhance workforce skills. Additionally, I coordinated employee engagement activities and maintained HR records to support organizational goals.","candidateAnswer":"I was more into people management and event management. So all the events that used to be That used to happen there I used I would be the lead of those events and I was responsible for the success of all the webinars or seminars or functions and the sports events that Was happening at the company","missing_concepts":["Recruitment and onboarding","Employee benefits administration","Labor law compliance","Employee relations and grievance handling","Performance evaluations","Training and development","HR record maintenance"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer mostly focused on event and people management related to organizing company events and sports activities. While this shows some involvement in employee engagement, it is a very narrow aspect of HR. The response did not cover critical HR functions such as recruitment, onboarding, employee relations, benefits, compliance, or training. There is a lack of demonstration of core HR responsibilities and problem solving in the HR domain. Additionally, the answer was clear but incomplete and only partially relevant to the question. To improve, the candidate should include a broader range of HR duties reflecting the full scope of their role.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate provided a limited and partial answer focusing on event management rather than core HR responsibilities. This indicates a weak understanding of the HR role scope and functions. The response lacked key HR components and did not demonstrate sufficient problem-solving skills related to HR. Overall, the answer was too narrow and incomplete to meet the expectations for the HR role."},{"prompt":"How do you approach problem-solving when dealing with employee conflicts or sensitive HR issues?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Recognizes the importance of communication in resolving conflicts","Mentions involving all parties for a conversation, showing willingness to mediate"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Answer is very brief and lacks detail about confidentiality, gathering facts, or legal compliance","No mention of documentation or escalation procedures","Does not highlight empathy or understanding different perspectives","Lacks clarity on how solutions are reached or how workplace harmony is preserved"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"I approach employee conflicts and sensitive HR issues by first gathering all relevant facts from involved parties confidentially to understand different perspectives. Then, I facilitate open, empathetic communication to help employees express concerns and work toward mutually acceptable solutions. I also ensure compliance with company policies and legal regulations throughout the process, documenting actions taken. If needed, I involve management or external experts to mediate or resolve complex cases. Ultimately, my goal is to preserve workplace harmony and trust while addressing issues fairly and promptly.","candidateAnswer":"Communication is what I understand as the most important aspect of it. So, I usually ask all the parties involved to come together and have a conversation and resolve the conflicts.","missing_concepts":["Confidential fact gathering","Empathetic and open communication facilitation","Compliance with company policies and legal regulations","Documentation of actions taken","Involving management or external experts if necessary","Focus on preserving workplace trust and fairness"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate correctly identifies communication as a key aspect of resolving employee conflicts and demonstrates a basic approach by bringing all parties together to talk. However, the answer is overly simplistic and insufficiently detailed. It lacks critical components such as gathering facts confidentially, ensuring legal and policy compliance, documenting the process, and using empathy to understand differing perspectives. The candidate also does not address escalation or the role of HR beyond facilitating dialogue. Overall, while the answer is relevant and clear, it falls short in completeness and technical correctness expected for this HR role, indicating a superficial understanding of handling sensitive employee issues.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate has a basic grasp of the importance of communication in employee conflict resolution but fails to demonstrate a comprehensive approach including confidentiality, compliance, and proper procedures. Additional training or experience would be needed to ensure effective handling of sensitive HR matters."},{"prompt":"And one final question: how do you ensure professional standards in your HR work?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":3,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["Mentioned the use of SOPs to guide work processes."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Answer is vague and very incomplete.","Did not mention adherence to policies, laws, or ethical guidelines.","No indication of efforts to maintain fairness or confidentiality.","No examples of continuous improvement or communication strategies.","Lacked clarity and a professional explanation of how standards are ensured."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"I ensure professional standards in my HR work by strictly adhering to established policies, labor laws, and ethical guidelines to maintain fairness and confidentiality. I regularly update my knowledge of legal requirements and best practices, apply consistent processes for recruitment, performance management, and employee relations, and promote transparent communication with all stakeholders. Additionally, I use SOPs and documentation to ensure accountability and continuous improvement in HR operations.","candidateAnswer":"So, there are certain things happening in the company and then the SOPs are good enough to you know, do proper work and conduct.","missing_concepts":["Adherence to labor laws and ethical guidelines","Maintaining fairness and confidentiality","Regular updates on legal requirements and HR best practices","Consistent HR processes for recruitment and performance management","Transparent communication with stakeholders","Use of documentation for accountability and improvement"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response is very vague and lacks the essential elements needed to demonstrate how professional standards are maintained in HR work. Mentioning SOPs is a minimal start but does not show an understanding of the broader context including legal compliance, ethics, or proactive communication. The answer was fragmented and unclear, reflecting a weak grasp of the question''s requirements. To improve, the candidate should provide concrete examples of policies they follow, how they keep their knowledge updated, and how they ensure fairness and transparency.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate did not adequately demonstrate their understanding of ensuring professional standards in HR. Their response was minimal, unclear, and missing key concepts such as adherence to laws, ethics, and effective communication. This indicates a lack of depth in their HR domain expertise and problem-solving skills related to maintaining professional standards."},{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq96dmfb0049o5014jpx00bm","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have over 5 years of experience in Human Resources, specializing in recruitment, employee relations, and performance management. In previous roles, I successfully implemented HR policies aligned with organizational goals, enhancing employee engagement and retention. I have a solid foundation in HR fundamentals, including compliance, talent acquisition, and conflict resolution, which directly applies to this role. Additionally, I have collaborated cross-functionally with management and legal teams to ensure professional standards and domain compliance. This background equips me to effectively address HR challenges and contribute to the company''s people strategy.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq9elnug005so501m5n9cd8p', 'cmq9eelzx004yo5013pl3mn1n', 30, 63, 54, 100, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-11 11:17:51.736', '2026-06-11 11:19:05.246', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Actually, recently I''m facing the problem in frontend when I''m completing my project. I just faced a problem in JavaScript with the frontend. It''s facing some bugs to complete this.","First of all I was just watching and since what the problem and where is the works create and how it''s to resolve then I checked the code and line by line for searching for a box then I fixed it.","Yeah, sure. For a product designer first of all you have to know about what kind of product you made and what kind of categories and implementation you have to done in this management and how to implement all in the market. That''s I think."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 20, '[{"prompt":"Can you tell me about a recent challenge you faced at work and how you handled it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":3,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["The candidate attempts to talk about a frontend problem related to JavaScript."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Answer is very vague and lacks any specific details about the challenge.","No mention of the nature of the bug or the context of the problem.","No explanation of how the problem was analyzed or solved.","No indication of impact, tools used, collaboration, or outcome.","Communication is unclear and incomplete."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a concrete, recent challenge related to their role, such as a complex UI design problem or a technical issue in React development. They should explain the impact of the challenge, how they analyzed the problem, the specific steps they took to resolve it (e.g., debugging techniques, user testing, collaboration with cross-functional teams), and the outcome or lessons learned. For example, they might discuss identifying a performance bottleneck in a React application, using profiling tools to locate inefficiencies, refactoring code for better state management, and verifying the improved user experience through testing.","candidateAnswer":"Actually, recently I''m facing the problem in frontend when I''m completing my project. I just faced a problem in JavaScript with the frontend. It''s facing some bugs to complete this.","missing_concepts":["Detailed description of the challenge","Problem analysis methods","Steps taken to solve the problem","Outcome or lessons learned","Relation to UI design or React"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is too brief and vague to evaluate technical correctness or problem-solving skills effectively. They mention encountering a JavaScript bug in the frontend but do not describe the nature of the challenge, how they approached it, what steps they took, or what the outcome was. There is no explanation of any debugging techniques, collaboration, or testing, which are expected for this question. The candidate''s response lacks depth, detail, and clarity, making it difficult to assess their understanding or abilities.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate fails to provide a specific or detailed example of a recent challenge. The answer is vague, incomplete, and does not demonstrate problem-solving or technical skills relevant to the role. They do not effectively communicate their approach or results. Overall, this response does not meet the expectations for this medium difficulty question."},{"prompt":"What steps did you take to solve that bug?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":4,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Candidate attempts to mention checking the code","References looking for the bug and fixing it"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Lacks clear, structured approach to debugging","No mention of reproducing the issue or understanding its scope","No use of debugging tools or logs","Does not describe testing or verifying the fix","Unclear and vague explanation, making understanding difficult"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"To solve the bug, I first clearly defined and reproduced the issue to understand its scope. Then, I examined the relevant code sections, using debugging tools and logs to isolate the root cause. After identifying the problem, I implemented targeted fixes and thoroughly tested the solution to ensure the bug was resolved without side effects. Finally, I documented the fix and updated relevant stakeholders.","candidateAnswer":"First of all I was just watching and since what the problem and where is the works create and how it''s to resolve then I checked the code and line by line for searching for a box then I fixed it.","missing_concepts":["Reproducing and defining the issue","Using debugging tools and logs","Testing the fix and ensuring no side effects","Documenting the fix and notifying stakeholders"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer shows a minimal attempt at describing how they approached fixing a bug, primarily focusing on checking the code line by line and then fixing it. However, the explanation is vague, lacks structure, and misses many essential steps such as reproducing the issue, isolating the root cause with debugging tools, testing the fix, and documenting changes. The communication is unclear, making it difficult to fully understand their process. Overall, the candidate demonstrates only a weak understanding of a systematic debugging approach.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate''s response is too vague and incomplete to demonstrate strong debugging skills. They need to improve on clearly outlining a thorough bug-solving process including issue reproduction, root cause analysis, testing, and documentation. Communication also needs enhancement for clarity."},{"prompt":"Can you tell me about your responsibilities as a product designer?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":4,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["Candidate shows some awareness that understanding the product and market is necessary."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Answer is vague and lacks technical details about product design responsibilities.","No mention of user research, prototyping, collaboration, or design systems.","Does not demonstrate understanding of key tasks in product design.","Communication is unclear and confusing in places."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"As a product designer, I am responsible for end-to-end design of digital products, which includes understanding user needs, creating wireframes and prototypes, conducting user research and testing, and collaborating cross-functionally with engineers and product managers to deliver intuitive and visually appealing interfaces. I ensure designs align with business goals and technical constraints while maintaining high usability and accessibility standards. Key responsibilities include defining design systems, iterating on UI components to improve user experience, and integrating feedback from stakeholders throughout the product lifecycle.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, sure. For a product designer first of all you have to know about what kind of product you made and what kind of categories and implementation you have to done in this management and how to implement all in the market. That''s I think.","missing_concepts":["End-to-end design process","User research and testing","Wireframing and prototyping","Collaboration with engineers and product managers","Aligning designs with business goals and technical constraints","Usability and accessibility standards","Iterating on UI components","Design systems"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is vague and lacks substantive details about the core responsibilities of a product designer. Although there is a brief mention about understanding the product and its market, the response fails to address the key aspects such as user needs analysis, wireframing, prototyping, cross-functional collaboration, and ensuring usability and accessibility. The explanation is also somewhat unclear and confusing, indicating a poor grasp of the role''s responsibilities. Overall, the answer falls significantly short of demonstrating a solid and complete understanding of product design duties.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate did not provide a clear or complete explanation of the responsibilities of a product designer. Their answer was superficial, lacked key technical concepts, and failed to demonstrate the necessary understanding of the role. Based on this response, the candidate does not meet the expectations for this position."},{"prompt":"Can you tell me more about your experience with UI design in your recent projects?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["Mentions UI design as a focus area"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Answer is vague and lacks concrete examples","Does not explain tools, frameworks, or specific approaches used","Lacks explanation of collaboration or design processes","Communication is unclear and difficult to understand","No evidence of problem-solving or design iteration"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"In my recent projects, I have led UI design efforts by collaborating closely with product managers and engineers to create intuitive, user-friendly interfaces. I focus on translating user needs and business goals into wireframes and high-fidelity prototypes using tools like Figma and Sketch. For example, in a recent React-based web application, I designed reusable component libraries and implemented accessible, responsive layouts that improved user engagement by 20%. My approach integrates user feedback and usability testing to iterate designs effectively, ensuring seamless interaction and visual consistency across platforms.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, basically it''s a UI design I''m using, like, for a background BG and a width length to work like animated kinds of UIX.","missing_concepts":["Collaboration with product managers and engineers","Use of design tools like Figma or Sketch","Creation of wireframes and prototypes","Reusable components and responsive design","User feedback and usability testing"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is largely unclear and vague. They mention ''background BG'' and ''animated kinds of UIX'' without explaining what they did or how it relates to UI design. There is no reference to tools, collaborative processes, or design methodologies. The answer does not demonstrate understanding of core UI design principles or problem-solving approaches. Clarity and relevance to the question are very low, resulting in a failing score. More concrete examples and structured explanation are needed.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate struggled to articulate their UI design experience effectively. Their response lacked technical detail, clarity, and relevance to the question. Key aspects such as tools, collaboration, prototyping, and user-focused design were missing. Overall, the answer did not meet the expectations for a product designer role."},{"prompt":"Could you give me an example of a specific UI you designed using animations?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":1,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Answer is too short and incomplete","Lacks any specific example or technical details","Does not address the question properly","No explanation of design choices or animation use"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"In a recent project, I designed an interactive onboarding flow for a mobile app where I integrated subtle animations to guide user focus and improve task completion rates. For example, I used micro-interactions to animate button presses and transitions that provided immediate visual feedback, enhancing user engagement. I employed CSS keyframe animations and React Transition Group to orchestrate smooth entrance and exit animations of UI elements, ensuring performance was not compromised. This approach not only improved the aesthetic appeal but also increased user retention by 15% as measured post-launch.","candidateAnswer":"That''s not much. I''m using a...","missing_concepts":["Specific UI example with animations","Technical implementation details","Impact or results of animation use","Use of relevant design and development tools"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response is extremely short and does not provide any meaningful information related to the question. There is no example of a UI design incorporating animations, no technical correctness or completeness, and no clarity. This answer suggests a lack of preparation or understanding of the question asked, resulting in a very low score across all criteria.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide a coherent or relevant answer to the question about designing a UI using animations. The response lacks detail, technical content, and any demonstration of problem-solving or communication skills. This answer would not meet the expectations for the role of product designer requiring UI animation experience."},{"prompt":"Could you describe any project where you applied UI animations successfully?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["Mentions React as a tool used for UI design."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["No description of any specific project or example involving UI animations.","No explanation of how animations were implemented or their impact.","Answer is vague and does not address the question directly.","Lacks demonstration of understanding or problem-solving related to UI animations."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"In a recent project redesigning a web application dashboard, I implemented UI animations to improve user feedback and engagement. For example, I used subtle fade-in effects and smooth transitions for loading data panels to indicate processing activity, which enhanced perceived performance. I also created animated hover states for interactive elements to provide clear affordances and improve usability. These animations were done using CSS and React animation libraries to ensure smooth performance and maintain responsiveness. The result was a more polished user experience with measurable increases in user satisfaction and decreased task completion time.","candidateAnswer":"Um...\\nLove it.\\nReact just helped me for UI designing for when I''m using a front-end in JavaScript. That''s the help for designing and understanding all this process.","missing_concepts":["Specific examples of UI animations used in a project.","Purpose and impact of animations on user experience.","Technical details on implementation methods (e.g., CSS, React animation libraries).","Evidence of measuring animation success or user feedback."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response is extremely vague and does not provide any meaningful information about applying UI animations in a project. They only briefly mention React related to UI design without describing any actual animation usage, its effect, or implementation details. There is no demonstration of problem-solving or understanding specific to the question asked. The answer does not meet even the minimal expectations and is considered insufficient for the role.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to provide a coherent or relevant example of applying UI animations in a project. The answer lacked technical detail and did not convey an understanding of the question scope. This indicates a poor grasp of practical UI animation application and problem-solving in product design."},{"prompt":"Tell me about your experience working with React.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have over 4 years of experience building user interfaces with React, designing reusable components and implementing responsive UI designs that align with product requirements. In my recent projects, I utilized React hooks extensively to manage component lifecycle and local state efficiently, improving performance and code maintainability. I collaborated closely with backend developers to integrate APIs using React''s context and managed global state for complex workflows using Redux when needed. This combination of UI design knowledge and React expertise enables me to deliver intuitive, scalable, and high-quality frontend experiences.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"How do you typically manage state in your React applications?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["Candidate indicates that state management is not challenging for them, implying some practical experience."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-7","weaknesses":["Does not describe any specific state management techniques or tools.","No mention of React hooks, context, or external libraries.","Answer is vague and does not address the question’s requirements.","Lacks demonstration of understanding of state management in React."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"In React applications, state management is typically handled using a combination of React''s built-in useState and useReducer hooks for local component state, while for more complex or global states, libraries like Redux or Zustand are employed. Context API is also used for passing state through the component tree without prop drilling when state sharing is minimal. The choice depends on the application''s scale and complexity, ensuring maintainability and performance.","candidateAnswer":"Not too much, it''s not giving any challenges, it''s easy for her to manage.","missing_concepts":["Use of useState and useReducer hooks for local state","Context API for prop drilling avoidance","State management libraries such as Redux or Zustand","Considerations based on application scale and complexity"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is too brief and vague. It fails to address the technical details about managing state in React applications. There''s no mention of any React-specific hooks, context, or state management libraries which are essential to demonstrate understanding in this area. The response also lacks clarity on how the candidate manages state or problem-solving approaches. Overall, it does not meet the expectations for a medium difficulty question on React state management.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has minimal insight into React state management and is unable to articulate key concepts or tools used. The answer is insufficient to demonstrate a solid understanding or practical approach. Recommend further training or clarification on React state management concepts."},{"prompt":"Can you share a bit more detail about how you handle state in one of your recent projects?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["The candidate acknowledges managing state."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-8","weaknesses":["Very vague and lacks any technical detail or explanation.","No mention of local versus global state or any state management tools or methods.","Does not demonstrate understanding of state concepts or best practices.","Answer is too short and does not address the question properly."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"In a recent project, I managed state by carefully distinguishing between local component state and global application state to optimize performance and maintainability. For local UI states like modal visibility or form inputs, I used React''s useState and useReducer hooks. For more complex or shared states such as user authentication data or theme settings, I implemented Context API combined with useReducer or integrated Redux for scalability. Additionally, I ensured state immutability and predictable updates by following best practices and used middleware like Redux Thunk for handling asynchronous actions. This approach allowed for clear data flow, easy debugging, and facilitated collaboration with frontend and backend teams.","candidateAnswer":"In my recent project, I managed all the states.","missing_concepts":["Distinguishing local vs global state","Use of React hooks like useState, useReducer","Use of Context API or Redux","State immutability and predictable updates","Handling asynchronous actions","Performance and maintainability considerations"],"detailed_feedback":"The answer provided is extremely brief and non-informative, merely stating that all states were managed without any elaboration. This does not demonstrate any technical knowledge or understanding of state management in React or UI design contexts. Important concepts like distinguishing between local and global state, specific tools such as useState, useReducer, Context API, or Redux, and best practices for predictable and maintainable state management are completely missing. The candidate needs to provide much more detailed and structured explanations to show competence.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate''s answer lacks depth, detail, and technical clarity needed for a product designer role dealing with state management. They did not showcase any relevant skills or understanding and failed to meet the expectations of the question."},{"prompt":"And what specific tools or libraries did you use for that state management?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-9","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"For state management in React applications, I typically use libraries like Redux or the Context API depending on the complexity of the project. Redux is preferred for larger applications needing predictable state transitions and middleware support, while Context API works well for simpler or medium-sized projects to avoid prop drilling. Additionally, I sometimes use libraries like Zustand or Recoil for more flexible and less boilerplate-heavy state management when working with complex component states.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"How do you ensure your UI designs are user-friendly?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["Mentioned React, which is relevant to UI design implementation"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-10","weaknesses":["Answer is extremely vague and incomplete","No mention of usability principles or design processes","Does not explain how to ensure user-friendliness","Lacks understanding or demonstration of problem solving in UI design","Communication is unclear and not informative"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"I ensure UI designs are user-friendly by prioritizing usability principles such as consistency, clarity, and accessibility throughout the design process. This involves conducting user research to understand target user needs and pain points, creating wireframes and prototypes to validate design decisions, and performing usability testing to gather feedback and iterate accordingly. Additionally, I align designs with established UI guidelines and ensure seamless interactions by collaborating closely with developers, often leveraging React components for responsiveness and accessibility.","candidateAnswer":"Thank you for helping and all.\\nfor using a React.","missing_concepts":["User research and understanding of user needs","Wireframing and prototyping for validation","Usability testing and iterative improvements","Consistency, clarity, and accessibility principles","Collaboration with developers and UI guidelines"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is too short and lacks any meaningful detail or explanation related to ensuring UI designs are user-friendly. It only references ''thank you'' and ''using React'' without addressing the core aspects of usability, research, testing, or design principles. The answer fails to demonstrate technical knowledge, problem-solving ability, or relevant processes. Overall, the answer does not meet expectations for the role and question.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows minimal understanding of how to create user-friendly UI designs. The answer is insufficient and lacks key concepts such as usability principles, user research, prototyping, testing, and collaboration, reflecting a very limited grasp of the requirements for a product designer role."},{"prompt":"tell me your self","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq9eelzy004zo501ix9ueatj","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq9fa1h7000hpb016ft5y9bg', 'cmq9f315i0001pb01dpggfzha', 19, 52, 45, 66, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-11 11:36:49.147', '2026-06-11 11:37:05.126', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["If there is any glitch or issue, you can show the error here. Okay. And from that error, you can see where there is a problem and where there is an issue. Okay. Mostly this happens. Yes. It will be written in the console that what is the issue and because of which it is coming.","I was talking in English for so long.","But I was speaking in English and you didn''t respond for almost 4 minutes. What happened to you?"]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 10, '[{"prompt":"Hi Ram, this is Sana from Test. Let''s begin. Can you tell me about a time when you faced a difficult challenge at work and how you handled it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["Mentions identifying issues through error messages."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Does not provide any specific work-related challenge or example.","No explanation of steps taken to handle the challenge.","Answer is vague and disconnected from the question context.","Lacks demonstration of problem-solving skills in the sales or service business context.","Overall irrelevant to the question asked."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe a specific workplace challenge related to sales or service delivery, such as a difficult negotiation, a lost client opportunity, or a service failure. They should explain the context clearly and outline the steps they took to address it, like analyzing the problem, communicating effectively with stakeholders, leveraging cross-functional teams, and adapting strategies to resolve the issue. For example, they might talk about salvaging a contract by renegotiating terms or working with technical teams to meet a tight service deadline, demonstrating resilience, problem-solving skills, and client focus. They should conclude by reflecting on the outcome and lessons learned that improved their approach in future situations.","candidateAnswer":"If there is any glitch or issue, you can show the error here. Okay. And from that error, you can see where there is a problem and where there is an issue. Okay. Mostly this happens. Yes. It will be written in the console that what is the issue and because of which it is coming.","missing_concepts":["Description of a specific workplace challenge.","Steps taken to resolve the challenge.","Communication with stakeholders.","Negotiation or strategic planning.","Reflection on outcome and lessons learned."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is largely irrelevant and does not address the question of describing a difficult challenge at work and how it was handled. The response seems to focus on identifying errors via the console, which is unrelated to sales or service business challenges. There is no example, no problem-solving process described, and no reflection on outcomes or lessons. The communication is unclear in terms of relevance and meaning. Overall, the candidate did not demonstrate the required skills or understanding expected for the role.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate failed to respond with a relevant example or demonstrate key skills such as negotiation, communication, or strategic problem-solving in a sales context. The answer was vague, off-topic, and lacked coherence, leading to an overall failing evaluation."},{"prompt":"How do you price an AMC contract?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq9f315i0002pb01sdmepwzh","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"What factors do you consider while preparing a service proposal for a corporate client?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq9f315i0003pb01ym6dnqtb","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"How do you calculate profitability for a long-term service contract?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq9f315i0004pb01rfictqts","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"What KPIs would you track for service delivery performance?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq9f315i0005pb014eolo4ep","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."},{"prompt":"How do you assess service requirements during a site visit?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq9f315i0006pb01t1kau4v1","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq9fojje001hpb01hp5gce7y', 'cmq9fgeo3000ppb01yvyl1c7m', 48, 70, 60, 82, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-11 11:48:05.738', '2026-06-11 11:48:56.695', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Yes, so I was working on a database project, which was to build a dashboard for solving new problems. So, the data that we had of our past projects were in different sources, text, Excel and in hard copied files and drawings. So, what we did is we made it into a single source of input for the dashboard. So, it took a lot of time and we had to employ almost 15 to 20 employees to do the same work.","What is an AMC contract?","So, to price an EMC contract, we take into consideration the services that we are going to offer to the clients, the amount of labor that will be required, the resources that will be deployed there, the duration for which the project would be going on. Based on all these considerations, we provide a contract and we price it."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 43, '[{"prompt":"Can you tell me about a time when you solved a difficult problem at work?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":3,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Described a problem involving disparate data sources","Mentioned resource mobilization with multiple employees","Some clarity in explanation"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Problem described is not directly related to sales or service contract management","Lacks detail on specific problem-solving techniques or strategic approach","No mention of negotiation, contract management or cross-functional collaboration","Outcome and impact on business goals not described","Vague on how the challenge was solved beyond basic data consolidation"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":4,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe a specific, challenging problem related to sales or service contract management, such as integrating disparate client requirements into a unified service offering or resolving a critical contract negotiation impasse. They would explain their approach methodically: identifying the root cause, collaborating across functions (sales, technical, legal), applying negotiation or strategic planning skills, and achieving a positive outcome that led to revenue growth or improved client satisfaction. For example, they might detail how they streamlined communication between clients and service teams to meet tight deadlines or customized an AMC pricing model to win a competitive bid. Throughout, the answer should demonstrate problem-solving under pressure, cross-functional coordination, and strategic thinking aligned with service business goals.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, so I was working on a database project, which was to build a dashboard for solving new problems. So, the data that we had of our past projects were in different sources, text, Excel and in hard copied files and drawings. So, what we did is we made it into a single source of input for the dashboard. So, it took a lot of time and we had to employ almost 15 to 20 employees to do the same work.","missing_concepts":["Negotiation skills","Strategic planning","Contract management","Cross-functional collaboration","Impact on client satisfaction or revenue growth"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate described a scenario involving consolidation of data from multiple sources into a single dashboard, which touches on a problem-solving context but is unrelated to sales or service business challenges expected for this role. The answer lacks relevant details about how the problem was identified, specific steps taken, cross-team collaboration, negotiation, or strategic planning reflective of a Senior Executive in Sales & Marketing. Additionally, the business impact or benefits achieved were not mentioned. Overall, the response is vague and incomplete in addressing the question from the perspective of the role''s key requirements.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate''s answer does not sufficiently demonstrate problem-solving skills in the context of sales and service contract challenges relevant to the role. The response lacks strategic depth, relevant business context, and key competencies such as negotiation and contract management, resulting in a failing evaluation."},{"prompt":"How do you price an AMC contract?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":1,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Did not address the question asked","No demonstration of relevant knowledge or process","No explanation or conceptual understanding shown"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Pricing an AMC contract involves assessing the scope and type of maintenance services offered, estimating the required labor and resources, incorporating parts and materials costs, and factoring in the contract duration. Additionally, considerations include expected service frequency, client-specific customization, risk contingencies, and competitive market rates to ensure profitability while remaining attractive to the client.","candidateAnswer":"What is an AMC contract?","missing_concepts":["Assessment of scope and type of maintenance services","Estimation of labor, resources, parts, and materials costs","Contract duration and service frequency considerations","Client customization and risk factors","Competitive market pricing and profitability"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response did not answer the question and instead asked a clarifying question regarding what an AMC contract is. This does not demonstrate any understanding or technical knowledge related to pricing AMC contracts. The answer is irrelevant and completely lacks completeness, technical correctness, and problem-solving. It is too short and does not provide any insight into the expected skills or process. Communication clarity is minimal but irrelevant.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate failed to provide any relevant answer about pricing AMC contracts. Lack of knowledge or unwillingness to answer led to a very low score. The candidate needs to prepare foundational knowledge and provide direct, detailed responses to technical questions in future interviews."},{"prompt":"An AMC is an Annual Maintenance Contract. Now, how do you go about pricing one?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Understanding of key pricing factors such as services offered, labor, resources, and project duration.","Answer is mostly relevant to the question.","Clear and understandable explanation."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Did not mention estimation of material costs or overheads.","Lacked discussion of risk factors and contract management considerations.","No mention of market benchmarking or competitive pricing.","Omitted strategic planning and negotiation aspects important for pricing."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"Pricing an AMC involves analyzing the scope and frequency of maintenance services required, estimating labor and material costs, factoring in resource allocation and overheads, and considering the contract duration and risk factors. Additionally, market benchmarks and competitive pricing strategies are incorporated to ensure profitability while remaining attractive to the client.","candidateAnswer":"So, to price an EMC contract, we take into consideration the services that we are going to offer to the clients, the amount of labor that will be required, the resources that will be deployed there, the duration for which the project would be going on. Based on all these considerations, we provide a contract and we price it.","missing_concepts":["Material costs estimation","Overheads and resource allocation","Risk factors and contract duration implications","Market benchmark and competitive pricing","Negotiation and strategic planning"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a basic understanding of pricing an AMC by focusing on services, labor, resources, and contract duration, which is technically correct and relevant. However, the answer lacks completeness as it omits critical elements such as material cost estimation, overheads, risk assessment, competitive market analysis, and strategic negotiation considerations. These missing points are essential for an accurate and profitable AMC pricing strategy. The communication is clear, but the problem-solving aspect appears partially developed due to missing strategic and analytical factors. Overall, the response is a good foundation but needs more depth and inclusion of key pricing components to meet expectations for the role.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate provides a basic but relevant approach to pricing an AMC focusing on core elements like labor and services. However, several important aspects such as risk factors, market benchmarks, and strategic negotiation are absent, reflecting an incomplete understanding. While communication is adequate, the candidate falls short on completeness and strategic insight required for senior-level s"},{"prompt":"What factors do you consider while preparing a service proposal for a corporate client?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Candidate identifies client requirements and complexity","Mentions duration of service and resource allocation","Considers location of service delivery","Acknowledges the importance of pricing structure"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Answer lacks mention of strategic alignment with client objectives","Does not address risks, compliance, or value-added services","Explanation is somewhat vague and incomplete","Limited mention of negotiation or contract management aspects"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"When preparing a service proposal for a corporate client, I consider the client''s specific requirements and service scope, including the complexity and scale of the project. I assess the duration and frequency of service delivery, resources needed such as manpower and equipment, and whether services are onsite or remote. Pricing structure and competitive market rates are analyzed alongside potential risks and compliance requirements. Finally, I factor in value-added services to differentiate our offer and ensure alignment with the client’s strategic objectives and budget constraints.","candidateAnswer":"Factors is basically again, first we look into the requirements of a client, how complex is the requirement for them, the duration for which we will be serving them, the complexity of the project and maybe the amount of resources that has to be deployed, whether we will ask them to work from our location or we have to take people to their location. So those are a few factors on which we collect all the information and then keeping tab on the pricing structure.","missing_concepts":["Alignment with client''s strategic objectives and budget","Assessment of potential risks and compliance requirements","Inclusion of value-added services to differentiate proposal","Competitive market rate analysis","Negotiation and contract management considerations"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a basic understanding of preparing a service proposal, correctly highlighting client requirements, project complexity, service duration, resources, location, and pricing. However, the response is incomplete, missing critical factors such as compliance, risk analysis, value-added services, and strategic alignment with the client’s objectives and budget. The communication is understandable but somewhat vague and lacks professional depth expected at a senior executive level. To improve, the candidate should provide a more structured and thorough approach, incorporating negotiation, contract management, and differentiating the proposal through value-added services and market analysis.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate has a reasonable grasp of key operational factors when preparing a service proposal, but falls short in addressing strategic and risk-related considerations. Their answer is relevant and mostly correct but incomplete and somewhat vague. Additional detail on compliance, value addition, and strategic alignment is necessary for a senior executive role. Overall, this answer does not meet"},{"prompt":"How do you calculate profitability for a long-term service contract?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Profitability for a long-term service contract is calculated by subtracting the total contract-related costs from the total revenue earned over the contract period. This involves carefully estimating and tracking all direct and indirect costs including manpower, materials, overheads, and any escalation or variable costs throughout the contract duration. The resulting gross profit margin percentage (Profit / Revenue * 100) indicates the contract''s profitability. Additionally, ongoing margin monitoring helps identify deviations early to maintain target profitability.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Take your time. Could you walk me through how you assess the costs and margins to figure out profitability?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":4,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Recognizes the importance of maintaining profit margins","Mentions cost cutting when profitability issues arise","Expresses focus on growth areas as part of strategy"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Does not describe how to assess or calculate costs and margins","Lacks specific mention of direct/indirect costs, gross margin, or contribution margin","No explanation of cost variance analysis or pricing strategy","Answer is vague and reactive rather than showing a proactive, systematic approach","Limited technical understanding demonstrated"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"To assess costs and margins for profitability, I start by accurately identifying all direct and indirect costs associated with service delivery, including labor, materials, overhead, and administrative expenses. Then, I calculate the gross margin by subtracting total costs from revenue generated by the contract, and express this as a percentage of revenue to evaluate profitability. Additionally, I analyze contribution margins to identify which contracts or services are most profitable and monitor cost variances against budgets to detect inefficiencies promptly. This detailed cost-margin analysis guides pricing strategies, contract negotiations, and decisions on cost control to ensure sustainable profitability.","candidateAnswer":"We assess the margins if we face difficulties in maintaining our profit margin to the pre-decided value then we start cutting costs and then focus on other growth areas.","missing_concepts":["Identification and classification of costs (direct, indirect, overhead)","Calculating gross margin and contribution margin","Analyzing cost variances against budgets","Using margin analysis to guide pricing and negotiation","Proactive profitability analysis rather than only reacting to issues"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s response lacks the necessary detail and technical depth expected for this role. While they acknowledge the importance of maintaining profit margins and cost control, they fail to describe how costs and margins are actually assessed or analyzed. Key concepts such as separating direct and indirect costs, calculating gross and contribution margins, and using margin data to make strategic decisions are missing. The approach described is reactive (cutting costs only when profitability declines) rather than demonstrating a systematic and data-driven process. Communication is somewhat clear but the explanation is too brief and vague to demonstrate a solid understanding. Overall, the candidate shows a weak grasp of how profitability assessment works in a service business context.","interviewer_summary":"The answer did not adequately address the question or demonstrate the candidate’s ability to systematically assess costs and margins to figure out profitability. The response was too generic and reactive without touching on important financial metrics and analysis techniques critical for the role. This indicates insufficient technical knowledge and experience with profitability evaluation methods,"},{"prompt":"What KPIs would you track for service delivery performance?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Key KPIs for service delivery performance include Service Level Agreement (SLA) compliance to ensure timely resolution, First-Time Fix Rate (FTFR) to measure efficiency in issue resolution, Customer Satisfaction Score (CSAT) to gauge client experience, Average Resolution Time to track how quickly issues are addressed, and Contract Renewal Rate to assess ongoing service value and client retention. Monitoring these ensures that service delivery aligns with contractual commitments and business objectives.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"How do you assess service requirements during a site visit?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Indicates interaction with multiple stakeholders at the site","Recognizes the importance of understanding pain points and documenting them","Mentions collecting feedback on proposed solutions"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-7","weaknesses":["Lacks mention of systematic evaluation of operational environment and service infrastructure","Does not specify reviewing compliance standards or maintenance records","No reference to tailored contract proposals or aligning with client objectives","Explanation is brief and lacks detail on methods used during assessment"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"During a site visit, I systematically evaluate the client''s operational environment, existing service infrastructure, and specific pain points by engaging key stakeholders and end users. I document all service gaps, verify compliance standards, and identify opportunities for customized solutions aligned with client objectives and our service capabilities. This assessment combines direct observation, structured interviews, and review of current maintenance records to develop a comprehensive understanding that supports tailored contract proposals and sustainable service delivery plans.","candidateAnswer":"We usually try to interact with as many people as possible at the site, understand their pain points, document them, get the feedback on the proposed solutions and go ahead.","missing_concepts":["Systematic evaluation of operational environment and existing service infrastructure","Verification of compliance and standards","Review of maintenance records","Developing tailored contract proposals and sustainable service plans","Engagement through structured interviews besides general interaction"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows a basic understanding of assessing service requirements by mentioning engagement with multiple stakeholders and documenting pain points. However, the answer lacks depth and key components such as a systematic approach, compliance verification, and review of existing maintenance records. The candidate also misses strategic elements like aligning solutions with client objectives or preparing tailored proposals, which are critical for this role. Communication is clear but minimal and does not demonstrate comprehensive problem-solving. Overall, the response is incomplete and somewhat vague, failing to fully meet the expectations for a senior sales and marketing executive in service business.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate has some awareness of the importance of stakeholder interaction and feedback collection during site visits but falls short of providing a thorough, structured, and strategic approach required for assessing service requirements. More detailed technical knowledge and strategic planning insight would be necessary to consider them ready for the role."}]'), ('cmq9ftrsv0029pb01snumdrbw', 'cmq9fmiop000wpb01jv6j4wk0', 41, 63, 54, 90, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-11 11:52:09.727', '2026-06-11 11:55:12.765', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["I worked on two projects. First, I deployed a static website on EC2 using Nuggets. And second, I hosted a website using S3 and CloudFront. This project helped me to understand networking, permission, and deployment.","Basically, I have worked mainly C2 like a virtual server service that provides a scalable computer resource for hosting applications and websites.","Sorry, I can''t get you um security group are stateful and work at instance level like I don''t think so"]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 40, '[{"prompt":"Can you tell me about a challenging project you worked on recently and what your role was?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Mentions working with EC2, S3, and CloudFront which are relevant AWS services.","Indicates some experience with networking, permissions, and deployment."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["The description is vague and lacks detail about specific technical challenges or their direct role.","No mention of VPC configuration, IAM roles, security groups, or how problems were solved.","Does not explain what Nuggets is or its relevance, which is unclear or possibly incorrect terminology.","Fails to clearly articulate their specific contributions or role in the projects."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific project involving AWS services, highlighting technical challenges and their direct contributions. For example, they might explain deploying an application on EC2 instances within a custom VPC, configuring networking and IAM roles for secure access, and optimizing cost or performance. The answer should mention their role, such as architecting the solution, defining infrastructure, setting up security groups, and collaborating with development teams to ensure deployment success.","candidateAnswer":"I worked on two projects. First, I deployed a static website on EC2 using Nuggets. And second, I hosted a website using S3 and CloudFront. This project helped me to understand networking, permission, and deployment.","missing_concepts":["VPC and networking configuration details","IAM role and security group setup","Explanation of the challenges faced and how they were addressed","Clarification on candidate''s role in the projects","Cost or performance optimization measures"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate vaguely mentions deploying a static website on EC2 and hosting a website using S3 and CloudFront, which demonstrates some familiarity with AWS services. However, the explanation is superficial, lacking key technical details such as networking setup (VPC), permission management (IAM roles), or security (security groups). The candidate does not clearly state their specific role in these projects or the challenges encountered and how they resolved them. The mention of ''Nuggets'' is unclear and might indicate uncertainty about the tools used. To meet expectations for this role, candidates should provide a detailed account of their architectural decisions, problem-solving approaches, and their direct contributions to AWS deployments with a focus on security and optimization.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a basic understanding of some AWS services but provides an incomplete and vague answer without technical depth or clarity on their role and problem-solving strategies. They do not sufficiently address the question about a challenging project or highlight relevant AWS architectural skills. Overall, the response is below the expected level for an AWS Solution Architect."},{"prompt":"What was your specific responsibility in the EC2 deployment?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":3,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":4,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Candidate recognizes EC2 as a virtual server service for scalable computing resources"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Answer confuses EC2 with ''C2'', indicating possible lack of familiarity","Did not mention any specific responsibilities related to deployment","No mention of provisioning, configuration, security, networking, or automation","Answer is very brief and vague without technical detail"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"My specific responsibility in the EC2 deployment included provisioning and configuring EC2 instances according to application requirements, selecting appropriate instance types, managing security groups and key pairs, ensuring proper network configuration within the VPC, and automating deployment processes using scripts or AWS tools like CloudFormation. I also monitored instance performance and managed scaling policies to maintain availability and cost efficiency.","candidateAnswer":"Basically, I have worked mainly C2 like a virtual server service that provides a scalable computer resource for hosting applications and websites.","missing_concepts":["Provisioning and configuring EC2 instances","Instance type selection","Security groups and key management","Network configuration within VPC","Automation with scripts or AWS tools like CloudFormation","Monitoring performance and scaling policies"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer lacks relevance and completeness regarding their specific responsibilities in the EC2 deployment. While there is an attempt to describe EC2 as a virtual server service, it is technically vague and contains a possible typo (''C2''). The answer does not cover any concrete tasks performed during deployment such as configuration, security, network settings, or automation. Overall, it suggests poor understanding and preparation, providing minimal insight into the candidate''s actual role or technical contribution.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrated very limited understanding and did not adequately describe their specific responsibilities in the EC2 deployment process. The answer is too brief, vague, and does not address key expected points. The candidate failed to convey meaningful technical knowledge or involvement in the deployment. Recommend further technical training or experience before advancing."},{"prompt":"Can you explain how you configured the security groups for that EC2 instance?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":1,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Incorrect statement about security groups not being stateful","Did not explain how security groups were configured","Did not mention inbound or outbound rules","Lacked demonstration of understanding or problem solving","Answer was too short and unclear"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"Security groups act as virtual firewalls that control inbound and outbound traffic at the instance level. I configured the security group by defining specific inbound rules that allowed only the required protocols, ports, and source IP ranges necessary for the EC2 instance’s operation, such as SSH (port 22) from trusted IPs for administration, and outbound rules permitting all traffic or restricted destinations as needed. I ensured that the security group was stateful, so return traffic is automatically allowed. Additionally, I regularly reviewed and updated these rules to follow the principle of least privilege, minimizing the attack surface.","candidateAnswer":"Sorry, I can''t get you um security group are stateful and work at instance level like I don''t think so","missing_concepts":["Security groups act as virtual firewalls at instance level","Security groups are stateful","Inbound and outbound rule configuration","Defining specific protocols, ports, and source IP ranges","Principle of least privilege and regular rule review"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate gave an incorrect statement about security groups not being stateful and failed to explain how they configured the security groups for the EC2 instance. The answer was very short, unclear, and demonstrated a lack of understanding of the key concepts such as statefulness, rule configuration, and security best practices. There was no mention of inbound/outbound rules or any example protocols/ports used. Overall, the answer did not address the question meaningfully and lacked technical correctness and completeness.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate showed limited knowledge on EC2 security group configuration, providing an incorrect statement and no real details. They failed to convey understanding or problem solving ability relevant to the question."},{"prompt":"No problem. Let me clarify. How did you manage the inbound and outbound rules in the security group for your EC2 instance?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":5,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":4,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Correctly identified that security groups are stateful and work at the instance level.","Mentioned the distinction between security groups and NACLs."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Did not explain how inbound and outbound rules were specifically managed for the EC2 instance.","No mention of protocols, ports, or source/destination specifications for rules.","Lacked explanation on least privilege principle or examples of rules.","Answer was vague and lacked completeness and depth about security group rule management."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":4,"expectedAnswer":"Security groups act as virtual firewalls for EC2 instances and are stateful, meaning if you allow an inbound rule, the corresponding outbound response is automatically allowed. To manage inbound and outbound rules, I specify traffic protocols, ports, and source/destination IP addresses or security groups explicitly—for example, allowing inbound SSH (port 22) from trusted IPs and outbound HTTP/HTTPS to the internet. I ensure the rules follow least privilege principles by only opening necessary ports and restricting IP ranges to enhance security.","candidateAnswer":"Basically security group and I work on NACL like security group are stateful and work at instance level and NACL are stateless and work at the subnet level.","missing_concepts":["Specifying inbound and outbound rules for security groups with protocols, ports, and IP ranges.","Least privilege principle in rule configuration.","Explanation of how outbound rules complement inbound rules in security groups.","Details about managing and configuring security groups effectively."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate correctly stated that security groups are stateful and operate at the instance level, and that network ACLs are stateless and operate at the subnet level. However, the answer did not address the core question of how inbound and outbound rules were managed for the EC2 instance specifically. There was no detail on rule specifications such as protocols, ports, and allowed IPs, nor was there mention of applying least privilege principles. The response lacked completeness and clarity, providing only a basic distinction between security groups and NACLs without elaboration relevant to the question.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates a basic understanding of the difference between security groups and network ACLs, recognizing the stateful versus stateless nature and their scope. However, they failed to explain how they specifically managed inbound and outbound rules for an EC2 instance security group. This shows weak practical knowledge in configuring security groups to enforce access controls. The a"},{"prompt":"Now, tell me about your background and how it maps to this AWS Solutions Architect role.","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Candidate correctly mentions foundational knowledge in computer science.","Candidate references core AWS services such as EC2, S3, IAM, and VPC.","Candidate provides specific examples of deploying static websites using EC2, S3, and CloudFront."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Lacks detail on hands-on experience with architectural design, security best practices, and cost optimization.","Does not clearly explain how their experience maps to solution architect responsibilities.","Missing mention of VPC design beyond just knowing the service name.","Limited insight into understanding of AWS architectural principles or scalable solutions."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"I have a foundational background in computer science with hands-on experience in cloud computing, particularly AWS. I''ve worked extensively with core AWS services such as EC2 for compute resources, S3 for storage solutions, IAM for security management, and VPC for network isolation and design. In my projects, I have deployed applications using these services, designed secure and scalable architectures, and implemented best practices for cloud security and cost optimization. This practical experience, combined with my understanding of AWS architectural principles, directly aligns with the responsibilities of an AWS Solutions Architect, enabling me to design effective cloud solutions tailored to business needs.","candidateAnswer":"Okay, I''ve completed my VTech in Computer Science and I''m currently building my career in cloud and DevOps. I have been learning in AWS services like EC2, S3, IAM and VPC and implementing them through hands-on projects, I have deployed a static website on EC2 and another website using S3 and CloudFront.","missing_concepts":["Designing secure and scalable architectures","Cloud security best practices","Cost optimization techniques","Architectural principles of AWS solutions"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates basic familiarity with important AWS services relevant to the Solutions Architect role, such as EC2, S3, IAM, and VPC, and provides examples of deploying websites which show practical exposure. However, the answer lacks depth in explaining architectural design, security considerations, scalability, and cost optimization—key components for this role. The response also doesn''t clearly tie their background and projects to the broader responsibilities of a Solutions Architect or illustrate clear problem-solving skills in cloud architecture. Improving the explanation of how these technical abilities map to the role and adding details about best practices and architectural frameworks would strengthen the response.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has foundational AWS knowledge and practical deployment experience but falls short of demonstrating a strong understanding of AWS architectural principles and the full scope of a Solutions Architect''s responsibilities. Overall, the answer is moderately relevant and clear but incomplete for a medium-difficulty role, resulting in a fail."},{"prompt":"How comfortable are you working with designing VPC architectures?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Candidate correctly identifies VPC as an isolated virtual network.","Mentions creation of subnets and internet gateways.","Acknowledges control of traffic and security via route tables and gateways."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Incorrectly refers to ''root tables'' instead of ''route tables'', indicating possible lack of familiarity.","Answer lacks mention of important VPC components like CIDR blocks, NAT gateways, security groups, network ACLs.","No mention of multi-AZ architecture or hybrid cloud connectivity like VPC peering or VPN connections.","Explanation is too brief and lacks detail to demonstrate strong understanding."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"I am comfortable designing VPC architectures, including creating and configuring VPCs with appropriate CIDR blocks, public and private subnets, route tables, internet gateways, and NAT gateways to enable secure and scalable network segmentation. I understand how to apply security groups and network ACLs to control traffic within and across subnets, and how to architect multi-AZ deployments for high availability. I have hands-on experience setting up VPC peering and VPN connections for hybrid cloud scenarios.","candidateAnswer":"VPC is an isolated virtual network where we create subnets, root tables and internet gateways to control traffic security.","missing_concepts":["CIDR block configuration","Distinction between public and private subnets","NAT gateways for outbound internet access from private subnets","Security groups and network ACLs for traffic control","Multi-AZ design for high availability","VPC peering and VPN for hybrid connectivity"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows a basic understanding that a VPC is an isolated network with components like subnets and internet gateways to control traffic. However, the answer is incomplete and contains some inaccuracies (e.g., ''root tables'' instead of ''route tables''). Important aspects of VPC design such as CIDR block assignment, subnet segmentation (public/private), NAT gateways, and security enforcement via security groups and network ACLs were not addressed. Additionally, advanced concepts like multi-AZ deployments and hybrid connectivity solutions were missing. The answer is brief and lacks depth, indicating only a partial grasp of VPC architecture design. For a solution architect role, more comprehensive and precise knowledge is expected.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate demonstrates a rudimentary familiarity with VPC components but lacks sufficient detail and accuracy to be considered comfortable with designing VPC architectures. More practical knowledge and understanding are needed before considering the candidate ready for this role."},{"prompt":"Can you give an example of how you''ve handled subnet configuration in a VPC?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"When configuring subnets in a VPC, I typically start by dividing the IP address range (CIDR block) into smaller subnets to separate resources for security and architectural needs. For example, I create public subnets that have routes to the Internet Gateway to host resources like web servers, and private subnets without direct internet access for databases or internal services. I ensure each subnet is placed in different Availability Zones to increase fault tolerance and high availability. Additionally, I configure routing tables to control traffic flow between subnets and external networks according to security policies.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"How have you used IAM to manage access in your projects?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":4,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Mentions roles and temporary credentials which are more secure than access keys","References the principle of least privilege","Indicates use of groups and roles for permissions"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-7","weaknesses":["Answer is vague and fragmented, making it hard to follow","Does not clearly explain how IAM policies are used","No mention of creating users or detailed management of permissions","Does not reference specific AWS resources like EC2, S3, or VPC","Lacks explanation of cross-account access or trust policies"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"I use AWS IAM to define fine-grained permissions by creating IAM users, groups, and roles following the principle of least privilege. Typically, I assign roles to resources and users to enable secure, temporary access using IAM policies that specify allowed actions on AWS services such as EC2, S3, and VPC. For cross-account access or application permissions, I leverage IAM roles with trust policies and temporary security credentials to enhance security and manageability.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, I am a role provider temporary credential and are more secure than access key like used to manage a user group role and a permission security following the least privilege principle.","missing_concepts":["Creation and use of IAM users and groups explicitly","IAM policies attached to roles, users, or groups","Use of roles for cross-account access or applications","Examples of managed AWS services (EC2, S3, VPC)","Explanation of trust policies and temporary security credentials in detail"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows some awareness of IAM concepts such as roles, temporary credentials, and the least privilege principle, which indicates partial understanding. However, the answer is very fragmented and lacks clarity, making it difficult to fully grasp their approach to managing access. Key aspects such as IAM policy attachment, managing users and groups, and how roles facilitate cross-account or application permissions were missing. Furthermore, the candidate did not mention AWS services typically managed via IAM like EC2, S3, or VPC, weakening the completeness and relevance of the answer. Overall, the explanation fell short of adequately demonstrating solid knowledge and practical application, resulting in a fail.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate has a fragmented and unclear understanding of AWS IAM. They touch on roles and the least privilege principle but fail to explain the broader use of IAM users, policies, and AWS resources. Their answer lacks completeness and clarity, showing a basic but incomplete grasp of IAM functionality. They need to improve explanation skills and cover core IAM concepts in detail."},{"prompt":"One final question: how do you ensure high availability in an S3-based architecture?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":2,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["The answer correctly identifies S3 as object storage."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-8","weaknesses":["Answer is extremely short and lacks any explanation of how to ensure high availability.","No mention of S3''s multi-AZ replication or durability guarantees.","No discussion of versioning, cross-region replication, retries, or caching strategies.","Does not demonstrate understanding of high availability concepts in S3 architecture."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":1,"expectedAnswer":"Amazon S3 is designed for 99.999999999% durability and 99.99% availability by default, replicating data across multiple geographically separated Availability Zones. To ensure high availability in an S3-based architecture, you leverage its inherent multi-AZ replication and consider versioning and cross-region replication (CRR) to maintain availability in case of region-wide failures. Additionally, design your application to retry failed requests gracefully and distribute load efficiently using features like S3 Transfer Acceleration or CloudFront caching.","candidateAnswer":"S3 is provide object storage.","missing_concepts":["S3 multi-AZ replication for durability and availability","Versioning to protect against accidental deletion or overwrite","Cross-region replication (CRR) to handle region-wide failures","Application-level retries and error handling","Use of Transfer Acceleration or CloudFront to improve availability and performance"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer is too brief and does not address the question of ensuring high availability in an S3-based architecture. While correctly identifying S3 as object storage, the answer fails to elaborate on critical aspects such as the inherent multi-AZ data durability, replication strategies, and design considerations like versioning or cross-region replication. There is no indication of understanding how to design for high availability, retry logic, or the use of other AWS features that enhance availability. This indicates a very weak grasp of the key concepts related to S3 high availability.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates minimal understanding of S3''s features related to high availability. The response is insufficient and incomplete, lacking critical details expected from an AWS Solution architect. The candidate did not adequately address the question, resulting in a failing score."},{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq9fmiop000xpb01n8ej31j3","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have a foundational background in cloud computing with hands-on experience in designing and deploying AWS infrastructure, including EC2 instances, S3 storage solutions, and configuring VPCs to ensure secure networking. During my previous internship/project, I developed scalable cloud architectures emphasizing security and cost optimization. I am familiar with AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) for defining roles and permissions to enforce least privilege access. This experience aligns well with the responsibilities expected in this junior AWS Solution Architect role, allowing me to contribute effectively to designing and implementing cloud solutions that meet business needs while adhering to AWS best practices.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq9giywj000vqo01j8rfnsp8', 'cmq9gb46t0003qo01zzg9dlnt', 57, 69, 59, 100, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-11 12:11:45.331', '2026-06-11 12:13:04.941', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hello.","I am Sam. I have five years of experience in product design and development. I have worked for three companies My role has been designing 2d and 3d models then conceptualization and design of Software products as well. I''ve worked for e-commerce platform development as well","Yes, so my current role is basically prototyping and conceptualization. So I convert ideas into realities by framing and developing mock-ups, which I convert into prototypes and then final design is taken care of by the engineering."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 53, '[{"prompt":"Hi Sam, I’m Sana from TEST. It’s great to have you here. Let’s dive right in: can you tell me about a time when you solved a challenging problem using data analysis?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe a specific instance where they identified a complex issue impacting product performance or user experience, collected and analyzed relevant quantitative and qualitative data to understand root causes, and applied their findings to drive actionable design or development changes. They would detail the tools or methods used (e.g., analytics platforms, user behavior tracking, A/B testing), how insights informed decision-making, and the measurable positive impact (such as improved UI metrics, increased user engagement, or resolution of a critical bug). This answer should demonstrate analytical rigor applied in a product design or development context and cross-functional collaboration if applicable.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Hello Sam, my name is Sana. I’ll be conducting this interview with you today. Let’s begin. Tell me about yourself.","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Mentioned five years of experience in product design and development","Included experience with e-commerce platform development","Referenced both design and software product conceptualization"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Did not mention UI design specifically","No mention of React or front-end development skills","Designing 2D and 3D models is not clearly connected to product design or UI/UX focus","Lacks detail on collaboration with engineering teams or user-centered design principles"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"I am a seasoned product designer with over five years of experience specializing in UI design and front-end development using React. My expertise spans designing intuitive user interfaces, creating interactive prototypes, and collaborating closely with engineering teams to translate design concepts into functional products. I have contributed to e-commerce platforms and SaaS products by driving end-to-end design processes from user research to final implementation, ensuring both usability and technical feasibility. In this role, I leverage my deep understanding of user-centered design principles and advanced React skills to deliver scalable and engaging digital experiences.","candidateAnswer":"I am Sam. I have five years of experience in product design and development. I have worked for three companies My role has been designing 2d and 3d models then conceptualization and design of Software products as well. I''ve worked for e-commerce platform development as well","missing_concepts":["UI design expertise","React or front-end development skills","User research or user-centered design process","Collaborating with engineering teams to translate designs","End-to-end design process for SaaS or e-commerce products"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a brief overview of their experience but missed several key aspects expected for the role. They mentioned five years of experience and some involvement with e-commerce platforms, which aligns partially with the ideal answer. However, they did not demonstrate specific skills in UI design or React, which are crucial for this position. The answer touched upon designing 2D and 3D models but did not clarify how this relates to product design or UI. Additionally, the candidate did not address collaboration with engineering teams or the user-centered design process. Their communication was generally understandable but lacked detail and focus on relevant skills. Overall, the answer is only partially correct and incomplete, leading to a failing score.","interviewer_summary":"Sam has moderate experience in product design and mentions working on e-commerce platforms and software product conceptualization. However, he lacks specific UI design and React expertise expected for this role. The answer lacks depth about the design process and collaboration with engineers, resulting in a partial but insufficient response. Further probing would be needed to assess suitability."},{"prompt":"Thanks for sharing that, Sam. Let’s dive a bit deeper: could you describe your current role and the key responsibilities you handle?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Candidate demonstrates understanding of prototyping and conceptualization as part of design role","Answer is mostly relevant to the question about current role"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Lacks mention of key aspects such as user research, collaboration with engineers, and end-to-end design process","Does not address alignment with user needs or business goals","No indication of involvement with UI design or technical details like React","Answer is vague and missing completeness on responsibilities"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"In my current role as a product designer, I lead the end-to-end design process from research and ideation through prototyping to final UI handoff, ensuring alignment with user needs and business goals. My key responsibilities include conducting user research, developing user personas and user journeys, creating wireframes and interactive prototypes, collaborating closely with engineers—particularly on React implementation details—and iterating designs based on testing feedback. I also facilitate cross-functional communication to maintain design consistency and usability across product iterations.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, so my current role is basically prototyping and conceptualization. So I convert ideas into realities by framing and developing mock-ups, which I convert into prototypes and then final design is taken care of by the engineering.","missing_concepts":["Conducting user research","Developing user personas and user journeys","Collaboration with engineering teams, especially regarding React implementation","Iterating designs based on feedback","Cross-functional communication and design consistency"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a partial description of their role focusing on prototyping and conceptualization, which is relevant but very high-level and incomplete. Important responsibilities such as user research, user journey development, collaboration with engineers, and ensuring alignment with user needs and business goals were not mentioned. The explanation lacks depth and does not sufficiently demonstrate a comprehensive understanding of the full scope of a product designer''s role. Communication was somewhat clear but could be more structured and detailed. Overall, the answer shows partial correctness but misses many critical responsibilities and technical details expected for the role.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows awareness of prototyping and concept development in their role but fails to articulate the full scope of responsibilities that include research, collaboration, iteration, and business alignment. Their description lacks technical depth and completeness, indicating a surface-level understanding of their duties as a product designer."},{"prompt":"And how do you ensure that your prototypes align with user needs?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Candidate understands the importance of gathering user requirements and developing user stories.","References user flows as a step in the process to ensure requirements are addressed."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Lacks mention of involving users throughout the design process through usability testing or feedback sessions.","Does not describe iterative validation or adjustments based on real user input.","Explanation is vague and somewhat repetitive, lacking detail and depth."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"To ensure prototypes align with user needs, I begin by thoroughly gathering and analyzing user requirements through interviews, surveys, and user personas. I translate these requirements into detailed user stories and flows that guide the prototype development. Throughout the design process, I involve users regularly to validate assumptions via usability testing and feedback sessions, iterating on the prototype based on real user input to ensure alignment with their goals and pain points.","candidateAnswer":"So we gather user requirements from We gather user requirements and develop user stories before making the prototypes based on every user story we prepare user flows and based on that we Make sure that the user requirements are taken care of","missing_concepts":["User involvement in usability testing or feedback during prototyping.","Iteration based on user feedback to refine prototypes.","Specific methods to validate prototypes align with user goals and pain points."],"detailed_feedback":"While the candidate correctly identifies key initial steps such as gathering requirements, creating user stories, and mapping user flows, the answer lacks depth in describing how to ensure alignment beyond the initial design phase. The absence of usability testing, user feedback sessions, and iteration based on real user data are critical gaps. Communication is somewhat unclear and repetitive, which hinders complete understanding. To improve, the candidate should discuss continuous user involvement and iterative refinement to truly confirm prototype alignment with user needs.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows basic understanding of designing prototypes with user needs in mind but misses important aspects of user validation and iteration. The answer is incomplete and only partially clear, resulting in a fail for this question."},{"prompt":"Now, can you walk me through your process for UI design?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Mentions use of Figma, which is appropriate for UI design.","Describes a basic process starting with wireframing and iterative changes."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Explanation is very brief and lacks detail.","Does not mention understanding user needs, stakeholder input, or business goals.","Misses key steps such as user flow, prototyping, usability testing, accessibility, and cross-functional collaboration.","Communication lacks clarity and professionalism; too informal and vague."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"My UI design process begins with understanding user needs and business goals through research and stakeholder interviews. I then create low-fidelity wireframes to establish layout and user flow, iterating based on feedback. After that, I develop high-fidelity prototypes using tools like Figma or Sketch to refine visual design and interactions. I involve cross-functional teams for feedback and perform usability testing to validate designs before handing off detailed specs to developers. Throughout, I prioritize accessibility, consistency, and responsiveness to ensure a seamless user experience.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, so for UI design I use Figma and first I do wireframing and then making a few changes in that and then finally going to the final product.","missing_concepts":["User research and understanding user needs","Stakeholder interviews and business goals alignment","Low-fidelity wireframes to high-fidelity prototypes transition","Usability testing and validation","Accessibility and responsiveness considerations","Cross-functional team involvement","Detailed handoff to developers","Prioritizing consistency in design"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate recognizes the importance of wireframing and using Figma in their UI design process, which shows some awareness of standard tools and basic workflow. However, the answer is very limited in scope and lacks depth, missing critical stages such as understanding user needs, business goals, iterative feedback loops, prototyping, usability testing, and accessibility practices. The explanation is too brief and informal, which reduces clarity and does not convey a professional or comprehensive understanding of the UI design process. To improve, the candidate should elaborate on each step, include user-centered design practices, mention collaboration with stakeholders and developers, and touch on quality assurance through testing.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has a rudimentary understanding of UI design tools and the concept of iterative wireframing but fails to demonstrate a comprehensive and structured design process. They do not address key aspects like user research, prototyping, and validation, which are essential for a product designer role. Communication is unclear and too brief. Overall, the answer shows partial knowledge but lacks th"},{"prompt":"Thanks for explaining. How do you typically gather feedback on your UI designs?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Recognizes the importance of gathering user feedback","Indicates making changes based on feedback"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Very vague and lacks detail about methods used to gather feedback","Does not mention usability testing, collaboration with teams, or quantitative feedback tools","Incomplete explanation of the feedback process","Lacks clear communication and professional terminology"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"I gather feedback on UI designs through multiple channels to ensure a comprehensive understanding: first, I conduct usability testing sessions with representative users to observe interactions and identify pain points. I also collaborate closely with cross-functional teams—product managers, developers, and QA—to gather their insights. Additionally, I use surveys and feedback forms post-release to collect quantitative and qualitative data. I prioritize feedback that impacts usability and visual clarity, iterating designs accordingly to improve user experience.","candidateAnswer":"I ask my users, I collect certain samples and then from there I make the changes.","missing_concepts":["Usability testing sessions with users","Cross-functional team collaboration (product managers, developers, QA)","Surveys and feedback forms for quantitative and qualitative data","Prioritization of feedback based on usability and visual clarity","Iterative design improvements"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a basic understanding of the need to gather user feedback and to make changes accordingly, which is a foundational concept in UI design. However, the answer is too vague and lacks critical details about how feedback is gathered and from whom. There is no mention of structured methods such as usability testing, collaboration with other stakeholders, or using surveys for quantitative data. The explanation does not reflect a comprehensive or systematic approach and is communicated in a minimal and unclear manner. Overall, the answer falls short of demonstrating a solid grasp of typical feedback processes in UI design.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a minimal understanding of gathering feedback but fails to articulate important methods and collaborative processes essential for effective UI design feedback loops. They need improvement in detail, completeness, and clarity to meet our expectations for a product designer role."},{"prompt":"Let’s move on to your experience with React. How comfortable are you working with it?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Candidate states specific experience of three years with React","Mentions use of React in practical projects (e-commerce platforms)","References creating reusable React elements, implying understanding of component design"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Lacks details on use of React features like hooks, state management, lifecycle methods","Does not mention performance optimization or collaboration aspects","Answer is brief and somewhat vague without elaborating on complexity or scale"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"I am highly comfortable working with React, having used it extensively over multiple projects spanning at least 3-5 years. I have built scalable and maintainable UI components, leveraged React hooks and context for state and side effects, and integrated with various state management libraries (like Redux or Zustand) when appropriate. My experience also includes optimizing React applications for performance, managing component lifecycles, and collaborating across teams to deliver consistent user interfaces aligned with design requirements.","candidateAnswer":"I''m very comfortable. I have three years of experience working with react and used it in the e-commerce platforms that I have developed react elements for reusability","missing_concepts":["Use of React hooks and context","State management libraries (Redux, Zustand)","Optimization and performance considerations","Component lifecycle management","Cross-team collaboration and design alignment"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a baseline level of comfort with React and has practical experience in building reusable components for e-commerce platforms, which is good. However, the answer is quite brief and lacks depth. Key advanced concepts such as the use of hooks, context, state management libraries, performance optimizations, and lifecycle methods are absent. These are important to evaluate true proficiency in React. Communication is clear but doesn''t provide enough insight into problem-solving skills or technical mastery. Overall, the answer is partially correct and relevant but incomplete for the expectations of this role.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows some practical React experience with reusable components and a few years of usage, indicating familiarity. However, the response is too concise and missing critical aspects of React development (hooks, state management, optimization), limiting assessment of deeper understanding or problem-solving abilities. Would benefit from probing further for detailed examples or advanced React "},{"prompt":"Great. Can you share an example of a complex component you built in React?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":4,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Candidate mentioned React components they have developed."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-7","weaknesses":["Answer lacks depth about the complexity of components.","No mention of advanced features, state management, or performance considerations.","Vague examples like carousel and presentations without technical details."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a React component that involved advanced functionality and architectural considerations. For example, building a dynamic, reusable data table with features like pagination, sorting, filtering, and asynchronous data fetching. They should explain the component’s structure, use of hooks or state management libraries like Redux or Context API for managing state, and how they ensured performance optimization and code maintainability.","candidateAnswer":"Complex component, yeah. So there have been a few components like carousel and presentations that I have developed in React.","missing_concepts":["Use of hooks or state management libraries like Redux or Context API.","Handling of asynchronous data fetching.","Techniques for performance optimization.","Component architecture and reusability."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a very brief and vague answer, mentioning only generic components like carousels and presentations without elaborating on any complex functionality or architectural decisions. They did not demonstrate understanding of advanced React concepts such as state management, asynchronous data handling, or performance optimization expected for a complex component. The answer is relevant but lacks completeness and clarity, indicating weak problem-solving and technical depth.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate showed minimal understanding of building complex React components. Their answer does not meet the expectations for the role, as it lacks detail and demonstrates insufficient knowledge of advanced React patterns and state management. This indicates the candidate is not yet ready to tackle complex UI design challenges in React."},{"prompt":"And how did you handle state management in those components?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-8","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I managed state in components primarily using React''s built-in hooks like useState for local component state and useReducer for more complex state logic. For shared or global state across multiple components, I utilized Context API or integrated external libraries such as Redux when the application required scalable state management. Additionally, I ensured state changes were efficient and minimal to avoid unnecessary re-renders, improving performance and user experience.","candidateAnswer":"Hmm, I don''t know.","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"How do you approach collaboration with developers when handing off your designs?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Answer is relevant to collaboration and includes basic steps like discussion and creating tickets.","Mentions decision making on timelines which is important in project planning."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-9","weaknesses":["Lacks detail on how to ensure developers understand the design through specifications or prototypes.","No mention of ongoing communication or feedback loops during development.","Does not address documentation aspects or accessibility considerations.","Does not demonstrate deeper understanding of collaboration tools or processes."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"I initiate collaboration early by sharing detailed design specifications and interactive prototypes to ensure clear understanding. I maintain open communication through regular syncs or standups to clarify any ambiguities and gather developer feedback. I also create design documentation including component behavior, responsive states, and accessibility considerations to facilitate implementation. Finally, I remain available throughout development to review builds, address challenges, and iterate on solutions jointly to ensure fidelity to the design vision.","candidateAnswer":"I discuss with them and then we create tickets for it and then decide timelines and then go ahead.","missing_concepts":["Early sharing of detailed design specs and interactive prototypes","Regular communication such as standups or sync meetings","Design documentation detailing component behaviors and accessibility","Availability during development for review and iteration"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate gives a very basic outline of collaboration focused mainly on discussion, ticket creation, and timeline decisions. While these are relevant parts, the answer lacks the depth expected for a medium difficulty question. Important aspects such as providing detailed design specs, maintaining ongoing communication loops, and supporting developers through documentation and feedback are missing. The explanation is somewhat vague and does not demonstrate strong technical understanding of effective design handoffs. The candidate should elaborate on processes and tools that facilitate clear understanding between designers and developers to improve the quality and fidelity of the implementation.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows awareness of some collaboration steps but does not provide sufficient detail or demonstrate strong understanding of design developer handoff best practices. Overall, the answer is too brief and incomplete to pass."},{"prompt":"One final question: what’s the most challenging design problem you’ve solved recently?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":4,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Candidate identified a relevant and recent challenging design problem related to a payment gateway.","Mentioned use of React elements and developing user stories which aligns somewhat with design and development processes."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-10","weaknesses":["Explanation lacks detail about the design challenge, constraints, or user pain points.","No clear description of the specific solution approach or design decisions made.","Communication is somewhat unclear and incomplete, making it difficult to fully understand the candidate’s thought process.","No mention of user research, testing, or collaboration which are important aspects of complex design problem solving."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe a recent complex design challenge by outlining the context, the constraints or user pain points involved, and their solution approach. For example, they might explain a scenario where improving a complex user interaction flow required balancing usability with technical constraints, such as designing a payment gateway checkout process with React components to deliver a seamless user experience. They would highlight key design decisions, user research or testing insights, and cross-functional collaboration to iterate and refine the solution, demonstrating problem-solving skills and attention to UX detail relevant to their senior product designer role.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah. So recently one of the most challenging problems was the payment gateway that I had to resolve and it was getting difficult for me to Make a user make the user experience seamless, but we finally sorted by making provisions in the By using react elements and going developing users stories that can be best","missing_concepts":["Detailed user pain points or constraints encountered.","Clear steps or methods used to solve the problem.","Use of user research or testing insights.","Cross-functional collaboration and iteration process."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate identified a relevant design problem—a payment gateway—and noted using React elements and user stories, which shows some technical relevance. However, the answer lacks depth and clarity with minimal information about the challenge context or the implemented solution. Critical elements such as user experience details, constraints, design decisions, and collaboration efforts are missing. Communication was vague and incomplete, which undermines confidence in problem-solving skills. For a senior product designer role, further elaboration on how the challenge was approached and resolved, supported by concrete examples, is necessary.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate provided a very brief and somewhat vague description of a challenging design problem they faced, mentioning React usage and user stories. While relevant, the overall answer misses critical detail and clarity required to demonstrate a strong understanding and effective problem solving in senior product design. The candidate should improve on articulating the context, constraints, solu"},{"prompt":"tell me your self","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq9gb46t0004qo01mq4lsrve","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq9gyp7a001nqo01145yfste', 'cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p', 58, 100, 97, 90, 'Strong performance with structured answers and solid topic understanding.', '2026-06-11 12:23:59.254', '2026-06-11 12:24:46.071', '["Clear communication flow","Good depth in responses"]', '["Add sharper quantified examples","Reduce filler and tighten transitions"]', '["um","During our deployment, I encountered multiple challenges. One issue was SSH connection failure due to incorrect key permission. I resolved it by assigning a proper permission and verifying the key pair. Another issue occurred when the website was inaccessible. After investigating, I found that port 80 was not allowed in the security group. While working with S3 static website hosting, I faced a deadline error because block public access was enabled and bucket policies were missing. After updating the bucket policy and enabling public access, the issue was resolved. I also encountered CloudFront cache and delays where updated files were not immediately visible. I solved this by creating cache and invalidation and clearing old content. This challenge improved my problem-sorting and problem-solving skill. Thank you.","I have completed my BTech in Computer Science and currently I am building my career in Cloud and DevOps. During my learning journey, I have worked on multiple AWS projects where I gained hands-on experience with services like EC2, S3, IAM, VPC and more. One of my projects was hosting a static website on Amazon EC2 using NGX web service. I launched an EC2 instance inside of VPC, configured a security group, installed NGX and deployed the website. I also worked on problem-solving issues related to SSH connectivity, security group and web server configuration, as I am saying. Another project was hosting a static website using S3 and CloudFront. I configured bucket policies, enabled static website hosting and used CloudFront CDN to improve performance and reduce latency. Apart from deployment, I have spent time understanding networking concepts like VPC, subnet, root tables, internet getaway, NAT, getaway and security mechanism. I enjoy troubleshooting infrastructure issues and continuously learning new cloud technology. My goal is to become a skilled cloud and DevOps engineer and contribute to scalable and secure infrastructure solution."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 48, '[{"prompt":"Can you tell me about a time when you faced a major challenge at work and how you handled it?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific, significant work-related challenge that required technical problem-solving and collaboration. For example, they might recount encountering a critical production issue with AWS EC2 instances impacting application availability. They should explain how they identified the root cause using AWS CloudWatch logs or metrics, coordinated with team members to implement a solution such as instance replacement or VPC reconfiguration, and validated the fix to prevent recurrence. The answer should demonstrate initiative, technical knowledge of AWS services like EC2 and VPC, effective communication, and a structured problem-solving approach.","candidateAnswer":"um","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Can you tell us about your background and how it maps to this AWS Solution Architect role?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":8,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Demonstrated practical hands-on experience with core AWS services such as EC2, S3, IAM, and VPC.","Provided specific examples of troubleshooting and resolving common AWS deployment issues.","Showed understanding of networking concepts relevant to AWS solutions.","Expressed enthusiasm for continuous learning and problem solving in cloud and DevOps."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Background description was somewhat scattered and focused more on anecdotal problem solving than structured mapping of experience to the role.","Lack of explicit mention of designing scalable and secure architectures at a solution level.","Some minor technical inaccuracies in terminology (e.g., ''internet getaway'' and ''NAT, getaway'').","No mention of collaboration or translating business requirements into AWS solutions."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe their educational background in computer science or related fields and practical experience with cloud computing, focusing on AWS services such as EC2, S3, VPC, and IAM. They should provide examples of designing and deploying scalable, secure AWS architectures, demonstrating knowledge of best practices for securely managing resources using IAM, configuring networking with VPC, and handling storage with S3. Experience collaborating across technical teams and translating business requirements into AWS solutions is important. For example:\\n- Designed and implemented EC2 instances with optimized configurations for specific workloads.\\n- Managed S3 bucket policies ensuring secure and cost-effective storage.\\n- Configured VPC subnets and security groups to enforce network segmentation.\\n- Administered IAM roles and policies to maintain principle of least privilege.\\nThis background shows readiness for the junior AWS Solution Architect role by combining foundational AWS knowledge with practical application and teamwork.","candidateAnswer":"During our deployment, I encountered multiple challenges. One issue was SSH connection failure due to incorrect key permission. I resolved it by assigning a proper permission and verifying the key pair. Another issue occurred when the website was inaccessible. After investigating, I found that port 80 was not allowed in the security group. While working with S3 static website hosting, I faced a deadline error because block public access was enabled and bucket policies were missing. After updating the bucket policy and enabling public access, the issue was resolved. I also encountered CloudFront cache and delays where updated files were not immediately visible. I solved this by creating cache and invalidation and clearing old content. This challenge improved my problem-sorting and problem-solving skill. Thank you. I have completed my BTech in Computer Science and currently I am building my career in Cloud and DevOps. During my learning journey, I have worked on multiple AWS projects where I gained hands-on experience with services like EC2, S3, IAM, VPC and more. One of my projects was hosting a static website on Amazon EC2 using NGX web service. I launched an EC2 instance inside of VPC, configured a security group, installed NGX and deployed the website. I also worked on problem-solving issues related to SSH connectivity, security group and web server configuration, as I am saying. Another project was hosting a static website using S3 and CloudFront. I configured bucket policies, enabled static website hosting and used CloudFront CDN to improve performance and reduce latency. Apart from deployment, I have spent time understanding networking concepts like VPC, subnet, root tables, internet getaway, NAT, getaway and security mechanism. I enjoy troubleshooting infrastructure issues and continuously learning new cloud technology. My goal is to become a skilled cloud and DevOps engineer and contribute to scalable and secure infrastructure solution.","missing_concepts":["Explicit explanation of designing and deploying scalable AWS architectures.","Best practices for securely managing AWS resources with IAM.","Role-based collaboration and translating business needs into technical AWS designs.","Details on managing cost-effective storage and advanced VPC configuration beyond basics."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrated solid technical knowledge and practical experience with key AWS services like EC2, S3, IAM, and VPC, including troubleshooting common issues such as SSH key permissions and security group rules. Though the examples show useful hands-on skills and problem-solving ability, the response lacked a clear, structured overview of how their background aligns holistically with the AWS Solution Architect role, especially in designing scalable and secure architectures and collaborating across teams to meet business needs. Additionally, some terminology inaccuracies slightly reduced clarity. Improving focus on architectural design and business alignment would strengthen the answer. Overall, the candidate shows promise for a junior AWS Solution Architect position and exhibits a good foundation to build upon.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has practical AWS deployment experience and good problem-solving skills with relevant services. Background is somewhat raw and anecdotal but contains enough technical grounding to pass for a junior AWS Solution Architect role. Future growth should focus on architectural design and solution-level thinking."},{"prompt":"How do you typically approach designing a secure VPC architecture for a new application?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Understood basic concepts of VPC and CIDR block","Mentioned segmentation into public and private subnets correctly","Accurately identified use cases for public and private subnets"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["CIDR block notation is incorrectly stated (10.0.0.0.0.16)","Did not mention multi-AZ deployment for high availability","Lack of details on route tables, NACLs, and security groups","No mention of VPC Flow Logs or VPC endpoints for enhanced security","Did not describe how to enforce least privilege principles in security groups"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"To design a secure VPC architecture, I start by defining an appropriate CIDR block to allocate IP space without conflict. I then segment the VPC into public and private subnets across multiple Availability Zones for high availability. Public subnets host resources like NAT gateways or load balancers that require internet access, while private subnets secure backend services and databases from direct internet exposure. I configure route tables carefully to control traffic flow and implement Network Access Control Lists (NACLs) and security groups with the principle of least privilege. Additionally, I enable VPC Flow Logs and consider VPC endpoints to keep traffic within the AWS network and enhance security.","candidateAnswer":"Amazon VPC stands for Virtual Private Cloud. It is a logical, isolated network in AWS where resources are launched securely. The first step is creating a VPC by defining a CIDR block such as 10.0.0.0.0.16 inside the VPC. Multiple subnets can be created. Public subnets are used to resource that need internet access, while private subnets are used to databases and internal services.","missing_concepts":["Proper CIDR block notation and planning","Subnet distribution across multiple Availability Zones","Route table configuration","Network ACLs and security groups with least privilege","Enabling VPC Flow Logs for monitoring","Use of VPC endpoints to keep traffic within AWS network"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows basic understanding of VPC architecture by defining a VPC and using public and private subnets appropriately. However, the answer contains a critical error in CIDR block notation, which undermines technical correctness. Important architectural best practices such as multi-AZ subnet deployment, detailed traffic control using route tables, and security configurations using NACLs and security groups are missing. The candidate also omitted monitoring (VPC Flow Logs) and advanced security features like VPC endpoints. The explanation was clear but too brief and somewhat incomplete to demonstrate solid problem-solving and thorough understanding of secure VPC design.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate demonstrates foundational knowledge of VPC segmentation and subnet roles but lacks depth in secure architecture design and best practices. The omission of key security controls and operational safeguards, combined with technical inaccuracies, prevents a pass. Further study and practical experience with VPC security features and architecture are recommended."},{"prompt":"How do you approach configuring IAM roles and policies for secure access management?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":1},"strengths":["Clear explanation of VPC network components and subnet segregation","Use of a practical example demonstrating understanding of network architecture"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["No mention or understanding of IAM roles, policies, or access management","Irrelevant answer content unrelated to IAM configuration","Lacks coverage of key security practices for IAM such as least privilege or role segmentation","Does not address policy conditions, auditing, or monitoring for access management"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"I start by following the principle of least privilege, granting only the minimum permissions necessary for a role to perform its tasks. I define IAM roles tailored to specific services or applications, using managed or custom policies with clear, restrictive actions and resource scope. I also use conditions to enforce constraints, such as MFA or IP addresses, and regularly audit permissions with tools like IAM Access Analyzer. Additionally, I separate duties by creating different roles for different user types or services and enable logging through CloudTrail to monitor access and changes for security compliance.","candidateAnswer":"An internet gateway, it attaches to the VPC to provide internet connectivity to public subnets. Root tables control traffic flow between the subnet and external network. Private subnets generally use a NAT gateway to access the internet without exposing resources publicly. Security could provide instance-level security and act as a virtue of firewalls. Network ACLs provide subnet security and are stateless. In one of my projects, I created a custom VPC with public and private subnets, where web servers were deployed in a public subnet while databases were placed in a private subnet. Internet access was provided using the internet, and gateway and outbound access for private. Resource was achieved using a NAT gateway. The architecture helped me to understand secure network design and resource isolation.","missing_concepts":["Principle of least privilege","IAM roles and policies configuration","Use of custom or managed policies","Conditions and constraints in IAM policies","Auditing with IAM Access Analyzer or CloudTrail","Segregation of duties through role definition","Security compliance via access monitoring"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer focuses entirely on VPC networking concepts such as internet gateways, NAT gateways, route tables, and subnets. While these demonstrate good understanding of AWS networking, they are irrelevant to the question about configuring IAM roles and policies for secure access management. There is no mention of IAM, role creation, permissions, policies, or security principles related to IAM, which is the core of the question. The explanation is clear but addresses the wrong topic. To improve, the candidate should focus on IAM concepts like least privilege, policy crafting, role definitions, use of conditions, auditing, and monitoring access. Overall, this answer does not satisfy the question requirements and shows a poor understanding of IAM-based security management.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate failed to address the question about IAM roles and policies, instead discussing unrelated VPC networking concepts. This indicates a significant gap in understanding secure access management with IAM in AWS. The answer is mostly irrelevant and lacks core knowledge expected for the role of AWS Solution Architect."},{"prompt":"For our final question, how do you ensure high availability when designing with EC2?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":4,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Candidate demonstrates understanding of basic EC2 instance setup including VPC, key pairs, and security groups","Experience with web server installation and troubleshooting security group rules"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["No mention of deploying instances across multiple Availability Zones","No discussion of Elastic Load Balancer or Auto Scaling for high availability","No mention of monitoring via CloudWatch or backup strategies","Focuses on single EC2 instance deployment rather than high availability design"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":4,"expectedAnswer":"To ensure high availability with EC2, you should deploy instances across multiple Availability Zones within a region to avoid single points of failure. Use an Elastic Load Balancer (ELB) to distribute traffic evenly across healthy instances, and implement Auto Scaling Groups to automatically replace unhealthy instances and scale based on demand. Additionally, use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor instance health and performance and configure proper backup strategies such as AMIs or snapshots for disaster recovery.","candidateAnswer":"The object of this EC2 is to understand how the web applications are hosted on the cloud server and how the networking components work together. First of all, I have to create a VPC environment and configure a network component. Then I launch an EC2 instance running Amazon Linux. While creating the instance, I generated a key pair for a secure SSH access and configured security group to allow inbound traffic on port 22 for SSH and port 80 for HTTP access. After launching the instance, I connected to the server using SSH. Once connected, I updated the server package and installed Nivex web server. After successfully installation, I start enable a service so that it would automatically start after system reboot. Then uploaded a website file including HTML, CSS, JavaScript into the web server directly. Once the deployment was completed, I test the website using the public IP address of the EC2 instance and verified that it was accessible for the internet. During the implement I faced when the website was not loading after investigation, I found that the HTTP port was not properly configured in the security group. After opening a port number to the website, the website became accessible.","missing_concepts":["Multi-AZ deployment to avoid single points of failure","Elastic Load Balancing (ELB)","Auto Scaling Groups for instance health and scaling","Monitoring with Amazon CloudWatch","Backup and disaster recovery strategies"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a detailed narrative on launching and configuring a single EC2 instance with network setup and web server deployment. While this shows practical experience with EC2 and networking basics, the answer does not address the key components of designing for high availability as asked. There is no mention of spreading instances across multiple Availability Zones to prevent downtime from AZ failures. The candidate also omits load balancing, auto scaling, monitoring and backup strategies which are crucial for high availability. The explanation is clear for what was discussed, but the overall response fails to answer the question fully and accurately.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate understands EC2 instance provisioning and basic networking/security considerations but lacks knowledge of best practices to ensure high availability including multi-AZ deployment, load balancing, auto scaling, and monitoring. The answer is incomplete and does not meet expectations for the role."},{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq9gjjw30012qo019ftx21zv","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"I have a foundational background in cloud computing with hands-on experience in designing and deploying AWS infrastructure, including EC2 instances, S3 storage solutions, and configuring VPCs to ensure secure networking. During my previous internship/project, I developed scalable cloud architectures emphasizing security and cost optimization. I am familiar with AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) for defining roles and permissions to enforce least privilege access. This experience aligns well with the responsibilities expected in this junior AWS Solution Architect role, allowing me to contribute effectively to designing and implementing cloud solutions that meet business needs while adhering to AWS best practices.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmq9heiyw001zqo018xq4melh', 'cmq9hdpw0001vqo01c5q6upb0', 9, 45, 40, 50, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-11 12:36:17.673', '2026-06-11 12:36:27.681', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '[]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 0, '[{"prompt":"Can you tell me about a challenging problem you solved recently and how you approached it?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate would describe a specific, complex problem related to product design or UI development, such as optimizing a React component for performance or resolving a usability issue. They would explain their systematic approach: identifying the problem through data or user feedback, researching alternatives, prototyping solutions, collaborating cross-functionally, and iterating based on testing results. They should highlight technical skills (like React for front-end performance) alongside design thinking, demonstrating impact on product quality or user experience.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"tell me your self","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmq9hdpw0001wqo013p7pl3li","weaknesses":["Question was not asked during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"Not asked."}]'), ('cmqam27s1000erq01ku87f5hp', 'cmqaly6tw0004rq0135rrnjz6', 50, 56, 49, 62, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-12 07:34:27.553', '2026-06-12 09:21:18.092', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["I first identified the root cause of the issue, gathered relevant information, advocated possible solutions, and then implemented the most effective approach. I also communicated regularly with the stakeholders and monitored the results to ensure the problem","My most difficult task was handling urgent hiring for multiple positions, similarly violating the strict deadlines. I managed candidates to succeed, screening interview coordinators and follow-ups efficiently. For proper planning and communication, I successfully closed the position on time. you","I am a fresher in HR, but I have a strong interest in human resource and talent acquisition. Throughout my academic background and project, I learned about the recruitment process, employee onboarding, performance management, HR policies. I have good communication, interpersonal skill, and I work to apply my knowledge in professional HR environment while continuing to learn and improve."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 50, '[{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Clear communication and interpersonal skills","Shows awareness of HR functions such as recruitment, onboarding, and performance management","Expresses motivation to learn and grow in the HR field"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmqaly6tw0005rq01vnoqyyv8","weaknesses":["No practical work experience in HR","Lacks coverage of key responsibilities like employee relations, compliance, policy implementation, and cross-functional collaboration","Limited demonstration of problem-solving or professional standards understanding"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"I have over 5 years of experience in HR, specializing in recruitment, employee relations, and compliance. I have successfully managed end-to-end hiring cycles, developed retention strategies, and implemented HR policies aligned with corporate goals. My background includes working cross-functionally with management and legal teams to ensure fair and consistent practices. This experience equips me to effectively handle the key responsibilities of this HR role, including problem solving, communication, and maintaining professional standards.","candidateAnswer":"I am a fresher in HR, but I have a strong interest in human resource and talent acquisition. Throughout my academic background and project, I learned about the recruitment process, employee onboarding, performance management, HR policies. I have good communication, interpersonal skill, and I work to apply my knowledge in professional HR environment while continuing to learn and improve.","missing_concepts":["End-to-end hiring cycle experience","Retention strategies","HR policy implementation aligned with corporate goals","Collaboration with management and legal teams","Professional standards in HR"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate presents themselves as a fresher with theoretical knowledge and interest in HR, which is relevant but insufficient for this role. While communication skills are adequate and the candidate recognizes some HR areas, they lack practical experience and omit important HR responsibilities expected for the role. The answer does not demonstrate the level of problem-solving, domain expertise, or handling of professional standards required. Overall, the response is incomplete and more aligned with an entry-level profile rather than one suited to this position.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows basic familiarity with HR concepts but lacks the necessary experience and depth to fulfill the requirements of this HR role. The answer is relevant and clear but incomplete and only partially correct, resulting in a failing score."}]'), ('cmqanfttm0016rq013gf3jw04', 'cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5', 69, 60, 52, 78, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-12 08:13:02.265', '2026-06-12 09:15:00.452', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hello.","The first law of thermodynamics tells you about conservation of energy, it says that energy cannot be created nor destroyed, it can just change its form from one to the other.","Yes casting is one of the common manufacturing processes which is used"]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 70, '[{"prompt":"Laws of thermodyanmics","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":8,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Accurate explanation of the first law of thermodynamics","Clear and understandable wording"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmqan99y2000nrq01rp8ca9rw","weaknesses":["Only covered the first law, missing the other key laws","Lacks mention of concepts such as entropy, thermal equilibrium, and absolute zero"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"The laws of thermodynamics describe fundamental principles governing energy and heat transfer. The zeroth law establishes thermal equilibrium, the first law states that energy is conserved (energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed), the second law introduces entropy and states that energy transfer increases disorder, and the third law states that entropy approaches a constant minimum as temperature approaches absolute zero.","candidateAnswer":"The first law of thermodynamics tells you about conservation of energy, it says that energy cannot be created nor destroyed, it can just change its form from one to the other.","missing_concepts":["Zeroth law - thermal equilibrium","Second law - entropy and increasing disorder","Third law - entropy approaching minimum at absolute zero"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate correctly stated the first law of thermodynamics, noting energy conservation and transformation. The explanation is clear and relevant to the question. However, the answer is incomplete as it only addresses one of the four laws, missing fundamental aspects such as the zeroth, second, and third laws. This limits the depth of understanding demonstrated. To improve, the candidate should aim to cover all four laws comprehensively and mention key terms like entropy and thermal equilibrium.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate demonstrated solid understanding of the first law of thermodynamics with clear communication. However, the answer is incomplete as it lacks coverage of the other laws. Overall, a pass with room for growth in breadth of knowledge."},{"prompt":"manufacturing process","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Candidate correctly identifies casting as a common manufacturing process.","Describes the casting process steps including pouring molten metal and cooling."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmqan99y2000orq0113bt0a7o","weaknesses":["Answer is focused only on casting and does not mention other manufacturing processes.","Lacks a general definition of a manufacturing process as transformation from raw materials to finished products.","No mention of factors influencing process selection like material, product design, or production volume."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"A manufacturing process is a series of steps through which raw materials are transformed into finished products. Common manufacturing processes include casting, machining, molding, forming, and joining, each selected based on product design, material, and production volume.","candidateAnswer":"Yes casting is one of the common manufacturing processes which is used. So, in casting molten metal is poured into the dye, it is allowed to cool and then the product is taken out, there are some finishing processes done and you get the final product.","missing_concepts":["General definition of manufacturing process","Other common manufacturing methods such as machining, molding, forming, and joining","Selection criteria for manufacturing processes"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a technically correct and clear explanation of the casting process, demonstrating understanding of one specific manufacturing method. However, the answer lacks completeness as it does not address other common manufacturing processes or provide a general definition of what a manufacturing process entails. The response would be stronger if it included multiple processes and considerations for process selection based on product and material properties. Communication is mostly clear, though slightly limited in scope.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a reasonable grasp of manufacturing by accurately describing casting, indicating foundational technical knowledge. However, the answer is narrowly focused and misses a broader explanation expected at this level. Overall, the candidate meets the minimum expectation but should aim to provide more comprehensive answers including multiple manufacturing techniques and contextual und"},{"prompt":"additive manufacturing","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Correctly identifies additive manufacturing as a layer-by-layer process","Distinguishes additive manufacturing from subtractive methods","Recognizes that additive manufacturing is suitable for complex product geometries"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmqan99y2000prq017o8v6okq","weaknesses":["Inaccurate claim that subtractive manufacturing is always faster without nuance","Terminology issues (mentions ''active manufacturing'' likely intending ''additive manufacturing'')","Does not mention benefits like material savings or applications such as rapid prototyping","Lacks explanation of the digital model basis for additive manufacturing"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process of creating three-dimensional objects by successively adding material layer by layer, based on digital 3D model data. It allows for complex geometries, reduces material waste compared to subtractive methods, and is useful for rapid prototyping and low-volume production in mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is basically a process in which a product is manufactured by depositing layers of the base metal and is done layer by layer. Subtractive Manufacturing is the most traditional method and Subtractive Manufacturing is faster to manufacture as well as by the editing manufacturing it takes much more time to finish the final product. If the product is very complex to manufacture and it involves multiple processes or probably it is difficult to manufacture from the traditional processes, I will go for additive manufacturing. If the manufacturing process needs speed and products are simple to make, then I will decide to go for active manufacturing.","missing_concepts":["Use of digital 3D models as the basis of additive manufacturing","Material efficiency compared to subtractive methods","Applicability for rapid prototyping and low-volume production"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a basic understanding that additive manufacturing builds products layer-by-layer and contrasts it with subtractive manufacturing. However, some technical points lack precision, such as relying too generally on subtractive methods being faster and confusing terminology near the end. Important aspects like the role of digital 3D model data and the benefits in material conservation and prototyping are omitted, limiting completeness. The explanation is generally clear but could improve in professional structure and accuracy. Overall, the answer shows solid foundational knowledge but needs refinement and additional details to fully meet expectations.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a reasonable grasp of additive manufacturing concepts appropriate for a junior mechanical engineer, understanding its basic principle and when it might be preferred over traditional methods. The answer is somewhat incomplete and includes minor inaccuracies, but the core idea is present with moderate clarity. This response is borderline adequate for a junior role and reflects po"}]'), ('cmqanrjih001wrq01l34t20eq', 'cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd', 53, 74, 63, 82, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-12 08:22:08.777', '2026-06-12 11:20:42.927', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Hello.","I am Raju from Mumbai. I have five years of experience in product design and development. I work for companies like Google and Apple. I have worked in building e-commerce platforms, prototyping as well as certain products where I used to make the MVP and 3D model and then convert it into the final product.","Yes, so UI design for me was limited to wireframing and conceptual withstanding where I was more into converting the ideas into designs or drawings in the paper followed by building mock-ups on Figma."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 54, '[{"prompt":"Hi Raju, this is Sana from Test. Let’s dive into the interview. Can you tell me about a challenging project you recently worked on and how you handled it?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"In a recent project, I led the redesign of a complex SaaS dashboard with tight timelines and cross-team dependencies. I managed the challenge by breaking the requirements into incremental milestones, collaborating closely with both engineering and product teams to align on priorities, and iterating designs based on user feedback. This ensured we delivered a user-friendly interface on time without compromising core functionalities.","candidateAnswer":"Hello.","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."},{"prompt":"Hi Raju, my name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today. Let’s dive right in. To start off, tell me about yourself.","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Provided relevant work experience in product design and development","Mentioned experience with prototyping and building MVPs","Described involvement in e-commerce platforms and product modeling"],"difficulty":"easy","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Did not specify technical skills such as UI design or React","Lacked detail on role specifics and achievements","No mention of collaboration with developers or business goals"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"I am a senior product designer with over 7 years of experience specializing in UI design and product development using React. I have worked extensively on consumer and enterprise products, focusing on intuitive user interfaces and scalable component-based design. My background combines strong visual design skills with technical knowledge, enabling me to collaborate effectively with developers and deliver high-impact solutions that meet business goals.","candidateAnswer":"I am Raju from Mumbai. I have five years of experience in product design and development. I work for companies like Google and Apple. I have worked in building e-commerce platforms, prototyping as well as certain products where I used to make the MVP and 3D model and then convert it into the final product.","missing_concepts":["UI Design","React","Specific design methodologies or tools","Focus on user interfaces and scalable components"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a general overview of their background with relevant experience in product design and prototyping. However, the answer lacks technical specifics such as UI design expertise or React knowledge, which were expected. Additionally, the candidate did not clearly articulate how they contribute to user experience or business objectives. The answer is understandable but somewhat vague and incomplete regarding key skills and professional strengths. Overall, the response is decent but could be improved with more focused information on technical skills and impact.","interviewer_summary":"Raju demonstrates relevant experience in product design and development roles and communicates reasonably clearly. However, he does not mention key technical skills like UI design or React, which are critical for this role. The answer is somewhat generic and misses details on collaboration and design impact. While competent, the response only partially meets the expectations for a senior product d"},{"prompt":"Thank you for that introduction. Can you tell me more about your experience with UI design in those projects?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Mentions using wireframing and paper drawings to conceptualize UI design.","References building mock-ups on Figma, indicating familiarity with design tools.","Answer is relevant to the question and generally clear."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Lacks mention of high-fidelity designs, prototypes, or responsive design.","No reference to user-centered design principles or accessibility.","Does not mention collaboration with developers or implementation aspects such as React components.","Limited detail about the scope and depth of UI design experience."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"My UI design experience includes creating wireframes, prototypes, and high-fidelity visual designs for responsive web and mobile applications. I focus on user-centered design principles, accessibility, and maintaining design consistency through reusable style guides and component libraries. For example, in my last role, I crafted interactive prototypes using Figma and worked closely with developers to translate designs into production-ready React components, ensuring pixel-perfect implementation.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, so UI design for me was limited to wireframing and conceptual withstanding where I was more into converting the ideas into designs or drawings in the paper followed by building mock-ups on Figma.","missing_concepts":["High-fidelity visual designs","Prototyping and interactivity","Responsive design","User-centered design principles","Accessibility considerations","Collaboration with developers","React or production-ready component implementation"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a basic understanding of UI design by discussing wireframing, conceptual sketches on paper, and using Figma for mock-ups. However, the answer is somewhat limited and lacks depth in key areas such as creating high-fidelity visual designs and prototypes, focusing on user-centered design principles, accessibility, and collaboration with developers which are critical for the role. The reference to React in the ideal answer is completely missing. The communication is generally clear but the answer does not fully exhibit a comprehensive or advanced UI design experience expected for the position.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows foundational experience in UI design tools and a conceptual approach but is missing important elements such as prototyping, accessibility, and developer collaboration. The answer was acceptable but only just meets the threshold for passing, indicating room for growth."},{"prompt":"Got it. How comfortable are you with using React in your product development work?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":4,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Candidate demonstrates some hands-on experience with React","Mentions making components and reusable toolkits"],"difficulty":"easy","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Answer is very repetitive and incomplete","Lacks mention of core React concepts such as state, props, lifecycle, hooks","Does not explain level of comfort or nuance in using React","Answer is somewhat unclear due to repetition and vague phrasing"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"I am very comfortable with React and use it regularly to implement and iterate UI components. I understand React''s core concepts such as state management, props, lifecycle methods, and hooks. This familiarity allows me to design components that are modular, reusable, and maintainable, and to communicate effectively with development teams about technical constraints and opportunities during the design process.","candidateAnswer":"I can say on a scale of five, I am good with React Act 2 or 3. I have used React for making components and reusable toolkits from the library for certain assignments in my previous projects. I have used React for making components and reusable toolkits from the library for certain assignments in my previous projects. I have used React for making components and reusable toolkits from the library for certain","missing_concepts":["Understanding of React core concepts (state management, props, lifecycle methods, hooks)","Ability to communicate technical constraints and opportunities during design","Explanation of modularity, reusability, and maintainability within React components"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows some basic familiarity with React by mentioning working on components and reusable toolkits, which is positive. However, the answer is very incomplete as it lacks references to key React concepts such as state, props, lifecycle, and hooks that demonstrate deeper understanding. The response is also hindered by repeated phrases and vague language, reducing clarity and professionalism. Overall, the answer falls short of the expected level for a product designer comfortable with React, so the candidate does not meet the bar for this question.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has minimal practical experience with React but does not demonstrate sufficient understanding of React core concepts or ability to articulate their comfort level clearly. The repetitive and incomplete answer suggests limited depth which is insufficient for the product designer role requiring solid React familiarity."},{"prompt":"Understood. Can you give an example of a project where you used React components in your product design work?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":5,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":4,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Mentions using React components in a project","References specific application areas: browser building and payment gateway"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Lacks details about design work and integration of React components","No explanation of component reusability, collaboration, or design system","Answer is vague and incomplete","Poor communication clarity with brief and ambiguous statements"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":4,"expectedAnswer":"In a recent project, I designed a dashboard interface where I developed a set of reusable React components like buttons, cards, and modals as part of a living design system. These components enabled quick iteration and ensured design consistency across different product modules. I collaborated with engineers to define component props and states to cover various UI scenarios, facilitating seamless integration and scalability.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, so I used it for browser building as well as ready-made react component for the payment gateway","missing_concepts":["Description of reusable React components and their purpose","Collaboration with engineers on component props and states","How React components facilitated design consistency and iteration","Specifics about design challenges solved using React components"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides only a very brief and vague answer mentioning use of React components related to browser building and payment gateway but fails to explain their role in product design or how these components were used effectively. There is no mention of reusability, collaboration, or managing component states which are important aspects in this context. The answer lacks completeness and depth, making it difficult to assess true understanding or problem solving skill. Communication is unclear and fragmented. Overall, the answer is insufficient to demonstrate the expected competencies for a product designer working with React.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows minimal understanding of using React components in product design. The response was too brief and lacked essential details about design and engineering collaboration, reusability, and scalability of components. More depth and clearer explanation are needed."},{"prompt":"Thanks for sharing that. Could you tell me about a specific challenge you faced when integrating those components?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Identified a real user experience problem with the payment flow","Mentioned use of user stories and perspective-taking to understand user interactions"],"difficulty":"hard","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Did not address technical challenges related to React component integration","Lacked reference to handling dynamic data or collaborating with backend developers","Did not explain concrete solutions applied in the context of component integration","Vague description without specific details on resolving the integration issues"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"One specific challenge was ensuring that the React components I designed could handle dynamic data and various user interaction states without breaking the visual integrity or usability. Additionally, coordinating with backend developers to align on data formats and API responses required extra iterations. To address this, I maintained close communication with engineers, created detailed component documentation, and used interactive prototypes to demonstrate expected behaviors under different conditions.","candidateAnswer":"Yeah, so the user interface was not really intuitive, so we used to get a lot of dropouts during the payment because it was not as user-friendly as it should be. So that was one of the problems. How did I tackle it is basically developing user stories and looking to the perspectives of how a user might interact and where exactly does it decide to not go through the payment.","missing_concepts":["Technical challenge of making React components handle dynamic data and user states","Coordination with backend developers to align on data formats and APIs","Use of documentation and interactive prototypes to resolve integration challenges"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate identified a genuine UX challenge related to payment dropouts and took a user-centered approach by developing user stories. However, they did not address the integration challenges of React components, nor did they mention working with backend developers or managing dynamic data states, which were key aspects of the ideal answer. The response was somewhat relevant and clear in terms of communication but lacked sufficient technical depth and completeness, resulting in a below passing score.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate showed awareness of a design challenge focusing on user experience but did not demonstrate an understanding of the technical challenges involved in integrating React components or coordinating with backend systems. More specific technical details and collaboration efforts were expected to meet the role''s requirements."},{"prompt":"Makes sense. And what was one key improvement you made to address that issue?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":5,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Focus on simplifying user experience","Improvement aimed at making the purchase process seamless"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Did not address technical aspects related to UI or component design","Lacked details on error handling or component improvements","No mention of React or prop-driven styling as indicated in the ideal answer"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"A key improvement was introducing a set of well-defined error and loading states within the components, which improved robustness and user experience during data fetching issues. I also implemented prop-driven styling variations to accommodate different content scenarios, which reduced the need for separate components and streamlined the codebase, making maintenance and future updates easier.","candidateAnswer":"Key improvement was we kept it as simple as possible so to make a purchase the customer does not really need to log in or create an account on the platform, they can directly you know enter their basic information and make a payment and they get the details of their order directly on the given what is given ID email ID or mobile number making it much more seamless and easier for them to place an order","missing_concepts":["Error and loading state handling","Component-level improvements","Prop-driven styling variations","Technical implementation details"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer focused mainly on a simplification of the user flow by removing the need for mandatory login, which is relevant to improving user experience but lacks the technical details expected for a product designer working with React components. The response misses critical points like introducing error and loading states or codebase improvements through styling variations, which were key in the ideal answer. While the explanation was understandable, the absence of core technical design elements demonstrates partial understanding but incomplete knowledge of the targeted improvements. More focus on UI component design and technical robustness would be necessary.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate showed a basic understanding of improving user experience by simplifying the purchase flow but failed to demonstrate technical knowledge related to UI component enhancements and error handling required for this role. The answer lacks depth and completeness expected for a medium-difficulty technical question for a product designer."},{"prompt":"Thank you, that’s a solid approach. One final question: how do you stay updated on the latest trends in product design?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Candidate mentions relevant sources for learning, such as LinkedIn pages and YouTube channels.","Includes reading articles in newspapers and product magazines indicating an effort to stay informed."],"difficulty":"easy","questionId":"txq-7","weaknesses":["Lacks mention of specific reputable product design blogs or communities.","Does not mention participation in webinars, conferences, or active engagement in design forums or channels.","No reference to hands-on experimentation with new tools or collaboration with cross-functional teams.","Some vagueness in the sources described (e.g., ''certain pages'', ''and so on'')."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"I regularly follow leading product design blogs and communities like Smashing Magazine, UX Collective, and Designer News. I participate in webinars and conferences, and I am active in design-focused forums and Slack channels. Additionally, I experiment with new tools and techniques in side projects to stay hands-on, and I engage with cross-functional teams to learn emerging trends in both design and front-end technologies like React.","candidateAnswer":"I follow certain pages on LinkedIn and a few channels specifically on products on YouTube. Other than that, I keep reading articles in newspaper and product magazines and so on.","missing_concepts":["Specific well-known design blogs or communities such as Smashing Magazine, UX Collective, Designer News.","Active participation in webinars and conferences.","Engagement in design-focused forums or Slack channels.","Practical experimentation with new tools and techniques.","Learning from cross-functional teams specifically related to UI design and front-end technologies like React."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a moderately relevant approach to staying updated by referencing LinkedIn pages, YouTube channels, and reading articles, which shows some level of engagement with external sources. However, the answer lacks detail and specificity, missing mention of known industry-standard resources and active involvement in professional communities. The absence of hands-on tool experimentation or multidisciplinary collaboration reflects incomplete understanding of how to thoroughly stay current in product design trends. Communication is generally clear but somewhat vague, which lowers completeness. To improve, the candidate should specify and demonstrate a more proactive and structured approach aligned with industry expectations.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a basic but incomplete understanding of how to stay current in product design trends, mentioning common but somewhat generic sources without demonstrating deeper engagement or use of industry-standard resources. The answer is acceptable but leaves room for improvement in specificity and proactiveness."}]'), ('cmqaqoyf1000lmv01zno61e6k', 'cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29', 80, 92, 78, 74, 'Strong performance with structured answers and solid topic understanding.', '2026-06-12 09:44:06.973', '2026-06-12 09:44:33.084', '["Clear communication flow","Good depth in responses"]', '["Add sharper quantified examples","Reduce filler and tighten transitions"]', '["Yeah, basically, I used two projects like first one is a static website hosting on EC2. Actually, one of the project I worked on was deploying a static website on Amazon EC2. I launched a Ubuntu instance, configured a security group instance, like installed Naginx and hosted the application. I also configured SSH access using TPS and managed firewalls rule through the security group. The challenges I faced like website was not inaccessible from browser, port 80 was not allowed in security group and when I solved this, like I modified inbound rule and allowed HTTP traffic on port 80 from anywhere. This is the first one. The second one is resume using S3 and CloudFront. Actually, in this website on Amazon S3 using a static website hosting and integrated CloudFront for global content, delivery and low latency. I configured a bucket policy to allow read access and enable caching through CloudFront. The challenge is access delay and error. Bucket policy was incorrect. Then I resolved with update the bucket policy and configured a public read permission.","Actually I have completed my B.Tech in Computer Science Engineering and currently I am focusing on Cloud and AWS technology. During my learning and hands-on practice, I work instinctively with the core AWS services such as EC2, S3, IAM and VPC. I have built multiple projects involving website hosting, secure network architecture, access management and cloud infrastructure. I am interested in designing a scalable and secure architecture. Apart from AWS services, I also have knowledge of Linux administration, networking fundamentals, Git and basic DevOps concepts. While working on the project, I learned how to important security, availability and cost optimization are in cloud environments. I enjoy troubleshooting issues, understanding root cause and implementing reliable solutions. My goal is to become a solution architect who can design a highly affordable, scalable and secure infrastructure according to my business requirements.","Identify and access management, commonly referred to IAM, is the service responsible for authentication and authorization in AWS. IAM enables the administration to securely manage user group, role and permission through IAM organization, and control who can access AWS resources and what actions they are not allowed to perform. IAM users represent individual identities, group collections of users with similar permissions. Policies are JSON documents that define permissions. Roles provide temporary credit intel and are generally assigned to AWS services rather than individuals. One of the most important principles followed in IAM is the principle of least privilege. According to this principle, users and services should only be granted the minimum permission necessary to perform their task. Multi-factor authentication adds on an additional layer of security by requiring a secondary authentication mechanism. IAM roles are widely used to provide secure access between AWS services without exposing access keys. For example, an EC2 instance can access an S3 bucket through an IAM role instead of storing credit details inside the application. At last, IAM is fundamental to AWS security because it ensures proper access control, minimizes security risks, and simplifies permission management. That''s all. Thank you."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 80, '[{"prompt":"Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role.","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":7,"problem_solving":7,"communication_clarity":8,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Clear demonstration of hands-on experience with core AWS services like EC2, S3, IAM, and VPC.","Good understanding of important cloud concepts such as security, availability, and cost optimization.","Includes additional relevant skills such as Linux administration, networking fundamentals, and DevOps concepts.","Shows motivation towards scalable and secure architecture design aligned with the role."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmqajccxy000cmt01l8phfgu8","weaknesses":["Lacks specific examples or detailed description of projects or architectures designed.","Does not explicitly mention IAM best practices or specifics about role/permission management.","Could provide more concrete evidence of designing cost-effective solutions or security enforcement."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":8,"expectedAnswer":"I have a foundational background in cloud computing with hands-on experience in designing and deploying AWS infrastructure, including EC2 instances, S3 storage solutions, and configuring VPCs to ensure secure networking. During my previous internship/project, I developed scalable cloud architectures emphasizing security and cost optimization. I am familiar with AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) for defining roles and permissions to enforce least privilege access. This experience aligns well with the responsibilities expected in this junior AWS Solution Architect role, allowing me to contribute effectively to designing and implementing cloud solutions that meet business needs while adhering to AWS best practices.","candidateAnswer":"Actually I have completed my B.Tech in Computer Science Engineering and currently I am focusing on Cloud and AWS technology. During my learning and hands-on practice, I work instinctively with the core AWS services such as EC2, S3, IAM and VPC. I have built multiple projects involving website hosting, secure network architecture, access management and cloud infrastructure. I am interested in designing a scalable and secure architecture. Apart from AWS services, I also have knowledge of Linux administration, networking fundamentals, Git and basic DevOps concepts. While working on the project, I learned how important security, availability and cost optimization are in cloud environments. I enjoy troubleshooting issues, understanding root cause and implementing reliable solutions. My goal is to become a solution architect who can design a highly affordable, scalable and secure infrastructure according to my business requirements.","missing_concepts":["Explicit mention of AWS best practices.","Detailed explanation of IAM role and permission configuration.","Specific examples of scalable architecture implementations."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates solid foundational knowledge and practical experience with key AWS services relevant to the role. Their answer is relevant and shows understanding of designing secure and scalable solutions, which fits the AWS Solution Architect role. However, the answer could be improved by providing more concrete examples from projects or previous experience, especially regarding IAM role configurations and detailing how they apply AWS best practices. Overall, the communication is clear and structured, but adding more depth would strengthen the response.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate has a good grasp of AWS core services and cloud fundamentals. They communicate their background and interests well, aligning with the role''s expectations. With some more depth and examples in future responses, they show potential to succeed as a junior AWS Solution Architect."}]'), ('cmqaqrrz7000wmv012bqw81j1', 'cmqaqqgd9000tmv01g12fkzuc', 44, 45, 40, 50, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-12 09:46:18.595', '2026-06-12 09:46:18.595', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '[]', 'heuristic-immediate', null, null, null), ('cmqar6fqw001omv01u5s146zc', 'cmqaqskju0010mv01zlahv6lh', 54, 86, 73, 90, 'Strong performance with structured answers and solid topic understanding.', '2026-06-12 09:57:42.584', '2026-06-12 11:07:18.776', '["Clear communication flow","Good depth in responses"]', '["Add sharper quantified examples","Reduce filler and tighten transitions"]', '["Once the project I worked was on deployment or static website on Amazon EC2, I launched an Ubuntu instance, configure, config security group, install NIC key and hosted the application. I also config SSH access using key pairs and manage firewall through security groups. Thank you.","The problems which I faced where website was inaccessible from browser then port 80 was not allowing at the security group. I modified IBON rules and allowed HTTP traffic for port 80 from anywhere. After updating the security group, the website become accessible. Thank you for watching.","Hello, my name is Gargi Rao. I have completed my B.Tech in Computer Science and currently I''m focusing on cloud and AWS technology. During my learning and hands-on practice, I worked extensively with core AWS services such as EC2, S3, IAM and VPC. I had built multiple projects involving website hosting, security network architecture, access management and cloud infrastructure."]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 48, '[{"prompt":"Hi Gargee, this is Sana from Test. Let''s begin. Can you tell me about a time when you had to solve a difficult problem under pressure?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":4,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Candidate mentions deploying a static website on EC2.","Candidate correctly refers to configuration of security groups and key pairs."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["Answer lacks any mention of a difficult problem or pressure situation.","No description of problem-solving steps or prioritization under pressure.","Does not reference key AWS services beyond EC2 and security groups; missing VPC, S3, or IAM context.","The explanation is basic and does not demonstrate understanding of troubleshooting or coordination.","Does not timestamp or describe the complexity or urgency of the task."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":4,"expectedAnswer":"An ideal answer will describe a specific situation involving time constraints where the candidate identified the root cause, prioritized actions, and resolved the issue successfully. For example, recounting a critical production issue during deployment requiring rapid diagnosis and coordination with team members to restore service quickly, demonstrating problem-solving and composure under pressure.","candidateAnswer":"Once the project I worked was on deployment or static website on Amazon EC2, I launched an Ubuntu instance, configure, config security group, install NIC key and hosted the application. I also config SSH access using key pairs and manage firewall through security groups. Thank you.","missing_concepts":["Handling of difficult problems or incidents under time constraints.","Problem identification, root cause analysis, and resolution steps.","Use or mention of VPC, S3, and IAM as per key skills expected.","Description of collaboration or communication under pressure."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a basic description of deploying a static website on an EC2 instance, including setting up security groups, SSH key pairs, and firewall rules. However, the answer does not address the question about solving a difficult problem under pressure. There is no mention of any challenge faced, urgency, problem-solving methodology, or outcome under stressful conditions. The response shows some technical correctness with AWS basics but lacks depth, completeness, and relevance to the question. To improve, the candidate should describe a specific incident illustrating how they managed a pressing issue, worked efficiently, and applied relevant AWS services and problem-solving skills.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows foundational knowledge of deploying on EC2 and configuring basic security but fails to demonstrate experience with problem-solving under pressure. The answer was general, lacked specificity about the challenge, and missed key AWS components. Due to insufficient relevance and completeness, the candidate is rated as not meeting the expectations for this behavioral/technical question."},{"prompt":"Thank you. Can you share a bit more about the challenge you faced during that deployment?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Correctly identified a security group misconfiguration blocking HTTP traffic.","Explained the resolution step by modifying inbound rules to allow port 80 traffic."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Did not elaborate on the troubleshooting process or operational context.","Did not mention use of logs, network verification, or rollback attempts.","Limited explanation on the challenge severity or how they managed time pressure."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"The candidate should detail the technical challenge, such as misconfiguration causing service outage or failed rollbacks. They should explain the steps taken to troubleshoot, e.g., checking logs, verifying network settings, and how they implemented a fix or workaround under time pressure, highlighting their methodical approach to incident resolution.","candidateAnswer":"The problems which I faced where website was inaccessible from browser then port 80 was not allowing at the security group. I modified IBON rules and allowed HTTP traffic for port 80 from anywhere. After updating the security group, the website become accessible. Thank you for watching.","missing_concepts":["Detailed troubleshooting steps such as checking logs or network settings.","Broader impact analysis and mitigation strategies.","Mention of other AWS components like EC2, VPC, or S3 related to the issue."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate correctly identified a common AWS security group misconfiguration that caused the website to be inaccessible and explained the remedial action to permit HTTP traffic on port 80. However, the response lacked depth in describing how the problem was diagnosed, the specific technical challenge, and the methodical approach under deployment pressure. The explanation was somewhat clear but brief and could be improved by adding details about troubleshooting steps, system components involved, and impact mitigation.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate demonstrates basic practical knowledge of AWS security groups and essential troubleshooting for network access issues. However, the answer is incomplete and lacks depth expected for an AWS Solution Architect regarding incident analysis and resolution strategy description. The candidate passes but should be encouraged to provide more thorough and structured responses."},{"prompt":"Got it. Let’s step back for a moment—tell me about your background and how it maps to this AWS Solution Architect role.","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":8,"technical_correctness":8},"strengths":["Candidate demonstrates familiarity with key AWS services like EC2, S3, IAM, and VPC.","Mentions practical experience with relevant projects involving website hosting, security, and cloud infrastructure.","Clear and coherent communication of background and skills."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Lacks mention of cloud architecture principles or deeper design experience.","No mention of certifications or formal training which could reinforce candidacy.","Problem-solving and architectural approach are only implied, not explicitly stated."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate will summarize relevant experience with AWS services like EC2, S3, VPC, and IAM, including any projects designing or managing cloud infrastructure. They should highlight familiarity with cloud architecture principles and mention any certifications or training. The answer should connect their technical skills and problem-solving abilities to the junior AWS Solution Architect responsibilities.","candidateAnswer":"Hello, my name is Gargi Rao. I have completed my B.Tech in Computer Science and currently I''m focusing on cloud and AWS technology. During my learning and hands-on practice, I worked extensively with core AWS services such as EC2, S3, IAM and VPC. I had built multiple projects involving website hosting, security network architecture, access management and cloud infrastructure.","missing_concepts":["Cloud architecture principles","Certifications or formal AWS training","Explicit connection of technical skills to AWS Solution Architect responsibilities"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provides a technically correct and relevant answer, showing experience with important AWS services typically used by solution architects. However, the answer is somewhat general and incomplete as it lacks mention of architectural principles and certifications which are important for this role. The candidate does not clearly articulate their problem-solving approach or how their skills directly map to solution architect responsibilities. Overall, the response is good but could be strengthened with more depth and explicit connection to the role.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows solid foundational AWS knowledge and hands-on experience with relevant services. Communication is clear and relevant. To improve, the candidate needs to demonstrate broader architectural understanding and certifications, and better relate their background to AWS Solution Architect tasks. Overall, a promising candidate with room to grow."},{"prompt":"Thank you for that—how have you applied IAM roles and policies in your projects so far?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Correctly identified IAM as the AWS service for authentication and authorization","Mentioned managing users, groups, roles, and permissions","Stated purpose of controlling access to AWS resources and allowed actions"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Did not explain applying IAM roles and policies specifically in projects","No mention of principle of least privilege or custom policies","Did not reference attaching roles to AWS services like EC2","Lacked examples of controlling access efficiently and securely","Basic description rather than applied experience or deeper understanding"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"The candidate should explain using IAM roles and policies to securely manage permissions, following the principle of least privilege. They may mention creating custom policies, attaching roles to AWS services like EC2, and managing user/group permissions to control access to resources efficiently and securely.","candidateAnswer":"Let me think about it, identify and access management commonly referred to as IAM is a service responsible for authentication and authorization in AWS. IAM is able administration to secure manage user groups, roles and permissions. Through this organization can control who can access AWS responses and what action they are allowed to perform.","missing_concepts":["Principle of least privilege","Creating and attaching custom IAM policies","Using IAM roles with AWS services such as EC2","Managing user/group permissions to enforce fine-grained access control"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrates a basic understanding of IAM as AWS''s service responsible for authentication and authorization by managing users, groups, roles, and permissions. However, the answer lacks specifics on how IAM roles and policies were applied in real projects, which is fundamental to the question. Key concepts like the principle of least privilege, creating custom policies, and attaching roles to AWS services (e.g., EC2) were omitted. The explanation was generally understandable but did not reflect a practical or deep experience with IAM. To improve, the candidate should provide examples of how they used roles and policies to secure AWS resources effectively and detail how permissions were controlled in their project contexts.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows foundational knowledge of IAM but falls short on demonstrating applied experience and depth, missing critical elements expected for an AWS Solution Architect role. The answer did not meet the completeness and problem-solving criteria necessary to pass."},{"prompt":"Understood. Can you give a specific example of how you used an IAM role in one of your projects?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":1,"completeness":1,"problem_solving":1,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":2},"strengths":["Used relevant AWS service names like S3, CloudFront, CloudWatch"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["No mention or example of IAM roles","No explanation on how permissions were granted or managed","Answer does not address the question about usage of IAM roles","Lacks completeness and relevance to the question","Poor demonstration of understanding of role-based access"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":2,"expectedAnswer":"An ideal answer would describe a scenario such as assigning an IAM role to an EC2 instance to grant it permissions to access S3 buckets without embedding credentials, specifying the role creation, policies attached, and how it enabled secure service-to-service communication.","candidateAnswer":"Basically, database are config with multiple AS development to ensure automatic failover. Static content is served through S3 and CloudFront to improve performance and reduce latency. Monitoring services such as CloudWatch continuously track resources, health and trigger alarm when predefined throws are accessed. Highly available minimizes downtime, improves reliability and ensures uninterrupted services delivery.","missing_concepts":["IAM role creation and attachment","Using IAM roles for EC2 instances or other services","Permissions management via IAM policies","Secure access without embedded credentials","Service-to-service communication security"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer describes some AWS services and features like database failover, S3, CloudFront, and CloudWatch, but completely misses addressing the core of the question which is about using IAM roles. There is no example given relating to IAM roles, nor explanation on how roles were created or used to manage permissions. The answer is largely irrelevant and incomplete, indicating a lack of understanding or inability to recall how IAM roles are implemented in projects. Communication clarity is acceptable but does not compensate for lack of technical correctness and relevance. Overall, the candidate fails to meet the requirements for this question.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrated familiarity with some AWS services but failed to provide any specific example or explanation of using IAM roles in projects as requested. The response lacks focus on the question and does not prove the necessary knowledge to fulfill the role expectations for IAM-related tasks."},{"prompt":"Thanks. Let’s clarify—how did you specifically use an IAM role in that setup?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":5,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Demonstrated understanding of basic IAM concepts such as users, groups, policies, and roles.","Mentioned the principle of least privilege which is important in IAM configurations.","Clear explanation and communication of basic IAM components."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Did not address how the IAM role was created with minimal permissions.","No explanation of attaching the IAM role to an EC2 instance profile or how it was specifically used in the setup.","Answer was generic and did not directly answer the question about specific use of IAM role in the setup.","Missed the core concept of how roles provide temporary credentials to AWS services like EC2.","No mention of managing access to AWS resources securely without manual credential management."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"A strong answer clarifies that the IAM role was created with policies granting minimal required permissions and then attached to the EC2 instance profile, enabling the instance to access specified AWS resources securely without manual credential management.","candidateAnswer":"IAM users represent individual identity, groups are collections of users with similar permissions, policies are JSON, document that define permissions, role provides temporary credentials and are generally assigned to AWS services, rather than individual. One of the most important principles followed in IAM is the principle of Least Privilege. According to this principle, users and services should only be granted the minimum permission necessary to perform their task.","missing_concepts":["Creation of IAM role with minimal required permissions","Attaching the IAM role to an EC2 instance profile","Using the role to enable EC2 instance to access specific AWS resources securely","Temporary credentials mechanism provided by IAM roles","How IAM roles differ in usage versus IAM users in service authentication"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrated a basic understanding of IAM components and the principle of least privilege, which is positive. However, the answer lacked specific details about how the IAM role was actually used in the setup. The question asked for a description of the usage of an IAM role within the setup, ideally explaining the minimal permission policies, role attachment to an EC2 instance profile, and how it enables the instance to securely access resources. The response was generic and did not address these key points, resulting in a lack of completeness and relevance to the question. Communication was clear but the content did not demonstrate sufficient problem-solving or practical application understanding.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate understands IAM concept basics and security principles but fails to describe the specific application of IAM roles in the scenario. Needs improvement in applying concepts to practical AWS setups and detailing role attachment and permissions."},{"prompt":"Understood. Let me ask this differently—can you walk me through a real scenario where you assigned an IAM role to an EC2 instance?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":5,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Demonstrated awareness that IAM roles are used to provide secure access without embedding credentials","Acknowledged EC2 instances accessing S3 using IAM roles"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-6","weaknesses":["Did not describe the process of creating and attaching the IAM role to the EC2 instance","No mention of instance profiles or applying the role during or after instance launch","Lacked a clear, step-by-step explanation or a concrete real scenario","The initial statement about ''authenticated added additional layer of security by requiring second authentication mechanism'' is unclear and irrelevant to the question"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"The candidate should describe creating an IAM role with appropriate policies (e.g., read-only access to S3), then attaching this role to the EC2 instance profile during or after instance launch, enabling applications on the instance to access S3 securely. They should also mention verifying permissions and testing access.","candidateAnswer":"Multiple factors as authenticated added additional layer of security by requiring second authentication mechanism. IAM and ROL are widely used to provide secure access between AWS servers without exposing access key. For example, an EC2 instance can access an S3 bucket through an IAM ROL instead of storing credentials inside the applications.","missing_concepts":["Creation of IAM role with appropriate policies","Attaching IAM role to EC2 instance profile","Testing and verifying permissions","Clear real example scenario with steps"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows a basic understanding that IAM roles avoid embedding credentials in applications and can be used by EC2 instances to access S3 buckets securely. However, the answer lacks specifics on how to create and assign the IAM role to an EC2 instance, omitting important details such as using instance profiles and verifying permissions. The initial part of the answer is somewhat confusing and not directly related to the question asked. Overall, the response is vague and incomplete and does not demonstrate full practical knowledge or problem-solving on the topic.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate has some conceptual understanding but failed to demonstrate a practical grasp of assigning IAM roles to EC2 instances. More detailed and concrete examples are needed to assess readiness for the AWS Solution Architect role."},{"prompt":"All right, thank you for explaining that. Now, how did you configure networking in a VPC for one of your deployments?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Correctly identified VPC as an isolated virtual network","Mentioned defining IP address range, subnet creation, and routing configuration","Answer is relevant to the question about VPC networking"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-7","weaknesses":["Did not specify types of subnets (public/private)","No mention of route tables configuration","Did not address Internet Gateways or NAT Gateways for connectivity","No details on security controls like security groups or NACLs","Overview was generic without deployment-specific configuration details"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"A thorough answer will describe designing the VPC with appropriate subnets (public/private), configuring route tables, setting up Internet Gateways or NAT Gateways for connectivity, and applying security groups and NACLs to control inbound and outbound traffic according to application requirements, ensuring secure and efficient network architecture.","candidateAnswer":"BPC. Amazon Virtual Private Cloud is a logical, isolated virtual network that enables users to surely launch AWS responses. A VPC allows an organization to define their own IP address range, create subnets and configure routing according to their security requirements.","missing_concepts":["Public and private subnet configuration","Route table setup","Internet Gateway and NAT Gateway configuration","Security Groups and Network ACLs","Specific application of these elements to deployment requirements"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided a basic description of what a VPC is and some of its capabilities, such as defining IP ranges, subnet creation, and routing. However, the answer lacked depth in describing how networking was actually configured for a deployment. Critical elements like types of subnets, route tables, and gateway configuration were missing, as were security aspects such as security groups and NACLs. The answer also did not link these configurations to the deployment''s needs or describe practical application steps. The communication was reasonably clear but mostly generic and introductory without showcasing detailed understanding or problem solving. To improve, the candidate should explicitly describe components they configured, their purpose, and how they ensured secure and efficient network design.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows a fundamental understanding of VPC concepts but falls short on demonstrating practical configuration know-how for deployment scenarios. The answer is relevant and technically sound at a basic level but lacks the completeness and detail expected for this role. With more detailed and deployment-specific insights, the candidate could meet expectations."},{"prompt":"Thanks. Can you describe how you set up subnets and routing in your VPC?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":4,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Candidate understands the basic idea that subnets divide the VPC into smaller segments.","Distinction between public subnets for internet-accessible resources and private subnets for protected resources is noted."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-8","weaknesses":["Answer lacks explanation of availability zones or fault tolerance.","No mention of routing tables or how routing is managed for internet access.","Technical details and structure of setting up routing (e.g., Internet Gateway, NAT Gateway) are missing.","Answer is fragmented and poorly communicated, leading to low clarity."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":4,"expectedAnswer":"I set up subnets by dividing the VPC CIDR block into smaller CIDR ranges, creating separate subnets across multiple Availability Zones for fault tolerance. I typically create public subnets for resources needing internet access and private subnets for internal resources. For routing, I associate each subnet with a route table that directs traffic appropriately, for example, routing internet-bound traffic from public subnets through an internet gateway and ensuring private subnets use NAT gateways for internet access if needed.","candidateAnswer":"subnets and routing subnets and routing divides the VPN into smaller segment public subnet contents resources that require internet access whereas private subnet host resources that should remain inaccessible from public internet such as database state you know you","missing_concepts":["Subnet creation across multiple Availability Zones.","Association of subnets with route tables.","Routing internet-bound traffic via Internet Gateway for public subnets.","Use of NAT Gateways for private subnet internet access."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate shows basic understanding of subnetting by dividing the VPC into smaller segments and differentiating public and private subnets with respect to internet accessibility. However, the answer lacks completeness as it does not cover routing configurations, route tables, and the association of subnets with these routing constructs. It misses important AWS-specific details such as the use of Internet Gateway and NAT Gateway, key to designing a functional VPC network. The response is also disorganized and hard to follow, which risks miscommunication during an interview. Overall, the answer is partially correct but incomplete and lacks sufficient AWS context and clarity.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate understands basic subnet segregation concepts but does not demonstrate sufficient knowledge about routing setups in VPCs, including route tables and gateways. Communication is poor, and important AWS networking elements are missing. They fail to meet the expected standards for an AWS Solutions Architect role for this question."},{"prompt":"Thanks for that explanation. How did you configure the internet gateway and route tables in that VPC setup?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":4,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":3,"communication_clarity":2,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Mentions the concept of enabling private subnet resources to access the internet"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-9","weaknesses":["No clear explanation of attaching an internet gateway to the VPC","No mention of updating route tables with route to internet gateway for public subnets","Confusing and unclear language with poor communication clarity","Lacks details about segregating public and private subnets route tables","Technical terms used incorrectly or vaguely"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"I attached an internet gateway to the VPC to enable communication between the VPC and the internet. Then, I updated the route tables associated with the public subnets to include a route directing 0.0.0.0/0 traffic to the internet gateway, ensuring resources in those subnets can access the internet. Private subnets have route tables without routes to the internet gateway to maintain isolation.","candidateAnswer":"the tables via routing and all that stuff we on network gateway translation gate cloud networking service that allows so resources in private subnet to access the internet without allowing inbound internet connection to this resources.","missing_concepts":["Attaching an internet gateway to the VPC","Adding a 0.0.0.0/0 route to internet gateway on public subnet route tables","Private subnets route tables excluding internet gateway route","Clear distinction between public and private subnet routing"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate failed to clearly articulate the key steps in configuring the internet gateway and route tables. Although there is a vague mention of private subnet resources accessing the internet, the answer lacks the fundamental explanation of attaching an internet gateway to the VPC and updating the route tables accordingly. The answer is disorganized and unclear, demonstrating poor communication and insufficient understanding of the routing setup in a VPC. Important details such as adding the default route to the internet gateway on public subnet route tables and maintaining isolation of private subnets are missing. Overall, the response shows weak technical comprehension and does not satisfactorily address the question.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows very limited understanding of configuring internet gateways and route tables in VPC. The explanation was incomplete and unclear, missing critical technical details necessary for proper AWS networking setup."},{"prompt":"Got it. Let’s move to a final question. How do you ensure high availability when designing a solution using EC2?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-10","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"To ensure high availability with EC2, I deploy instances across multiple Availability Zones within a region to avoid single points of failure. I use Elastic Load Balancers to distribute traffic evenly and detect unhealthy instances, automatically routing traffic away from them. Additionally, I implement Auto Scaling Groups to maintain the desired number of instances and replace unhealthy ones automatically, ensuring continuous availability.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."}]'), ('cmqask2y3002cmv01n4snp32g', 'cmqasdu2p0022mv01qafmigqu', 58, 48, 42, 58, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-12 10:36:18.796', '2026-06-12 10:36:37.623', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["So, I worked on a database management project where my responsibility was to prepare a dashboard.","yes we have four laws of thermodynamics zeroth law about temperature equivalence first law conservation of energy second law about entropy and fourth law about absolute entropy you"]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 60, '[{"prompt":"Laws of thermodyanmics","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":9,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":6},"strengths":["Correctly identified four laws of thermodynamics","Mentioned key points such as temperature equivalence, conservation of energy, entropy, and the relation to absolute entropy"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmqasdu2p0023mv01fkc8s2rs","weaknesses":["Incorrectly named ''fourth law'' instead of third law","Did not explain the zeroth law as establishing thermal equilibrium clearly","Second law explanation was vague, didn''t mention increase of entropy or disorder explicitly","Explanation of the third law was inaccurate referring to ''fourth law about absolute entropy'' rather than third law"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":6,"expectedAnswer":"The laws of thermodynamics describe fundamental principles governing energy and heat transfer. The zeroth law establishes thermal equilibrium, the first law states that energy is conserved (energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed), the second law introduces entropy and states that energy transfer increases disorder, and the third law states that entropy approaches a constant minimum as temperature approaches absolute zero.","candidateAnswer":"Yes we have four laws of thermodynamics: zeroth law about temperature equivalence, first law conservation of energy, second law about entropy, and fourth law about absolute entropy.","missing_concepts":["Clear definition of the zeroth law establishing thermal equilibrium","Explicit mention that the first law is about energy conservation and transformation","Detailed explanation of second law involving entropy and irreversibility","Proper identification and explanation of the third law about entropy approaching a constant minimum at absolute zero"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate correctly identified that there are four laws of thermodynamics and named the zeroth, first, second, and what they called the fourth law, which should be the third law. The descriptions, however, were incomplete and somewhat inaccurate. The zeroth law was reduced to temperature equivalence without mentioning thermal equilibrium explicitly. The first law was described as conservation of energy but lacked details on energy transformation. The second law was mentioned as about entropy but no mention of the increase of entropy or disorder was given. The third law was incorrectly called the fourth law and vaguely described as ''absolute entropy'' without clarifying entropy approaches a constant minimum as temperature reaches absolute zero. Communication was generally understandable but lacked depth. Overall, the answer shows some basic understanding but misses important explanations and correct nomenclature.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a basic recognition of the four laws of thermodynamics but confuses their order and provides incomplete explanations. They demonstrate some understanding of key concepts such as conservation of energy and entropy but do not clearly articulate the fundamental principles or implications of each law. With further study and clarification, the candidate could improve. For now, the a"},{"prompt":"manufacturing process","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmqasdu2p0024mv01dmj5bltt","weaknesses":["Question was asked but the candidate did not respond."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"A manufacturing process is a series of steps through which raw materials are transformed into finished products. Common manufacturing processes include casting, machining, molding, forming, and joining, each selected based on product design, material, and production volume.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"The interviewer asked this question, but no candidate response appears in the transcript.","interviewer_summary":"Asked — no response."},{"prompt":"additive manufacturing","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"cmqasdu2p0025mv019u68pg7a","weaknesses":["Question was asked but the candidate did not respond."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing is a process of creating three-dimensional objects by successively adding material layer by layer, based on digital 3D model data. It allows for complex geometries, reduces material waste compared to subtractive methods, and is useful for rapid prototyping and low-volume production in mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"The interviewer asked this question, but no candidate response appears in the transcript.","interviewer_summary":"Asked — no response."}]'), ('cmqc689ll000nmp01eug1u5m4', 'cmqc5xtlv0007mp01nx9s3y6x', 50, 67, 57, 70, 'Needs more concise and evidence-backed responses. Practice follow-up handling.', '2026-06-13 09:46:48.345', '2026-06-13 09:47:15.935', '["Stayed engaged through interview","Attempted structured responses"]', '["Use concrete examples with outcomes","Answer more directly before elaborating"]', '["Yes. So, this challenge was about the database development project, where I was responsible to collect all the information from the past projects data, the information was all spread in different file formats like Excel or PDF or hard copies or drawings. So, to collect them and structure them and clean the entire data to make it reusable for the platform was a tough task. So, I decided to make a team of 10 people who would be working on different data sets independently and then provide solution as per the requirement and it worked well. It was a tedious task, but we achieved.","Yes, there are four laws of thermodynamics, the zeroth law which is about temperature equivalence, where which sees that when two objects are at different temperatures when brought together will come to a common temperature. This first law which is about conservation of energy, so energy cannot be created nor destroyed it can be it can change its form. Second law of thermodynamics is about entropy which says entropy of a system always tends to increase and the fourth law is about absolute entropy.","It is used in power plants for heat sink related activities, which says that when Heat is applied to any object. It''s energy loser and then for key increases"]', 'question-grade-hybrid', 'gpt-4.1-mini', 46, '[{"prompt":"Hello 01test1306, this is Sana from test. Let’s begin with the first question: Can you tell me about a time when you faced a difficult challenge and how you handled it?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":6,"completeness":5,"problem_solving":5,"communication_clarity":7,"technical_correctness":4},"strengths":["Provided a concrete example of a challenging project.","Demonstrated initiative by organizing a team to tackle the problem.","Communication was generally clear and easy to follow."],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-0","weaknesses":["The challenge described is not directly related to mechanical engineering or expected key skills such as thermodynamics or manufacturing.","Lacks technical depth or explanation of the methodology used to process or clean data.","Did not discuss how the challenge impacted the project technically or outcomes in engineering context.","No reflection on learning or adaptability from the experience."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"A strong candidate should describe a specific challenge they faced, ideally related to engineering or academic projects, outlining the situation clearly. They should explain the steps they took to analyze the problem, the approach or methodology applied to resolve it, and how they adapted or learned from the experience. For example, they might mention managing tight project deadlines by prioritizing tasks and collaborating effectively with team members. This shows problem-solving skills and resilience relevant to the trainee role.","candidateAnswer":"Yes. So, this challenge was about the database development project, where I was responsible to collect all the information from the past projects data, the information was all spread in different file formats like Excel or PDF or hard copies or drawings. So, to collect them and structure them and clean the entire data to make it reusable for the platform was a tough task. So, I decided to make a team of 10 people who would be working on different data sets independently and then provide solution as per the requirement and it worked well. It was a tedious task, but we achieved.","missing_concepts":["Engineering-specific challenges relevant to the role.","Technical approach or analytical methods used to solve the problem.","Explanation linking the challenge to mechanical engineering skills.","Reflection on lessons learned or how the challenge improved skills."],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate provided an example of managing a complex data organization task by forming a team, which shows team management and basic problem-solving skills. However, the challenge described is not related to mechanical engineering nor does it involve any technical concepts related to thermodynamics or manufacturing, which are key areas for the role. The answer lacks technical detail about how data cleaning or structuring was done. There is also no mention of learning or adapting from the challenge, which would indicate resilience and continuous improvement. Overall, the answer is somewhat relevant to a general challenge question but does not align well with the role''s expectations or demonstrate strong engineering problem-solving skills. More technical, role-specific examples and deeper explanation are needed to meet the requirements of this question.","interviewer_summary":"Candidate shows some ability to manage and organize tasks under challenge, with clear communication. However, the example given is not related to mechanical engineering or key role skills, and the technical depth is insufficient. Candidate should be encouraged to provide role-relevant challenges including specific technical problem-solving and reflection on learning outcomes."},{"prompt":"Understood, that sounds like a complex data integration challenge. Now, let’s dive into the fundamentals: can you walk me through the laws of thermodynamics?","result":"Pass","scores":{"relevance":8,"completeness":6,"problem_solving":6,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":7},"strengths":["Correct mention of all four laws of thermodynamics","Accurately stated the zeroth law establishing thermal equilibrium","Properly explained the first law as conservation of energy","Recognized the second law is about entropy increasing"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-1","weaknesses":["Incorrectly referred to the fourth law instead of the third law of thermodynamics","Description of the third law was incomplete and vague (''about absolute entropy'')","Lacked explanation of the significance or implications of each law beyond brief statements","Somewhat unclear phrasing and repetitions reduced communication clarity"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":7,"expectedAnswer":"The candidate should accurately state the four laws of thermodynamics: 1) The Zeroth Law defines thermal equilibrium and the basis of temperature measurement. 2) The First Law states that energy cannot be created or destroyed, only transformed (conservation of energy). 3) The Second Law states that entropy of an isolated system tends to increase, implying spontaneous processes and irreversibility. 4) The Third Law states that as temperature approaches absolute zero, the entropy of a perfect crystal approaches zero. These fundamental principles are essential for understanding energy systems in mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, there are four laws of thermodynamics, the zeroth law which is about temperature equivalence, where which sees that when two objects are at different temperatures when brought together will come to a common temperature. This first law which is about conservation of energy, so energy cannot be created nor destroyed it can be it can change its form. Second law of thermodynamics is about entropy which says entropy of a system always tends to increase and the fourth law is about absolute entropy.","missing_concepts":["Third law states entropy approaches zero as temperature approaches absolute zero in a perfect crystal","More precise and formal articulation of the second law including irreversibility and spontaneity","Explanation of why the zeroth law underpins temperature measurement"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate demonstrated a basic understanding of the four laws of thermodynamics by mentioning all laws by name and providing short summaries of each. The first and second laws were reasonably described, showing awareness of conservation of energy and entropy increase. However, the candidate confused the numbering by calling the last law the ''fourth'' instead of the ''third'' law and gave an inaccurate and vague explanation of it. The explanation of the zeroth law''s significance could be clearer, and the answer overall lacked depth and technical precision. Communication was somewhat repetitive and unclear in places. While the candidate showed foundational knowledge, more completeness and polish are needed to fully meet the expectations for this topic.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate knows the four laws generally and their basic concepts but lacks precision and completeness, especially regarding the third law. Communication is adequate but not polished. This response meets the minimal expectations for a junior mechanical engineer and demonstrates sufficient understanding to pass, though improvement in clarity and detail is recommended."},{"prompt":"Thanks for that overview. Let’s explore a bit more: can you explain how the second law applies in practical engineering scenarios?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":4,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":3,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Mentions application in power plants, implying some real-world context","Attempts to discuss heat and energy transfer"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-2","weaknesses":["Explanation is vague and unclear","Incorrect or confused statements about energy ''loser'' and ''key increases''","Does not clearly explain the Second Law or its implications such as entropy, energy efficiency, or direction of heat transfer","Lacks examples like heat engines or refrigeration to show understanding"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"A good answer explains that the Second Law governs the direction of energy transfer and efficiency limits in engineering systems. For example, it explains why heat engines cannot have 100% efficiency due to entropy increase and why refrigeration requires work input. It also underpins thermodynamic cycle analysis and design, helping engineers optimize energy usage in engines, HVAC, and manufacturing processes by minimizing irreversibilities and losses.","candidateAnswer":"It is used in power plants for heat sink related activities, which says that when Heat is applied to any object. It''s energy loser and then for key increases","missing_concepts":["Entropy and its role in the Second Law","Why 100% efficiency is impossible in heat engines","Work input requirement in refrigeration","Thermodynamic cycle analysis and optimization","Importance of irreversibilities and losses"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate attempts to relate the Second Law to power plants and heat transfer, which is somewhat relevant, but the explanation is unclear and contains inaccuracies. Key concepts such as entropy, directionality of heat transfer, efficiency limits, and practical implications like refrigeration work are omitted. The answer lacks completeness and clarity to demonstrate adequate understanding of the Second Law in engineering. Greater focus on clear, technically accurate examples and terminology would improve the response.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows a very limited and unclear understanding of the Second Law of Thermodynamics in practical engineering settings. The explanation does not meet the expected level for a junior mechanical engineer. More study of basic thermodynamic principles and their applications is necessary."},{"prompt":"Got it, that’s a good example. Now, let’s move on to manufacturing: can you describe a common manufacturing process that you’ve worked with?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":5,"completeness":2,"problem_solving":2,"communication_clarity":4,"technical_correctness":3},"strengths":["Identifies casting as the manufacturing process experienced"],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-3","weaknesses":["Does not describe any steps or key aspects of the casting process","No mention of process parameters, equipment, or quality considerations","Very short and vague answer showing limited understanding","Lacks details that demonstrate hands-on experience or depth"],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":3,"expectedAnswer":"The candidate should describe a manufacturing process such as machining, welding, casting, or injection molding they have hands-on experience with, detailing the key steps involved. For instance, if discussing machining, they should mention material removal by cutting tools, selection of tool parameters, and quality control aspects. Demonstrating familiarity with process parameters, equipment, and quality considerations reflects practical understanding relevant to manufacturing in mechanical engineering.","candidateAnswer":"Yes, casting was one of the manufacturing processes on which I worked so Yes","missing_concepts":["Detailed description of casting process steps","Process parameters and equipment used","Quality control aspects in casting","Demonstration of practical manufacturing understanding"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate correctly identifies casting as a manufacturing process they have worked with, which is relevant. However, the answer lacks any detail about the process itself — no explanation of the steps involved, important parameters, or equipment used. There is also no indication of understanding quality control or problem-solving within the process. The response is very brief and vague, showing limited practical knowledge or communication clarity about manufacturing. To improve, the candidate should provide a clear step-by-step overview of the casting process, discuss key considerations, and reflect on their direct experience.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate shows minimal understanding by naming a manufacturing process but fails to elaborate or demonstrate practical knowledge. The answer lacks completeness and depth, resulting in a failing score."},{"prompt":"Understood. Can you briefly outline the key steps involved in the casting process?","result":"Fail","scores":{"relevance":7,"completeness":3,"problem_solving":4,"communication_clarity":6,"technical_correctness":5},"strengths":["Candidate correctly mentions pouring molten metal and cooling.","Includes finishing process after casting."],"difficulty":"easy","questionId":"txq-4","weaknesses":["Misses major steps such as pattern making and mold preparation.","Does not mention melting process explicitly.","No mention of shakeout or inspection steps.","Answer is quite brief and lacks depth.","Limited evidence of understanding the full casting process."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":5,"expectedAnswer":"Casting typically involves: 1) Pattern making to create a replica of the desired part, 2) Mold preparation by packing sand or other materials around the pattern, 3) Melting of the metal to be cast, 4) Pouring molten metal into the mold cavity, 5) Cooling and solidification of the metal, 6) Removing the casting from the mold (shakeout), and 7) Cleaning, finishing, and inspection of the cast part. Understanding these steps shows fundamental knowledge of this common manufacturing method.","candidateAnswer":"In the casting process, the molten metal is first poured into the die, then it is allowed to cool. Once the product cools, it is taken out and some amount of finishing process is done before handing over.","missing_concepts":["Pattern making","Mold preparation","Metal melting","Shakeout (removal of casting from mold)","Inspection of the cast part"],"detailed_feedback":"The candidate''s answer shows only a partial understanding of the casting process. While pouring molten metal and cooling are correctly mentioned, key initial steps such as pattern making and mold preparation are completely omitted. The melting step is implied but not explicitly stated. Also missing are post-casting steps like shakeout and inspection. The answer is brief and lacks important details that demonstrate a complete grasp of the process. Communication is clear but minimal. Overall, the answer is technically correct where present but too incomplete to pass.","interviewer_summary":"The candidate demonstrates very basic knowledge of casting but misses many critical steps, indicating incomplete understanding. More comprehensive knowledge of the manufacturing process is necessary for this role."},{"prompt":"Thank you for summarizing that. Now, could you explain what additive manufacturing is and how it differs from casting?","result":"Not Answered","scores":{"relevance":0,"completeness":0,"problem_solving":0,"communication_clarity":0,"technical_correctness":0},"strengths":[],"difficulty":"medium","questionId":"txq-5","weaknesses":["Question was not answered during the interview."],"isMandatory":true,"overallScore":0,"expectedAnswer":"Additive manufacturing (AM), or 3D printing, builds parts layer by layer directly from digital models, allowing complex geometries and internal features that are difficult or impossible with traditional methods. In contrast, casting is a subtractive process involving pouring molten material into molds to form parts. AM reduces material waste, offers faster prototyping, and enables customization, while casting is suited for large volume production of metal parts but can have limitations in design complexity and requires tooling.","candidateAnswer":"","missing_concepts":[],"detailed_feedback":"This question was not addressed in the interview.","interviewer_summary":"No answer provided."}]');